Œ	¶÷ñ)•>wÂ©ù                                                                                                                                                   ,Ž~‚SThe waters returned and covered the chariots and the charioteers, and all the army of Pharaoh that had gone into the sea after them; not even one of them survived.‚Ž}„%So Moses stretched out his hand over the sea, and the sea returned to its normal flow at sunrise; and the Egyptians retreated right into it <n>[being met by the returning water]</n>; so the LORD overthrew the Egyptians <i>and</i> tossed them into the midst of the sea.1Ž|‚]<pb/>Then the LORD said to Moses, "Stretch out your hand over the sea so that the waters may come back over the Egyptians, on their war-chariots and their charioteers."CŽ{ƒHe made their chariot wheels hard to turn, and the chariots difficult to drive; so the Egyptians said, "Let us flee from Israel, for the LORD is fighting for them against the Egyptians."JŽzƒSo it happened at the early morning watch <n>[before dawn]</n>, that the LORD looked down on the army of the Egyptians through the pillar of fire and cloud and put them in a state of confusion.Žy‚Then the Egyptians pursued them into the middle of the sea, even all Pharaoh's horses, his war-chariots and his charioteers.Žx‚The Israelites went into the middle of the sea on dry land, and the waters formed a wall to them on their right hand and on their left.DŽwƒ<pb/>Then Moses stretched out his hand over the sea; and the LORD swept the sea back by a strong east wind all that night and turned the seabed into dry land, and the waters were divided.‚ŽvƒSo it came between the camp of Egypt and the camp of Israel. It was a cloud along with darkness <n>[even by day to the Egyptians]</n>, but it gave light by night <n>[to the Israelites]</n>; so one <n>[army]</n> did not come near the other all night.;Žu‚q<pb/>The<f>[3]</f> angel of God, who had been going in front of the camp of Israel, moved and went behind them. The pillar of the cloud moved from in front and stood behind them.RŽtƒAnd the Egyptians shall know <n>[without any doubt]</n> <i>and</i> acknowledge that I am the LORD, when I am glorified <i>and</i> honored through Pharaoh, through his war-chariots and his charioteers."nŽsƒWAs for Me, hear this: I will harden the hearts of the Egyptians, and they will go in <n>[the sea]</n> after them; and I will be glorified <i>and</i> honored through Pharaoh and all his army, and his war-chariots and his horsemen.*Žr‚OAs for you, lift up your staff and stretch out your hand over the sea and divide it, so that the sons of Israel may go through the middle of the sea on dry land.}Žqu<pb/>The LORD said to Moses, "Why do you cry to Me? Tell the sons of Israel to move forward <n>[toward the sea]</n>.iŽpMThe LORD will fight for you while you <n>[only need to]</n> keep silent <i>and</i> remain calm."‚
