ƒC$They received from Moses all the offerings which the Israelites had brought for the construction of the sanctuary, to prepare it for service. And they continued to bring him freewill (voluntary) offerings every morning.&”	‚G$<pb/>So Moses called Bezalel and Oholiab and every skilled person in whom the LORD had put ability, everyone whose heart stirred him, to come to do the work.m”	ƒW$<pb/>"Bezalel and Oholiab, and every skilled person in whom the LORD has put ability and understanding to know how to do all the work in the construction of the sanctuary, shall work according to all that the LORD has commanded."y”ƒm##He has filled them with skill to do the work of an engraver, of a designer, and of an embroiderer, in blue, purple, and scarlet fabric, and in fine linen, and of a weaver; makers of every work and embroiderers of <n>[excellent]</n> designs.*”‚O#"He has also put in Bezalel's heart <n>[the willingness]</n> to teach <n>[others the same skills]</n>, both he and Oholiab, son of Ahisamach, of the tribe of Dan.n”W#!and in the cutting of stones for setting and in the carving of wood, for work in every skilled craft.H”# to devise artistic designs to work in gold, silver, and bronze,;”‚q#and He has filled him with the Spirit of God, with wisdom <i>and</i> skill, with intelligence <i>and</i> understanding, and with knowledge in all <n>[areas of]</n> craftsmanship,	”‚
#<pb/>Then Moses said to the Israelites, "See, the LORD called by name Bezalel son of Uri, the son of Hur, of the tribe of Judah;[”ƒ1#The Israelites, all the men and women whose heart moved them to bring <i>material</i> for all the work which the LORD had commanded through Moses to be done, brought a freewill (voluntary) offering to the LORD.o” Y#and spice and <n>[olive]</n> oil for the light and for the anointing oil and for the fragrant incense.v“g#The leaders brought onyx stones and other stones to be put in settings for the ephod and for the breastpiece,T“~##All the women whose heart stirred with a skill spun the goats' <i>hair</i>.#“}‚A#All the skilled <i>and</i> talented women spun thread with their hands, and brought what they had spun, blue and purple and scarlet fabric and fine linen.B“|‚#Everyone who could make an offering of silver or bronze brought it as the <e>Lord's</e> offering; every man who had in his possession acacia wood for any work of the service brought it.E“{ƒ#Every man who had in his possession blue or purple or scarlet fabric, and fine linen, and goats' <i>hair</i>, and<f>[5]</f> rams' skins dyed red and<f>[6]</f> porpoise skins, brought them.\“zƒ3#Then all whose hearts moved them, both men and women, came and brought brooches, earrings <i>or</i> nose rings, signet rings, and necklaces, all jewels of gold; everyone bringing an offering of gold to the LORD.M“yƒ#Everyone whose heart stirred him and everyone whose spirit moved him came and brought the <e>Lord's</e> offering to be used for the Tent of Meeting, for all its service, and for the holy garments.J“x#Then all the congregation of the Israelites left Moses' presence.%“w‚E#the finely-woven garments for ministering in the Holy Place, the holy garments for Aaron the priest and the garments for his sons, to minister as priests.'"N“v#the pegs of the tabernacle and the pegs of the court and their cords;r“u_#the court's curtains, its support poles and their sockets, and the curtain for the gate of the courtyard;“t‚#the altar of burnt offering with its bronze grating, its carrying poles, and all its utensils, the wash basin and its base (stand);-“s‚U#and the altar of incense and its carrying poles, the anointing oil and the fragrant incense, the screen (curtain) for the doorway at the entrance of the tabernacle;d“rC#the lampstand also for the light and its utensils and its lamps, and the oil for the light;{“qq#
the table and its carrying poles, and all its utensils, and the bread of the <n>[divine]</n> Presence (showbread);N“pƒ#the ark <n>[of the covenant]</n> and its carrying poles, with the<f>[4]</f> mercy seat and the veil (partition curtain) of the screen <n>[to hang between the Holy Place and the Holy of Holies]</n>;“o‚#the tabernacle (sacred dwelling of God), its tent and its covering, its hooks, its boards, its bars, its pillars, and its sockets;t“nc#
'Let every skilled <i>and</i> talented man among you come, and make everything that the LORD has commanded:`“m;#	and<f>[3]</f> onyx stones and other stones to be set for the ephod and the breastpiece.q“l]#and <n>[olive]</n> oil for the lighting, and balsam for the anointing oil, and for the fragrant incense,_“k9#and<f>[1]</f> rams' skins dyed red, and skins of<f>[2]</f> porpoises, and acacia wood,J“j#blue, purple, and scarlet fabric, fine linen, goats' <i>hair</i>,“i‚5#'Take from among you an offering to the LORD. Whoever has a willing heart, let him bring it as the <e>Lord's</e> offering: gold, silver, and bronze,|“hs#<pb/>And Moses said to all the congregation of the sons of Israel, "This is the thing which the LORD has commanded:R“g#You shall not kindle a fire in any of your dwellings on the Sabbath day."G“fƒ	#<pb/>"For six days work may be done, but the seventh day shall be a holy day for you, a Sabbath of complete rest to the LORD; whoever does any kind of work on that day shall be put to death. “e	‚=#<pb/>Moses gathered all the congregation of the sons of Israel together, and said to them, "These are the things which the LORD has commanded you to do:4“d‚c"#the Israelites would see the face of Moses, how his skin shone <n>[with a unique radiance]</n>. So Moses put the veil on his face again until he went in to speak with God.V“cƒ'""But whenever Moses went in before the LORD to speak with Him,<f>[6]</f> he would take off the veil until he came out. When he came out and he told the Israelites what he had been commanded <n>[by God]</n>,Q“b"!When Moses had finished speaking with them, he put a veil over his face.
“a‚" Afterward all the Israelites approached him, and he commanded them to do everything that the LORD had said to him on Mount Sinai.{“`q"But Moses called to them, and Aaron and all the leaders of the congregation returned to him; and he spoke to them.“_y"When Aaron and all the Israelites saw Moses, behold, the skin of his face shone, and they were afraid to approach him.^“^ƒ7"When Moses came down from Mount Sinai with the two tablets of the Testimony in his hand, he did not know that the skin of his face was shining <n>[with a unique radiance]</n> because he had been speaking with God.4“]‚c"Moses was there with the LORD forty days and forty nights; he ate no bread and drank no water. And he wrote on the tablets the words of the covenant, the Ten Commandments.“\‚!"<pb/>Then the LORD said to Moses, "Write these words, for in accordance with these words I have made a covenant with you and with Israel."\“[ƒ3"<pb/><t>"You shall bring the very first of the first fruits of your ground to the house of the LORD your God. </t><br/>"You shall not<f>[5]</f> boil a young goat in his mother's milk <n>[as some pagans do]</n>."5“Z‚e"<pb/>"You shall not offer the blood of My sacrifice with leavened bread, nor shall the sacrifice of the Feast of the Passover (Unleavened Bread) be left over until morning.d“YƒC"For I will drive out <i>and</i> dispossess nations before you and enlarge your borders; nor shall any man covet (actively seek for himself) your land when you go up to appear before the LORD your God three times a year.i“XM"Three times a year all your males shall appear before the Lord<f>[4]</f> GOD, the God of Israel.X“Wƒ+"You shall observe <i>and</i> celebrate the Feast of Weeks (Harvest, First Fruits, or Pentecost), the first fruits of the wheat harvest, and the Feast of Ingathering (Booths or Tabernacles) at the year's end.'“V‚I"<pb/>"You shall work for six days, but on the seventh day you shall rest; <n>[even]</n> in plowing time and in harvest you shall rest <n>[on the Sabbath]</n>._“Uƒ9"You shall redeem the firstborn of a donkey with a lamb; but if you do not redeem it, then you shall break its neck. You shall redeem all the firstborn of your sons. None of you are to appear before Me empty-handed.b“T?"<pb/>"All the firstborn males among your livestock belong to Me, whether cattle or sheep.n“SƒW"<pb/>"You shall observe the Feast of Unleavened Bread (Passover). For seven days you shall eat unleavened bread, as I have commanded you, at the appointed time in the month of Abib; for in the month of Abib you came out of Egypt.5“Rg"You shall make for yourselves no molten gods.‚	“Q„
"and you might take some of his daughters for your sons, and his daughters would play the prostitute with their gods and cause your sons also to play the prostitute (commit apostasy) with their gods <n>[that is, abandon the true God for man-made idols]</n>.a“Pƒ="otherwise you might make a covenant with the inhabitants of the land and they would play the prostitute with their gods and sacrifice to their gods, and someone might invite you<f>[3]</f> to eat his sacrifice (meal),2“O‚_"â€”for you shall not worship any other god; for the LORD, whose name is Jealous, is a jealous (impassioned) God <n>[demanding what is rightfully and uniquely His]</n>â€”6“N‚g"
But you shall tear down <i>and</i> destroy their <n>[pagan]</n> altars, smash in pieces their <n>[sacred]</n> pillars (obelisks, images) and cut down their<f>[2]</f> AsherimG“Mƒ	"Watch yourself so that you do not make a covenant (solemn agreement, treaty) with the inhabitants of the land into which you are going, or it will become a <n>[dangerous]</n> trap among you.I“Lƒ
"<pb/>"Be sure to observe what I am commanding you this day: behold, I am going to drive out the Amorite before you, and the Canaanite, the Hittite, the Perizzite, the Hivite, and the Jebusite.‚q“K…]"
Then God said, "Behold, I am going to make a covenant. Before all your people I will do wondrous works (miracles) such as have not been created <i>or</i> produced in all the earth nor among any of the nations; and all the people among whom you live shall see the working of the LORD, for it is a fearful <i>and</i> awesome thing that I am going to do with you.‚	“J„
"	And he said, "If now I have found favor <i>and</i> lovingkindness in Your sight, O Lord, let the Lord, please, go in our midst, though it is a stiff-necked (stubborn, rebellious) people, and pardon our iniquity and our sin, and take us as Your possession."N“I"Moses bowed to the earth immediately and worshiped <n>[the Lord]</n>.ƒ“H†"keeping mercy <i>and</i> lovingkindness for thousands, forgiving iniquity and transgression and sin; but He will by no means leave <i>the guilty</i> unpunished, visiting (avenging) the iniquity (sin, guilt) of the fathers upon the children and the grandchildren to the third and fourth generations <n>[that is, calling the children to account for the sins of their fathers]</n>."?“G‚y"Then the LORD passed by in front of him, and proclaimed, "The LORD, the LORD God, compassionate and gracious, slow to anger, and abounding in lovingkindness and truth (faithfulness);
