and the two kidneys with the fat that is on them at the loins, and the lobe of the liver, which he shall remove with the kidneys.{•dƒq	From the sacrifice of peace offerings he shall bring as an offering by fire to the LORD, its fat, the entire fat tail which he shall remove close to the backbone, and the fat that covers the entrails, and all the fat which is on the entrails,%•c‚Eand he shall lay his hand on the head of his offering and kill it before the Tent of Meeting, and Aaron's sons shall sprinkle its blood around on the altar.W•b)If he offers a lamb as his offering, then he shall present it before the LORD,•aIf his peace offering to the LORD is an animal from the flock, male or female, he shall offer the animal without blemish.[•`ƒ1Aaron's sons shall offer it up in smoke on the altar <n>[placing it]</n> on the burnt offering which is on the wood that is on the fire. It is an offering by fire, a sweet <i>and</i> soothing aroma to the LORD.•_‚!and the two kidneys with the fat that is on them at the loins, and the<f>[1]</f> lobe of the liver which he shall remove with the kidneys.1•^‚]From the sacrifice of the peace offerings, an offering by fire to the LORD, he shall present the fat that covers the entrails, and all the fat which is on the entrails,v•]ƒgHe shall lay his hand on the head of his offering <n>[transferring symbolically his guilt to the sacrifice]</n> and kill it at the doorway of the Tent of Meeting; and Aaron's sons the priests shall sprinkle the blood around on the altar.5•\	‚g<pb/>'If a man's offering is a sacrifice of peace offerings, if he offers an animal from the herd, whether male or female, he shall offer it without blemish before the LORD.,•[‚SThe priest shall offer up in smoke its memorial portion, part of the crushed grain and part of its oil with all its incense; it is an offering by fire to the LORD.O•ZYou shall put oil on it and lay incense on it