What is left of the grain offering belongs to Aaron and his sons; it is a most holy part of the offerings to the LORD by fire.<•T‚s	The priest shall take from the grain offering its memorial portion and offer it up in smoke on the altar. It is an offering by fire, a sweet <i>and</i> soothing aroma to the LORD.8•S‚kWhen you bring the grain offering that is made of these things to the LORD, it shall be presented to the priest, and he shall bring it to the altar <n>[of burnt offering]</n>.g•RINow if your offering is grain cooked in a lidded pan, it shall be made of fine flour with oil._•Q9You are to break it into pieces, and you shall pour oil on it; it is a grain offering.l•PSIf your offering is grain baked on a griddle, it shall be of fine unleavened flour, mixed with oil.0•O‚[<pb/>'When you bring an offering of grain baked in the oven, it shall be<f>[2]</f> unleavened cakes of fine flour mixed with oil, or unleavened wafers spread with oil.•N‚	What is left of the grain offering belongs to Aaron and his sons; it is a most holy part of the offerings to the LORD by fire.‚O•M…He shall bring it to Aaron's sons the priests. Out of it he shall take a handful of the fine flour and oil, with all of its frankincense, and the priest shall offer this up in smoke on the altar <n>[of burnt offering]</n> as the memorial portion of it. It is an offering by fire, a sweet <i>and</i> soothing aroma to the LORD.8•L	‚m<pb/>'When<f>[1]</f> anyone presents a grain offering to the Lord, his offering shall be of fine flour, and he shall pour <n>[olive]</n> oil over it and put frankincense on it.}•K	ƒwThen he shall tear it open by its wings, but shall not sever it. And the priest shall offer it up in smoke on the altar, on the wood that is on the fire. It is a burnt offering, an offering by fire, a sweet <i>and</i> soothing aroma to the LORD.•J	‚He shall remove its<f>[4]</f> crop with its feathers and throw it next to the east side of the altar, in the place for ashes.+•I	‚SThe priest shall bring it to the altar, and wring off its head, and offer it up in smoke on the altar; and its blood is to be drained out on the side of the altar.
