Moses then put the breastpiece on Aaron, and he put in the breastpiece the Urim and the Thummim <n>[the sacred articles the high priest used when seeking God's will concerning the nation]</n>.z–mƒoHe put the undertunic on Aaron, tied the sash around him, clothed him in the robe, and put the<f>[1]</f> ephod (an upper vestment) on him. He tied the <n>[skillfully woven]</n> band of the ephod around him, with which he secured it to Aaron.O–l<pb/>Then Moses brought Aaron and his sons and washed them with water.X–k+Moses said to the congregation, "This is what the LORD has commanded us to do."w–jiMoses did as the LORD commanded him, and the congregation was assembled at the doorway of the Tent of Meeting.U–i%and assemble the entire congregation at the doorway of the Tent of Meeting."X–hƒ+"Take Aaron and his sons with him, and the garments <n>[which are symbols of their office]</n>, and the anointing oil, and the bull for the sin offering, and the two rams, and the basket of unleavened bread;1–g	a<pb/>Then the LORD spoke to Moses, saying,!–f‚=&which the LORD commanded Moses at Mount Sinai on the day He commanded the Israelites to present their offerings to the LORD, in the Wilderness of Sinai.<–e‚s%<pb/>This is the law of the burnt offering, the grain offering, the sin offering, the guilt offering, the consecration (ordination) offering, and the sacrifice of peace offerings,6–d‚g$The LORD commanded this to be given to the priests by the Israelites on the day that He anointed them. It is <i>their</i> portion perpetually throughout their generations.'"E–cƒ#<pb/>'This is the <i>consecrated</i> portion from the offerings by fire to the LORD that was designated for Aaron and his sons on the day he presented them to serve as priests to the LORD.‚
–b„"For I have taken the breast of the wave offering and the thigh of the heave offering from the Israelites, from the sacrifices of their peace offerings, and I have given them to Aaron the priest and to his sons as their perpetual portion from the Israelites.|–as!The son of Aaron who offers the blood of the peace offerings and the fat shall have the right thigh as his portion.t–`c You shall give the right thigh to the priest as a contribution from the sacrifices of your peace offerings.q–_]The priest shall offer up the fat in smoke on the altar, but the breast shall be for Aaron and his sons.9–^‚mWith his own hands he is to bring offerings by fire to the LORD; he shall bring the fat with the breast, so that the breast may be presented as a wave offering before the LORD.B–]‚"Speak to the children of Israel, saying, 'He who offers the sacrifice of his peace offerings to the LORD shall bring his offering to the LORD from the sacrifice of his peace offerings.2–\a<pb/>Then the LORD spoke to Moses, saying,P–[Whoever eats any blood, that person shall be cut off from his people.'" –Z{Moreover, you are not to eat any blood <n>[of any kind]</n>, whether of bird or animal, in any of your dwelling places.W–Yƒ)For whoever eats the fat of the animal from which an offering by fire is presented to the LORD, that person who eats shall be cut off from his people <n>[excluding him from the atonement made for them]</n>.P–XƒThe fat of an animal which dies <n>[of natural causes]</n> and the fat of one which is torn <n>[to pieces by a predator]</n> may be put to any other use, but under no circumstances are you to eat it.m–WU"Speak to the children of Israel, saying, 'You shall not eat any fat from an ox, a sheep, or a goat.2–Va<pb/>Then the LORD spoke to Moses, saying,‚;–U„qWhen anyone touches any unclean thingâ€”human uncleanness, or an unclean animal, or any unclean<f>[2]</f> detestable thingâ€”and then eats the meat of the sacrifice of the <e>Lord's</e> peace offerings, that person shall be cut off from his people <n>[excluding him from the atonement made for them]</n>.'"f–TƒGBut the one who eats meat from the sacrifice of peace offerings which belong to the LORD, in his uncleanness, that person shall be<f>[1]</f> cut off from his people <n>[excluding him from the atonement made for them]</n>.
