The one who kills an animal shall replace it, animal for animal.r›_'If a man takes the life of any human being <n>[unlawfully]</n>, he shall most certainly be put to death.y›ƒmFurther, the one who blasphemes the name of the LORD shall most certainly be put to death; all the congregation shall stone him. The stranger as well as the native-born shall be put to death when he blasphemes the Name <n>[of the LORD]</n>.}›uYou shall speak to the Israelites, saying, 'Whoever curses his God will bear his sin <n>[through his own death]</n>.M›ƒ"Bring the one who has cursed <n>[the LORD]</n> outside the camp, and let all who heard him lay their hands on his head <n>[as witnesses to his guilt]</n>; then let all the congregation stone him.2›a
<pb/>Then the LORD spoke to Moses, saying,k›QThey put him in custody until the will <i>and</i> command of the LORD might be made clear to them.H›ƒThe Israelite woman's son blasphemed the Name <n>[of the LORD]</n> and cursed. So they brought him to Moses. (Now his mother's name was Shelomith, the daughter of Dibri, of the tribe of Dan.)D›ƒ
<pb/>Now the son of an Israelite woman, whose father was an Egyptian, went out among the Israelites, and he and a man of Israel quarreled <i>and</i> struggled with each other in the camp.P› ƒ	The bread of the Presence shall be for Aaron and his sons, and they shall eat it in a sacred place, for it is for Aaron a most holy portion of the offerings by fire to the LORD, his portion forever."š‚Every Sabbath day Aaron shall arrange the showbread before the LORD continually; it is an everlasting covenant for the Israelites./š~‚YYou shall put pure frankincense <n>[in two censers, one]</n> beside each row, so that it may be with the bread as a memorial portion, an offering by fire to the LORD.š}‚You shall set the bread of the Presence (showbread) in two rows, six in a row, on the pure <i>gold</i> table before the LORD.+š|‚Q<pb/>"Then you shall take fine flour and bake twelve cakes (bread of the Presence, showbread) with it; two-tenths of <i>an ephah</i> shall be in each cake (loaf).gš{IHe shall keep the lamps burning on the pure <i>gold</i> lampstand before the LORD continually.‚šz„)Outside the veil of the Testimony <n>[between the Holy Place and the Most Holy Place]</n> in the Tent of Meeting, Aaron shall always keep the lamps<f>[1]</f> burning before the LORD from evening until morning; it shall be a permanent statute throughout your generations.&šy‚G"Command the children of Israel to bring to you clear oil from beaten olives for the light <n>[of the golden lampstand]</n>, to make a lamp burn continually.1šx	a<pb/>Then the LORD spoke to Moses, saying,Nšw,So Moses declared to the Israelites the appointed feasts of the LORD.šv‚9+so that your generations may know that I had the sons of Israel live in booths when I brought them out of the land of Egypt. I am the LORD your God.'"všug*You shall live in booths (temporary shelters) for seven days; all native-born in Israel shall live in booths,<št‚s)You shall celebrate it as a feast to the LORD for seven days in the year. It shall be a permanent statute throughout your generations; you shall celebrate it in the seventh month.‚šs„(Now on the first day you shall take for yourselves the foliage of beautiful trees, branches of palm trees, and boughs of thick (leafy) trees, and willows of the brook <n>[and make booths of them]</n>; and you shall rejoice before the LORD your God for seven days.‚šr„'<pb/>'On exactly the fifteenth day of the seventh month (nearly October), when you have gathered in the crops of the land, you shall celebrate the feast of the LORD for seven days, with a Sabbath rest on the first day and a Sabbath rest on the eighth day.Ašq‚}&This is in addition to the <n>[weekly]</n> Sabbaths of the LORD, and in addition to your gifts and all your vowed offerings and all your freewill offerings, which you give to the LORD.‚šp„%<pb/>'These are the appointed times (established feasts) of the LORD, which you shall proclaim to be holy convocations, to present an offering by fire to the LORD, a burnt offering and a grain offering, sacrifices and drink offerings, each on its own day.šoƒy$For seven days you shall present an offering by fire to the LORD. On the eighth day you shall have a holy convocation and present an offering by fire to the LORD. It is a festive assembly; you shall not do any laborious work <n>[on that day]</n>.zšno#The first day is a holy convocation (calling together); you shall not do any laborious work <n>[on that day]</n>.šm‚1""Say to the children of Israel, 'On the fifteenth day of this seventh month, and for seven days, is the Feast of Booths (Tabernacles) to the LORD..šlY!Again the LORD spoke to Moses, saying,8šk‚k It is to be to you a Sabbath of complete rest, and you shall humble yourselves. On the ninth day of the month at evening, from evening to evening you shall keep your Sabbath."šj‚You shall do no work at all <n>[on that day]</n>. It is a permanent statute throughout your generations wherever you may be.ušieIf there is any person who does any work on this same day, I will destroy that person from among his people.*šh‚OIf there is any person who will not humble himself on this same day, he shall be cut off from his people <n>[excluding him from the atonement made for them]</n>.šg‚You shall not do any work on this same day, for it is the Day of Atonement, to make atonement on your behalf before the LORD your God.^šfƒ7"Also the tenth day of this seventh month is the Day of Atonement; it shall be a holy convocation for you, and you shall<f>[6]</f> humble yourselves <n>[by fasting]</n> and present an offering by fire to the LORD.(šeMThe LORD spoke to Moses, saying,{šdqYou shall not do any laborious work <n>[on that day]</n>, but you shall present an offering by fire to the LORD.'"dšcƒC"Say to the children of Israel, 'On the first day of the seventh month (almost October), you shall observe a day of solemn sabbatical rest, a memorial day announced by the blowing <i>of trumpets</i>, a holy convocation..šbYAgain the LORD spoke to Moses, saying,ašaƒ=<pb/>'When you reap the harvest of your land, you shall not reap to the edges of your field, nor gather the gleaning of your harvest; you are to leave them for the poor and for the stranger. I am the LORD your God.'"zš`ƒoOn this same day you shall make a proclamation, you are to have a holy convocation (calling together); you shall not do any laborious work <n>[on that day]</n>. It is to be a permanent statute throughout your generations wherever you may be.6š_‚gThe priest shall wave them before the LORD as a wave offering, together with the bread of the first fruits and the two lambs. They are to be holy to the LORD for the priest.š^‚And you shall sacrifice one male goat as a sin offering and two male lambs, one year old as a sacrifice of peace offerings.‚š]„9And you shall offer with the bread seven unblemished lambs, one year old, and one young bull and two rams. They are to be a burnt offering to the LORD, with their grain offering and their drink offerings. It is an offering by fire, a sweet <i>and</i> soothing aroma to the LORD.Hš\ƒYou shall bring in from your places two loaves of bread as a wave offering, made from two-tenths <i>of an ephah</i> of fine flour; they shall be baked with leaven as first fruits to the LORD.š[‚You shall count<f>[5]</f> fifty days to the day after the seventh Sabbath; then you shall present a new grain offering to the LORD.LšZƒ'You shall count from the day after the Sabbath, from the day when you brought in the sheaf (tied bundle of grain) of the wave offering; there shall be seven complete Sabbaths (seven full weeks).OšYƒYou shall not eat any bread or roasted grain or new growth, until this same day when you bring in the offering to your God; it is a permanent statute throughout your generations wherever you may be.‚šX„	
Its grain offering shall be two-tenths of an ephah of fine flour mixed with <n>[olive]</n> oil, an offering by fire to the LORD for a sweet <i>and</i> soothing aroma, with its drink offering <n>[to be poured out]</n>, a fourth of a<f>[4]</f> hin of wine.	šW‚
Now on the day when you wave the sheaf you shall offer a male lamb one year old without blemish as a burnt offering to the LORD.šV‚He shall wave the sheaf before the LORD so that you may be accepted; the priest shall wave it on the day after the Sabbath.VšUƒ'
"Speak to the children of Israel and say to them, 'When you enter the land which I am giving you and reap its harvest, you shall bring the<f>[3]</f> sheaf of the first fruits of your harvest to the priest.-šTW	Then the LORD spoke to Moses, saying,@šS‚{But you shall present an offering by fire to the LORD for seven days; on the seventh day there shall be a holy convocation; you shall not do any laborious work <n>[on that day]</n>.'"	šR‚
On the first day you shall have a holy convocation (calling together); you shall not do any laborious work <n>[on that day]</n>.šQ‚The Feast of Unleavened Bread to the LORD is on the fifteenth day of the same month; for seven days you shall eat unleavened bread.fšPGThe <e>Lord's</e> Passover is on the fourteenth day of the first month<f>[2]</f> at twilight.yšOm'These are the appointed times of the LORD, holy convocations which you shall proclaim at their appointed times:qšNƒ]'For six days work may be done, but the seventh day is the Sabbath of complete rest, a holy convocation (calling together). You shall not do any work <n>[on that day]</n>; it is the Sabbath of the LORD<f>[1]</f> wherever you may be.>šM‚w"Speak to the children of Israel and say to them, 'The appointed times (established feasts) of the LORD which you shall proclaim as holy convocationsâ€”My appointed times are these:2šL	c<pb/>The LORD spoke again to Moses, saying,QšK!who brought you out of the land of Egypt to be your God; I am the LORD."‚šJ„ <pb/>"You shall not profane My holy name <n>[using it to honor an idol, or treating it with irreverence or contempt or as a byword]</n>; but I will be sanctified (set apart as holy) among the Israelites. I am the LORD, who sanctifies <i>and</i> declares you holy,FšISo you shall keep My commandments and do them; I am the LORD.tšHcIt shall be eaten on the same day; you shall leave none of it until <i>the next</i> morning; I am the LORD.xšGkWhen you sacrifice an offering of thanksgiving to the LORD, you shall sacrifice it so that you may be accepted.ršF_And whether <n>[the mother]</n> is a cow or a sheep, you shall not kill both it and its young in one day.5šE‚e"When a bull or a sheep or a goat is born, it shall remain for seven days with its mother; and after the eighth day it shall be accepted as an offering by fire to the LORD.2šDa<pb/>Then the LORD spoke to Moses, saying,hšCƒKNor shall you offer as the food of your God any such <n>[animals obtained]</n> from a foreigner, because their corruption <i>and</i> blemish makes them unfit; there is a defect in them, they shall not be accepted for you.'"šB‚You shall not offer to the LORD any animal which has its testicles bruised or crushed or torn or cut off, or sacrifice it in your land.;šA‚qFor a freewill offering you may offer either a bull or a lamb which has an overgrown or stunted member (deformity), but for <n>[the payment of]</n> a vow it will not be accepted.Wš@ƒ)Animals <i>that are</i> blind or fractured or mutilated, or have a sore or a running wound or an itch or scabs, you shall not offer to the LORD nor make an offering of them by fire on the altar to the LORD.fš?ƒGWhoever offers a sacrifice of peace offerings to the LORD to fulfill a special vow to the LORD or as a freewill offering from the herd or from the flock, it must be perfect to be accepted; there shall be no blemish in it.cš>AYou shall not offer anything which has a blemish, because it will not be accepted for you.rš=_so that you may be acceptedâ€”it must be a male without blemish from the cattle, the sheep, or the goats.‚;š<„q"Speak to Aaron and his sons and to all the Israelites and say to them, 'Any man of the house of Israel or any stranger in Israel who presents his offering, whether to <i>fulfill</i> any of their vows or as any of their freewill (voluntary) offerings which they presented to the LORD as a burnt offeringâ€”-š;WThen the LORD spoke to Moses, saying,>š:‚wand so cause them <n>[by neglect of any essential observance]</n> to bear the<f>[1]</f> punishment of guilt when they eat their holy things; for I am the LORD who sanctifies them.'"Xš9+The priests shall not profane the holy things the Israelites offer to the LORD,@š8‚{But if a person unknowingly eats a holy <i>gift</i> <n>[which has been offered to God]</n>, then he shall add one-fifth of its value to it and give the holy <i>gift</i> to the priest.=š7‚u
But if a priest's daughter is a widow or divorced, and has no child, and returns to her father's house as in her youth, she shall eat her father's food; but no layman shall eat it.š6‚'If a priest's daughter is married to a layman <n>[one not part of the priestly tribe]</n>, she shall not eat the offering of the holy things.,š5‚SBut if a priest buys a slave as his property with his money, the slave may eat the holy thing, and those who are born in the priest's house; they may eat his food.eš4ƒE
<pb/>'No layman <n>[that is, someone outside of Aaron's family]</n> is to eat the holy <i>gift</i> <n>[which has been offered to God]</n>; a foreigner residing with the priest or a hired man shall not eat the holy thing.&š3‚G	Therefore the priests shall observe My ordinance, so that they will not bear sin because of it and die if they profane it; I am the LORD who sanctifies them.š2‚He shall not eat that which dies <n>[of natural causes]</n> or is torn by a predator, becoming unclean by it; I am the LORD.kš1QWhen the sun sets, he will be clean, and afterward he may eat the holy things, for it is his food.š0‚)the person who touches any such thing shall be unclean until evening and shall not eat the holy things unless he has bathed his body in water.	š/‚
or whoever touches any crawling thing by which he is made unclean, or any person by whom he is made unclean, whatever it may be,‚&š.„GNo man of the descendants of Aaron who is a leper or has a discharge may eat the holy things <n>[the offerings and the showbread]</n> until he is clean. And whoever touches any person <i>or</i> thing made unclean by <i>contact with</i> a corpse or a man who has had a seminal emission,‚(š-„KSay to them, 'Any one of your descendants throughout your generations who approaches the holy things which the Israelites dedicate to the LORD, while he is <n>[ceremonially]</n> unclean, that person shall be cut off from My presence <i>and</i> excluded from the sanctuary; I am the LORD.=š,‚u"Tell Aaron and his sons to be careful with the holy things (offerings, gifts) which the children of Israel dedicate to Me, so that they do not profane My holy name; I am the LORD.1š+	a<pb/>Then the LORD spoke to Moses, saying,Lš*So Moses spoke to Aaron and to his sons, and to all the Israelites.Eš)ƒbut he shall not go within the veil or approach the altar <n>[of incense]</n>, because he has a defect, so that he will not profane My sanctuaries; for I am the LORD who sanctifies them.'"Vš('He may eat the food of his God, both of the most holy and of the holy things,‚2š'„_No man among the descendants of Aaron the priest who has a <n>[physical]</n> defect <i>and</i> is disfigured <i>or</i> deformed is to approach <n>[the altar]</n> to present the offerings of the LORD by fire. He has a defect; he shall not approach <n>[the altar]</n> to present the food of his God.oš&Yor a hunchback or a dwarf, or one who has a defect in his eye or eczema or scabs or crushed testicles.8š%mor a man who has a broken foot or a broken hand,-š$‚UFor no man who has a defect shall approach <n>[God's altar as a priest]</n>: no man who is blind or lame, or who has a disfigured face, or any deformed <i>limb</i>,5š#‚e"Say to Aaron, 'Throughout their generations none of your descendants who has any <n>[physical]</n> defect shall approach <n>[the altar]</n> to present the food of his God.2š"a<pb/>Then the LORD spoke to Moses, saying,
š!‚so that he will not profane <i>or</i> dishonor his children among his people; for I am the LORD who sanctifies the high priest.'"š ‚He may not marry a widow or a divorced woman or one who is profaned by prostitution, but he is to marry a virgin from his own people,.šY
He shall take a wife in her virginity.>š‚wnor shall he go out of the sanctuary nor profane (make ceremonially unclean) the sanctuary of his God, for the consecration of the anointing oil of his God is on him; I am the LORD.šynor shall he approach any dead person, nor defile himself <n>[by doing so, even]</n> for his father or for his mother;yšƒm
<pb/>'But he who is the high priest among his brothers, on whose head the anointing oil has been poured and who has been consecrated to wear the <n>[sacred]</n> garments, shall not uncover his head nor tear his clothes <n>[in mourning]</n>,zšo	The daughter of any priest who profanes herself by prostitution profanes her father; she shall be burned in fire.š‚)You shall consecrate him, therefore, for he offers the food of your God; he shall be holy to you; for I the LORD, who sanctifies you, am holy.š‚5They shall not take <n>[as a wife]</n> a woman who is a prostitute, nor a woman who is divorced from her husband; for the priest is holy to his God.1š‚]They shall be holy to their God and not profane the name of their God; for they present the offerings by fire to the LORD, the food of their God; so they shall be holy.š‚The priests<f>[1]</f> shall not shave their heads, nor shave off the edges of their beards, nor make any cuts in their body.hšKHe shall not become unclean as a relative by marriage among his people, and so profane himself.rš_also his virgin sister, who is near to him because she has had no husband; for her he may become unclean.yšmexcept for his relatives who are nearest to him, his mother, his father, his son, his daughter, and his brother,‚ š	„=<pb/><t>Then the LORD said to Moses, "Speak to the priests, the sons of Aaron, and say to them: </t><br/>'No one shall defile himself <n>[that is, become ceremonially unclean]</n> for the dead among his people <n>[by touching a corpse or assisting in preparing it for burial]</n>,Išƒ
<pb/>'A man or woman who is a medium <n>[who pretends to consults the dead]</n> or who is a spiritist shall most certainly be put to death, and be stoned with stones; their blood is on them.'"xškYou are to be holy to Me; for I the LORD am holy, and have set you apart from the peoples (nations) to be Mine.‚4š„cYou are therefore to make a distinction between the <n>[ceremonially]</n> clean animal and the unclean, and between the unclean bird and the clean; and you shall not make yourselves detestable by animal or by bird or by anything that crawls on the ground, which I have set apart from you as unclean.‚š„'But I have said to you, "You are to inherit <i>and</i> take possession of their land, and I will give it to you to possess, a land <n>[of plenty]</n><f>[3]</f> flowing with milk and honey." I am the LORD your God, who has separated you from the peoples (pagan nations).8š‚kYou shall not follow the statutes (laws, practices, customs) of the nation which I am driving out before you; for they did all these things, and therefore I have loathed them.<š
‚s<pb/>'Therefore keep all My statutes and all My ordinances and do them, so that the land where I am bringing you to live may not vomit you out <n>[as it did those before you]</n>.š‚%If a man takes his brother's wife, it is a hated <i>and</i> unclean thing; he has uncovered his brother's nakedness. They will be childless.0š‚[If <i>there is</i> a man who lies <n>[intimately]</n> with his uncle's wife, he has uncovered his uncle's nakedness; they will bear their sin. They will die childless.Iš
ƒ
You shall not uncover the nakedness of (have intimate relations with) your mother's sister or your father's sister, for such a one has uncovered his blood relative; they will bear their guilt.‚š	„7If a man lies <n>[intimately]</n> with a woman during her menstrual cycle and uncovers her nakedness, he has exposed her flow, and she has uncovered the flow of her blood; both of them shall be cut off from their people <n>[excluding them from the atonement made for them]</n>.‚Bš„<pb/>'If a man takes his sister, his father's daughter or his mother's daughter, so that he sees her nakedness and she sees his nakedness, it is a disgrace; and they shall be cut off in the sight of the sons of their people. He has uncovered his sister's nakedness; he bears <n>[responsibility for]</n> his guilt.&š‚GIf a woman approaches any animal to mate with it, you shall kill the woman and the animal; they shall most certainly be put to death; their blood is on them.š}If a man has intimate relations with an animal, he shall most certainly be put to death; you shall kill the animal also.%š‚EIt is immoral <i>and</i> shameful if a man marries a woman and her mother; all three shall be burned in fire, so that there will be no immorality among you.Pšƒ
If a man lies <n>[intimately]</n> with a male as if he were a woman, both men have committed a detestable (perverse, unnatural) act; they shall most certainly be put to death; their blood is on them.+š‚QIf a man lies <n>[intimately]</n> with his daughter-in-law, both of them shall most certainly be put to death; they have committed incest; their blood is on them.?š‚yThe man who lies <n>[intimately]</n> with his father's wife has<f>[2]</f> uncovered his father's nakedness; both of them shall most certainly be put to death; their blood is on them.!š‚=
<pb/>'The man who commits adultery with another's wife, even his neighbor's wife, the adulterer and the adulteress shall most certainly be put to death.[š ƒ1	<pb/>'If anyone curses his father or mother, he shall most certainly be put to death; he has cursed his father or mother; his blood is on him <n>[that is, he bears full responsibility for the consequences]</n>.R™You shall keep My statutes and do them. I am the LORD who sanctifies you.\™~3You shall consecrate yourselves therefore, and be holy; for I am the LORD your God.‚™}„<pb/>'As for the person who turns to mediums <n>[who consult the dead]</n> or to spiritists, to play the prostitute after them, I shall set My face against that person and will cut him off from his people <n>[excluding him from the atonement made for them]</n>.d™|ƒCthen I shall set My face against that man and against his <n>[extended]</n> family, and I will cut off from their people both him and all who follow him in<f>[1]</f> playing the prostitute (commit apostasy) with Molech.D™{ƒIf the people of the land should ever tolerate that man when he gives any of his children <n>[as a burnt offering]</n> to Molech, and fail to put him to death <n>[as My law requires]</n>,‚5™z„eI will also set My face against that man <n>[opposing him, withdrawing My protection from him]</n> and will cut him off from his people <n>[excluding him from the atonement made for them]</n>, because he has given some of his children to Molech, so as to defile My sanctuary and profane My holy name.‚5™y„e<t>"Moreover, you shall say to the children of Israel, </t><br/>'Any Israelite or any stranger residing in Israel who gives any of his children to Molech (the god of the Ammonites) <n>[as a human sacrifice]</n> shall most certainly be put to death; the people of the land shall stone him with stones.1™x	a<pb/>Then the LORD spoke to Moses, saying,n™wW%You shall observe <i>and</i> keep all My statutes and all My ordinances and do them. I am the LORD.'"2™v‚_$You shall have just <i>and</i> accurate balances, just weights, a just ephah, and a just<f>[3]</f> hin. I am the LORD your God, who brought you out of the land of Egypt.W™u)#<pb/>'You shall do no wrong in judgment, in measurement of weight or quantity.K™tƒ"But the stranger who resides with you shall be to you like someone native-born among you; and you shall love him as yourself, for you were strangers in the land of Egypt; I am the LORD your God.k™sQ!<pb/>'When a stranger resides with you in your land, you shall not oppress <i>or</i> mistreat him.™r‚% <pb/>'You shall rise before the gray-headed and honor the aged, and you shall fear your God <n>[with profound reverence]</n>; I am the LORD.L™qƒ<pb/>'Do not turn to mediums <n>[who pretend to consult the dead]</n> or to spiritists <n>[who have spirits of divination]</n>; do not seek them out to be defiled by them. I am the LORD your God.K™pYou shall keep My Sabbaths and revere My sanctuary. I am the LORD.™o‚%<pb/>'Do not profane your daughter by making her a prostitute, so that the land will not fall to prostitution and become full of wickedness.™n‚You shall not make any cuts on your body <n>[in mourning]</n> for the dead, nor make any tattoo marks on yourselves; I am the LORD.™m‚You shall not trim <i>and</i> round off the side-growth of <n>[the hair on]</n> your heads, nor mar the edges of your beard.™l‚<pb/>'You shall not eat <i>anything</i> with the blood, nor practice divination <n>[using omens or witchcraft]</n> or soothsaying.™k‚In the fifth year you may eat the fruit <n>[of the trees]</n>, this is so that their yield may increase for you; I am the LORD your God.[™j1In the fourth year all the fruit shall be holy, an offering of praise to the LORD.R™iƒ<pb/>'When you enter the land and plant all kinds of trees for food, then you shall consider their fruit<f>[2]</f> forbidden. For three years the fruit shall be forbidden to you; it shall not be eaten.-™h‚UThe priest shall make atonement for him with the ram of the guilt offering before the LORD for his sin which he has committed; and he shall be forgiven for his sin.|™gsbut he shall bring his guilt offering to the LORD to the doorway of the Tent of Meeting, a ram as a guilt offering.‚.™f„W<pb/>'Now if a man has intimate relations with a woman who is a slave acquired for <n>[marriage to]</n> <i>another</i> man, but who has not been redeemed nor given her freedom, there shall be punishment <n>[after an investigation]</n>; they shall not be put to death, because she was not free;R™eƒ<pb/>'You are to keep My statutes. You shall not breed together two kinds of your cattle; you shall not sow your field with two kinds of seed, nor wear clothing of two kinds of material mixed together.:™d‚oYou shall not take revenge nor bear any grudge against the sons of your people, but you shall love your neighbor (acquaintance, associate, companion) as yourself; I am the LORD.™c‚<pb/>'You shall not hate your brother in your heart; you may most certainly rebuke your neighbor, but shall not incur sin because of him.1™b‚]You shall not go around as a gossip among your people, and you are not to act against the life of your neighbor <n>[with slander or false testimony]</n>; I am the LORD. ™a‚;<pb/>'You shall not do injustice in judgment; you shall not be partial to the poor nor show a preference for the great, but judge your neighbor fairly. ™`‚;You shall not curse a deaf man nor put a stumbling block before the blind, but you shall fear your God <n>[with profound reverence]</n>; I am the LORD.™_‚1
<pb/>'You shall not oppress <i>or</i> exploit your neighbor, nor rob him. You shall not withhold the wages of a hired man overnight until morning.w™^iYou shall not swear <n>[an oath]</n> falsely by My name, so as to profane the name of your God; I am the LORD.Q™]<pb/>'You shall not steal, nor deal deceptively, nor lie to one another.'™\‚I
And you shall not glean your vineyard, nor shall you gather its fallen grapes; you shall leave them for the poor and for the stranger. I am the LORD your God.:™[‚o	'Now when you reap the harvest of your land, you shall not reap to the very corners of your field, nor shall you gather the gleanings (grain left after reaping) of your harvest.o™ZƒYEveryone who eats it will bear <n>[the responsibility for]</n> his wickedness, for he has profaned a holy thing of the LORD; and that person shall be cut off from his people <n>[excluding him from the atonement made for them]</n>.}™YuBut if it is eaten at all on the third day, it is repulsive; it will not be accepted <n>[by God as an offering]</n>.™X‚1It shall be eaten the same day you offer it and on the day following; and if anything remains until the third day, it shall be burned in the fire.
