and his offering was one silver dish, the weight of which was a hundred and thirty <i>shekels</i>, one silver basin of seventy shekels, according to the shekel of the sanctuary, both of them full of fine flour mixed with oil as a grain offering;~žw(<pb/>Now the one who presented his offering on the first day was Nahshon the son of Amminadab, of the tribe of Judah;žy(Then the LORD said to Moses, "Let them present their offerings, one leader each day, for the dedication of the altar."$ž‚C(
<pb/>The leaders offered the dedication <i>sacrifices</i> for the altar on the day that it was anointed; and they offered their sacrifice before the altar.8ž‚k(	But to the sons of Kohath he gave nothing, because they were assigned the care of the holy things which they carried on their shoulders <n>[when the tabernacle was moved]</n>.Vžƒ'(and he gave four carts and eight oxen to the sons of Merari, according to their service <n>[in transporting the tabernacle]</n>, under the supervision of Ithamar the son of Aaron, the <n>[high]</n> priest.ž‚(He gave two carts and four oxen to the sons of Gershon, according to their service <n>[in transporting the tabernacle]</n>;Kž(So Moses took the carts and the oxen and gave them to the Levites.Až‚}("Accept <i>these things</i> from them, so that they may be used in the service of the Tent of Meeting (tabernacle), and give them to the Levites, to each man according to his service."-žW(Then the LORD spoke to Moses, saying,Bž‚(They brought their offering before the LORD, six covered carts and twelve oxen; a cart for each two of the leaders and an ox for each one; and they presented them before the tabernacle.Jž
ƒ(Then the leaders of Israel, the heads of their fathers' households, made offerings. (These were the leaders of the tribes; they were the ones who<f>[1]</f> were over the men who were numbered.)jž	ƒQ(<pb/>On the day that Moses had finished setting up the tabernacle and had anointed and consecrated it and all its furniture, and the altar and all its utensils; he also anointed them and consecrated them <n>[for holy use]</n>.jžO(<pb/>So Aaron and his sons shall put My name upon the children of Israel, and I will bless them."#ž
