The first ripe fruits of all that is in the land, which they bring to the LORD, shall be yours; everyone in your household who is <n>[ceremonially]</n> clean may eat it.4¡.‚c(All the best of the fresh <n>[olive]</n> oil, and all the best of the new wine and of the grain, the first fruits of those which they give to the LORD, I give them to you.‚¡-„9(This also is yours: the heave offering of their gift, including all the wave offerings of the Israelites. I have given them to you and to your sons and to your daughters with you as a continual allotment; everyone in your household who is <n>[ceremonially]</n> clean may eat it.{¡,q(
You shall eat it as the most holy thing; every male <n>[of your family]</n> shall eat it. It shall be holy to you.‚¡+ƒ(	This shall be yours of the most holy things, <n>[reserved]</n> from the fire: every offering of the people, every grain offering and sin offering and guilt offering, which they shall render (give) to Me, shall be most holy for you and for your sons.p¡*ƒ[(Then the LORD spoke to Aaron, "Now behold, I <n>[the LORD]</n> have entrusted you with My heave offerings, even all the holy gifts of the Israelites, I have given them to you as a portion, and to your sons as a continual allotment.‚p¡)…[(Therefore you and your sons with you shall attend to your priesthood for everything concerning the altar <n>[of burnt offering and the altar of incense]</n> and <n>[of the Holy of Holies]</n> within the veil, and you are to serve. I am giving you the priesthood as a bestowed service, but the stranger (outsider, layman) who approaches shall be put to death."F¡(ƒ(Behold, I Myself have taken your fellow Levites from among the sons of Israel; they are a gift to you, given (dedicated) to the LORD, to do the service for the Tent of Meeting (tabernacle).p¡'ƒ[(So you shall attend to the duties of the sanctuary and the duties of the altar <n>[of burnt offering and the altar of incense]</n>, so that there will no longer be wrath on the Israelites <n>[as with Korah, Dathan, and Abiram]</n>.T¡&ƒ#(They shall join you and attend to the duties of the Tent of Meetingâ€”all the service of the tentâ€”and no stranger <n>[no layman, anyone who is not a Levite]</n> may approach you <n>[and your sons]</n>.b¡%ƒ?(And the Levites shall attend to your duty <n>[as assistants]</n> and to the duties of all the tent (tabernacle); only they shall not approach the articles of the sanctuary and the altar, or both they and you will die.‚c¡$…A(But bring with you also your brothers, the tribe of Levi, the tribe of your father (ancestor), so that they may join with you and serve you <n>[as assistants]</n>, while you and your sons with you are before the Tent of the Testimony <n>[the Holy Place where only priests may go, and the Most Holy Place which only the high priest may enter]</n>.ƒc¡#	‡C(<pb/>So the LORD said to Aaron, "You and your sons and your father's household (family) with you shall bear the guilt in connection with the sanctuary <n>[that is, through your service as priests you will atone for the offenses which the people unknowingly commit when brought into contact with the manifestations of God's presence]</n>; and you and your sons with you shall bear the guilt in connection with your priesthood <n>[that is, your own unintentional offenses]</n>.t¡"c(
Everyone who approaches, who approaches the tabernacle of the LORD, must die. Are we to perish completely?"\¡!3(<pb/>The sons of Israel said to Moses, "Look, we perish, we are doomed, all doomed!I¡ 
