and you shall bring as the drink offering one-half a hin of wine as an offering by fire, as a sweet <i>and</i> soothing aroma to the LORD. C‚(	then you shall offer with the bull a grain offering of three-tenths <i>of an ephah</i> of fine flour mixed with half a hin of oil; B(When you prepare a bull as a burnt offering or as a sacrifice, in fulfilling a special vow or peace offering to the LORD, Ay(And for the drink offering you shall offer a third of a hin of wine, as a sweet <i>and</i> soothing aroma to the LORD. @‚(Or for a ram you shall prepare as a grain offering two-tenths <i>of an ephah</i> of fine flour mixed with a third of a hin of oil. ?‚(and you shall prepare wine for the drink offering, a fourth of a hin, with the burnt offering or for the sacrifice, for each lamb.0 >‚[(The one who presents his offering shall present to the LORD a grain offering of a tenth <i>of an ephah</i> of fine flour mixed with a fourth of a<f>[1]</f> hin of oil,| =ƒs(then make an offering by fire to the LORD, a burnt offering or a sacrifice to fulfill a special vow, or as a freewill offering or in your appointed feasts, to make a sweet <i>and</i> soothing aroma to the LORD, from the herd or from the flock.} <u("Speak to the Israelites and say to them, 'When you come into the land where you are to live, which I am giving you,0 ;	_(<pb/>Now the LORD spoke to Moses, saying, :‚)(-Then the Amalekites and the Canaanites who lived in that hill country came down and struck the Israelites and scattered them as far as Hormah., 9‚S(,But <n>[in their arrogance]</n> they dared to go up to the ridge of the hill country; however, neither the ark of the covenant of the LORD nor Moses left the camp.M 8ƒ(+For the Amalekites and the Canaanites will be there in front of you, and you will fall by the sword, because you have turned away from following the LORD; therefore the LORD will not be with you."e 7E(*Do not go up, or you will be struck down before your enemies, for the LORD is not among you.o 6Y()But Moses said, "Why then are you transgressing the commandment of the LORD, when it will not succeed?G 5ƒ	((They got up early in the morning and went up to the ridge of the hill country, saying, "Look, here we are; we have indeed sinned, but we will go up to the place which the LORD has promised."\ 43('Moses spoke the Lord's words to all the Israelites, and the people mourned greatly. 3y(&But Joshua the son of Nun and Caleb the son of Jephunneh remained alive out of those men who went to spy out the land.w 2i(%even those <n>[ten]</n> men who brought back the very bad report of the land died by a plague before the LORD.J 1ƒ($<pb/>As for the men whom Moses sent to spy out the land, and who returned and made all the congregation murmur <i>and</i> complain against him by bringing back a bad report concerning the land,p 0ƒ[(#I, the LORD, have spoken. I will most certainly do this to all this evil congregation who are gathered together against Me. In this wilderness they shall be consumed <n>[by war, disease, and plagues]</n>, and here they shall die.'"‚> /„w("According to the number of days in which you spied out the land <n>[of Canaan]</n>, forty days, for each day, you shall bear <i>and</i> suffer a year for your sins <i>and</i> guilt, for forty years, and you shall know My displeasure <n>[the revoking of My promise and My estrangement because of your sin]</n>.U .ƒ%(!Your sons shall be wanderers <i>and</i> shepherds in the wilderness for forty years, and they will suffer for your unfaithfulness (spiritual infidelity), until your corpses are consumed in the wilderness.G -	( But as for you, your dead bodies will fall in this wilderness. ,‚+(But your children whom you said would become plunder, I will bring in, and they will know the land which you have despised <i>and</i> rejected. +‚7(Except for Caleb the son of Jephunneh and Joshua the son of Nun, not one of you shall enter the land in which I swore <n>[an oath]</n> to settle you.- *‚U(your dead bodies will fall in this wilderness, even all who were numbered of you, your entire number from twenty years old and upward, who have murmured against Me.{ )q(Say to them, 'As I live,' says the LORD, 'just what you have spoken in My hearing I will most certainly do to you;C (ƒ("How long <i>shall I put up with</i> this evil congregation who murmur <n>[in discontent]</n> against Me? I have heard the complaints of the Israelites, which they are making against Me.7 'k(<pb/>The LORD spoke to Moses and Aaron, saying, &‚	(Now the Amalekites and the Canaanites live in the valley; tomorrow turn and set out for the wilderness by way of the Red Sea."> %‚w(But My servant Caleb, because he has a different spirit and has followed Me fully, I will bring into the land into which he entered, and his descendants shall take possession of it." $‚?(will by no means see the land which I swore to <n>[give to]</n> their fathers; nor will any who treated me disrespectfully <i>and</i> rejected Me see it.T #ƒ#(Surely all the men who have seen My glory and My <n>[miraculous]</n> signs which I performed in Egypt and in the wilderness, yet have put Me to the test these ten times and have not listened to My voice,W ")(but indeed as I live, all the earth will be filled with the glory of the LORD.O !(So the LORD said, "I have pardoned <i>them</i> according to your word;=  ‚u(Please pardon the wickedness <i>and</i> guilt of these people according to the greatness of Your lovingkindness, just as You have forgiven these people, from Egypt even until now."‚n …W('The LORD is slow to anger, and abundant in lovingkindness, forgiving wickedness and transgression; but He will by no means clear <i>the guilty</i>, visiting (avenging) the wickedness <i>and</i> guilt of the fathers on the children, to the third and fourth <i>generations</i> <n>[that is, calling the children to account for the sins of their fathers]</n>.'` ;(But now, please, let the power of the Lord be great, just as You have declared, saying, ‚5('Because the LORD was not able to bring these people into the land which He promised to give them, therefore He slaughtered them in the wilderness.'t c(Now if You kill these people as one man, then the nations (Gentiles) that have heard of Your fame will say,‚. „W(and they will tell it to the inhabitants of this land. They have heard that You, LORD, are among these people <n>[of Israel]</n>, that You, LORD, are seen face to face, while Your cloud stands over them; and that You go before them in a pillar of cloud by day and in a pillar of fire by night. ‚(
