he LORD: two young bulls, one ram, seven male lambs one year old;T£|ƒ#(<pb/>'Also on the day of the first fruits, when you offer a new grain offering to the LORD at your <i>Feast of</i> Weeks, you shall have a holy <n>[summoned]</n> assembly; you shall do no laborious work.m£{U(On the seventh day you shall have a holy <n>[summoned]</n> assembly; you shall do no laborious work.i£zƒM(In this way you shall present daily, for seven days, the food of the offering by fire, a sweet <i>and</i> soothing aroma to the LORD; it shall be presented with its drink offering in addition to the continual burnt offering.{£yq(You shall present these in addition to the burnt offering of the morning, which is for a continual burnt offering.G£x	(and one male goat as a sin offering to make atonement for you.W£w)(you shall offer a tenth <n>[of an ephah]</n> for each of the seven male lambs;£v‚+(For their grain offering you shall offer fine flour mixed with oil; three-tenths <n>[of an ephah]</n> for the bull, and two-tenths for the ram;£u‚-(But you shall present an offering by fire, a burnt offering to the LORD: two bulls, one ram, and seven male lambs one year old, without blemish.{£tq(On the first day there shall be a holy <n>[summoned]</n> assembly; you shall do no laborious work <i>that day</i>.s£sa(There shall be a feast on the fifteenth day of this month; unleavened bread shall be eaten for seven days.r£r_(<pb/>'The <e>Lord's</e> Passover shall be on the fourteenth day of the first month <n>[of each year]</n>.£q‚(And one male goat as a sin offering to the LORD; it shall be offered with its drink offering in addition to the continual burnt offering.T£pƒ#(Their drink offerings shall be half a hin of wine for a bull, and a third of a hin for a ram, and a fourth of a hin for a lamb. This is the burnt offering of each month throughout the months of the year.D£oƒ(
