And the <e>Lord's</e> anger was kindled on that day and He swore an oath, saying,;¤x‚q( 	For when they went up to the Valley of Eshcol and saw the land, they discouraged the hearts of the Israelites so that they did not go into the land which the LORD had given them.[¤w1( This is what your fathers did when I sent them from Kadesh-barnea to see the land!¤v( Now why are you discouraging the hearts of the Israelites from crossing over into the land which the LORD has given them?z¤uo( <pb/>But Moses said to the sons of Gad and the sons of Reuben, "Shall your brothers go to war while you sit here?%¤t‚E( They said, "If we have found favor in your sight, let this land be given to your servants as a possession. Do not take us across the Jordan <n>[River]</n>."8¤s‚k( the land which the LORD conquered before the congregation of Israel, is a land <n>[suitable]</n> for livestock, and your servants have <n>[very large herds of]</n> livestock."m¤rU( "<n>[The country around]</n> Ataroth, Dibon, Jazer, Nimrah, Heshbon, Elealeh, Sebam, Nebo, and Beon,	¤q‚
( So the sons of Gad and of Reuben came and spoke to Moses, to Eleazar the priest, and to the leaders of the congregation, saying,v¤p	ƒi( <pb/>Now the sons of Reuben and the sons of Gad had very large herds of cattle, and they saw the land of Jazer and the land of Gilead <n>[on the east side of the Jordan River]</n>, and indeed, the place was suitable for raising livestock.W¤oƒ)(6So Moses and Eleazar the priest received the gold from the commanders of thousands and of hundreds, and brought it into the Tent of Meeting (tabernacle) as a memorial for the sons of Israel before the LORD.E¤n(5For the men of war had taken plunder, every man for himself.¤m‚(4All the gold of the offering which they presented to the LORD from the commanders of thousands and of hundreds was 16,750 shekels.Y¤l-(3Moses and Eleazar the priest took the gold from them, all the handmade articles.K¤kƒ(2So we have brought as an offering to the LORD what each man obtainedâ€”articles of gold, armlets, bracelets, signet rings, earrings, necklacesâ€”to make atonement for ourselves before the LORD."|¤js(1and they said to him, "Your servants have counted the warriors under our command, and not one man of us is missing.¤i‚(0<pb/>Then the officers who were over the thousands of the army, the commanders of thousands and hundreds, approached Moses,]¤hƒ5(/and from the Israelites' half, Moses took one out of every fifty, both of persons and animals, and gave them to the Levites, who were in charge of the tabernacle of the LORD, just as the LORD had commanded Moses.¤g5(.and 16,000 peopleâ€”¤f3(-and 30,500 donkeys,¤e1(,and 36,000 cattle,6¤di(+now the congregation's half was 337,500 sheep,]¤c5(*<pb/>As for the Israelites' half, which Moses separated from that of the warriorsâ€”~¤bw()Moses gave the levy which was the <e>Lord's</e> offering to Eleazar the priest, just as the LORD had commanded Moses.R¤a((the persons were 16,000, from whom the <e>Lord's</e> levy was 32 persons.K¤`('the donkeys were 30,500, from which the <e>Lord's</e> levy was 61;J¤_(&the cattle were 36,000, from which the <e>Lord's</e> levy was 72;>¤^y(%and the <e>Lord's</e> levy (tax) of the sheep was 675;`¤];($<pb/>The half share, the portion of those who went to war, was 337,500 sheep in number,U¤\%(#and 32,000 persons in all, of the <n>[Midianite]</n> women who were virgins.¤[3("and 61,000 donkeys,¤Z1(!and 72,000 cattle,n¤YW( <pb/>The plunder that remained from the spoil of war which the warriors had taken, was 675,000 sheep,O¤X(Moses and Eleazar the priest did just as the LORD had commanded Moses.z¤Wƒo(From the Israelites' half <n>[of the spoil]</n> you shall take one out of every fifty of the persons, the oxen, the donkeys, the flocks, and of all the livestock, and give them to the Levites who are in charge of the tabernacle of the LORD."p¤V[(Take this tribute from the warriors' half and give it to Eleazar the priest as an offering to the LORD.¤U‚(Levy a tax for the LORD from the warriors who went to battle, one in five hundred of the persons, the oxen, the donkeys, and the flocks.8¤T‚k(Divide the spoil into two <n>[equal]</n> parts between those who were involved in the war, that is, those who went out to battle and all <n>[the rest of]</n> the congregation.9¤S‚m("You and Eleazar the priest and the leaders of the fathers' households of the congregation are to take a count of the spoil of war that was captured, both people and livestock.-¤RW(Then the LORD spoke to Moses, saying,t¤Qc(And you shall wash your clothes on the seventh day and be clean, and afterward you may come into the camp."‚¤P„/(everything that can stand fire, you shall pass through fire, and it shall be clean. Nevertheless, it shall also be purified with the water of purification <n>[to remove its impurity]</n>; and all that cannot stand fire <n>[such as fabrics]</n> you shall pass through water.P¤O(only the gold, the silver, the bronze, the iron, the tin, and the lead,¤N‚+(<pb/>Then Eleazar the priest said to the men of war who had gone to battle, "This is the statute of the law which the LORD has commanded Moses:¤M‚(You shall purify every garment and every article made of leather and all the things made of goats' hair, and every article made of wood."A¤L‚}(Camp outside the camp for seven days; whoever has killed any person and whoever has touched any dead body, purify yourselves and your captives, on the third day and on the seventh day.r¤K_(But all the young girls who have not known a man intimately, keep alive for yourselves <n>[to marry]</n>.e¤JE(Now therefore, kill every male among the children, and kill every woman who is not a virgin.M¤Iƒ(Look, these <n>[are the women who]</n> caused the Israelites, by the counsel of Balaam, to trespass against the LORD in the matter of Peor, and so a plague came among the congregation of the LORD.A¤H(And Moses said to them, "Have you let all the women live?¤Gy(But Moses was angry with the officers of the army, the commanders of thousands and of hundreds, who served in the war.z¤Fo(
<pb/>Moses and Eleazar the priest and all the leaders of the congregation went out to meet them outside the camp.e¤EƒE(Then they brought the captives, the spoils, and the plunder to Moses and to Eleazar the priest and to the congregation of the Israelites at the camp on the plains of Moab by the Jordan <n>[River]</n> across from Jericho.X¤D+(They took all the plunder and all the spoils of war, both people and livestock.
