For the land which you are entering to possess is not like the land of Egypt from which you have come, where you sowed your seed and watered<f>[5]</f> it with your foot like a garden of vegetables.\¨bƒ32	so that you may live long on the land which the LORD swore (solemnly promised) to your fathers to give to them and to their descendants, a land <n>[of great abundance,]</n><f>[4]</f> flowing with milk and honey.^¨aƒ72<pb/>"Therefore, you shall keep all the commandments which I am commanding you today, so that you may be strong and go in and take possession of the land which you are crossing over <n>[the Jordan]</n> to possess;M¨`2For your eyes have seen all the great work of the LORD which He did.x¨_ƒk2and what He did to Dathan and Abiram, the sons of Eliab, the son of Reuben, when the earth opened its mouth and swallowed them, their households, their tents, and every living thing that<f>[3]</f> followed them, in the midst of all Israel.O¨^2and what He did to you in the wilderness until you came to this place;U¨]ƒ%2and what He did to the army of Egypt, to its horses and its chariots, when He made the water of the<f>[1]</f> Red Sea engulf them as they pursued you, and how the LORD<f>[2]</f> completely destroyed them;y¨\m2and His signs and His works which He did in the midst of Egypt to Pharaoh the king of Egypt and to all his land;‚¨[„)2Know this day that I am not <i>speaking</i> to your children who have not known <n>[by personal experience]</n> and who have not seen <n>[firsthand]</n> the instruction <i>and</i> discipline of the LORD your Godâ€”His greatness, His mighty hand and His outstretched arm;-¨Z	‚W2<pb/>"Therefore you shall love the LORD your God, and always keep His charge, His statutes, His precepts, and His commandments <n>[it is your obligation to Him]</n>.¨Y‚%2
