The LORD gave me the two tablets of stone written with the finger of God; and on them <i>were written</i> all the words which the LORD had spoken to you at the mountain from the midst of the fire on the day of the assembly.Z¨/ƒ/2		When I went up the mountain to receive the tablets of stone, the tablets of the covenant which the LORD made with you, I remained on the mountain forty days and forty nights; I did not eat food or drink water.¨.2	And at Horeb (Sinai) you provoked the LORD to wrath, and the LORD was so angry with you that He would have destroyed you.l¨-ƒS2	Remember <n>[with remorse]</n> and do not forget how you provoked the LORD your God to wrath in the wilderness; from the day you left the land of Egypt until you arrived in this place, you have been rebellious against the LORD.J¨,ƒ2	<pb/>"Know <n>[without any doubt]</n>, that the LORD your God is not giving you this good land to possess because of your righteousness, for you are a stiff-necked (stubborn, obstinate) people.‚5¨+„e2	It is not for your righteousness or for the uprightness of your heart that you are going to possess their land, but because of the wickedness of these nations the LORD your God is driving them out before you, and to confirm the oath which the LORD swore to your fathers, to Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob.‚¨*„	2	<pb/>"Do not say in your heart when the LORD your God has driven them out before you, 'Because of my righteousness the LORD has brought me in to possess this land,' but because of the wickedness of these nations the LORD is dispossessing them before you.‚$¨)„C2	So know today <n>[with confident assurance]</n> that the LORD your God is crossing <n>[the Jordan]</n> before you like a devouring fire. He will destroy them and He will subdue them before you, and you shall drive them out and destroy them quickly, just as the LORD has promised you.¨(‚!2	a people great and tall, sons of Anakim, whom you know and of whom you have heard <i>it said</i>, 'Who can stand before the sons of Anak?'$¨'	‚E2	<pb/>"Hear, O Israel! You are crossing the Jordan today to go in to dispossess nations greater and more powerful than you, great cities fortified to heaven,*¨&‚O2Like the nations which the LORD causes to perish before you, so shall you perish; because you would not listen to <i>and</i> obey the voice of the LORD your God.=¨%‚u2And it shall come about if you ever forget the LORD your God and follow other gods and serve them and worship them, I testify against you today that you will most certainly perish.n¨$ƒW2But you shall remember <n>[with profound respect]</n> the LORD your God, for it is He who is giving you power to make wealth, that He may confirm His covenant which He swore (solemnly promised) to your fathers, as it is this day.j¨#O2Otherwise, you may say in your heart, 'My power and the strength of my hand made me this wealth.'h¨"ƒK2"He fed you manna in the wilderness, <n>[a substance]</n> which your fathers did not know, so that He might humble you <n>[by dependence on Him]</n> and that He might test you, to do good <n>[things]</n> for you at the end.U¨!ƒ%2"He led you through the great and terrible wilderness, <i>with its</i> fiery serpents and scorpions and thirsty ground where there was no water; it was He who brought water for you out of the flinty rock.@¨ ‚{2then your heart will become lifted up <n>[by self-conceit and arrogance]</n> and you will forget the LORD your God who brought you from the land of Egypt, out of the house of slavery.u¨e2
and when your herds and flocks multiply, and your silver and gold multiply, and all that you have increases,o¨Y2otherwise, when you have eaten and are satisfied, and have built good houses and lived <i>in them</i>,1¨‚]2<pb/>"Beware that you do not forget the LORD your God by failing to keep His commandments and His judgments (precepts) and His statutes which I am commanding you today; ¨{2
When you have eaten and are satisfied, then you shall bless the LORD your God for the good land which He has given you.#¨‚A2	a land where you will eat bread without shortage, in which you will lack nothing; a land whose stones are iron, and out of whose hills you can dig copper.m¨U2a land of wheat and barley, and vines and fig trees and pomegranates, a land of olive oil and honey;¨‚-2For the LORD your God is bringing you into a good land, a land of brooks of water, of fountains and springs, flowing forth in valleys and hills;e¨ƒE2Therefore, you shall keep the commandments of the LORD your God, to walk <n>[that is, to live each and every day]</n> in His ways and fear <n>[and worship]</n> Him <n>[with awe-filled reverence and profound respect]</n>./¨‚Y2Therefore, know in your heart (be fully cognizant) that the LORD your God disciplines <i>and</i> instructs you just as a man disciplines <i>and</i> instructs his son.Z¨/2Your clothing did not wear out on you, nor did your feet swell these forty years.‚O¨…2He humbled you and allowed you to be hungry and fed you with manna, <n>[a substance]</n> which you did not know, nor did your fathers know, so that He might make you understand <n>[by personal experience]</n> that man does not live by bread alone, but man lives by every <i>word</i> that proceeds out of the mouth of the LORD.‚¨„2And you shall remember <n>[always]</n> all the ways which the LORD your God has led you these forty years in the wilderness, so that He might humble you and test you, to know what was in your heart (mind), whether you would keep His commandments or not.S¨	ƒ#2<pb/>"Every commandment that I am commanding you today you shall be careful to do, so that you may live and multiply, and go in and possess the land which the LORD swore <n>[to give]</n> to your fathers.O¨ƒ2You shall not bring an abomination (idol) into your house, and like it come under the ban (doomed to destruction); you shall utterly detest and you shall utterly hate it, for it is something banned.‚)¨„M2You shall burn the carved <i>and</i> sculpted images of their gods in the fire. You shall not covet the silver or gold that is on them, nor take it for yourselves, so that you will not be ensnared by it <n>[in a deadly trap]</n>, for it is an abomination (repulsive) to the LORD your God.0¨‚[2And He will hand over their kings to you, and you will make their name perish from under heaven; no man will be able to stand before you until you have destroyed them.}¨u2But the LORD your God will hand them over to you, and will confuse them with a great panic until they are destroyed._¨ƒ92The LORD your God will clear away these nations before you little by little; you will not be able to put an end to them quickly, for <n>[if you did]</n> the<f>[1]</f> wild animals would become too numerous for you.c¨
A2You shall not dread them, for the LORD your God is in your midst, a great and awesome God.¨‚2Moreover, the LORD your God will send the hornet (His terror) against them, until those who are left and hide themselves from you perish.u¨ƒe2the great trials which you saw with your own eyes, and the signs, the wonders, the mighty hand and the outstretched arm by which the LORD your God brought you out. So shall the LORD your God do to all the peoples of whom you are afraid.¨
‚2you shall not be afraid of them; you shall remember <n>[with confidence]</n> what the LORD your God did to Pharaoh and to all Egyptâ€”j¨	O2<pb/>"If you say in your heart, 'These nations are greater than I am; how can I dispossess them?'K¨ƒ2And you shall consume all the peoples whom the LORD your God will give over to you; your eye shall not pity them, nor shall you serve their gods, for that would be a <n>[deadly]</n> trap to you.M¨ƒ2The LORD will take away from you all sickness; and He will not subject you to any of the harmful diseases of Egypt which you have known, but He will impose them on all <n>[those]</n> who hate you.¨‚2You shall be blessed above all peoples; there will be no male or female barren (childless, infertile) among you or among your cattle.‚+¨„Q2
He will love you and bless you and multiply you; He will also bless the fruit of your womb and the fruit of your land, your grain and your new wine and your <n>[olive]</n> oil, the offspring of your cattle and the young of your flock, in the land which He swore to your fathers to give you.`¨ƒ;2"Then it shall come about, because you listen to these judgments and keep and do them, that the LORD your God will keep with you the covenant and the <n>[steadfast]</n> lovingkindness which He swore to your fathers.¨‚2Therefore, you shall keep (follow, obey) the commandment and the statutes and judgments (precepts) which I am commanding you today.¨‚'2
but repays those who hate Him to their faces, by destroying them; He will not hesitate with him who hates Him, He will repay him to his face.‚¨„2	Therefore know <n>[without any doubt]</n> <i>and</i> understand that the LORD your God, He is God, the faithful God, who is keeping His covenant and His <n>[steadfast]</n> lovingkindness to a thousand generations with those who love Him and keep His commandments;l¨ ƒS2But because the LORD loves you and is keeping the oath which He swore to your fathers, the LORD has brought you out with a mighty hand and redeemed (bought) you from the house of slavery, from the hand of Pharaoh king of Egypt.(§‚K2<pb/>"The LORD did not love you and choose you because you were greater in number than any of the <i>other</i> peoples, for you were the fewest of all peoples.o§~ƒY2For you are a holy people <n>[set apart]</n> to the LORD your God; the LORD your God has chosen you out of all the peoples on the face of the earth to be a people for His own possession <n>[that is, His very special treasure]</n>.~§}ƒw2But this is how you shall deal with them: you shall tear down their altars and smash to pieces their <i>sacred</i> pillars, and cut down their Asherim (symbols of the goddess Asherah), and burn their carved <i>or</i> sculpted images in the fire.9§|‚m2for they will turn your sons away from following Me to serve other gods; then the anger of the LORD will be kindled <i>and</i> burn against you and He will quickly destroy you.§{‚	2You shall not intermarry with them; you shall not give your daughter to his son, nor shall you take his daughter for your son;S§zƒ!2and when the LORD your God gives them over to you and you defeat them, then you shall utterly destroy them. You shall not make a covenant (treaty) with them nor show mercy <i>and</i> compassion to them.‚/§y	„[2<pb/>"When the LORD your God brings you into the land which you are entering to possess, and has cleared away many nations before you, the Hittite and the Girgashite and the Amorite and the Canaanite and the Perizzite and the Hivite and the Jebusite, seven nations greater and mightier than you,O§xƒ2It will be <n>[considered]</n> righteousness for us <n>[that is, right standing with God]</n> if we are careful to observe all this commandment before the LORD our Godâ€”just as He has commanded us.m§wƒU2So the LORD commanded us to do all these statutes, to fear <n>[and worship]</n> the LORD our God <n>[with awe-filled reverence and profound respect]</n> for our good always and so that He might preserve us alive, as it is today.§v‚2He brought us out from there in order to bring us in, to give us the land which He had sworn to <n>[give]</n> our fathers.'§u‚2Moreover, the LORD showed great and terrible signs and wonders before our eyes against Egypt, Pharaoh and all his household;§t‚2then you shall say to your son, 'We were Pharaoh's slaves in Egypt, and the LORD brought us out of Egypt with a mighty hand.>§s‚w2<pb/>"When your son asks you in time to come, saying, 'What <i>is the meaning</i> of the testimonies and statutes and judgments (precepts) which the LORD our God has commanded you?'Q§r2by driving out all your enemies from before you, as the LORD has spoken.K§qƒ2You shall do what is right and good in the sight of the LORD, so that it may be well with you and that you may go in and possess the good land which the LORD swore to <n>[give]</n> your fathers,=§p‚u2You shall diligently keep <n>[foremost in your thoughts and actively do]</n> the commandments of the LORD your God, and His testimonies and His statutes which He has commanded you.\§o32<pb/>"You shall not put the LORD your God to the test, as you tested Him at Massah.‚§n„12for the LORD your God who is among you is a<f>[6]</f> jealous (impassioned) God <n>[demanding what is rightfully and uniquely His]</n>â€”otherwise the anger of the LORD your God will be kindled <i>and</i> burn against you, and He will destroy you from the face of the earth.Z§m/2You shall not follow other gods, any of the gods of the peoples who surround you,=§l‚u2
You shall fear <n>[only]</n> the LORD your God; and you shall serve Him <n>[with awe-filled reverence and profound respect]</n> and swear <n>[oaths]</n> by His name <n>[alone]</n>.§k‚2then<f>[5]</f> beware that you do not forget the LORD who brought you out of the land of Egypt, out of the house of slavery.j§jƒO2and houses full of all good things which you did not fill, and hewn (excavated) cisterns (wells) which you did not dig out, and vineyards and olive trees which you did not plant, and you eat and are full <i>and</i> satisfied,‚§i„2
<pb/>"Then it shall come about when the LORD your God brings you into the land which He swore (solemnly promised) to <n>[give]</n> your fathersâ€”to Abraham, Isaac, and Jacobâ€”to give you, <n>[a land with]</n> great and splendid cities which you did not build,Y§h-2	You shall write them on the<f>[4]</f> doorposts of your house and on your gates.§g‚#2And you shall bind them as a sign on your hand (forearm), and they shall be used as<f>[3]</f> bands (frontals, frontlets) on your forehead.‚§f„72You shall teach them diligently to your<f>[2]</f> children <n>[impressing God's precepts on their minds and penetrating their hearts with His truths]</n> and shall speak of them when you sit in your house and when you walk on the road and when you lie down and when you get up.o§eY2These words, which I am commanding you today, shall be <n>[written]</n> on your heart <i>and</i> mind.§d‚12You shall love the LORD your God with all your heart <i>and</i> mind and with all your soul and with all your strength <n>[your entire being]</n>.Z§c/2<pb/>"Hear, O Israel! The LORD is our God, the LORD is one <n>[the only God]</n>!‚§b„2Therefore listen, O Israel, and be careful to do <i>them</i>, that it may go well with you and that you may increase greatly <n>[in numbers]</n>, as the LORD, the God of your fathers, has promised you, in a land<f>[1]</f> flowing with milk and honey.‚;§a„q2so that you and your son and your grandson may fear <i>and</i> worship the LORD your God <n>[with awe-filled reverence and profound respect]</n>, to keep <n>[and actively do]</n> all His statutes and His commandments which I am commanding you, all the days of your life, so that your days may be prolonged.x§`	ƒm2<pb/>"Now this is the command; the statutes and the judgments (precepts) which the LORD your God has commanded me to teach you, so that you might do (follow, obey) them in the land which you are crossing over <n>[the Jordan]</n> to possess,u§_ƒe2!You shall walk <n>[that is, live each and every day]</n> in all the ways which the LORD your God has commanded you, so that you may live and so that it may be well with you, and that you may live long in the land which you will possess.Q§^ƒ2 Therefore you shall pay attention <i>and</i> be careful to do just as the LORD your God has commanded you; you shall not turn aside to the right or to the left <n>[deviating from My commandments]</n>.X§]ƒ+2But as for you, stand here by Me, and I will tell you all the commandments and the statutes and the judgments which you shall teach them, so that they may obey them in the land which I give them to possess.'
