When you set him free, you shall not let him go away empty-handed.9©T‚m2<pb/>"If your fellow Israelite, a Hebrew man or woman, is sold to you, and serves you for six years, then in the seventh year you shall set him free <n>[from your service]</n>.;©S‚q2For the poor will never cease to be in the land; therefore I command you, saying, 'You shall freely open your hand to your brother, to your needy, and to your poor in your land.'q©Rƒ]2
You shall freely <i>and</i> generously give to him, and your heart shall not be resentful when you give to him, because for this <n>[generous]</n> thing the LORD your God will bless you in all your work and in all your undertakings.‚k©Q…Q2	Beware that there is no wicked thought in your heart, saying, 'The seventh year, the year of release (remission, pardon), is approaching,' and your eye is hostile (unsympathetic) toward your poor brother, and you give him nothing <n>[since he would not have to repay you]</n>; for he may cry out to the LORD against you, and it will become a sin for you.r©P_2but you shall freely open your hand to him, and shall generously lend to him<f>[7]</f> whatever he needs.z©Oƒo2<pb/>"If there is a poor man among you, one of your fellow Israelites, in<f>[4]</f> any of your cities in the land that the LORD your God is giving you, you shall not<f>[5]</f> be heartless, nor<f>[6]</f> close-fisted with your poor brother;P©Nƒ2When the LORD your God blesses<f>[3]</f> you as He has promised you, then you will lend to many nations, but you will not borrow; and you will rule over many nations, but they will not rule over you. ©M‚;2if only you will listen to <i>and</i> obey the voice of the LORD your God, to observe carefully all these commandments which I am commanding you today./©L‚Y2However, there will be no poor among you, since the LORD will most certainly bless you in the land which the LORD your God is giving you as an inheritance to possess,©K‚2You may require repayment from a foreigner, but whatever of yours is with your brother <n>[Israelite]</n> your hand shall release.~©Jƒw2This is the regulation for the release: every<f>[1]</f> creditor shall forgive what he has loaned to his neighbor; he shall not<f>[2]</f> require repayment from his neighbor and his brother, because the <e>Lord's</e> release has been proclaimed.m©I	W2<pb/>"At the end of every seven years you shall grant a release