but you may not eat anything that does not have fins and scales; it is unclean for you.©42	<pb/>"Of all <n>[creatures]</n> that are in the waters, you may eat these: anything that has fins and scales you may eat,)©3‚M2The swine, because it has a divided hoof but <i>does</i> not <i>chew</i> the cud; it is unclean for you. You shall not eat their meat nor touch their carcasses.‚©2„2However, you are not to eat any of these <n>[animals]</n> among those which chew the cud, or among those that divide the hoof in two: the camel, the hare and the<f>[3]</f> shaphan, for though they chew the cud, they do not split the hoof; they are unclean for you.>©1‚w2Among the animals, you may eat any animal that has the divided hoof <n>[that is, a hoof]</n> split into two parts <n>[especially at its distal extremity]</n> and that chews the cud.j©0O2the deer, the gazelle, the roebuck, the wild goat, the ibex, the antelope and the mountain sheep.M©/2These are the animals that you may eat: the ox, the sheep, the goat,g©.I2<pb/>"You shall not eat anything that is detestable <n>[to the LORD and forbidden by Him]</n>.:©-‚o2for you are a holy people <n>[set apart]</n> to the LORD your God; and the LORD has chosen you out of all the peoples who are on the earth to be a people for His own possession.©,	‚+2<pb/>"You are the sons of the LORD your God;<f>[1]</f> you shall not cut yourselves nor<f>[2]</f> shave your forehead for the sake of the dead,O©+ƒ2
