<t>"He found him in a desert land, </t><t>In the howling wasteland of a wilderness; </t><t>He kept circling him, He took care of him, </t><t>He protected him as the<f>[1]</f> apple of His eye.</t><br/>­‚%2 	<t>"For the <e>Lord's</e> portion <i>and</i> chosen share is His people; </t><t>Jacob (Israel) is the allotment of His inheritance.</t><br/>X­ƒ+2 <t>"When the Most High gave the nations their inheritance, </t><t>When He separated the sons of man, </t><t>He set the boundaries of the peoples </t><t>According to the number of the sons of Israel.</t><br/>:­‚o2 <t>"Remember the days of old, </t><t>Consider the years of many generations. </t><t>Ask your father, and he will inform you, </t><t>Your elders, and they will tell you.</t><br/>]­ƒ52 <t>"Do you thus repay the LORD, </t><t>O foolish and unwise people? </t><t>Is not He your Father who has acquired you <n>[as His own]</n>? </t><t>He has made you and established you <n>[as a nation]</n>.</t><br/>G­ƒ	2 <t>"They (Israel) have acted corruptly toward Him. </t><t>They are not His children, because of their <n>[moral]</n> defect; </t><t><i>But are</i> a perverse and crooked generation.</t><br/>0­‚[2 <t>"The Rock! His work is perfect, </t><t>For all His ways are just; </t><t>A God of faithfulness without iniquity (injustice), </t><t>Just and upright is He.</t><br/>­‚2 <t>"For I proclaim the name <n>[and presence]</n> of the LORD; </t><t>Ascribe greatness <i>and</i> honor to our God!</t><br/><­‚s2 <t>"Let my teaching drop as the rain, </t><t>My speech distill as the dew, </t><t>As the light rain upon the tender grass, </t><t>And as the spring showers upon the herb.</t><br/>s­ 	c2 <pb/><t>"Listen, O heavens, and I will speak; </t><t>And let the earth hear the words of my mouth.</t><br/>~¬w2<pb/>Then Moses spoke in the hearing of all the congregation of Israel the words of this song, until they were ended:‚¬~„2For I know that after my death you will behave corruptly and turn from the way which I have commanded you; and evil will come upon you in the latter days, because you will do evil in the sight of the LORD, provoking Him to anger with the work of your hands."2¬}‚_2Assemble before me all the elders of your tribes and your officers, so that I may speak these words in their hearing and call heaven and earth as witnesses against them.N¬|ƒ2For I know your rebellion <i>and</i> contention and your stubbornness; behold, while I am still alive with you today, you have been rebellious against the LORD; how much more, then, after my death?¬{‚-2"Take this Book of the Law and put it beside the ark of the covenant of the LORD your God, so that it may remain there as a witness against you.Z¬z/2he commanded the Levites who carried the ark of the covenant of the LORD, saying,Y¬y-2<pb/>And when Moses completely finished writing the words of this law in a book,]¬xƒ52Then He commanded <i>and</i> commissioned Joshua, the son of Nun, and said, "Be strong and courageous, for you will bring the sons of Israel into the land which I have sworn to give them, and I will be with you."X¬w+2So Moses wrote this song the same day, and taught it to the children of Israel.‚Z¬v…/2Then it shall come about, when many evils and troubles have come on them, that this <n>[sacred]</n> song will confront them as a witness; for it will not be forgotten from the mouth of their descendants. For I know their inclination which is developing even now, before I bring them into the land which I have sworn <i>to give them</i>."‚9¬u„m2For when I bring them into the land which I have sworn to their fathers, a land <n>[of plenty]</n><f>[4]</f> flowing with milk and honey, and they have eaten and are satisfied and become prosperous, then they will turn to other gods and serve them, and despise <i>and</i> reject Me and break My covenant.9¬t‚m2<pb/>"Now then, write this song for yourselves, and teach it to the sons of Israel; put it in their mouth, so that this song may be a witness for Me against the sons of Israel.T¬sƒ#2But I will certainly hide My face <n>[from them]</n> in that day because of all the evil which they will do, for they will turn to other gods <n>[to worship lifeless idols, to honor handmade relics]</n>.‚L¬r…2Then My anger will be kindled <i>and</i> burn against them in that day, and I will abandon (turn away from) them and hide My face from them. They will be devoured, and many evils and troubles will come on them, so that they will say in that day, 'Is it not because our God is not among us that these evils have come on us?'‚j¬q…O2The LORD said to Moses, "Behold, you are about to lie down <n>[in death]</n> with your fathers; and this people will arise and<f>[3]</f> play the prostitute (commit apostasy) with the foreign gods <n>[of the people]</n> of the land, where they go to be among them. They will abandon (turn away from) Me and break My covenant which I have made with them.¬py2Then the LORD appeared in the tent in a pillar of cloud, and the pillar of cloud stood beside the doorway of the tent.t¬oƒc2Then the LORD said to Moses, "Behold, the time for you to die is near; call Joshua, and present yourselves at the Tent of Meeting, so that I may commission him." So Moses and Joshua went and presented themselves at the Tent of Meeting.Q¬nƒ2
"Their children, who have not known <n>[the law]</n>, will hear and learn to fear <n>[and worship]</n> the LORD your God, as long as you live in the land which you are crossing the Jordan to possess."‚'¬m„I2Assemble the people, the men and the women and children and the stranger (resident alien, foreigner) within your cities, so that they may hear and learn and fear the LORD your God <n>[with awe-filled reverence and profound respect]</n>, and be careful to obey all the words of this law.B¬l‚2when all Israel comes to appear before the LORD your God in the place which He chooses, you shall read this law before all <n>[the people of]</n> Israel<f>[2]</f> so that they may hear.'¬k‚I2
Then Moses commanded them, saying, "At the end of <i>every</i> seven years, at the time of year when debts are forgiven, at the Feast of Booths (Tabernacles),$¬j‚C2	<pb/>So Moses wrote this law and gave it to the priests, the sons of Levi who carried the ark of the covenant of the LORD, and to all the elders of Israel.¬i‚2It is the LORD who goes before you; He will be with you. He will not fail you or abandon you. Do not fear or be dismayed."‚¬h„72<pb/>Then Moses called to Joshua and said to him in the sight of all <n>[the people of]</n> Israel, "Be strong and courageous, for you will go with this people into the land which the LORD has sworn to their fathers to give them, and you will give it to them as an inheritance.)¬g‚M2Be strong and courageous, do not be afraid or tremble in dread before them, for it is the LORD your God who goes with you. He will not fail you or abandon you."
¬f‚2The LORD will hand them over to you, and you shall do to them in accordance with all the commandments which I have commanded you.¬e‚	2The LORD will do to them just as He did to Sihon and Og, the kings of the Amorites, and to their land, when He destroyed them.g¬dƒI2It is the LORD your God who will cross ahead of you; He will destroy these nations before you, and you shall dispossess them. Joshua is the one who will go across before you <n>[to lead you]</n>, just as the LORD has said.m¬cƒU2And he said to them, "I am<f>[1]</f> a hundred and twenty years old today; I am no longer able to come in and go out <n>[as your spiritual and military leader]</n>, and the LORD has said to me, 'You shall not cross this Jordan.'>¬b	{2<pb/>So Moses went and spoke these words to all Israel.‚?¬a„y2by loving the LORD your God, by obeying His voice, and by holding closely to Him; for He is your life <n>[your good life, your abundant life, your fulfillment]</n> and the length of your days, that you may live in the land which the LORD promised (swore) to give to your fathers, to Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob."^¬`ƒ72I call heaven and earth as witnesses against you today, that I have set before you life and death, the blessing and the curse; therefore, you shall choose life in order that you may live, you and your descendants,¬_‚!2I declare to you today that you will certainly perish. You will not live long in the land which you cross the Jordan to enter and possess.¬^‚2But if your heart turns away and you will not hear <i>and</i> obey, but are drawn away and worship other gods and serve them,‚I¬]…
2in that I command you today to love the LORD your God, to walk <n>[that is, to live each and every day]</n> in His ways and to keep His commandments and His statutes and His judgments (precepts), so that you will live and multiply, and that the LORD your God will bless you in the land which you are entering to possess.q¬\]2"Listen closely, I have set before you today life and prosperity (good), and death and adversity (evil);a¬[=2But the word is very near you, in your mouth and in your heart, so that you may obey it.¬Z‚2
Nor is it beyond the sea, that you should say, 'Who will cross the sea for us and bring it to us, so that we may hear it and obey it?'%¬Y‚E2It is not <n>[a secret hidden]</n> in heaven, that you should say, 'Who will go up to heaven for us and bring it to us, so that we may hear it and obey it?'¬X‚2<pb/>"For this commandment which I am commanding you today is not too difficult for you, nor is it<f>[3]</f> out of reach.‚¬Wƒ2
if you listen to <i>and</i> obey the voice of the LORD your God to keep His commandments and His statutes which are written in this Book of the Law, and if you turn to the LORD your God with all your heart and with all your soul (your entire being).‚'¬V„I2	Then the LORD your God shall make you abundantly prosperous in<f>[2]</f> everything that you do, in the offspring of your body and in the offspring of your cattle and in the produce of your land; for the LORD will again delight over you for good, just as He delighted over your fathers,¬U‚2And you shall again listen to <i>and</i> obey the voice of the LORD, and do all His commandments which I command you today.|¬Ts2The LORD your God will inflict all these curses on your enemies and on those who hate you, who have persecuted you.‚3¬S„a2<pb/>"And the LORD your God will circumcise your heart and the hearts of your descendants <n>[that is, He will remove the desire to sin from your heart]</n>, so that you will love the LORD your God with all your heart and all your soul, so that you may live <n>[as a recipient of His blessing]</n>.C¬Rƒ2The LORD your God will bring you into the land which your fathers possessed, and you will take possession of it; and He shall make you prosper and multiplyâ€”even more than your fathers."¬Q‚?2Even if any of your dispersed are at the ends of the earth, the LORD your God will gather you together from there, and from there He will bring you back.X¬Pƒ+2then the LORD your God will restore your fortunes <n>[in your return from exile]</n>, and have compassion on you, and will gather you together again from all the peoples (nations) where He has scattered you.e¬OƒE2and you have returned to the LORD your God and have listened to <i>and</i> obeyed His voice with all your heart and with all your soul, in accordance with everything that I am commanding you today, you and your children,[¬N	ƒ32<pb/>"So it shall be when all these things have come on you, the blessing and the curse which I have set before you, and you<f>[1]</f> call them to mind in all the nations where the LORD your God has driven you,M¬Mƒ2<pb/>"The secret things belong to the LORD our God, but the things which are revealed <i>and</i> disclosed belong to us and to our children forever, so that we may do all of the words of this law.¬L‚+2and the LORD uprooted them from their land in anger and in wrath and in great indignation, and cast them into another land, as it is this day.'t¬Kc2So the anger of the LORD burned against this land, bringing on it every curse that is written in this book;¬J‚12For they went and served other gods and worshiped them, <n>[false]</n> gods whom they have not known and whom He had not allotted (given) to them.F¬Iƒ2Then <i>people</i> will say, 'It is because they abandoned (broke) the covenant of the LORD, the God of their fathers, which He made with them when He brought them out of the land of Egypt.u¬He2All the nations will say, 'Why has the LORD done this thing to this land? Why this great outburst of anger?'h¬GƒK2'The whole land is brimstone and salt, a burning waste, unsown and unproductive, and no grass grows in it; it is like the overthrow of Sodom and Gomorrah, Admah and Zeboiim, which the LORD overthrew in His anger and wrath.'`¬Fƒ;2<pb/>Now the next generation, your children who come after you and the foreigner who comes from a distant land, when they see the plagues of this land and the diseases with which the LORD has afflicted it, will say,N¬Eƒ2Then the LORD will single him out for disaster from all the tribes of Israel <n>[making an example of him]</n>, according to all the curses of the covenant that are written in this Book of the Law.~¬Dƒw2the LORD will not be willing to forgive him, but then the anger of the LORD and His<f>[4]</f> jealousy will burn against that man, and every curse which is written in this book will rest on him; the LORD will blot out his name from under heaven.‚m¬C…U2It will happen that when he (a renegade) hears the words of this oath, and he<f>[3]</f> imagines himself as blessed, saying, 'I will have peace <i>and</i> safety even though I walk within the stubbornness of my heart <n>[rejecting God and His law]</n>, in order that the watered <i>land</i> dwindles away along with the dry <n>[destroying everything]</n>,'‚1¬B„]2so that there will not be among you a man or woman, or family or tribe, whose heart turns away today from the LORD our God, to go and serve the <n>[false]</n> gods of these nations; so that there will not be among you a root <n>[of idolatry]</n> bearing poisonous fruit and wormwood (bitterness).5¬A‚e2and you have seen their detestable acts and their <n>[repulsive]</n> idols of wood and stone, <n>[lifeless images]</n> of silver and gold, which <i>they had</i> with them),n¬@W2(for you know how we lived in the land of Egypt, and how we passed through the nations along the way;)¬?‚M2but with those <n>[future Israelites]</n> who are not here with us today, as well as with those who stand here with us today in the presence of the LORD our GodU¬>%2<pb/>"It is not with you alone that I am making this covenant and this oath,-¬=‚U2
so that He may establish you today as His people and that He may be your God, just as He spoke to you and as He swore to your fathers, to Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob.¬<‚92so that you may enter into the covenant of the LORD your God, and into His oath <i>and</i> agreement which the LORD your God is making with you today,N¬;ƒ2your little ones, your wives, and the stranger (resident alien, foreigner) who is in your camps, from<f>[2]</f> the one who chops <i>and</i> gathers your firewood to the one who draws your waterâ€”¬:‚32
<pb/>"All of you stand today before the LORD your Godâ€”your chiefs, your tribes, your elders and your officers, <i>even</i> all the men of Israel,¬9‚2	So keep the words of this covenant and obey them, so that you may prosper <i>and</i> be successful in everything that you do.¬8‚	2and we took their land and gave it as an inheritance to the tribe of Reuben, the tribe of Gad, and the half-tribe of Manasseh.¬7‚2When you reached this place, Sihon the king of Heshbon and Og the king of Bashan came out to meet us in battle, but we defeated them; ¬6‚;2You have not eaten bread, nor have you drunk wine or strong drink, so that you might know that I am the LORD your God <n>[on whom you must depend]</n>.¬5‚2I have led you in the wilderness forty years; your clothes have not worn out on you, and your sandals have not worn out on your feet.}¬4u2Yet to this day the LORD has not given you a heart <i>and</i> mind to understand, nor eyes to see, nor ears to hear.k¬3Q2the great trials <n>[of Pharaoh]</n> which your eyes have seen, the signs and those great wonders.E¬2ƒ2<pb/><f>[1]</f> Moses summoned all Israel and said to them, "You have seen all that the LORD did before your eyes in the land of Egypt to Pharaoh, to all his servants, and to all his land;J¬1	ƒ2<pb/>These are the words of the covenant which the LORD commanded Moses to make with the sons of Israel in the land of Moab, in addition to the covenant which He made with them at Horeb (Sinai).z¬0ƒo2DThe LORD will bring you back to Egypt in ships, by the way about which I said to you, 'You will never see it again!' And there you will offer yourselves for sale to your enemies as male and female slaves, but there will be no one to buy you.q¬/ƒ]2CIn the morning you will say, 'I wish it were evening!' and in the evening you will say, 'I wish it were morning!'â€”because of the dread in your heart with which you tremble, and because of the sight of your eyes which you will see. ¬.{2BYour life will hang in doubt before you; night and day you will be filled with anxiety and have no assurance of living.R¬-ƒ2AAmong those nations you will find no peace (rest), and there will be no resting place for the sole of your foot; but there the LORD will give you a trembling heart, failing eyes, and a despairing soul.y¬,ƒm2@And the LORD will scatter you among all the nations, from one end of the earth to the other; and there you will <n>[be forced to]</n> serve other gods, <n>[lifeless gods of]</n> wood and stone, which neither you nor your fathers have known.‚¬+„)2?It shall come about that just as the LORD delighted over you to make you prosper and multiply, so the LORD will delight over you to bring you to ruin and destruction; and you will be<f>[15]</f> uprooted <n>[violently]</n> from the land which you are entering to possess.¬*‚2>Because you did not obey the voice of the LORD your God, you who were as numerous as the stars of heaven shall be left few in number.¬)‚2=Also the LORD will bring on you every sickness and every plague which is not written in this book of this law, until you are destroyed.w¬(i2<Moreover, He will bring on you all the diseases of Egypt of which you were afraid, and they will cling to you.¬'‚12;then the LORD will bring extraordinary plagues on you and your descendants, even severe and lasting plagues, and miserable and chronic sicknesses.?¬&‚y2:<pb/>"If you are not careful to do all the words of this law that are written in this book, to fear <i>and</i> honor with reverence this glorious and awesome name, the LORD your God,z¬%ƒo29and toward her afterbirth that comes from between her legs and toward the children whom she bears; for she will eat them secretly for lack of anything else, during the siege and the misery by which your enemy will oppress you in your cities.‚¬$„/28The most refined and well-bred woman among you, who would not venture to set the sole of her foot on the ground because she is so delicate and pampered,<f>[13]</f> will be cruel <i>and</i> hostile toward<f>[14]</f> the husband she cherishes and toward her son and daughter,~¬#ƒw27so that he will not give <i>even</i> one of them any of the flesh of his children<f>[11]</f> which he will eat,<f>[12]</f> because he has nothing else left, during the siege and the misery by which your enemy will oppress you in all your cities.V¬"ƒ'26The man who is most refined and well-bred among you<f>[9]</f> will be cruel <i>and</i> hostile toward his brother and toward<f>[10]</f> the wife he cherishes and toward the rest of his children who remain,h¬!ƒK25Then you will eat the offspring of your own body <n>[to avoid starvation]</n>, the flesh of your sons and daughters whom the LORD your God has given you, during the siege and the misery by which your enemy will oppress you.s¬ ƒa24They will besiege you in all your cities until your high and fortified walls in which you trusted come down throughout your land; and they will besiege you in all your cities throughout your land which the LORD your God has given you.z¬ƒo23and it will eat the offspring of your herd and the produce of your ground until you are destroyed, who will leave you no grain, new wine, or oil, nor the offspring of your herd or the young of your flock until they have caused you to perish.p¬[22a<f>[7]</f> defiant nation who will<f>[8]</f> have no respect for the old, nor show favor to the young,Q¬ƒ21<pb/>"The LORD will bring a nation against you from far away, from the end of the earth, <n>[as swift]</n> as the eagle swoops down <n>[to attack]</n>, a nation whose language you will not understand,j¬ƒO20you will therefore serve your enemies whom the LORD sends against you, in hunger and in thirst, in nakedness and in lack of all things; and He will put an iron yoke <n>[of slavery]</n> on your neck until He has destroyed you.$¬‚C2/<pb/>"Because you did not serve the LORD your God with a heart full of joy and gladness for the abundance of all things <n>[with which He blessed you]</n>,N¬2.They will be a sign and a wonder to you and your descendants forever.o¬ƒY2-<pb/>"So all these curses will come on you and pursue you and overtake you until you are destroyed, because you would not obey the voice of the LORD your God by keeping His commandments and His statutes which He has commanded you.!¬‚=2,He will lend to you <n>[out of his affluence]</n>, but you will not lend to him <n>[because of your poverty]</n>; he will be the head, and you the tail.v¬g2+The stranger who lives among you will rise above you higher and higher, and you will go down lower and lower.[¬12*The cricket will take possession of all your trees and the produce of your ground.}¬u2)You will have sons and daughters, but they will not be yours <n>[for long]</n>, because they will go into captivity.¬‚/2(You will have olive trees throughout your territory but you will not<f>[6]</f> anoint yourselves with the oil, because your olives will drop off.¬‚2'You will plant vineyards and cultivate them, but you will not drink the wine or gather <i>the grapes</i>, because the worm will eat them.¬‚2&<pb/>"You will bring out a great quantity of seed to the field, but you will gather in little, because the locusts will consume it.'¬‚I2%And you will become a horror, a proverb <n>[a mere object lesson]</n>, and a taunt <n>[a derisive joke]</n> among all the people to which the LORD drives you.d¬ƒC2$The LORD will bring you and your king, whom you appoint over you, to a nation which you and your fathers have never known; there you will <n>[be forced to]</n> serve other gods, <n>[lifeless gods of]</n> wood and stone.¬‚/2#The LORD will strike you on the knees and on the legs with sore boils that you cannot heal, from the sole of your foot to the crown of your head.N¬2"You shall be driven mad by the sight of<f>[5]</f> the things you see.H¬
ƒ2!A people whom you do not know will eat the produce of your land and all the products of your labors, and you will never be anything but oppressed <i>and</i> exploited and crushed continually.¬‚72 Your sons and daughters will be given to another people, while your eyes look on and long for them continually; but there will be nothing you can do.r¬ƒ_2Your ox will be slaughtered before your eyes, but you will not eat any of it; your donkey will be torn away from you, and it will not be returned to you; your sheep will be given to your enemies, and you will have no one to save you.\¬
ƒ32You will be pledged to marry a wife, but another man will be intimate with her <n>[before you]</n>; you will build a house, but you will not live in it; you will plant a vineyard, but you will not use its fruit.s¬	ƒa2and you will be groping at noon <n>[in broad daylight]</n>, just as the blind grope in the darkness, and nothing you do will prosper; but you will only be oppressed <i>and</i> exploited and robbed continually, with no one to save you.q¬]2The LORD will strike you with madness and with blindness and with bewilderment of heart <i>and</i> mind;¬‚2<pb/>"The LORD will strike you with the boils of Egypt and with tumors and with the scab and the itch that you cannot heal.¬‚2Your carcasses will be food for all the birds of the sky and the beasts of the earth, and there will be no one to frighten them away.‚¬„	2<pb/>"The LORD will cause you to be defeated before your enemies; you will go out against them one way, but flee before them seven ways, and you will be <i>an example of</i> terror to all the kingdoms of the earth <n>[when they see your destruction]</n>. ¬{2The LORD will make the rain of your land powder and dust; from heaven it will come down on you until you are destroyed.C¬ƒ2The heaven which is over your head shall be bronze <n>[giving no rain and blocking all prayers]</n>, and the earth which is under you, iron <n>[hard to plow and yielding no produce]</n>.‚¬„2The LORD will strike you with consumption <n>[causing you to waste away]</n> and with fever and with inflammation and with fiery heat and with the sword and with blight and with mildew <n>[on your crops]</n>; and they will pursue you until you perish.*¬‚O2The LORD will make the pestilence <i>and</i> plague cling to you until He has consumed <i>and</i> eliminated you from the land which you are entering to possess.n¬ ƒW2<pb/>"The LORD will send upon you curses, confusion, and rebuke in everything that you undertake to do, until you are destroyed, perishing quickly because of the evil of your deeds, because you have<f>[4]</f> turned away from Me.h«K2<pb/>"You <i>will be</i> cursed when you come in and you <i>will be</i> cursed when you go out.«~‚%2<pb/>"The offspring of your body and the produce of your land, the offspring of your herd and the young of your flock <i>will be</i> cursed.H«}2<pb/>"Your basket and your kneading bowl <i>will be</i> cursed.M«|2<pb/>"You <i>will be</i> cursed in the city and cursed in the field.‚ «{ƒ{2"But it shall come about, if you do not listen to <i>and</i> obey the voice of the LORD your God, being careful to do all His commandments and His statutes which I am commanding you today, then all these curses will come upon you and overtake you:«z‚2Do not turn aside from any of the words which I am commanding you today, to the right or to the left, to follow and serve other gods.‚«y„#2
The LORD will make you the head (leader) and not the tail (follower); and you will be above only, and you will not be beneath, if you listen <i>and</i> pay attention to the commandments of the LORD your God, which I am commanding you today, to observe them carefully.U«xƒ%2The LORD will open for you His good treasure house, the heavens, to give rain to your land in its season and to bless all the work of your hand; and you will lend to many nations, but you will not borrow.T«wƒ#2The LORD will give you great prosperity, in the offspring of your body and in the offspring of your livestock and the produce of your ground, in the land which the LORD swore to your fathers to give you.~«vw2
So all the peoples of the earth will see that you are called by the name of the LORD, and they will be afraid of you.q«uƒ]2	The LORD will establish you as a people holy <n>[and set apart]</n> to Himself, just as He has sworn to you, if you keep the commandments of the LORD your God and walk <n>[that is, live your life each and every day]</n> in His ways.6«t‚g2The LORD will command the blessing upon you in your storehouses and in<f>[3]</f> all that you undertake, and He will bless you in the land which the LORD your God gives you.)«s‚M2<pb/>"The LORD will cause the enemies who rise up against you to be defeated before you; they will come out against you one way, but flee before you seven ways.j«rO2<pb/>"You <i>will be</i> blessed when you come in and you <i>will be</i> blessed when you go out.I«q
2<pb/>"Your basket and your kneading bowl <i>will be</i> blessed.N«pƒ2<pb/>"The<f>[1]</f> offspring of your<f>[2]</f> body and the produce of your ground and the offspring of your animals, the offspring of your herd and the young of your flock <i>will be</i> blessed.c«oA2<pb/>"You <i>will be</i> blessed in the city, and you <i>will be</i> blessed in the field.x«nk2All these blessings will come upon you and overtake you if you pay attention to the voice of the LORD your God.«m	ƒ{2<pb/>"Now it shall be, if you diligently listen to <i>and</i> obey the voice of the LORD your God, being careful to do all of His commandments which I am commanding you today, the LORD your God will set you high above all the nations of the earth.@«l‚{2<pb/>'Cursed is he who does not confirm the words of this law by doing them <n>[keeping them, taking them to heart as the rule of his life]</n>.' And all the people shall say, 'Amen.'y«km2<pb/>'Cursed is he who accepts a bribe to strike down an innocent person.' And all the people shall say, 'Amen.'f«jG2<pb/>'Cursed is he who strikes his neighbor in secret.' And all the people shall say, 'Amen.'j«iO2<pb/>'Cursed is he who is intimate with his mother-in-law.' And all the people shall say, 'Amen.' «h‚;2<pb/>'Cursed is he who is intimate with his <n>[half]</n> sister, whether his father's or his mother's daughter.' And all the people shall say, 'Amen.'c«gA2<pb/>'Cursed is he who is intimate with any animal.' And all the people shall say, 'Amen.'8«f‚k2<pb/>'Cursed is he who is intimate with his father's <n>[former]</n> wife, because he has<f>[3]</f> violated what belongs to his father.' And all the people shall say, 'Amen.'
