Then Joshua commanded the officers of the people, saying,­e	‚9<	Have I not commanded you? Be strong and courageous! Do not be terrified or dismayed (intimidated), for the LORD your God is with you wherever you go."‚6­d	„i<This Book of the Law shall not depart from your mouth, but you shall read <n>[and meditate on]</n> it day and night, so that you may be careful to do <n>[everything]</n> in accordance with all that is written in it; for then you will make your way prosperous, and then you will be<f>[4]</f> successful.‚­c	„<Only be strong and very courageous; be careful to do <n>[everything]</n> in accordance with the entire law which Moses My servant commanded you; do not turn from it to the right or to the left, so that you may prosper <i>and</i> be successful wherever you go.(­b	‚M<Be strong <i>and</i> confident and courageous, for you will give this people as an inheritance the land which I swore to their fathers (ancestors) to give them.J­a	ƒ<No man will <n>[be able to]</n> stand before you <n>[to oppose you]</n> as long as you live. Just as I was <n>[present]</n> with Moses, so will I be with you; I will not fail you or abandon you.‚:­`	„q<From the wilderness <n>[of Arabia in the south]</n> and this Lebanon <n>[in the north]</n>, even as far as the great river, the river Euphrates <n>[in the east]</n>, all the land of the<f>[3]</f> Hittites (Canaan), and as far as the Great <n>[Mediterranean]</n> Sea toward the west shall be your territory.h­_	M<I have given you every place on which the sole of your foot treads, just as I promised to Moses.W­^	ƒ+<"Moses My servant is dead; now therefore<f>[1]</f> arise <n>[to take his place]</n>, cross over this Jordan, you and all this people, into the land which I am giving to them, to the<f>[2]</f> sons of Israel.­]		‚=<<pb/>Now it happened after the death of Moses the servant of the LORD, that the LORD spoke to Joshua the son of Nun, Moses' servant (attendant), saying,­\2