So they stationed the people, all the armyâ€”the main encampment that was north of the city, and their rear guard on the west side of the cityâ€”and Joshua spent that night in the valley.|®s<And Joshua took about five thousand men and set them in ambush between Bethel and Ai, on the west side of the city.;®~‚q<Then all the fighting men who were with him went up and advanced and arrived in front of the city, and camped on the north side of Ai. Now there was a ravine between them and Ai.
