FIt happened when Israel became strong, that they put the Canaanites to forced labor, but they did not drive them out completely.‚3³		„cFBut <n>[the tribe of]</n> Manasseh did not take possession of Beth-shean and its villages, or Taanach and its villages, or the inhabitants of Dor and its villages, or the inhabitants of Ibleam and its villages, or the inhabitants of Megiddo and its villages; so the Canaanites remained in that land.~³	yFThe man went into the<f>[5]</f> land of the Hittites and built a city and named it Luz, which is its name to this day.³	‚/FSo he showed them the entrance to the city, and they struck the city with the edge of the sword, but they let the man and all his family go free.³	‚FThe spies saw a man coming out of the city and they said to him, "Please show us the entrance to the city and we will treat you kindly."Y³	/FThe house of Joseph spied out Bethel (now the name of the city was formerly Luz).c³	CF<pb/>The<f>[4]</f> house of Joseph also went up against Bethel, and the LORD was with them.)³	‚OFBut the sons of Benjamin did not drive out the Jebusites who inhabited Jerusalem; so the Jebusites have lived with the sons of Benjamin in Jerusalem to this day.n³	YFThen they gave Hebron to Caleb, as Moses had said, and he drove out from there the three sons of Anak.T³	ƒ%FThe LORD was with Judah, and <n>[the tribe of]</n> Judah took possession of the hill country, but they could not dispossess <i>and</i> drive out those inhabiting the valley because they had iron chariots.
³ 	‚FAlso <n>[the warriors of]</n> Judah captured Gaza with its territory and Ashkelon with its territory and Ekron with its territory.t²	ƒeFThen <n>[the warriors of the tribe of]</n> Judah went with <n>[the warriors of the tribe of]</n> Simeon his brother, and they struck the Canaanites living in Zephath and utterly destroyed it. So the city was called Hormah (destruction).‚²~	„!F<pb/>The sons of <n>[<f>[3]</f> Jethro]</n> the Kenite, Moses' father-in-law, went up from the City of Palms (Jericho) with the sons of Judah, to the wilderness of Judah which is in the Negev (South country) <i>near</i> Arad; and they went and lived with the people.G²}	ƒFShe said to him, "Give me a blessing; since you have given me the land of the Negev (South country), give me springs of water, too." So Caleb gave her the upper springs and the lower springs.l²|	ƒUFWhen she came <i>to Othniel</i>, she persuaded him to <n>[allow her to]</n> ask her father <n>[Caleb]</n> for a field. Then she <n>[rode up to Caleb and]</n> dismounted from her donkey, and Caleb said to her, "What do you want?"u²{	gF
Othniel the son of Kenaz, Caleb's younger brother, captured it; so he gave him his daughter Achsah as a wife.|²z	uFAnd Caleb said, "Whoever attacks Kiriath-sepher and captures it, I will even give him my daughter Achsah as a wife."(²y	‚MFFrom there <n>[the tribe of]</n> Judah went against the inhabitants of Debir (the name of Debir formerly was Kiriath-sepher <n>[city of books and scribes]</n>).!²x	‚?F
So Judah went against the Canaanites who lived in Hebron (the name of Hebron formerly was Kiriath-arba); and they defeated Sheshai and Ahiman and Talmai.²w	‚7F	Afterward the sons of Judah went down to fight against the Canaanites who lived in the hill country, in the Negev (South country) and in the lowland.+²v	‚SF<pb/>Then the sons of Judah fought against <n>[Jebusite]</n> Jerusalem and<f>[2]</f> captured it and struck it with the edge of the sword and set the city on fire.v²u	ƒiFAdoni-bezek said, "Seventy kings with their thumbs and big toes cut off used to gather up <i>scraps of food</i> under my table; as I have done <n>[to others]</n>, so God has repaid me." So they brought him to Jerusalem, and he died there.j²t	QFBut Adoni-bezek fled; and they pursued him and caught him and cut off his thumbs and his big toes.²s	‚	FThen they found Adoni-bezek in Bezek and fought against him, and they struck down in defeat the Canaanites and the Perizzites.²r	‚1FThen Judah went up, and the LORD gave the Canaanites and the Perizzites into their hand, and they struck down in defeat ten thousand men at Bezek.‚#²q	„CFAnd <n>[the tribe of the sons of]</n> Judah said to <n>[the tribe of the sons of]</n> Simeon his brother, "Come up with me into my allotted territory, so that we may fight against the Canaanites; and I likewise will go with you into your allotted territory." So Simeon went with him.
