So the men of Jabesh said <n>[to Nahash the Ammonite]</n>, "Tomorrow we will come out to you <n>[to surrender]</n>, and you may do to us whatever seems good to you."‚º„3Z	They said to the messengers who had come, "You shall say to the men of Jabesh-gilead: 'Tomorrow, by the time the sun is hot, you will have<f>[5]</f> help <n>[against the Ammonites]</n>.'" So the messengers came and reported this to the men of Jabesh; and they were overjoyed.}ºuZHe assembled <i>and</i> counted them at Bezek; and the sons of Israel numbered 300,000, and the men of Judah 30,000.‚Xº…+ZHe took a team of oxen and cut them in pieces, and sent them throughout the territory of Israel by the hand of messengers, saying, "Whoever does not come out to follow Saul and Samuel, the same shall be done to his oxen." Then fear of the LORD fell on the people, and they came out <n>[united]</n> as one man <n>[with one purpose]</n>.lºSZThe Spirit of God came upon Saul mightily when he heard these words, and he became extremely angry.KºƒZ<pb/>Now Saul was coming out of the field behind the oxen, and he said, "What is <i>the matter</i> with the people that they are weeping?" So they told him about the report of the men of Jabesh.º‚'Z<f>[4]</f> Then the messengers came to Gibeah of Saul and told the news to the people; and all the people raised their voices and wept aloud.Zºƒ/ZThe elders of Jabesh said to Nahash, "Give us seven days so that we may send messengers throughout the territory of Israel. Then, if there is no one to save us, we will come out <n>[and surrender]</n> to you."PºƒZBut Nahash the Ammonite told them, "I will make <i>a treaty</i> with you on this condition, that I will<f>[3]</f> gouge out the right eye of every one of you, and make it a disgrace upon all Israel."Uº	ƒ'Z<pb/>Now Nahash the<f>[1]</f> Ammonite <n>[king]</n> went up and<f>[2]</f> besieged Jabesh-gilead; and all the men of Jabesh said to Nahash, "Make a trea