Cˆ    7¼M‚iZYet Saul did not say anything that day, for he thought, "It is an incident <n>[of some kind]</n> and<f>[13]</f> he is not <n>[ceremonially]</n> cleanâ€”surely he is unclean."C¼LƒZThe king sat on his seat as on previous occasions, on his seat by the wall; then Jonathan stood up, and Abner <n>[his commander]</n> sat down by Saul's side, but David's place was empty.u¼KeZ<pb/>So David hid in the field; and when the New Moon <n>[festival]</n> came, the king sat down to eat food.¼J‚7ZAs for the agreement of which you and I have spoken, behold, the LORD is between you and me forever <n>[making sure that we each keep our word]</n>."m¼IUZBut if I say to the boy, 'Look, the arrows are beyond you,' then go, for the LORD has sent you away.‚#¼H„AZAnd I will send a boy, <i>saying</i>, 'Go, find the arrows.' If I specifically say to the boy, 'Look, the arrows are on this side of you, get them,' then come <n>[back to my father's table]</n>; for it is<f>[11]</f> safe for you and there is<f>[12]</f> no danger, as the LORD lives.S¼G!ZI will shoot three arrows to the side of it, as though I shot at a target.a¼Fƒ=ZWhen you have stayed for three days, you shall go down quickly and come to the place where you hid yourself<f>[10]</f> on that eventful day <n>[when my father tried to kill you]</n>, and shall stay by the stone Ezel.¼E‚Z<pb/>Then Jonathan said to David, "Tomorrow is the New Moon <n>[festival]</n>, and you will be missed because your seat will be empty.f¼DGZJonathan made David vow again because of his love for him, for Jonathan loved him as himself.}¼CƒuZSo Jonathan made a <i>covenant</i> with the<f>[7]</f> house of David. <n>[<f>[8]</f> He added,]</n> "May<f>[9]</f> the LORD require it at the hands of David's enemies. <n>[that is, hold them accountable for any harm they inflict on David]</n>.";¼B‚qZ"You shall never cut off your lovingkindness <i>and</i> faithfulness from my hou