Then David said to Jonathan, "Who will tell me if your father answers you harshly?"%¼<‚EZ	Jonathan said, "Far be it from <n>[happening to]</n> you! In fact, if I indeed learn that my father has decided to harm you, would I not tell you about it?"z¼;ƒoZTherefore show kindness to your servant, because you have brought your servant into a covenant of the LORD with you. But if there is iniquity (guilt) in me, kill me yourself; for why should you bring me to your father <n>[to be killed]</n>?"¼:ZIf he says, 'All right,' your servant will be safe; but if he is very angry, then be certain that he has decided on evil.C¼9ƒZIf your father misses me at all, then say, 'David earnestly asked <i>permission</i> from me to go to Bethlehem, his city, because it is the yearly sacrifice there for the entire family.'x¼8ƒkZDavid said to Jonathan, "Behold, tomorrow is the New Moon <n>[observance]</n>, and I should sit at the table to eat <n>[the sacrificial meal]</n> with the king; but let me go, so that I may hide myself in the field until the third evening.L¼7ZThen Jonathan said to David, "Whatever you say, I will do for you."‚¼6„%ZBut David vowed again, saying "Your father certainly knows that I have found favor in your sight, and he has said, 'Do not let Jonathan know this, or he will be worried.' But truly as the LORD lives and as your soul lives, there is hardly a step between me and death."G¼5ƒ	ZJonathan said to him, "Far from it! You shall not die. My father does nothing<f>[2]</f> important or insignificant without telling me. So why would he hide this thing from me? It is not so!"G¼4	ƒZ<pb/>David fled from Naioth in Ramah and he came and said to Jonathan, "What have I done? What is my<f>[1]</f> guilt? What is my sin before (against) your father, that he is seeking my life?"=¼3‚uZHe also took off his <n>[royal]</n> robes <n>[and armor]</n> and prophesied before Samuel and lay down naked all that day and night. So they say, "Is Saul also among the prophets?"¼2‚9ZSo he went on to Naioth in Ramah; and the Spirit of God came upon him too, and he went along continually prophesying until he came to Naioth in Ramah.K¼1ƒZThen Saul went to Ramah himself and came to the great well that is in Secu; and he asked, "Where are Samuel and David?" And he was told, "They are at Naioth <n>[with the prophets]</n> in Ramah." ¼0‚;ZWhen Saul was informed, he sent other messengers, and they also prophesied. So Saul sent messengers again, the third time, and they prophesied as well._¼/ƒ9ZThen Saul sent messengers to take David; but when they saw the group of prophets prophesying, and Samuel standing and presiding over them, the Spirit of God came on the messengers of Saul; and they also prophesied.5¼.gZSaul was told, "David is at Naioth in Ramah."$¼-‚CZ<pb/>So David fled and escaped and came to Samuel at Ramah, and told him everything that Saul had done to him. And he and Samuel went and stayed in Naioth.:¼,‚oZSaul said to Michal, "Why have you deceived me like this and let my enemy go, so that he has escaped?" Michal answered Saul, "He said to me, 'Let me go! Why should I kill you?'"¼+‚	ZWhen the messengers came in, there was the<f>[3]</f> household idol on the bed with a quilt of goats' <i>hair</i> at its head.¼*‚/ZThen Saul sent the messengers <n>[again]</n> to see David, saying, "Bring him up to me on his bed <n>[if necessary]</n>, so that I may kill him."M¼)ZAnd when Saul sent messengers to take David, she said, "He is sick."¼(‚/Z
