Toi sent<f>[4]</f> Joram his son to King David to<f>[5]</f> greet and congratulate him for his battle and defeat of Hadadezer; for Hadadezer had been at war with Toi. <i>Joram</i> brought with him articles of silver, gold, and bronze <n>[as gifts]</n>.`À;d	<pb/>When Toi king of Hamath heard about David's defeat of all the forces of Hadadezer,iÀMdAnd from Betah and Berothai, cities of Hadadezer, King David took an immense quantity of bronze.vÀgdDavid took the shields of gold that were carried by the servants of Hadadezer, and brought them to Jerusalem.#À‚AdThen David put garrisons among the Arameans in Damascus, and the Arameans became his servants and brought tribute. The LORD helped David wherever he went.zÀodWhen the Arameans (Syrians) of Damascus came to help Hadadezer, king of Zobah, David struck down 22,000 Arameans.DÀƒdDavid captured from him 1,700 horsemen and 20,000 foot soldiers. David also hamstrung all the chariot horses (making them lame), but reserved <i>enough</i> of them for a hundred chariots.À‚)d<pb/>Then David defeated Hadadezer the son of Rehob, king of<f>[3]</f> Zobah, as he went to restore his power at the River <n>[Euphrates]</n>.‚QÀ…d<pb/>He defeated<f>[1]</f> Moab, and<f>[2]</f> measured them with a length of rope, making them lie down on the ground; he measured two lengths to <n>[choose those to]</n> put to death, and one full length to <n>[choose those to]</n> be kept alive. And the <n>[surviving]</n> Moabites became servants to David, bringing tribute.FÀ	ƒ	d<pb/>Now it came about after this that David defeated the Philistines and subdued (humbled) them, and he took control of Metheg-ammah <n>[the main city]</n> from the hand of the Philistines.xÀƒkdTherefore now, may it please You to bless the house (royal dynasty) of Your servant, so that it may continue forever before You; for You, O Lord GOD, have spoken it, and with Your blessing may the house of Your servant be blessed forever."{ÀqdAnd now, O Lord GOD, You are God, and Your words are truth, and You have promised this good thing to Your servant.hÀƒKdFor You, O LORD of hosts, God of Israel, have<f>[5]</f> revealed this to Your servant, saying, 'I will build you a house (royal dynasty).' For that reason Your servant has found<f>[6]</f> courage to pray this prayer to You.JÀƒdso that Your Name may be magnified forever, saying, 'The LORD of hosts (armies) is God over Israel;' and may the house (royal dynasty) of Your servant David be established<f>[4]</f> before You.9À‚mdNow, O LORD God, confirm forever the word <n>[of the covenant]</n> that You have spoken in regard to Your servant and his house (royal dynasty); and do just as You have spoken,xÀ
