ÃD‚d)<t>"You have also made my enemies turn their backs to me <n>[in retreat]</n>, </t><t>And I destroyed those who hated me.</t><br/>ÃC‚d(<t>"For You have surrounded me with strength for the battle; </t><t>You have subdued under me those who stood against me.</t><br/>tÃBcd'<t>"I consumed them and shattered them, so that they did not rise; </t><t>They fell under my feet.</t><br/>ÃA‚d&<t>"I pursued my enemies and destroyed them, </t><t>And I did not turn back until they were consumed (eliminated).</t><br/>YÃ@-d%<t>"You enlarge my steps under me, </t><t>And my feet have not slipped.</t><br/>Ã?‚d$<t>"You have also given me the shield of Your salvation, </t><t>And Your help <i>and</i> gentleness make me great.</t><br/>nÃ>Wd#<t>"He trains my hands for war, </t><t>So that my arms can bend (pull back) a bow of bronze.</t><br/>Ã=‚5d"<t>"He makes my feet like the doe's <i>feet</i> <n>[firm and swift]</n>; </t><t>He sets me <n>[secure and confident]</n> on my high places.</t><br/>YÃ<-d!<t>"God is my strong fortress; </t><t>He sets the blameless in His way.</t><br/>bÃ;?d <t>"For who is God, besides the LORD? </t><t>And who is a rock, besides our God?</t><br/>=Ã:‚ud<t>"As for God, His way is blameless <i>and</i> perfect; </t><t>The word of the LORD is tested. </t><t>He is a shield to all those who take refuge <i>and</i> trust in Him.</t><br/>aÃ9=d<t>"For by You I can run upon a troop; </t><t>By my God I can leap over a wall.</t><br/>mÃ8Ud<t>"For You, O LORD, are my lamp; </t><t>The LORD illumines <i>and</i> dispels my darkness.</t><br/>Ã7‚d<t>"And You save the afflicted people; </t><t>But Your eyes are on the haughty <i>whom</i> You abase (humiliate).</t><br/>oÃ6Yd<t>"With the pure You show Yourself pure, </t><t>With the perverted You show Yourself astute.</t><br/>Ã5‚+d<t>"With the loving <i>and</i> loyal You show Yourself loving <i>and</i> loyal, </t><t>With the blameless You show Yourself blameless.</t><br/>Ã4‚d<t>"Therefore the LORD has rewarded me according to my righteousness, </t><t>According to my cleanness in His sight.</t><br/>^Ã37d<t>"I was also blameless before Him, </t><t>And kept myself from wrongdoing.</t><br/> Ã2{d<t>"For all His judgments (legal decisions) were before me, </t><t>And from His statutes I did not turn aside.</t><br/>nÃ1Wd<t>"For I have kept the ways of the LORD, </t><t>And have not acted wickedly against my God.</t><br/>Ã0‚d<t>"The LORD has dealt with me according to my righteousness; </t><t>According to the cleanness of my hands He has rewarded me.</t><br/>oÃ/Yd<t>"He also brought me out to an open place; </t><t>He rescued me because He delighted in me.</t><br/>fÃ.Gd<t>"They came upon me in the day of my calamity, </t><t>But the LORD was my support.</t><br/>zÃ-od<t>"He rescued me from my strong enemy, </t><t>From those who hated me, for they were too mighty for me.</t><br/>\Ã,3d<t>"He sent from above, He took me; </t><t>He drew me out of great waters.</t><br/>?Ã+‚yd<t>"The channels of the sea appeared, </t><t>The foundations of the world were uncovered </t><t>At the rebuke of the LORD, </t><t>At the blast of the breath of His nostrils.</t><br/>aÃ*=d<t>"He sent out arrows and scattered them; </t><t>Lightning, and confused them.</t><br/>aÃ)=d<t>"The LORD thundered from heaven, </t><t>And the Most High uttered His voice.</t><br/>\Ã(3d
