	¦îƒ‡mÊ»                                                                           ‚Äx„nSo now, O LORD my God, You have made Your servant king in place of David my father; and as for me, I am but a little boy <n>[<f>[4]</f> in wisdom and experience]</n>; I do not know how to go out or come in <n>[that is, how to conduct business as a king]</n>.‚CÄw…nThen Solomon said, "You have shown Your servant David my father great lovingkindness, because he walked before You in faithfulness and righteousness and with uprightness of heart toward You; and You have kept for him this great lovingkindness, in that You have given him a son to sit on his throne, as it is today.{ÄvqnIn Gibeon the LORD appeared to Solomon in a dream at night; and God said, "Ask <n>[Me]</n> what I shall give you."ZÄuƒ/nThe king went to Gibeon <n>[near Jerusalem, where the tabernacle and the bronze altar stood]</n> to sacrifice there, for that was the great high place. Solomon offered a thousand burnt offerings on that altar.‚Ät„'n<pb/>Now Solomon loved the LORD, walking <n>[at first]</n> in the statutes of David his father, except <n>[for the fact that]</n> he sacrificed and burned incense in the high places <n>[ignoring the law that required all sacrifices to be offered at the tabernacle]</n>.xÄsƒknBut <n>[in the meantime]</n> the people were still sacrificing <n>[to God]</n> on the high places (hilltops) <n>[as the pagans did to their idols]</n>, for there was no <n>[permanent]</n> house yet built for the<f>[3]</f> Name of the LORD.‚gÄr	…Kn<pb/>Now Solomon became a son-in-law to Pharaoh king of Egypt <n>[and formed an alliance]</n> by<f>[1]</f> taking Pharaoh's daughter <n>[in marriage]</n>. He brought her to the<f>[2]</f> City of David <n>[where she remained temporarily]</n> until he had finished building his own house (palace) and the house of the LORD and the wall around Jerusalem.4Äq‚cn.So the king commanded Benaiah the son of Jehoiada, and he went out and struck down Shimei, and he died. </t><br/><t>So the kingdom was established in the hands of Solomon.rÄp_n-But King Solomon shall be blessed, and the throne of David shall be established before the LORD forever."(Äo‚Kn,The king also said to Shimei, "You are aware in your own heart of all the evil you did to my father David; so the LORD shall return your evil on your own head.\Än3n+Why then have you not kept the oath of the LORD, and the command which I gave you?"‚6Äm„gn*So the king sent <i>word</i> and called for Shimei and said to him, "Did I not make you swear by the LORD and solemnly warn you, saying, 'Know for certain that on the day you leave <n>[Jerusalem]</n> and go anywhere, you shall surely die'? And you said to me, 'The word (ruling) I have heard is good.'\Äl3n)Now Solomon was told that Shimei had gone from Jerusalem to Gath, and had returned.(Äk‚Kn(So Shimei arose, saddled his donkey, and went to Gath to <n>[King]</n> Achish to look for his servants. And Shimei went and brought them <i>back</i> from Gath.\Äjƒ3n'<pb/>But it happened after three years, that two of Shimei's servants ran away to Achish the son of Maacah, the king of<f>[16]</f> Gath. And Shimei was told, "Behold, your <n>[runaway]</n> servants are in Gath."!Äi‚=n&Shimei said to the king, "The word (ruling) is good. As my lord the king has said, so will your servant do." So Shimei lived in Jerusalem for many days. Äh‚;n%For on the day you leave and cross over the<f>[15]</f> Brook Kidron, know for certain that you shall surely die; your blood shall be on your own head."6Äg‚gn$Now the king sent <i>word</i> and called for Shimei and said to him, "Build yourself a house in Jerusalem and live there. Do not go from there to<f>[14]</f> any other place.Äf‚n#The king appointed Benaiah the son of Jehoiada over the army in Joab's place, and appointed Zadok the priest in place of Abiathar..Äe‚Wn"So Benaiah the son of Jehoiada went up <n>[to the tabernacle]</n> and struck and killed Joab, and he was buried at his own house in the wilderness <n>[of Judah]</n>.HÄdƒn!So shall their blood return on the head of Joab and the heads of his descendants forever. But for David, his descendants, his house, and his throne, may there be peace from the LORD forever."‚:Äc„on The LORD will return his bloody deeds upon his own head, because he struck down two men more righteous and honorable than he and killed them with the sword, without my father David knowing: Abner the son of Ner, commander of the army of Israel, and Amasa the son of Jether, commander of the army of Judah.9Äb‚mnThe king said to him, "Do as he has said.<f>[13]</f> Strike him down and bury him, so that you may remove from me and from my father's house the innocent blood which Joab shed.‚Äa„'nSo Benaiah came to the tent of the LORD and told Joab, "This is what the king commands, 'Come out <i>of there</i>.'" But Joab said, "No, for I will die here." Then Benaiah brought word to the king again, saying, "This is what Joab said, and this is how he answered me."KÄ`ƒnKing Solomon was told that Joab had fled to the tent of the LORD and was at that moment beside the altar. Then Solomon sent Benaiah the son of Jehoiada, saying, "Go,<f>[12]</f> strike him down."tÄ_ƒcnNow the news reached Joab, for Joab had supported <i>and</i> followed Adonijah, although he had not followed Absalom. So Joab fled to the <n>[sacred]</n> tent of the LORD and took hold of the horns of the altar <n>[to seek asylum]</n>.LÄ^ƒnSo Solomon dismissed Abiathar <n>[a descendant of Eli]</n> from being priest to the LORD, fulfilling the word of the LORD, which He had spoken concerning the house (descendants) of Eli in Shiloh.‚,Ä]„Sn<pb/>Then the king said to Abiathar the priest, "Go to Anathoth to your own fields, for you<f>[11]</f> certainly deserve to die; but I will not put you to death this day, because you carried the ark of the Lord GOD before my father David, and you suffered everything that my father endured."iÄ\MnSo King Solomon sent Benaiah the son of Jehoiada, and he<f>[10]</f> struck Adonijah and he died.AÄ[‚}nSo now, as the LORD lives, who has established me and set me on the throne of David my father, and who has made me a house as He promised, Adonijah shall indeed be put to death today."=ÄZ‚unThen King Solomon swore by the LORD, saying, "May God do the same to me, and more also, if Adonijah has not requested this <n>[deplorable]</n> thing against his own<f>[9]</f> life.‚)ÄY„MnKing Solomon answered and said to his mother, "And why are you asking for<f>[8]</f> Abishag the Shunammite for Adonijah? Ask the kingdom for him alsoâ€”since he is my older brotherâ€”<n>[ask it]</n> for him and for Abiathar the priest and Joab the son of Zeruiah <n>[his supporters]</n>!"_ÄX9nSo she said, "Let Abishag the Shunammite be given to your brother Adonijah as a wife."ÄW‚+nThen she said, "I am making one small request of you; do not refuse me." And the king said to her, "Ask, my mother, for I will not refuse you."dÄVƒCnSo Bathsheba went to King Solomon to speak to him for Adonijah. And the king rose to meet her, bowed before her, and sat down on his throne; then he had a throne set for her, the king's mother, and she sat on his right.JÄUnBathsheba replied, "Very well; I will speak to the king for you."ÄT‚nHe said, "Please speak to King Solomon, for he will not refuse you; <i>ask</i> that he may give me Abishag the Shunammite as a wife."jÄSOnSo now I am making one request of you; do not<f>[7]</f> refuse me." And she said to him, "Speak."‚ÄR„nSo he said, "You know that the kingdom belonged to me <n>[as the eldest living son]</n> and all Israel<f>[6]</f> looked to me <i>and</i> expected me to be king. However, the kingdom has passed <n>[from me]</n> and became my brother's, for it was his from the LORD.VÄQ'nThen he said, "I have something <i>to say</i> to you." And she said, "Speak."$ÄP‚Cn
<pb/>Now Adonijah the son of <n>[David and]</n> Haggith came to Bathsheba the mother of Solomon. She said, "Do you come in peace?" And he said, "In peace."dÄOCnThen Solomon sat on the throne of David his father, and his kingdom was firmly established.ÄN‚	nThe time that David reigned over Israel was forty years: he reigned seven years in Hebron and thirty-three years in Jerusalem.lÄMSn
So David lay down with his fathers <n>[in death]</n> and was buried in the<f>[5]</f> City of David.8ÄL‚kn	But now do not let him go unpunished, for you are a wise man; and you will know what to do to him, and you will bring his gray head down to Sheol <n>[covered]</n> with blood."‚;ÄK„qnAnd look, you have with you Shimei the son of Gera, the Benjamite of Bahurim; he is the one who cursed me with a sinister curse the day I went to Mahanaim. But he came down to meet me at the Jordan <n>[on my return]</n>, and I swore to him by the LORD, saying, 'I will not put you to death with the sword.'lÄJƒSnBut be gracious <i>and</i> kind to the sons of Barzillai the Gileadite, and let them be among those who <n>[have the honor to]</n> eat at your table; for they met me <n>[with kindness]</n> when I fled from your brother Absalom.ÄIynSo act in accordance with your wisdom, but do not let his gray head go down to Sheol (the place of the dead) in peace.ƒZÄH‡/n<pb/>Now you also know what Joab the son of Zeruiah <n>[my sister]</n> did to me, and what he did to the two commanders of the armies of Israel, to Abner the son of Ner and to Amasa the son of Jether, <n>[both of]</n> whom he murdered;<f>[2]</f> avenging the blood of war in <n>[a time of]</n> peace. And he put the <n>[innocent]</n> blood of war <n>[of Abner and Amasa]</n> on his<f>[3]</f> belt that was around his<f>[4]</f> waist, and on his sandals on his feet.‚3ÄG„anso that the LORD may fulfill His<f>[1]</f> promise concerning me, saying, 'If your sons are careful regarding their way <n>[of life]</n>, to walk before Me in truth with all their heart <i>and</i> mind and with all their soul, you shall not fail to have a man (descendant) on the throne of Israel.'‚$ÄF„CnKeep the charge of the LORD your God, <n>[that is, fulfill your obligation to]</n> walk in His ways, keep His statutes, His commandments, His precepts, and His testimonies, as it is written in the Law of Moses, so that you may succeed in everything that you do and wherever you turn,kÄEQn"I am going the way of all the earth <n>[as dust to dust]</n>. Be strong and prove yourself a man.bÄD	An<pb/>When David's time to die approached, he gave instructions to Solomon his son, saying,dÄC	ƒEn5So King Solomon sent <n>[soldiers]</n>, and they brought Adonijah down from the altar <n>[that was in front of the tabernacle]</n>. And he came and bowed down to King Solomon, and Solomon said to him, "Go to your house."-ÄB	‚Wn4Solomon said, "If he <n>[proves he]</n> is a worthy man, not <i>even</i> one of his hairs shall fall to the ground; but if wickedness is found in him, he shall die."‚ ÄA	ƒ}n3Now Solomon was told, "Behold, Adonijah is afraid of King Solomon, and behold, he has grasped the horns of the altar <n>[seeking God's protection]</n>, saying, 'King Solomon must swear to me today that he will not kill his servant with the sword.'"#Ä@	‚Cn2And Adonijah feared Solomon, and he got up and went <n>[to the tabernacle on Mt. Zion]</n> and took hold of the horns of the altar <n>[seeking asylum]</n>."Ä?	‚An1<pb/>Then all Adonijah's guests were terrified <n>[of being branded as traitors]</n> and stood up <i>and</i> left the feast, and each one went on his way.>Ä>	‚yn0The king has also said this: 'Blessed be the LORD, the God of Israel, who has granted one <n>[of my descendants]</n> to sit on my throne today and <i>allowed</i> my eyes to see it.'"‚!Ä=	„?n/Moreover, the king's servants came to bless (congratulate) our lord King David, saying, 'May<f>[15]</f> your God make the name of Solomon better (more famous) than your name and make his throne greater than your throne.' And the king bowed himself <n>[before God]</n> upon the bed.IÄ<	n.Besides, Solomon has taken his seat on the throne of the kingdom.IÄ;	ƒn-Also, Zadok the priest and Nathan the prophet have anointed him king in Gihon, and they have come up from there celebrating, so the city is in an uproar. This is the noise which you have heard.LÄ:	ƒn,The king has sent him with Zadok the priest, Nathan the prophet, Benaiah the son of Jehoiada, the Cherethites, and the Pelethites; and they have had him ride on the king's <n>[own royal]</n> mule.qÄ9	_n+But Jonathan replied to Adonijah, "No, <i>on the contrary</i>, our lord King David has made Solomon king!EÄ8	ƒn*While he was still speaking, behold, Jonathan the son of Abiathar the priest arrived. And Adonijah said, "Come in, for you are a valiant <i>and</i> trustworthy man and you bring good news."=Ä7	‚wn)<pb/>Now Adonijah and all the guests who were with him heard it as they finished eating. When Joab heard the trumpet sound, he said, "<f>[14]</f> Why is the city in such an uproar?"AÄ6	‚n(All the people went up after him, and they were playing on flutes and rejoicing with great joy, so that the earth shook <i>and</i> seemed to burst open with their <n>[joyful]</n> sound.?Ä5	‚{n'Zadok the priest took a horn of <n>[olive]</n> oil from the <n>[sacred]</n> tent and anointed Solomon. They blew the trumpet, and all the people said, "<i>Long</i> live King Solomon!"‚Ä4	„n&So Zadok the priest, Nathan the prophet, Benaiah the son of Jehoiada, the Cherethites, and the Pelethites <n>[the king's bodyguards]</n> went down <n>[from Jerusalem]</n> and had Solomon ride on King David's mule, and brought him to <n>[the spring at]</n> Gihon.#Ä3	‚Cn%<f>[13]</f> Just as the LORD has been with my lord the king, so may He be with Solomon, and make his throne greater than the throne of my lord King David!"9Ä2	‚on$Benaiah <n>[the overseer of the king's bodyguards]</n>, the son of Jehoiada answered the king and said, "Amen! (So be it!) May the LORD, the God of my lord the king, say so too.RÄ1	ƒ!n#Then you shall come up <n>[to Jerusalem]</n> after him, and he shall come and sit on my throne and he shall reign <i>as king</i> in my place; for I have appointed him to be ruler over Israel and Judah."Ä0	‚/n"Let Zadok the priest and Nathan the prophet anoint him there as king over Israel. Then blow the trumpet and say, '<i>Long</i> live King Solomon!'dÄ/	ƒEn!The king told them, "Take the<f>[10]</f> servants of your lord with you and have Solomon my son<f>[11]</f> ride on my own mule, and bring him down to <n>[the spring at]</n><f>[12]</f> Gihon <n>[in the Kidron Valley]</n>.Ä.	‚'n <pb/>Then King David said, "Call Zadok the priest, Nathan the prophet, and Benaiah the son of Jehoiada to me." And they came before the king.Ä-	‚'nBathsheba bowed down with her face to the ground, and laid herself face down before the king and said, "May my lord King David live forever!"QÄ,	ƒneven as I swore to you by the LORD, the God of Israel, saying, 'Solomon your son shall certainly be king after me, and he shall sit on my throne in my place'; I will indeed do so this <i>very</i> day."mÄ+	WnThen the king swore an oath and said, "As the LORD lives, who has redeemed my soul from all distress,uÄ*	gn<pb/>King David answered, "Call Bathsheba to me." And she came into the king's presence and stood before him.Ä)	‚/nIf this thing has been done by my lord the king, why have you not shown your servants who shall sit on the throne of my lord the king after him?"Ä(	nBut he has not invited me, your servant, nor Zadok the priest, nor Benaiah the son of Jehoiada, nor your servant Solomon.‚dÄ'	…EnBecause he has gone down today <n>[to En-Rogel]</n> and has sacrificed oxen and fattened steers and sheep in abundance, and has invited all the king's sons, the commanders of the army and Abiathar the priest <n>[to this feast]</n>; and <n>[right now]</n> they are eating and drinking in his presence; and they say, '<i>Long</i> live King Adonijah!'}Ä&	wnThen Nathan said, "My lord the king, have you said, 'Adonijah shall be king after me, and he shall sit on my throne'?Ä%	‚nThe king was told, "Here is Nathan the prophet." And when he came before the king, he bowed before the king with his face to the ground.TÄ$	%n<pb/>While she was still speaking with the king, Nathan the prophet came in.3Ä#	‚cnOtherwise it will come about when my lord the king lies down <n>[in death]</n> with his fathers, that I and my son Solomon will be considered<f>[9]</f> political enemies."6Ä"	‚inNow as for you, my lord the king, the eyes of all<f>[8]</f> Israel are on you <n>[waiting for you]</n> to tell them who shall sit on the throne of my lord the king after him.jÄ!	ƒQnHe has sacrificed oxen and fattened steers and sheep in abundance, and has invited all the king's sons and Abiathar the priest and Joab the commander of the army <n>[to a feast]</n>, but he did not invite your servant Solomon.Ä 	‚nBut now, behold, Adonijah is <n>[acting as]</n> king; and now <n>[as things stand]</n>, my lord the king, you do not know it.8Ä	‚mnShe said to him, "My lord, you swore by the LORD your God to your maidservant, <i>saying</i>, 'Solomon your son shall certainly be king after me and he shall sit on my throne.'oÄ	[nSo Bathsheba bowed down and paid respect to the king. And the king said, "<f>[7]</f> What do you wish?"Ä	‚-n<pb/>So Bathsheba went to the king in his bedroom. Now the king was very old <i>and</i> weak, and Abishag the Shunammite was attending the king.sÄ	cnBehold, while you are still there speaking with the king, I will come in after you and confirm your words."jÄ	ƒQn
