and Johanan became the father of Azariah (it was he who was priest in the house (temple) which Solomon built in Jerusalem)]Ñ`3 ‚	and Ahimaaz became the father of Azariah, and Azariah became the father of Johanan,XÑ_) ‚and Ahitub became the father of Zadok, and Zadok became the father of Ahimaaz,YÑ^+ ‚Meraioth became the father of Amariah, and Amariah became the father of Ahitub,]Ñ]3 ‚and Uzzi became the father of Zerahiah, and Zerahiah became the father of Meraioth,VÑ\% ‚and Abishua became the father of Bukki, and Bukki became the father of Uzzi,WÑ[' ‚Eleazar became the father of Phinehas, Phinehas became the father of Abishua,pÑZY ‚The sons of Amram: Aaron, Moses and Miriam. And the sons of Aaron: Nadab, Abihu, Eleazar, and Ithamar.>ÑYw ‚The sons of Kohath: Amram, Izhar, Hebron, and Uzziel.FÑX	 ‚<pb/><f>[1]</f> The sons of Levi: Gershom, Kohath and Merari.‚XÑW…) ‚So the God of Israel stirred up the spirit of Pul, king of Assyria, <n>[that is,]</n> the spirit of Tilgath-pilneser king of Assyria, and he carried them away into exileâ€”the Reubenites, the Gadites, and the half-tribe of Manassehâ€”and brought them to Halah, Habor, Hara, and the river Gozan, <n>[where they remain]</n> to this day.4ÑV‚a ‚<pb/>But they acted treacherously against the God of their fathers and played the prostitute with the gods of the peoples of the land, whom God had destroyed before them.tÑUƒa ‚These were the heads of their fathers' households: Epher, Ishi, Eliel, Azriel, Jeremiah, Hodaviah, and Jahdiel, warriors of valor <n>[willing and able to encounter danger]</n>, famous men, and heads of the households of their fathers. ÑT‚9 ‚Now the sons (people) of the half-tribe of Manasseh lived in the land; their settlements spread from Bashan to Baal-hermon and Senir and Mount Hermon.FÑSƒ ‚For a great number fell mortally wounded, because the battle was of God. And these Israelites settled in their territory until the exile <n>[by Assyria more than five centuries later]</n>.ÑR‚ ‚These Israelites took away their livestock: their 50,000 camels, and 250,000 sheep, and 2,000 donkeys; and 100,000<f>[3]</f> people.‚ÑQ„ ‚They were given help against them, and the Hagrites were handed over to them, and all who were <i>allied</i> with them; for they cried out to God <n>[for help]</n> in the battle; and He granted their entreaty because they relied on <i>and</i> trusted in Him.(ÑP‚I ‚And these Israelites, <n>[on the east side of the Jordan River]</n> made war with the Hagrites <n>[a tribe of northern Arabia]</n>, Jetur, Naphish, and Nodab.IÑOƒ ‚<pb/>The sons of Reuben, the Gadites, and the half-tribe of Manassehâ€”valiant men able to bear shield and sword, and to shoot with the bow, and skillful in warâ€”were 44,760 who went to war.ÑN‚ ‚All these were enrolled in the genealogies in the days of Jotham king of Judah and in the days of Jeroboam <n>[II]</n> king of Israel.ÑM‚ ‚They lived in Gilead, in Bashan and in its towns, and in all the <n>[surrounding]</n> pasture lands of Sharon, as far as their borders.YÑL+ ‚Ahi the son of Abdiel, the son of Guni, was chief in their fathers' households.+ÑK‚O ‚These were the sons of Abihail the son of Huri, the son of Jaroah, the son of Gilead, the son of Michael, the son of Jeshishai, the son of Jahdo, the son of Buz;
ÑJ‚ ‚
Their relatives from the households of their fathers: Michael, Meshullam, Sheba, Jorai, Jacan, Zia, and Eberâ€”seven <i>in all</i>.SÑI ‚Joel was the chief, Shapham the second, then Janai and Shaphat in Bashan.WÑH' ‚The sons of Gad lived opposite them in the land of Bashan, as far as Salecah:,ÑG‚Q ‚
In the days of King Saul they made war with the<f>[2]</f> Hagrites, who fell by their hands; and they lived in their tents throughout all the land east of Gilead.ÑF‚5 ‚	To the east Bela settled as far as the entrance into the desert from the river Euphrates, because their cattle had multiplied in the land of Gilead.sÑE_ ‚Bela the son of Azaz, the son of Shema, the son of Joel, who lived in Aroer as far as Nebo and Baal-meon.ÑD‚ ‚And his brothers (relatives) by their families, in the genealogy of their generations, were the chief Jeiel, and Zechariah, ÑCy ‚Beerah his son, whom Tilgath-pilneser king of Assyria carried away into exile; he was a leader of the tribe of Reuben.5ÑBe ‚Micah his son, Reaiah his son, Baal his son,JÑA
 ‚The sons of Joel: Shemaiah his son, Gog his son, Shimei his son,WÑ@' ‚the sons of Reuben the firstborn of Israel: Hanoch, Pallu, Hezron, and Carmi.'Ñ?‚G ‚Though Judah prevailed over his brothers, and from him came <n>[David]</n> the leader <n>[and eventually the Messiah]</n>, yet the birthright was Joseph'sâ€”ƒÑ>	†	 ‚<pb/>Now <n>[we come to]</n> the sons of Reuben the firstborn of Israelâ€”for Reuben was the eldest, but because he defiled his father's bed <n>[with Bilhah his father's<f>[1]</f> concubine]</n>, his birthright was given to <n>[Manasseh and Ephraim]</n> the sons of Joseph <n>[the favorite]</n> son of Israel, so that he is not enrolled in the genealogy according to the birthright.Ñ=‚ ‚+They destroyed the remnant of the Amalekites who escaped, and they have lived there to this day (the date of this writing).$Ñ<‚A ‚*From them, from the sons of Simeon, five hundred men went to Mount Seir, with Pelatiah, Neariah, Rephaiah, and Uzziel, the sons of Ishi, as their leaders.‚Ñ;„3 ‚)These, registered by name, came in the days of Hezekiah king of Judah, and they attacked their tents and the Meunites (foreigners) who were found there, and utterly destroyed them to this day; and they settled in their place, because there was pasture there for their flocks.cÑ:ƒ? ‚(They found rich, good pasture, and the <n>[cleared]</n> land was wide, quiet, and peaceful; for those who had lived there previously came from Ham <n>[and had left it a better place for those who came after them]</n>.wÑ9g ‚'So they journeyed to the entrance of Gedor, to the east side of the valley, to seek pasture for their flocks.Ñ8‚ ‚&these mentioned by name were leaders in their families; and their fathers' houses increased greatly <n>[so they needed more land]</n>.oÑ7W ‚%Ziza the son of Shiphi, the son of Allon, the son of Jedaiah, the son of Shimri, the son of Shemaiah;PÑ6 ‚$also Elioenai, Jaakobah, Jeshohaiah, Asaiah, Adiel, Jesimiel, Benaiah,PÑ5 ‚#Joel, Jehu the son of Joshibiah, the son of Seraiah, the son of Asiel,;Ñ4q ‚"<pb/>Meshobab, Jamlech, Joshah the son of Amaziah,Ñ3‚! ‚!and all their villages that were around these towns as far as Baal. These were their settlements, and they have their genealogical record.aÑ2; ‚ <i>These were</i> their villages: Etam, Ain, Rimmon, Tochen, and Ashanâ€”five citiesâ€”tÑ1a ‚Beth-marcaboth, Hazar-susim, Beth-biri, and at Shaaraim. These were their cities until the reign of David.!Ñ0= ‚Bethuel, Hormah, Ziklag,Ñ/5 ‚Bilhah, Ezem, Tolad,7Ñ.i ‚They lived at Beersheba, Moladah, Hazar-shual,Ñ-‚/ ‚Shimei had sixteen sons and six daughters; but his brothers did not have many sons, neither did all their family multiply like the sons of Judah.NÑ, ‚The sons of Mishma: Hammuel his son, Zaccur his son, Shimei his son.AÑ+} ‚Shallum was Shaul's son, Mibsam his son, Mishma his son.EÑ* ‚The sons of Simeon: Nemuel, Jamin, Jarib, Zerah, and Shaul;Ñ)‚5 ‚These were the potters and those who lived <n>[among plantations and hedges]</n> at Netaim and Gederah; they lived there with the king for his work.Ñ(‚ ‚and Jokim, the men of Cozeba, Joash, and Saraph, who ruled in Moab, and Jashubi-lehem. These are ancient words (genealogical records).'Ñ'‚G ‚The sons of Shelah son of Judah: Er the father of Lecah and Laadah the father of Mareshah, and the families of the house of the linen workers at Beth-ashbea;jÑ&M ‚The sons of Shimon: Amnon, Rinnah, Benhanan, and Tilon. The sons of Ishi: Zoheth and Ben-zoheth.Ñ% ‚The sons of the wife of Hodiah, the sister of Naham, were: the fathers of Keilah the Garmite and Eshtemoa the Maacathite.Ñ$‚ ‚Mered's Jewish wife gave birth to Jered the father of Gedor, Heber the father of Soco, and Jekuthiel the father of Zanoah.[Ñ#ƒ/ ‚The sons of Ezrah: Jether, Mered, Epher, and Jalon. These are the sons of Bithia daughter of Pharaoh, whom Mered took: she conceived <i>and gave birth to</i> Miriam, Shammai, and Ishbah the father of Eshtemoa.AÑ"} ‚The sons of Jehallelel: Ziph, Ziphah, Tiria, and Asarel.zÑ!m ‚The sons of Caleb <n>[Joshua's companion]</n> the son of Jephunneh: Iru, Elah, and Naam. The son of Elah: Kenaz.8Ñ ‚i ‚Meonothai became the father of Ophrah, and Seraiah became the father of Joab the father of Ge-harashim <n>[the Valley of Craftsmen, so named]</n> because they were craftsmen.bÑ= ‚
