 ‚	"These were heads of fathers' <i>households</i> of the Levites according to their generations, chief men, who lived in Jerusalem.VÓƒ% ‚	!<pb/>Now these are the singers, heads of the fathers' <i>households</i> of the Levites, <i>living</i> in the <i>temple</i> chambers, free <i>from other service</i> because they were on duty day and night.hÓI ‚	 Some of their Kohathite relatives were in charge of the showbread to prepare it every Sabbath.~Óu ‚	Mattithiah, one of the Levites, the firstborn of Shallum the Korahite, was responsible for the things baked in pans.BÓ ‚	Other sons of the priests prepared the mixture of spices.eÓƒC ‚	Some of them also were appointed over the furniture and over all the <n>[sacred]</n> utensils of the sanctuary, as well as over the fine flour and the wine and the <n>[olive]</n> oil and the frankincense and the spices.Ó‚ ‚	<pb/>Now some of them were in charge of the serving utensils, being required to count them when they brought them in or took them out.+Ó‚O ‚	They spent the night around the house of God, for the <n>[night]</n> watch was theirs, and they were in charge of opening <i>the house</i> morning after morning.Ó‚# ‚	for these Levites, the four chief gatekeepers, had an official duty, and were in charge of the chambers and treasuries of the house of God.oÓW ‚	Their relatives in their villages were to come in every seven days from time to time to be with them;iÓK ‚	The gatekeepers were <i>stationed</i> on the four sides â€”on the east, west, north, and south.Ó‚ ‚	So they and their sons were in charge of the gates of the house of the LORD, that is, the house of the tabernacle, as guards.‚Óƒ ‚	All those chosen to be gatekeepers at the thresholds were 212. They were enrolled by their genealogies in their villages <n>[around Jerusalem]</n>, these men <n>[whose grandfathers]</n> David and Samuel the seer had appointed to their official duty.]Ó
