the third to Zaccur, his sons and his relatives, twelve;zÖ0m ‚	<pb/>The first lot for Asaph fell to Joseph; the second to Gedaliah, to him, his relatives and his sons, twelve; Ö/‚9 ‚The musicians cast lots for their duties, everyone alike, the small (younger) as well as the great (older), the teacher <i>as well</i> as the student.$Ö.‚A ‚So their number <n>[who led the remainder of the 4,000]</n>, with their relatives who were trained in singing to the LORD, all who were skillful, was 288.uÖ-ƒc ‚All these were under the direction of their father to sing in the house of the LORD, with cymbals, harps, and lyres, for the service of the house of God. Asaph, Jeduthun, and Heman were under the order <i>and</i> direction of the king.9Ö,‚k ‚All these <n>[men]</n> were the sons of Heman the king's seer to<f>[4]</f> exalt him in accordance with the words of God; for God gave Heman fourteen sons and three daughters.8Ö+‚i ‚Of Heman, the sons of Heman: Bukkiah, Mattaniah, Uzziel, Shebuel, Jerimoth, Hananiah, Hanani, Eliathah, Giddalti, Romamti-ezer, Joshbekashah, Mallothi, Hothir, and Mahazioth.aÖ*ƒ; ‚Of Jeduthun, the sons of Jeduthun: Gedaliah, Zeri, Jeshaiah, Shimei, Hashabiah, and Mattithiah, six, under the direction of their father Jeduthun, who prophesied with the lyre in thanksgiving and praise to the LORD.BÖ)‚} ‚Of the sons of Asaph: Zaccur, Joseph, Nethaniah, and Asharelah; the sons of Asaph were under the direction of Asaph, who prophesied<f>[2]</f> under the<f>[3]</f> direction of the king.‚!Ö(	„= ‚<pb/>Moreover, David and the commanders of the army selected for the <n>[temple]</n> service some of the sons of Asaph, Heman, and Jeduthun, who were to<f>[1]</f> prophesy with lyres, harps, and cymbals. The list of the musicians who performed their service was <i>as follows</i>:‚ Ö'„9 ‚These also cast lots as did their relatives the sons of Aaron in the presence of David the king, Zadok, Ahimelech, and the heads of the fathers' <i>households</i> of the priests and of the Levitesâ€”the head of father's <i>households</i> as well as those of his younger brother.Ö&} ‚The sons of Mushi: Mahli, Eder, and Jerimoth. These were the sons of the Levites according to their fathers' households..Ö%W ‚By Kish: the sons of Kish, Jerahmeel.,Ö$S ‚By Mahli: Eleazar, who had no sons.MÖ# ‚The sons of Merari: by Jaaziah were Beno, Shoham, Zaccur, and Ibri.IÖ" ‚The sons of Merari: Mahli and Mushi; the sons of Jaaziah, Beno.KÖ! ‚The brother of Micah, Isshiah; of the sons of Isshiah, Zechariah.EÖ  ‚Of the sons of Uzziel, Micah; of the sons of Micah, Shamir.zÖm ‚The sons <i>of Hebron</i>: Jeriah <i>the first</i>, Amariah the second, Jahaziel the third, Jekameam the fourth.HÖ	 ‚Of the Izharites: Shelomoth; of the sons of Shelomoth, Jahath.AÖ} ‚Of Rehabiah: of the sons of Rehabiah: Isshiah the first.xÖi ‚<pb/>Now as for the rest of the sons of Levi: of the sons of Amram: Shubael; of the sons of Shubael: Jehdeiah._Öƒ7 ‚These were their offices <i>and</i> positions for their service in the house of the LORD according to the ordinance given to them by their father (ancestor) Aaron, just as the LORD God of Israel had commanded him.DÖ ‚the twenty-third to Delaiah, the twenty-fourth to Maaziah.@Ö{ ‚the twenty-first to Jachin, the twenty-second to Gamul,@Ö{ ‚the nineteenth to Pethahiah, the twentieth to Jehezkel,?Öy ‚the seventeenth to Hezir, the eighteenth to Happizzez,9Öm ‚the fifteenth to Bilgah, the sixteenth to Immer,?Öy ‚
