g like it had ever been made for any <n>[other]</n> kingdom..Øw‚U Œ	<i>There were</i> six steps to the throne and a golden footstool attached to the throne, and arms on each side of the seat, with two lions standing beside the arms.^Øv5 Œ	<pb/>Moreover, the king made a great throne of ivory and overlaid it with pure gold.NØuƒ Œ	And <i>he made</i> three hundred <n>[smaller]</n> shields of beaten gold, using three hundred shekels of gold on each shield; and the king put them in the<f>[5]</f> house of the Forest of Lebanon.Øt‚ Œ	King Solomon made two hundred large shields of beaten gold, using six hundred <i>shekels of</i> beaten gold on each large shield.Øs‚- Œ	besides what the traders and merchants brought; and all the kings of Arabia and the governors of the country brought gold and silver to Solomon.SØr Œ	
