  <pb/>So we built the wall and the entire wall was joined together to half its <i>height</i>, for the people had a heart to work.àM‚-  Do not forgive their wrongdoing and do not let their sin be wiped out before You, for they have offended the builders <n>[and provoked You]</n>.&àL‚E  <pb/><n>[And Nehemiah prayed]</n> Hear, O our God, how we are despised! Return their taunts on their own heads. Give them up as prey in a land of captivity."àK‚=  Now Tobiah the Ammonite was beside him, and he said, "Even what they are buildingâ€”if a fox should get up on it, he would break down their stone wall."‚'àJ„G  He spoke before his brothers and the army of Samaria, "What are these feeble Jews doing? Can they restore it for themselves? Can they offer sacrifices? Can they finish in a day? Can they revive the stones from the heaps of dust <i>and</i> rubbish, even the ones that have been burned?"àI	‚%  <pb/><f>[1]</f> But when Sanballat heard that we were rebuilding the wall, he became furious, completely enraged, and he ridiculed the Jews.}àHs   Between the upper room of the corner and<f>[9]</f> the Sheep Gate the goldsmiths and merchants carried out repairs.`àGƒ9  After him Malchijah, one of the goldsmiths, carried out repairs as far as the house of the temple servants and of the merchants, in front of the<f>[8]</f> Inspection Gate and as far as the upper room of the corner.JàFƒ
  After him Hananiah the son of Shelemiah, and Hanun the sixth son of Zalaph, repaired another section. After him Meshullam the son of Berechiah carried out repairs in front of his own quarters.2àE‚]  After them Zadok the son of Immer carried out repairs in front of his house. After him Shemaiah the son of Shecaniah, keeper of the East Gate, repaired <i>the wall</i>.aàD;  <pb/>Above the Horse Gate the priests made repairs, each one in front of his own house.àC}  After them the Tekoites repaired another section in front of the great projecting tower and as far as the wall of Ophel.BàB‚}  The temple servants were living in Ophel <n>[the hill south of the temple]</n>, and they <i>made repairs</i> as far as the front of the Water Gate on the east and the projecting tower.‚àAƒ  Palal the son of Uzai <i>made repairs</i> in front of the Angle <n>[in the wall]</n> and the tower projecting from the upper house (palace) of the king, which is by the courtyard of the guard. After him Pedaiah the son of Parosh <i>made repairs</i>.+à@‚O  After him Binnui the son of Henadad repaired another section <n>[of the wall]</n>, from the house of Azariah to the Angle <n>[in the wall]</n> and to the corner.5à?‚c  After them Benjamin and Hasshub made repairs in front of their house. After them Azariah the son of Maaseiah, the son of Ananiah, carried out repairs beside his own house.bà>=  After him the priests, the men of the <n>[lower Jordan]</n> valley, carried out repairs..à=‚U  After him Meremoth the son of Uriah, the son of Hakkoz, repaired another <n>[eastern]</n> section, from the door of Eliashib's house as far as the end of his house.?à<‚w  After him Baruch son of Zabbai zealously repaired another section <n>[toward the hill]</n>, from the Angle <n>[in the wall]</n> to the door of the house of Eliashib the high priest.9à;‚k  Next to him Ezer the son of Jeshua, the official of Mizpah, repaired another section <n>[northward]</n> in front of the ascent to the armory at the Angle <n>[in the wall]</n>.à:‚3  After him their brothers carried out repairs <i>under</i> Bavvai the son of Henadad, official of <n>[the other]</n> half of the district of Keilah.=à9‚s  After him the Levites carried out repairs <i>under</i> Rehum the son of Bani. Next to him Hashabiah, official of half the district of Keilah, carried out repairs for his district.xà8ƒi  After him<f>[7]</f> Nehemiah the son of Azbuk, official of half the district of Beth-zur, repaired <n>[the wall]</n> as far as <n>[a point]</n> in front of the tombs of David, and as far as the artificial pool and the house of the guards.ƒ/à7†W  <pb/>Shallum the son of Col-hozeh, official of the district of Mizpah repaired the<f>[6]</f> Fountain Gate. He rebuilt it and covered it <n>[with a roof]</n>, and set up its doors with its bolts and its bars, and <n>[he rebuilt]</n> the wall of the Pool of Shelah (Siloam) by the King's Garden as far as the stairs that descend <n>[the eastern slope]</n> from <n>[the section of Jerusalem known as]</n> the City of David.1à6‚[  <pb/>Malchijah the son of Rechab, the official of the district of Beth-haccherem repaired the Refuse Gate. He rebuilt it and set its doors with its bolts and its bars.eà5ƒC  
