They made a proclamation throughout Judah and Jerusalem to all the <n>[former]</n> exiles, that they were to assemble at Jerusalem,‚ ßcƒy –
Then Ezra got up from before the house of God and went into the chamber of Jehohanan the son of Eliashib <n>[and spent the night there]</n>. He did not eat bread nor drink water, for he was mourning over the <n>[former]</n> exiles' faithlessness.:ßb‚m –
<pb/>Then Ezra stood and made the leaders of the priests, the Levites, and all Israel, take an oath that they would act in accordance with this proposal; so they took the oath.Tßa! –
Stand up, for it is your duty, and we will be with you. Be brave and act."‚*ß`„M –
Therefore let us now make a covenant with our God to send away all the <n>[foreign]</n> wives and their children, in accordance with the advice of my lord and of those who tremble <n>[in reverent obedience]</n> at the commandment of our God; and let it be done in accordance with the Law.]ß_ƒ3 –
Shecaniah the son of Jehiel, of the sons of Elam, said to Ezra, "We have been unfaithful to our God and have married foreign women from the peoples of the land; yet now there is hope for Israel in spite of this.bß^	ƒ? –
<pb/>Now while Ezra was praying and confessing, weeping and laying himself face down before the house of God, a very large group from Israel, of men, women, and children, gathered to him, for the people wept bitterly.dß]ƒA –	O LORD God of Israel, You are <n>[uncompromisingly]</n> just (righteous), for we have been left as survivors, as it is this day. Behold, we are before You in our guilt, for no one can stand before You because of this."eß\ƒC –	shall we again break Your commandments and intermarry with the peoples who practice these repulsive acts? Would You not be angry with us to the point of total destruction, so that there would be no remnant nor survivor?Uß[ƒ# –	
And after everything that has come upon us for our evil deeds and for our great guilt, since You our God have punished us less than our wrongdoings <i>deserve</i>, and have given us survivors like these,‚ßZ„ –	So now do not give your daughters to their sons or take their daughters for your sons; and never seek their peace or their prosperity, so that you may be strong and eat the good <i>things</i> of the land and leave it as an inheritance to your children forever.'‚'ßY„G –	which You have commanded by Your servants the prophets, saying, 'The land which you are entering to possess is a defiled land with the uncleanness of the peoples of the lands, through their repulsive acts which have filled it from one end to the other <i>along</i> with their impurity.yßXk –	
<pb/>"Now, O our God, what shall we say after this? For we have abandoned (turned away from) Your commandments,‚"ßW„= –		For we are slaves; yet our God has not abandoned us in our bondage, but has extended lovingkindness to us before the kings of Persia, to revive us to rebuild the house of our God, to repair the site of its ruins and to give us a wall <n>[of protection]</n> in Judah and Jerusalem.‚
ßV„ –	But now for a brief moment grace has been <n>[shown to us]</n> from the LORD our God, who has left us a surviving remnant and has given us a peg (secure hold) in His holy place, that our God may enlighten our eyes and give us a little reviving in our bondage.‚ßU„) –	Since the days of our fathers to this day we have been exceedingly guilty; and on account of our wrongdoings we, our kings, and our priests have been handed over to the kings of the lands, to the sword, to captivity, to plundering, and to complete shame, as it is today.=ßT‚s –	and I said, "O my God, I am ashamed and embarrassed to lift up my face to You, my God, for our wrongdoings have risen higher than our heads and our guilt has grown to the heavens.NßSƒ –	At the evening offering I arose from my <n>[time of]</n> humiliation <i>and</i> penitence and having torn my clothing and my robe, I fell on my knees and stretched out my hands to the LORD my God,/ßR‚W –	Then everyone who trembled at the words of the God of Israel because of the unfaithfulness of the exiles gathered to me as I sat appalled until the evening offering.:ßQ‚m –	When I heard this, I tore my clothing and my robe <n>[in grief]</n>, I pulled out some of the hair from my head and my beard, and sat down appalled <n>[at the shame of it]</n>.‚EßP… –	For they have taken some of their daughters <i>as wives</i> for themselves and for their sons, so that the holy<f>[1]</f> race has<f>[2]</f> intermingled with the peoples of the lands. Indeed, the officials and chief men have been foremost in this unfaithful act <i>and</i> direct violation <n>[of God's will]</n>."‚IßO	…
 –	<pb/>When these things were completed, the officials came to me and said, "The people of Israel and the priests and Levites have not separated themselves from the peoples of the lands, but have committed the repulsive acts of the Canaanites, Hittites, Perizzites, Jebusites, Ammonites, Moabites, Egyptians, and Amorites.FßNƒ –$And they delivered the king's edicts to the king's satraps (lieutenants) and to the governors<f>[6]</f> west of the <n>[Euphrates]</n> River, and they supported the people and God's house.yßMƒk –#<pb/>Also the <n>[former]</n> exiles who had come from the captivity offered burnt offerings to the God of Israel: 12 bulls for all Israel, 96 rams, 77 lambs, and 12 male goats for a sin offering. All this was a burnt offering to the LORD.\ßL1 –"Every piece was counted and weighed, and all the weight was recorded at that time.‚,ßK„Q –!On the fourth day the silver and the gold and the utensils were weighed out in the house of our God into the hand of Meremoth the son of Uriah the priest, and with him was Eleazar the son of Phinehas; and with them were the Levitesâ€”Jozabad the son of Jeshua and Noadiah the son of Binnui.DßJ – So we came to Jerusalem and remained there for three days.pßIƒY –<pb/>We set out from the river Ahava on the twelfth <n>[day]</n> of the first month to go to Jerusalem; and the hand of our God was upon us, and He rescued us from the hand of the enemy and those who lay in ambushes along the way.ßH‚) –So the priests and the Levites received the weighed out silver and gold, and the utensils, to bring them to Jerusalem to the house of our God.RßGƒ –Guard and keep them until you weigh them before the leading priests and the Levites and the leaders of the fathers' <i>households</i> of Israel in Jerusalem, in the chambers of the house of the LORD."%ßF‚C –Then I said to them, "You are holy to the LORD, the utensils are holy, and the silver and the gold are a freewill offering to the LORD God of your fathers.}ßEs –also 20 bowls of gold <i>worth</i> 1,000 darics, and two utensils of fine<f>[5]</f> shiny bronze, precious as gold.ßD} –I weighed into their hands 650 talents of silver, and silver utensils <i>worth</i> 100 talents, and 100 talents of gold;QßCƒ –and I weighed out to them the silver, the gold, and the utensils, the offering for the house of our God which the king, his advisers, his officials, and all Israel who were present there had offered.tßBa –<pb/>Then I set apart twelve leading priests, Sherebiah, Hashabiah, and ten of their brothers (relatives),tßAa –So we fasted and sought <n>[help from]</n> our God concerning this <n>[matter]</n>, and He heard our plea.‚(ß@„I –For I was ashamed to request troops and horsemen from the king to protect us from the enemy along the way, because we had told the king, "The hand of our God is favorable toward all those who seek Him, but His power and His anger are against all those who abandon (turn away from) Him."Fß?ƒ –Then I proclaimed a fast there at the river Ahava, so that we might humble ourselves before our God to seek from Him a safe journey for us, our<f>[4]</f> children, and all our possessions.5ß>‚c –also 220 of the temple servants, whom David and the leaders had set apart <n>[with their descendants]</n> for the service of the Levites. They were all designated by name.{ß=o –and Hashabiah, and with him Jeshaiah of the sons of Merari, with his brothers (relatives) and their sons, 20 men;oß<ƒW –And as the good hand of our God was upon us, they brought us a man of understanding (insight) from the sons of Mahli, the son of Levi, the son of Israel, <i>named</i> Sherebiah, with his sons and his brothers (relatives), 18 men;rß;ƒ] –And I sent them to Iddo, the leading man at the place Casiphia, telling them what to say to Iddo and his brothers, the temple servants at the place Casiphia, <i>that is</i>, to bring us servants (ministers) for the house of our God.Lß:ƒ –So I sent for Eliezer, Ariel, Shemaiah, Elnathan, Jarib, Elnathan, Nathan, Zechariah, and Meshullam, <n>[who were]</n> leading men, and also for Joiarib and Elnathan, <n>[who were]</n> teachers.4ß9‚a –Now I gathered them together at the river that runs to Ahava, where we camped for three days. I observed the people and the priests, and I did not find any Levites there.Mß8 –and of the sons of Bigvai, Uthai and<f>[3]</f> Zabbud, with 70 men.{ß7o –
