<pb/>On that day they read aloud from the book of Moses so that the people could hear <n>[its words]</n>, and in it was found written that<f>[1]</f> no Ammonite or Moabite could ever enter the assembly of God,‚<ã „q  /So in the days of Zerubbabel and <n>[later of]</n> Nehemiah, all Israel would give the daily portions for the singers and the gatekeepers; and they set apart the consecrated <i>portion</i> for the Levites, and the Levites set apart the consecrated <i>portion</i> for the sons of Aaron <n>[the priests]</n>.â‚  .For in the days of David and Asaph, in ancient times, there were leaders of singers, songs of praise and hymns of thanksgiving to God.&â~‚E  -And they performed the worship of their God and the service of purification; so did the singers and gatekeepers, as David and his son Solomon had commanded.‚4â}„a  ,<pb/>On that day men were appointed over the chambers for the stores, the contributions, the first fruits, and the tithes, to gather into them from the fields of the cities the portions required by the law for the priests and the Levites; for Judah rejoiced over the priests and Levites who served.Gâ|ƒ  +Also on that day they offered great sacrifices and rejoiced because God had given them great joy; the women and children also rejoiced, so that the joy of Jerusalem was heard from far away.â{‚  *and Maaseiah, Shemaiah, Eleazar, Uzzi, Jehohanan, Malchijah, Elam, and Ezer. And the singers sang, with Jezrahiah as their leader.pâzY  )and the priests Eliakim, Maaseiah, Miniamin, Micaiah, Elioenai, Zechariah and Hananiah, with trumpets;eâyC  (Then the two choirs stood in the house of God. So did I, and half of the officials with me;Jâxƒ
