But he said to her, "You speak as one of the <n>[spiritually]</n> foolish women speaks <n>[ignorant and oblivious to God's will]</n>. Shall we indeed accept <n>[only]</n> good from God and not <n>[also]</n> accept adversity <i>and</i> disaster?" In <n>[spite of]</n> all this Job did not sin with <n>[words from]</n> his lips."äe‚= Ü	<pb/>Then his wife said to him, "Do you still cling to your integrity <n>[and your faith and trust in God, without blaming Him]</n>? Curse God and die!"äd‚	 ÜAnd Job took a piece of broken pottery with which to scrape himself, and he sat <n>[down]</n> among the ashes (rubbish heaps).Bäc‚} Ü<pb/>So Satan departed from the presence of the LORD and struck Job with <i>loathsome</i> boils <i>and</i> agonizingly painful sores from the sole of his foot to the crown of his head.Wäb' ÜSo the LORD said to Satan, "Behold, he is in your hand, only spare his life."äa‚ ÜBut put forth Your hand now, and touch his bone and his flesh <n>[and severely afflict him]</n>; and he will curse You to Your face."kä`O ÜSatan answered the LORD, "<f>[1]</f> Skin for skin! Yes, a man will give all he has for his life.ƒ%ä_†C ÜThe LORD said to Satan, "Have you considered <i>and</i> reflected on My servant Job? For there is none like him on the earth, a blameless and upright man, one who fears God <n>[with reverence]</n> and abstains from <i>and</i> turns away from evil <n>[because he honors God]</n>. And still he maintains <i>and</i> holds tightly to his integrity, although you incited Me against him to destroy him without cause."ä^‚3 ÜThe LORD said to Satan, "From where have you come?" Then Satan answered the LORD, "From roaming around on the earth and from walking around on it."Eä]	ƒ Ü<pb/>Again there was a day when the sons of God (angels) came to present themselves before the LORD, and Satan (adversary, accuser) also came among them to present himself before the LORD.Dä\	 Ü<pb/>Through all this Jo