<t>They have closed their<f>[2]</f> unfeeling <i>heart</i> <n>[to kindness and compassion]</n>; </t><t>With their mouths they speak proudly <i>and</i> make presumptuous claims.</t><br/>~î!u æ	<t>From the wicked who despoil <i>and</i> deal violently with me, </t><t>My deadly enemies who surround me.</t><br/>/î ‚W æ<t>Keep me <n>[in Your affectionate care, protect me]</n> as the<f>[1]</f> apple of Your eye; </t><t>Hide me in the <n>[protective]</n> shadow of Your wings</t><br/>Hîƒ	 æ<t>Wondrously show Your <n>[marvelous and amazing]</n> lovingkindness, </t><t>O Savior of those who take refuge at Your right hand </t><t>From those who rise up <i>against them</i>.</t><br/>î{ æ<pb/><t>I have called upon You, for You, O God, will answer me; </t><t>Incline Your ear to me, hear my speech.</t><br/>]î3 æ<t>My steps have held closely to Your paths; </t><t>My feet have not staggered.</t>î} æ<t>Concerning the deeds of men, by the word of Your lips </t><t>I have kept away from the paths of the violent.</t><br/>Nîƒ æ<t>You have tried my heart; </t><t>You have visited me in the night; </t><t>You have tested me and You find nothing <n>[evil in me]</n>; </t><t>I intend that my mouth will not transgress.</t><br/>î‚- æ<t>Let my verdict of vindication come from Your presence; </t><t>May Your eyes look with equity <i>and</i> behold things that are just.</t><br/>?î	‚y æ<pb/>A Prayer of David. <pb/><t>Hear the just (righteous) cause, O LORD; listen to my loud <n>[piercing]</n> cry; </t><t>Listen to my prayer, that comes from guileless lips.</t><br/>î‚- æ<t>You will show me the path of life; </t><t>In Your presence is fullness of joy; </t><t>In Your right hand there are pleasures forevermore.</t>î‚7 æ
<t>For You will not abandon me to Sheol (the nether world, the place of the dead), </t><t>Nor will You allow Your Holy One to undergo decay.</t><br/> î‚9 æ	<t>Therefore my heart is glad and my glory <n>[my innermost self]</n> rejoices; </t><t>My body too will dwell <n>[confidently]</n> in safety,</t><br/>}îs æ<t>I have set the LORD continually before me; </t><t>Because He is at my right hand, I will not be shaken.</t><br/> îy æ<pb/><t>I will bless the LORD who has counseled me; </t><t>Indeed, my heart (mind) instructs me in the night.</t><br/>î‚' æ<t>The <n>[boundary]</n> lines <n>[of the land]</n> have fallen for me in pleasant places; </t><t>Indeed, my heritage is beautiful to me.</t>î} æ<pb/><t>The LORD is the portion of my inheritance, my cup <n>[He is all I need]</n>; </t><t>You support my lot.</t><br/>‚î„ æ<t>The sorrows <n>[pain and suffering]</n> of those who have chosen another <i>god</i> will be multiplied <n>[because of their idolatry]</n>; </t><t>I will not pour out their drink offerings of blood, </t><t>Nor will I take their names upon my lips.</t>6î‚e æ<t>As for the saints (godly people) who are in the land, </t><t>They are the majestic <i>and</i> the noble <i>and</i> the excellent ones in whom is all my delight.</t><br/>_î7 æ<t>I said to the LORD, "You are my Lord; </t><t>I have no good besides You."</t><br/>Rî	ƒ æ<pb/>A<f>[1]</f> Mikhtam of David <n>[probably intended to record memorable thoughts]</n>. <pb/><t>Keep <i>and</i> protect me, O God, for in You I have placed my trust <i>and</i> found refuge.</t><br/>Gî
ƒ æ<t>He does not put out his money at interest <n>[to a fellow Israelite]</n>, </t><t>And does not take a bribe against the innocent. </t><t>He who does these things will never be shaken.</t>‚,î„Q æ<t>In his eyes an evil person is despised, </t><t>But he honors those who fear the LORD <n>[and obediently worship Him with awe-inspired reverence and submissive wonder]</n>. </t><t>He keeps his word even to his own disadvantage and does not change it <n>[for his own benefit]</n>;</t><br/>î‚ æ<t>He does not slander with his tongue, </t><t>Nor does evil to his neighbor, </t><t>Nor takes up a reproach against his friend;</t><br/>#î
