 æ!<t>Let all the earth fear <i>and</i> worship the LORD; </t><t>Let all the inhabitants of the world stand in awe of Him.</t><br/>zð&m æ!<t>He gathers the waters of the sea together as in a wineskin; </t><t>He puts the deeps in storehouses.</t><br/>ð%w æ!<pb/><t>By the word of the LORD were the heavens made, </t><t>And all their host by the breath of His mouth.</t><br/>pð$Y æ!<t>He loves righteousness and justice; </t><t>The earth is full of the lovingkindness of the LORD.</t>ið#K æ!<t>For the word of the LORD is right; </t><t>And all His work is done in faithfulness.</t><br/>ð"{ æ!<t>Sing to Him a new song; </t><t>Play skillfully <n>[on the strings]</n> with a loud <i>and</i> joyful sound.</t><br/>uð!c æ!<t>Give thanks to the LORD with the lyre; </t><t>Sing praises to Him with the harp of ten strings.</t><br/>Qð 	ƒ æ!<pb/><t>Rejoice in the LORD, you righteous ones; </t><t>Praise is becoming <i>and</i> appropriate for those who are upright <n>[in heartâ€”those with moral integrity and godly character]</n>.</t><br/>#ð‚? æ <t>Be glad in the LORD and rejoice, you righteous <n>[who actively seek right standing with Him]</n>; </t><t>Shout for joy, all you upright in heart.</t>2ð‚] æ 
<t>Many are the sorrows of the wicked, </t><t>But he who trusts in <i>and</i> relies on the LORD shall be surrounded with compassion <i>and</i> lovingkindness.</t><br/>Zðƒ- æ 	<t>Do not be like the horse or like the mule which have no understanding, </t><t>Whose trappings include bridle and rein to hold them in check, </t><t><i>Otherwise</i> they will not come near to you.</t><br/>(ð‚I æ <pb/><t>I will instruct you and teach you in the way you should go; </t><t>I will counsel you <n>[who are willing to learn]</n> with My eye upon you.</t><br/>ð‚) æ <t>You are my hiding place; You, LORD, protect me from trouble; </t><t>You surround me with songs <i>and</i> shouts of deliverance. Selah.</t>‚ð„/ æ <t>Therefore, let everyone who is godly pray to You <n>[for forgiveness]</n> in a time when You <n>[are near and]</n> may be found; </t><t>Surely when the great waters <n>[of trial and distressing times]</n> overflow they will not reach <n>[the spirit in]</n> him.</t><br/>[ðƒ/ æ <t>I acknowledged my sin to You, </t><t>And I did not hide my wickedness; </t><t>I said, "I will confess <n>[all]</n> my transgressions to the LORD"; </t><t>And You forgave the guilt of my sin. Selah.</t><br/>Hðƒ	 æ <t>For day and night Your hand <n>[of displeasure]</n> was heavy upon me; </t><t>My<f>[2]</f> energy (vitality, strength) was drained away as with the burning heat of summer. Selah.</t><br/>ð æ <pb/><t>When I kept silent <i>about my sin</i>, my body wasted away </t><t>Through my groaning all the day long.</t><br/>ðw æ <t>Blessed is the man to whom the LORD does not impute wickedness, </t><t>And in whose spirit there is no deceit.</t>‚ð	ƒ} æ <pb/><i>A Psalm</i> of David. A skillful<f>[1]</f> song, <i>or</i> a didactic <i>or</i> reflective poem. <pb/><t>Blessed <n>[fortunate, prosperous, favored by God]</n> is he whose transgression is forgiven, </t><t>And whose sin is covered.</t><br/> ðy æ<t>Be strong and let your hearts take courage, </t><t>All you who wait for <i>and</i> confidently expect the LORD.</t>eðƒC æ<pb/><t>O love the LORD, all you His godly ones! </t><t>The LORD preserves the faithful <n>[those with moral and spiritual integrity]</n> </t><t>And fully repays the <n>[self-righteousness of the]</n> arrogant.</t><br/>Sðƒ æ<t>As for me, I said in my alarm, </t><t>"I am cut off from Your eyes." </t><t>Nevertheless You heard the voice of my supplications (specific requests) </t><t>When I cried to You <n>[for help]</n>.</t>'ð‚G æ<t>Blessed be the LORD, </t><t>For He has shown His marvelous favor <i>and</i> lovingkindness to me <n>[when I was assailed]</n> in a besieged city.</t><br/>Iðƒ æ<t>In the secret place of Your presence You hide them from the plots <i>and</i> conspiracies of man; </t><t>You keep them secretly in a shelter (pavilion) from the strife of tongues.</t><br/>mðƒS æ<pb/><t>How great is Your goodness, </t><t>Which You have stored up for those who <n>[reverently]</n> fear You, </t><t>Which You have prepared for those who take refuge in You, </t><t><f>[3]</f> Before the sons of man!</t><br/>,ð‚Q æ<t>Let the lying lips be mute, </t><t>Which speak insolently <i>and</i> arrogantly against the <n>[consistently]</n> righteous </t><t>With pride and contempt.</t>Dð
