<pb/>Blessed be the LORD, the God of Israel, </t><t>From everlasting to everlasting <n>[from this age to the next, and forever]</n>. </t><t>Amen and Amen (so be it).jñ[M æ)<t>As for me, You uphold me in my integrity, </t><t>And You set me in Your presence forever.</t>ñZ‚	 æ)<t>By this I know that You favor <i>and</i> delight in me, </t><t>Because my enemy does not shout in triumph over me.</t><br/>ñY‚ æ)
