 æ)<t>And when one comes to see me, he speaks empty words, </t><t>While his heart gathers malicious gossip <n>[against me]</n>; </t><t>When he goes away, he tells it <n>[everywhere]</n>.</t><br/>pñTY æ)<t>My enemies speak evil of me, <i>saying</i>, </t><t>"When will he die and his name perish?"</t><br/>~ñSu æ)<pb/><t>As for me, I said, "O LORD, be gracious to me; </t><t>Heal my soul, for I have sinned against You."</t><br/>ñR‚ æ)<t>The LORD will sustain <i>and</i> strengthen him on his sickbed; </t><t>In his illness, You will restore him to health.</t>3ñQ‚_ æ)<t>The LORD will protect him and keep him alive; </t><t>And he will be called blessed in the land; </t><t>You do not hand him over to the desire of his enemies.</t><br/>MñP	ƒ æ)<pb/>To the Chief Musician. A Psalm of David. <pb/><t>Blessed <n>[by God's grace and compassion]</n> is he who considers the helpless; </t><t>The LORD will save him in the day of trouble.</t><br/>=ñO‚s æ(<t>Even though I am afflicted and needy, </t><t>Still the Lord takes thought <i>and</i> is mindful of me. </t><t>You are my help and my rescuer. </t><t>O my God, do not delay.</t> ñN‚9 æ(<t>Let all who seek You rejoice and be glad in You; </t><t>Let those who love Your salvation say continually, </t><t>"The LORD be magnified!"</t><br/>ñM‚1 æ(<t>Let those be appalled <i>and</i> desolate because of their shame </t><t>Who say to me, "Aha, aha <n>[rejoicing in my misfortune]</n>!"</t><br/>JñLƒ
