rverse man spreads strife, </t><t>And one who gossips separates intimate friends.</t><br/>ƒd} ð<t>A worthless man devises <i>and</i> digs up evil, </t><t>And the words on his lips are like a scorching fire.</t><br/>aƒc; ð<t>The appetite of a worker works for him, </t><t>For his hunger urges him on.</t><br/>ƒb‚ ð<t>There is a way which seems right to a man <i>and</i> appears straight before him, </t><t>But its end is the way of death.</t><br/>ƒa} ð<t>Pleasant words are like a honeycomb, </t><t>Sweet <i>and</i> delightful to the soul and healing to the body.</t><br/>~ƒ`u ð<t>The heart of the wise instructs his mouth <n>[in wisdom]</n> </t><t>And adds persuasiveness to his lips.</t><br/>Uƒ_ƒ# ð<t>Understanding (spiritual insight) is a <n>[refreshing and boundless]</n> wellspring of life to those who have it, </t><t>But to give instruction <i>and</i> correction to fools is foolishness.</t><br/>1ƒ^‚[ ð<t>The wise in heart will be called understanding, </t><t>And sweet speech increases persuasiveness <i>and</i> learning <n>[in both speaker and listener]</n>.</t><br/>@ƒ]‚y ð<t>He who pays attention to the word <n>[of God]</n> will find good, </t><t>And blessed (happy, prosperous, to be admired) is he who trusts <n>[confidently]</n> in the LORD.</t><br/>ƒ\‚ ð<t>It is better to be humble in spirit with the lowly </t><t>Than to divide the spoil with the proud (haughty, arrogant).</t><br/>_ƒ[7 ð<t>Pride goes before destruction, </t><t>And a haughty spirit before a fall.</t><br/>ƒZ‚ ð<t>The highway of the upright turns away <i>and</i> departs from evil; </t><t>He who guards his way protects his life (soul).</t><br/>ƒY} ð<t>How much better it is to get wisdom than gold! </t><t>And to get understanding is to be chosen above silver.</t><br/>}ƒXs ð<t>In the light of the king's face is life, </t><t>And his favor is like a cloud bringing the spring rain.</t><br/>nƒW