<t>Righteous lips are the delight of kings, </t><t>And he who speaks right is loved.</t><br/>*ƒU‚M ð<t>It is repulsive <n>[to God and man]</n> for kings to behave wickedly, </t><t>For a throne is established on righteousness (right standing with God).</t><br/>8ƒT‚i ð<t>A just balance and <n>[honest]</n> scales are the <e>Lord's</e>; </t><t>All the weights of the bag are His concern <n>[established by His eternal principles]</n>.</t><br/>@ƒS‚y ð
<t>A divine decision <n>[given by God]</n> is on the lips of the king <n>[as His representative]</n>; </t><t>His mouth should not be unfaithful <i>or</i> unjust in judgment.</t><br/>ƒR‚+ ð	<t>A man's mind plans his way <n>[as he journeys through life]</n>, </t><t>But the LORD directs his steps <i>and</i> establishes them.</t><br/>tƒQa ð<t>Better is a little with righteousness </t><t>Than great income <n>[gained]</n> with injustice.</t><br/>rƒP] ð<t>When a man's ways please the LORD, </t><t>He makes even his enemies to be at peace with him.</t><br/>=ƒO‚s ð<t>By mercy <i>and</i> lovingkindness and truth <n>[not superficial ritual]</n> wickedness is cleansed from the heart, </t><t>And by the fear of the LORD one avoids evil.</t><br/>1ƒN‚[ ð<t>Everyone who is proud <i>and</i> arrogant in heart is disgusting <i>and</i> exceedingly offensive to the LORD; </t><t>Be assured he will not go unpunished.</t><br/>ƒM‚! ð<t>The LORD has made everything for its own purpose, </t><t>Even the wicked <n>[according to their role]</n> for the day of evil.</t><br/>:ƒL‚m ð<t><f>[1]</f> Commit your works to the LORD <n>[submit and trust them to Him]</n>, </t><t>And your plans will succeed <n>[if you respond to His will and guidance]</n>.</t><br/>‚
ƒK„
 ð<t>All the ways of a man are clean <i>and</i> innocent in his own eyes <n>[and he may see nothing wrong with his actions]</n>, </t><t>But the LORD weighs <i>and</i> examines the motives <i>and</i> intents <n>[of the heart and knows the truth]</n>.</t><br/>ƒJ	‚/ ð<pb/><t>The plans <i>and</i> reflections of the heart belong to man, </t><t>But the <n>[wise]</n> answer of the tongue is from the LORD.</t><br/>nƒIƒU ð!<t>The <n>[reverent]</n> fear of the LORD <n>[that is, worshiping Him and regarding Him as truly awesome]</n> is the instruction for wisdom <n>[its starting point and its essence]</n>; </t><t>And before honor comes humility.</t>FƒHƒ ð <t>He who neglects <i>and</i> ignores instruction <i>and</i> discipline despises himself, </t><t>But he who learns from rebuke acquires understanding <n>[and grows in wisdom]</n>.</t><br/>ƒG‚ ð<t>The ear that listens to <i>and</i> learns from the life-giving rebuke (reprimand, censure) </t><t>Will remain among the wise.</t><br/>vƒFe ð<t>The light of the eyes rejoices the hearts of others, </t><t>And good news puts fat on the bones.</t><br/>iƒEƒK ð<t>The LORD is far from the wicked <n>[and distances Himself from them]</n>, </t><t>But He hears the prayer of the <n>[consistently]</n> righteous <n>[that is, those with spiritual integrity and moral courage]</n>.</t><br/>ZƒDƒ- ð<t>The heart of the righteous thinks carefully about how to answer <n>[in a wise and appropriate and timely way]</n>, </t><t>But the <n>[babbling]</n> mouth of the wicked pours out malevolent things.</t><br/>'ƒC‚G ð<t>He who profits unlawfully brings suffering to his own house, </t><t>But he who hates bribes <n>[and does not receive nor pay them]</n> will live.</t><br/>*ƒB‚M ð<t>Evil plans <i>and</i> thoughts of the wicked are exceedingly vile <i>and</i> offensive to the LORD, </t><t>But pure words are pleasant words to Him.</t><br/>[ƒAƒ/ ð<t>The LORD will tear down the house of the proud <i>and</i> arrogant (self-righteous), </t><t>But He will establish <i>and</i> protect the boundaries <n>[of the land]</n> of the <n>[godly]</n> widow.</t><br/>*ƒ@‚M ð<t>The <n>[chosen]</n> path of life leads upward for the wise, </t><t>That he may keep away from Sheol (the nether world, the place of the dead) below.</t><br/>%ƒ?‚C ð<t>A man has joy in giving an appropriate answer, </t><t>And how good <i>and</i> delightful is a word spoken at the right momentâ€”how good it is!</t><br/>ƒ>‚- ð<t>Without consultation <i>and</i> wise advice, plans are frustrated, </t><t>But with many counselors they are established and succeed.</t><br/>Pƒ=ƒ ð<t>Foolishness is joy to him who is without heart <i>and</i> lacks <n>[intelligent, common]</n> sense, </t><t>But a man of understanding walks uprightly <n>[making his course straight]</n>.</t><br/>cƒ<? ð<t>A wise son makes a father glad, </t><t>But a foolish man despises his mother.</t><br/>Rƒ;ƒ ð<t>The way of the lazy is like a hedge of thorns <n>[it pricks, lacerates, and entangles him]</n>, </t><t>But the way <n>[of life]</n> of the upright is smooth <i>and</i> open like a highway.</t><br/>ƒ:w ð<t>A hot-tempered man stirs up strife, </t><t>But he who is slow to anger <i>and</i> patient calms disputes.</t><br/>ƒ9‚ ð<t>Better is a dinner of vegetables <i>and</i> herbs where love is present </t><t>Than a fattened ox served with hatred.</t><br/>ƒ8‚ ð<t>Better is a little with the <n>[reverent, worshipful]</n> fear of the LORD </t><t>Than great treasure and trouble with it.</t><br/>ƒ7‚! ð<t>All the days of the afflicted are bad, </t><t>But a glad heart has a continual feast <n>[regardless of the circumstances]</n>.</t><br/>Fƒ6ƒ ð<t>The mind of the intelligent <i>and</i> discerning seeks knowledge <i>and</i> eagerly inquires after it, </t><t>But the mouth of the <n>[stubborn]</n> fool feeds on foolishness.</t><br/>ƒ5‚% ð
<t>A heart full of joy <i>and</i> goodness makes a cheerful face, </t><t>But when a heart is full of sadness the spirit is crushed.</t><br/>=ƒ4‚s ð<t>A scoffer <n>[unlike a wise man]</n> resents one who rebukes him <i>and</i> tries to teach him; </t><t>Nor will he go to the wise <n>[for counsel and instruction]</n>.</t><br/>rƒ3ƒ] ð<t>Sheol (the nether world, the place of the dead) and Abaddon (the abyss, the place of eternal punishment) <i>lie open</i> before the LORDâ€” </t><t>How much more the hearts <i>and</i> inner motives of the children of men.</t><br/>!ƒ2‚; ð
<t>There is severe discipline for him who<f>[1]</f> turns from the way <n>[of righteousness]</n>; </t><t>And he who hates correction will die.</t><br/>kƒ1ƒO ð	<t>The way <n>[of life]</n> of the wicked is hateful <i>and</i> exceedingly offensive to the LORD, </t><t>But He loves one who pursues righteousness <n>[personal integrity, moral courage and honorable character]</n>.</t><br/>ƒ0‚7 ð<t>The sacrifice of the wicked is hateful <i>and</i> exceedingly offensive to the LORD, </t><t>But the prayer of the upright is His delight!</t><br/>)ƒ/‚K ð<t>The lips of the wise spread knowledge <n>[sifting it as chaff from the grain]</n>; </t><t>But the hearts of <n>[shortsighted]</n> fools are not so.</t><br/>‚
ƒ.„
 ð<t>Great <i>and</i> priceless treasure is in the house of the <n>[consistently]</n> righteous one <n>[who seeks godly instruction and grows in wisdom]</n>, </t><t>But trouble is in the income of the wicked one <n>[who rejects the laws of God]</n>.</t><br/>eƒ-ƒC ð<t>A <n>[flippant, arrogant]</n> fool rejects his father's instruction <i>and</i> correction, </t><t>But he who <n>[is willing to learn and]</n> regards <i>and</i> keeps in mind a reprimand acquires good sense.</t><br/>Tƒ,ƒ! ð<t>A soothing tongue <n>[speaking words that build up and encourage]</n> is a tree of life, </t><t>But a perversive tongue <n>[speaking words that overwhelm and depress]</n> crushes the spirit.</t><br/>ƒ+‚ ð<t>The eyes of the LORD are in every place, </t><t>Watching the evil and the good <n>[in all their endeavors]</n>.</t><br/>#ƒ*‚? ð<t>The tongue of the wise speaks knowledge that is pleasing <i>and</i> acceptable, </t><t>But the <n>[babbling]</n> mouth of fools spouts folly.</t><br/>.ƒ)	‚W ð<pb/><t>A soft <i>and</i> gentle <i>and</i> thoughtful answer turns away wrath, </t><t>But harsh <i>and</i> painful <i>and</i> careless words stir up anger.</t><br/><ƒ(‚q ð#<t>The king's favor <i>and</i> good will are toward a servant who acts wisely <i>and</i> discreetly, </t><t>But his anger <i>and</i> wrath are toward him who acts shamefully.</t>ƒ'‚5 ð"<t>Righteousness <n>[moral and spiritual integrity and virtuous character]</n> exalts a nation, </t><t>But sin is a disgrace to any people.</t><br/>-ƒ&‚S ð!<t>Wisdom rests <n>[silently]</n> in the heart of one who has understanding, </t><t>But what is in the heart of <n>[shortsighted]</n> fools is made known.</t><br/>3ƒ%‚_ ð <t>The wicked is overthrown through his wrongdoing, </t><t>But the righteous has hope <i>and</i> confidence <i>and</i> a refuge <n>[with God]</n> even in death.</t><br/>/ƒ$‚W ð<t>He who oppresses the poor taunts <i>and</i> insults his Maker, </t><t>But he who is kind <i>and</i> merciful <i>and</i> gracious to the needy honors Him.</t><br/>6ƒ#‚e ð<t>A calm <i>and</i> peaceful <i>and</i> tranquil heart is life <i>and</i> health to the body, </t><t>But passion <i>and</i> envy are like rottenness to the bones.</t><br/>Xƒ"ƒ) ð<t>He who is slow to anger has great understanding <n>[and profits from his self-control]</n>, </t><t>But he who is quick-tempered exposes <i>and</i> exalts his foolishness <n>[for all to see]</n>.</t><br/>	ƒ!‚ ð<t>In a multitude of people is a king's glory, </t><t>But in a lack of people is a <n>[pretentious]</n> prince's ruin.</t><br/>2ƒ ‚] ð<t>The <n>[reverent]</n> fear of the LORD <n>[that leads to obedience and worship]</n> is a fountain of life, </t><t>So that one may avoid the snares of death.</t><br/> ƒ‚9 ð<t>In the <n>[reverent]</n> fear of the LORD there is strong confidence, </t><t>And His children will <n>[always]</n> have a place of refuge.</t><br/>cƒ? ð<t>A truthful witness saves lives, </t><t>But he who speaks lies is treacherous.</t><br/>)ƒ‚K ð<t>The crown of the wise is their wealth <n>[of wisdom]</n>, </t><t>But the foolishness of <n>[closed-minded]</n> fools is <n>[nothing but]</n> folly.</t><br/>_ƒ7 ð<t>In all labor there is profit, </t><t>But mere talk leads only to poverty.</t><br/>,ƒ‚Q ð<t>Do they not go astray who devise evil <i>and</i> wander from the way of righteousness? </t><t>But kindness and truth will be to those who devise good.</t><br/>Lƒƒ ð<t>He who despises his neighbor sins <n>[against God and his fellow man]</n>, </t><t>But happy <n>[blessed and favored by God]</n> is he who is gracious <i>and</i> merciful to the poor.</t><br/>nƒU ð<t>The poor man is hated even by his neighbor, </t><t>But those who love the rich are many.</t><br/>	ƒ‚ ð<t>The evil will bow down before the good, </t><t>And the wicked <n>[will bow down]</n> at the gates of the righteous.</t><br/>Iƒƒ ð<t>The naive <n>[are unsophisticated and easy to exploit and]</n> inherit foolishness, </t><t>But the sensible <n>[are thoughtful and far-sighted and]</n> are crowned with knowledge.</t><br/>ƒ‚ ð<t>A quick-tempered man acts foolishly <i>and</i> without self-control, </t><t>And a man of wicked schemes is hated.</t><br/>zƒm ð<t>A wise man suspects danger and cautiously avoids evil, </t><t>But the fool is arrogant and careless.</t><br/>[ƒƒ/ ð<t>The naive <i>or</i> inexperienced person <n>[is easily misled and]</n> believes every word he hears, </t><t>But the prudent man <n>[is discreet and astute and]</n> considers well where he is going.</t><br/>xƒƒi ð<t>The backslider in heart will have his fill with his own <n>[rotten]</n> ways, </t><t>But a good man will <i>be satisfied</i> with his ways <n>[the godly thought and action which his heart pursues and in which he delights]</n>.</t><br/>hƒI ð
