e is a deep pit, </t><t>And an immoral woman is a narrow well.</t><br/>b…/= ð<pb/><t>My son, give me your heart </t><t>And let your eyes delight in my ways,</t><br/>….‚ ð<t>Let your father and your mother be glad, </t><t>And let her who gave birth to you rejoice <n>[in your wise and godly choices]</n>.</t>…-‚ ð<pb/><t>The father of the righteous will greatly rejoice, </t><t>And he who sires a wise child will have joy in him.</t><br/>o…,W ð<t><f>[3]</f> Buy truth, and do not sell it; </t><t>Get wisdom and instruction and understanding.</t>w…+g ð<pb/><t>Listen to your father, who sired you, </t><t>And do not despise your mother when she is old.</t><br/>…*‚1 ð<t>For the heavy drinker and the glutton will come to poverty, </t><t>And the drowsiness <n>[of overindulgence]</n> will clothe one with rags.</t>t…)a ð<t>Do not associate with heavy drinkers of wine, </t><t><i>Or</i> with gluttonous eaters of meat,</t><br/>p…(Y ð<t>Listen, my son, and be wise, </t><t>And direct your heart in the way <n>[of the LORD]</n>.</t><br/>…'‚ ð<t>Surely there is a future <n>[and a reward]</n>, </t><t>And your hope <i>and</i> expectation will not be cut off.</t><br/>c…&ƒ? ð<pb/><t>Do not let your heart envy sinners <n>[who live godless lives and have no hope of salvation]</n>, </t><t>But <n>[continue to]</n> live in the <n>[reverent, worshipful]</n> fear of the LORD day by day.</t><br/>U…%# ð<t>Yes, my heart will rejoice </t><t>When your lips speak right things.</t>\…$1 ð<pb/><t>My son, if your heart is wise, </t><t>My heart will also be glad;</t><br/>…#‚1 ð<t>You shall<f>[2]</f> swat him with the <i>reed-like</i> rod </t><t>And rescue his life from Sheol (the nether world, the place of the dead).</t>7…"‚g ð
<pb/><t>Do not withhold discipline from the child; </t><t>If you<f>[1]</f> swat him with a <i>reed-like</i> rod <n>[applied with godly wisdom]</n>, he will not die.</t><br/>[…!/ ð<t>Apply your heart to discipline </t><t>And your ears to words of knowledge.</t>r… ] ð<t>For their Redeemer is strong <i>and</i> mighty; </t><t>He will plead their case against you.</t><br/><…‚q ð
<pb/><t>Do not move the ancient landmark <n>[at the boundary of the property]</n> </t><t>And do not go into the fields of the fatherless <n>[to take what is theirs]</n>,</t><br/>}…s ð	<pb/><t>Do not speak in the ears of a fool, </t><t>For he will despise the <n>[godly]</n> wisdom of your words.</t>o…W ð<t>The morsel which you have eaten you will vomit up, </t><t>And you will waste your compliments.</t>^…ƒ5 ð<t>For as he thinks in his heart, so is he <n>[in behaviorâ€”one who manipulates]</n>. </t><t>He says to you, "Eat and drink," </t><t>Yet his heart is not with you <n>[but it is begrudging the cost]</n>.</t><br/>b…= ð<pb/><t>Do not eat the bread of a selfish man, </t><t>Or desire his delicacies;</t><br/>6…‚e ð<t>When you set your eyes on wealth, it is <n>[suddenly]</n> gone. </t><t>For <i>wealth</i> certainly makes itself wings </t><t>Like an eagle that flies to the heavens.</t>…‚% ð<pb/><t>Do not weary yourself <n>[with the overwhelming desire]</n> to gain wealth; </t><t>Cease from your own understanding of it.</t><br/>…{ ð<t>Do not desire his delicacies, </t><t>For it is deceptive food <n>[offered to you with questionable motives]</n>.</t>o…W ð<t>For you will put a knife to your throat </t><t>If you are a man of <i>great</i> appetite.</t><br/>|…	s ð<pb/><t>When you sit down to dine with a ruler, </t><t>Consider carefully what is <n>[set]</n> before you;</t><br/>.…‚U ð<pb/>Do you see a man skillful <i>and</i> experienced in his work? </t><t>He will stand <n>[in honor]</n> before kings; </t><t>He will not stand before obscure men.… ð<pb/><t>Do not move the ancient landmark <n>[at the boundary of the property]</n> </t><t>Which your fathers have set.</t>…‚3 ð<t>If you have nothing with which to pay <n>[another's debt when he defaults]</n>, </t><t>Why should his creditor take your bed from under you?</t>:…‚m ð<pb/><t>Do not be among those who give