ƒ# ð<t>For it will be pleasant if you keep them in mind <n>[incorporating them as guiding principles]</n>; </t><t>Let them be ready on your lips <n>[to guide and strengthen yourself and others]</n>.</t><br/>…	{ ð<pb/><t>Listen carefully and hear the<f>[1]</f> words of the wise, </t><t>And apply your mind to my knowledge;</t><br/>6…‚e ð<t>He who oppresses <i>or</i> exploits the poor to get more for himself </t><t>Or who gives to the rich <n>[to gain influence and favor]</n>, will only come to poverty.</t>F…ƒ ð<t>Foolishness is bound up in the heart of a child; </t><t>The rod of discipline <n>[correction administered with godly wisdom and lovingkindness]</n> will remove it far from him.</t><br/>>…‚u ð<t>The mouth of an immoral woman is a deep pit <n>[deep and inescapable]</n>; </t><t>He who is cursed by the LORD <n>[because of his adulterous sin]</n> will fall into it.</t><br/>*…‚M ð
