<pb/><i>(The Shulammite Bride)</i> <t>"My beloved is exquisitely handsome and ruddy, </t><t>Outstanding among ten thousand.</t><br/>m‰HƒS	<pb/><i>(The Chorus)</i> <t>"What is your beloved more than another beloved, </t><t>O most beautiful among women? </t><t>What is your beloved more than another beloved, </t><t>That you should so command us to take an oath?"</t>a‰Gƒ;<t>"I command that you take an oath, O daughters of Jerusalem, </t><t>If you find my beloved, </t><t>As to what you tell himâ€” </t><t><n>[Say that]</n> I am sick from love <n>[sick from being without him]</n>."</t>.‰F‚U<t>"The watchmen who make the rounds in the city found me. </t><t>They struck me, they wounded me; </t><t>The guardsmen of the walls took my shawl from me.</t><br/>}‰Eƒs<t>"I opened for my beloved, </t><t>But my beloved had turned away and was gone. </t><t>My heart went out <i>to him</i> when he spoke. </t><t>I searched for him, but I could not find him; </t><t>I called him, but he did not answer me.</t><br/>A‰D‚{<t>"I arose to open for my beloved; </t><t>And my hands dripped with myrrh, </t><t>And my fingers with liquid <n>[sweet-scented]</n> myrrh, </t><t>On the handles of the bolt.</t><br/>
