"<t><n>[Say to the ruler]</n> "Give us advice, make a decision <n>[for Moab, king of Judah]</n>; </t><t>Cast your shadow <n>[over us]</n> like night in the midst of noon; </t><t>Hide the outcasts, do not betray the fugitive <n>[to his pursuer]</n>.</t><br/>Œ4‚#"<t>For like wandering birds or scattered nestlings, </t><t>The daughters of Moab will be at the fords of the <n>[river]</n> Arnon.</t><br/>\Œ3	ƒ3"<pb/><t>Send lambs to the ruler of the land <n>[<f>[1]</f> you Moabites]</n>, </t><t>From Sela <n>[that is, Petra in Edom]</n> through the wilderness to the mountain of the Daughter of Zion (Jerusalem).</t><br/>CŒ2‚"	<t>For the waters of Dimon are full of blood; </t><t>Yet I will bring even more <i>woes</i> on Dimonâ€” </t><t>A lion upon those of Moab who escape and upon the remnant of the land.</t>)Œ1‚K"<t>For the cry of distress has echoed around the territory of Moab; </t><t>The wailing <i>goes</i> as far as Eglaim and the mournful cry to Beer-elim.</t><br/>Œ0‚"<t>Therefore the abundance <i>which</i> they have acquired and stored away </t><t>They carry off over the Brook of the Willows.</t><br/>Œ/‚%"<t>For the waters of Nimrim are desolate. </t><t>Indeed the grass is withered, the new growth dies; </t><t>There is no green thing.</t><br/>‚Œ.„"<t>My heart cries out for Moab; </t><t>His fugitives are <n>[fleeing]</n> as far as Zoar and Eglath-shelishiyah. </t><t>For they go up the ascent of Luhith weeping; </t><t>For on the road to Horonaim they raise a cry of distress over their destruction.</t><br/>WŒ-ƒ'"<t>Heshbon and Elealeh <n>[cities claimed by Moab]</n> cry out; </t><t>Their voice is heard as far as Jahaz. </t><t>Therefore the armed men of Moab cry out; </t><t>Moab's soul trembles within him.</t><br/>EŒ,ƒ"<t>In their streets they have wrapped themselves with sackcloth; </t><t>On their <n>[flat]</n> housetops and in their open squares </t><t>Everyone is wailing, dissolved in tears.</t><br/>_Œ+ƒ7"<t>They have gone up to the temple and to Dibon, to the high places to weep. </t><t>Moab wails over Nebo and over Medeba; </t><t>Everyone's head is shaved, and every beard is cut off <n>[in mourning]</n>.</t><br/>yŒ*	ƒm"<pb/><t>The <n>[mournful, inspired]</n> oracle (<f>[1]</f> a burden to be carried) concerning Moab: </t><br/><t>Because in a night Ar of Moab is devastated and ruined; </t><t>Because in a night Kir of Moab is devastated and ruined.</t><br/>YŒ)ƒ+" <t>"Then what answer will one give the messengers of the <n>[Philistine]</n> nation? </t><t>That the LORD has founded Zion, </t><t>And the afflicted of His people will seek <i>and</i> find refuge in it."</t>xŒ(ƒi"<t>"Howl, O gate; cry, O city! </t><t>Melt away, O Philistia, all of you; </t><t>For smoke comes out of the north, </t><t>And there is no straggler in his ranks <i>and</i> no one stands detached <n>[in Hezekiah's battalions]</n>.</t><br/>tŒ'ƒa"<t>"The firstborn of the helpless <n>[of Judah]</n> will feed <n>[on My meadows]</n>, </t><t>And the needy will lie down in safety; </t><t>But I will kill your root with famine, </t><t>And your survivors will be put to death.</t><br/>‚Œ&„"<pb/><t>"Do not rejoice, O Philistia, any of you, </t><t>Because the rod <n>[of Judah]</n> that struck you is broken; </t><t>For out of the serpent's root will come a viper <n>[King Hezekiah of Judah]</n>, </t><t>And its offspring will be a flying serpent.</t><br/>Œ%‚!"<t>In the year that King Ahaz <n>[of Judah]</n> died this <n>[mournful, inspired]</n> oracle (<f>[5]</f> a burden to be carried) came:</t>Œ$‚"For the LORD of hosts has decided <i>and</i> planned, and who can annul it? His hand is stretched out, and who can turn it back?"XŒ#ƒ)"This is the plan <n>[of God]</n> decided for the whole earth <n>[regarded as conquered and put under tribute by Assyria]</n>; and this is the hand <n>[of God]</n> that is stretched out 