ŽI‚"<t>For at the voice of the LORD the Assyrians will be terrified, </t><t><i>When</i> He strikes <n>[them]</n> with the rod.</t><br/>‚ŽH„1"<t>And the LORD will make His majestic voice heard, </t><t>And show the descending of His arm <n>[striking]</n> in <n>[His]</n> fierce anger, </t><t>And in the flame of a devouring fire, </t><t>In the crashing sound <i>of heavy rain</i>, cloudburst, and hailstones.</t><br/>~ŽGƒu"<t>You will have a song as in the night when a holy feast is kept, </t><t>And joy of heart as when one marches <n>[in procession]</n> with a flute, </t><t>To go to the <n>[temple on the]</n> mountain of the LORD, to the Rock of Israel.</t><br/>ŽFƒw"<t>His breath is like an overflowing river, </t><t>Which reaches to the neck, </t><t>To sift the nations back and forth in a sieve <n>[of disaster]</n>, </t><t>And <i>to put</i> in the jaws of the peoples the bridle which leads to ruin.</t><br/>zŽEƒm"<pb/><t>Now look, the<f>[6]</f> name of the LORD comes from far away, </t><t>Burning with His anger, and heavy with<f>[7]</f> smoke; </t><t>His lips are full of<f>[8]</f> indignation, </t><t>And His tongue is like a consuming fire.</t><br/>‚DŽD…"<t>The light of the full moon will be like the light of the sun, and the light of the sun will be seven times <i>brighter</i>, like the light of seven days <n>[concentrated in one]</n>, in the day the LORD binds up the fracture of His people and heals the wound He has inflicted <n>[because of their sins]</n>.</t>QŽCƒ"On every lofty mountain and on every high hill there will be streams of water on the day of the great slaughter (the day of the LORD), when the towers fall <n>[and all His enemies are destroyed]</n>.
ŽB‚"Also the oxen and the young donkeys that work the ground will eat salted fodder, which has been winnowed with shovel and pitchfork.{ŽAƒo"<pb/>Then He will give you rain for the seed with which you sow the ground, and bread <n>[grain]</n> from the produce of the ground, and it will be rich and plentiful. In that day your livestock will graze in large <i>and</i> roomy pastures.FŽ@ƒ"And you will defile your carved images overlaid with silver, and your cast images plated with gold. You will scatter them like a bloodstained <i>cloth</i>, and will say to them, "Be gone!"~Ž?u"Your ears will hear a word behind you, "This is the way, walk in it," whenever you turn to the right or to the left.>Ž>‚u"Though the Lord gives you the bread of adversity and the water of oppression, yet your Teacher will no longer hide Himself, but your eyes will <n>[constantly]</n> see your Teacher.PŽ=ƒ"<pb/><f>[5]</f> O people in Zion, inhabitant in Jerusalem, you will weep no longer. He will most certainly be gracious to you at the sound of your cry for help; when He hears it, He will answer you.‚DŽ<…"<t>Therefore the LORD waits <n>[expectantly]</n> <i>and</i> longs to be gracious to you, </t><t>And therefore He waits on high to have compassion on you. </t><t><f>[4]</f> For the LORD is a God of justice; </t><t>Blessed (happy, fortunate) are all those who long for Him <n>[since He will never fail them]</n>.</t>iŽ;ƒK"<t>A thousand <i>of you will flee</i> at the threat of one <i>man</i>; </t><t>You will flee at the threat of five, </t><t>Until you are left like a flag on the top of a mountain, </t><t>And like a signal on a hill.</t><br/>pŽ:ƒY"<t>And you said, "No! We will flee on horses!" </t><t>Therefore you will flee <n>[from your enemies]</n>! </t><t>And <n>[you said]</n>, "We will ride on swift horses!" </t><t>Therefore those who pursue you shall be swift.</t><br/>tŽ9ƒa"<pb/><t>For the Lord GOD, the Holy One of Israel has said this, </t><br/><t>"In returning <n>[to Me]</n> and rest you shall be saved, </t><t>In quietness and confident trust is your strength." </t><t>But you were not willing,</t><br/>‚Ž8„+"<t>"Whose collapse is like the smashing of a potter's jar, </t><t>Crushed so savagely </t><t>that there cannot be found among its pieces a potsherd <n>[large enough]</n> </t><t>To take <n>[coals of]</n> fire from a fireplace, </t><t>Or to scoop water from a cistern."</t>zŽ7ƒm"
<t>Therefore this wickedness <n>[this sin, this injustice, this wrongdoing]</n> will be to you </t><t>Like a crack <n>[in a wall]</n> about to fall, </t><t>A bulge in a high wall, </t><t>Whose collapse comes suddenly in an instant,</t><br/>mŽ6ƒS"<pb/><t>Therefore, the Holy One of Israel says this, </t><br/><t>"Because you have refused <i>and</i> rejected this word <n>[of Mine]</n> </t><t>And have put your trust in oppression and guile, and have relied on them,</t><br/>Ž5‚!"<t>"Get out of the <n>[true]</n> way, turn aside from the path <n>[of God]</n>, </t><t>Stop bothering us with the Holy One of Israel."</t>‚%Ž4„C"
<t>Who say to the seers, "You must not see <i>visions from God</i>"; </t><t>And to the prophets, "You must not prophesy to us what is right! </t><t>Speak to us pleasant things <i>and</i> smooth words, </t><t>Prophesy <n>[deceitful]</n> illusions <n>[that we will enjoy]</n>.</t><br/>Ž3‚+"	<t>For this is a rebellious people, lying sons, </t><t>Sons who refuse to listen to </t><t>The law <i>and</i> instruction of the LORD;</t><br/>JŽ2ƒ
"<t>Now, go, write it on a tablet before them </t><t>And inscribe it on a scroll, </t><t>So that it may serve in the time to come </t><t>As a witness <n>[against them]</n> forevermore.</t><br/>Ž1‚'"<t>For Egypt's help is worthless and good for nothing. </t><t>Therefore, I have called her </t><t>"Rahab Who Has Been Exterminated."</t><br/>ƒUŽ0‡#"<pb/><t>A <n>[mournful, inspired]</n> oracle (<f>[2]</f> a burden to be carried) concerning the beasts of the Negev (the South): </t><br/><t>Through a land of trouble and anguish, </t><t>From<f>[3]</f> where <i>come</i> lioness and lion, viper and <n>[fiery]</n> flying serpent, </t><t>They carry their riches on the shoulders of young donkeys </t><t>And their treasures on the humps of camels, </t><t>To a people (Egyptians) who cannot benefit them.</t><br/>*Ž/‚M"<t>"All will be ashamed because of a people (the Egyptians) who cannot benefit them, </t><t>Who are not a help or benefit, but a shame and also a disgrace."</t>pŽ.Y"<t>"For his princes are at Zoan </t><t>And his ambassadors arrive at Hanes <n>[in Egypt]</n>.</t><br/>3Ž-‚_"<t>"Therefore the safety <i>and</i> protection of Pharaoh will be your shame </t><t>And the refuge in the shadow of Egypt, your humiliation <i>and</i> disgrace.</t><br/>=Ž,‚s"<t>Who proceed down to Egypt </t><t>Without consulting<f>[1]</f> Me, </t><t>To take refuge in the stronghold of Pharaoh </t><t>And to take shelter in the shadow of Egypt!</t><br/>‚Ž+	„"<pb/><t>"Woe (judgment is coming) to the rebellious children," declares the LORD, </t><t>"Who carry out a plan, but not Mine, </t><t>And make an alliance <n>[by pouring out a libation]</n>, but not of My Spirit, </t><t>In order to add sin to sin;</t><br/>Ž*‚#"<t>"Those who err in mind will know the truth, </t><t>And those who criticize <i>and</i> murmur discontentedly will accept instruction.</t>wŽ)ƒg"<t>For when he sees his children, the work of My hands, in his midst, </t><t>They will sanctify My Name; </t><t>They will sanctify the Holy One of Jacob </t><t>And will stand in awe <i>and</i> reverent fear of the God of Israel.</t><br/>‚Ž(„5"<pb/><t>Therefore, the LORD, who redeemed Abraham <n>[from paganism]</n> says this, concerning the house of Jacob (Israel): </t><br/><t>"Jacob will not be ashamed, nor will his face turn pale <n>[with disappointment because of his children's degenerate behavior]</n>;</t><br/>fŽ'ƒE"<t>Those who cause a person to be condemned with a <n>[false]</n> word, </t><t>And lay a trap for him who upholds justice at the <n>[city]</n> gate, </t><t>And defraud the one in the right with meaningless arguments.</t>Ž&‚1"<t>For the tyrant will come to an end and the scorner will be finished, </t><t>Indeed all who are intent on doing evil will be cut offâ€”</t><br/>*Ž%‚M"<t>The afflicted also will increase their joy in the LORD, </t><t>And the needy of mankind will rejoice <i>and</i> celebrate in the Holy One of Israel.</t><br/>:Ž$‚m"<t>On that day the deaf will hear the words of a book, </t><t>And out of <i>their</i> gloom and darkness the eyes of the blind will see <n>[the words of the book]</n>.</t><br/>$Ž#‚A"<t>Is it not yet a very little while </t><t>Until Lebanon will be turned into a fertile field, </t><t>And the fertile field regarded as a forest?</t><br/>‚;Ž"„o"<t>You turn <i>things</i> upside down <n>[with your perversity]</n>! </t><t>Shall the potter be considered equal with the clay, </t><t>That the thing that is made would say to its maker, "He did not make me"; </t><t>Or the thing that is formed say to him who formed it, "He has no understanding"?</t><br/>aŽ!ƒ;"<pb/><t>Woe (judgment is coming) to those who <n>[try to]</n> deeply hide their plans from the LORD, </t><t>Whose deeds are <i>done</i> in a dark place, </t><t>And who say, "Who sees us?" or "Who knows us?"</t><br/>‚Ž „"<t>Therefore, listen carefully, I will again do marvelous <i>and</i> amazing things with this people, wonderful and astonishing things; </t><t>And the wisdom of their wise men will perish, </t><t>And the understanding of their discerning men will be hidden."</t>‚eŽ…C"
<pb/><t>Then the Lord said, </t><br/><t>"Because this nation approaches <n>[Me only]</n> with their words </t><t>And honors Me <n>[only]</n> with their lip service, </t><t>But they remove their hearts far from Me, </t><t>And their reverence for Me is a tradition that is learned <i>by rote</i> <n>[without any regard for its meaning]</n>,</t><br/> Žy"Then the book will be given to the one who cannot read, saying, "Read this, please." And he will say, "I cannot read."eŽƒC"<pb/>The entire vision <n>[of all these things]</n> will be to you like the words of a scroll that is sealed, which they give to one who can read, saying, "Read this, please," he shall say, "I cannot, for it is sealed."RŽƒ"
<t>For the LORD has poured over you a spirit of deep sleep. </t><t>He has closed your eyes, <n>[you who are]</n> the prophets; </t><t>And He has covered your heads, <n>[you who are]</n> the seers.</t>‚Ž„1"	<pb/><t>Stop <i>and</i> take some time and wonder <n>[at this prophecy]</n>, </t><t>Blind yourselves and be blinded <n>[at its fulfillment by your spiritual incompetence]</n>. </t><t>They are drunk, but not from wine; </t><t>They stagger, but not from strong drink.</t><br/>ƒŽ†"<t>It will be as when a hungry man dreams </t><t>That he is eating, </t><t>But when he awakens, his<f>[5]</f> hunger is not satisfied; </t><t>Or as when a thirsty man dreams </t><t>That he is drinking, </t><t>But when he awakens, in fact, he is faint </t><t>And his thirst is not quenched. </t><t>So will the multitude of all the nations be </t><t>Who fight against Mount Zion.</t>dŽƒA"<t>And the multitude of all the nations that fight against Ariel (Jerusalem), </t><t>Even all who fight against her and her stronghold, and who distress her, </t><t>Will be like a dream, a vision of the night.</t><br/>1Ž‚["<t>You will be punished by the LORD of hosts with thunder and earthquake and great noise, </t><t>With whirlwind and tempest and the flame of a consuming fire.</t><br/>‚Ž„5"<pb/><t>But the multitude of your enemies <n>[that assault you]</n> will become like fine dust, </t><t>And the multitude of the tyrants like the chaff which<f>[4]</f> blows away; </t><t>And it will happen in an instant, suddenly <n>[that your enemy is destroyed]</n>.</t><br/>‚uŽ…c"<t>Then you <n>[Jerusalem]</n> will be brought low, </t><t>You will speak from the earth, </t><t>And from the dust where you lie face down </t><t>Your muffled words <i>will come</i>. </t><t>Your voice will also be like that of a spirit from the earth <n>[like one produced by a medium]</n>, </t><t>And your speech will whisper <i>and</i> squeak from the dust.</t>"Ž‚="<t>I will camp against you and encircle you, </t><t>And I will hem you in with siege works, </t><t>And I will raise fortifications against you.</t><br/>SŽƒ"<t>Then I will harass Ariel, </t><t>And she will be a <i>city of</i> mourning and lamenting (crying out in grief) </t><t>Yet she will be like an<f>[3]</f> Ariel <n>[an altar hearth]</n> to Me.</t><br/>cŽ	ƒA"<pb/><t>Woe (judgment is coming) to<f>[1]</f> Ariel, to Ariel, the city where David <n>[once]</n> camped! </t><t>Add<f>[2]</f> yet another year; let the feasts run their course <n>[but only one year more]</n>.</t><br/>xŽi"<t>This also comes from the LORD of hosts, </t><t>Who has made His counsel wonderful and His wisdom great.</t>qŽƒ["<t>Bread <i>grain</i> is crushed fine, </t><t>Indeed, the farmer does not continue to thresh it forever. </t><t>Because the wheel of his cart and his horses <i>eventually</i> damage it, </t><t>He does not thresh it longer.</t><br/><Ž‚q"<t>For dill is not threshed with a sharp threshing sledge, </t><t>Nor is a cartwheel rolled over cumin; </t><t>But dill is beaten out with a staff, and cumin with a rod.</t><br/>\Ž1"<t>For his God instructs <n>[him correctly]</n> and teaches him properly.</t><br/>pŽƒY"<t>When he has leveled its surface, </t><t>Does he not sow <n>[the seed of]</n> dill and scatter cumin, </t><t>And plant wheat in rows, </t><t>And barley in its <n>[intended]</n> place and<f>[3]</f> rye within its border?</t><br/>$Ž
‚A"<t>Does the farmer plow all day to plant seed? </t><t>Does he <i>continually</i> dig furrows and harrow his ground <n>[after it is prepared]</n>?</t><br/>_Ž7"<pb/><t>Listen and hear my voice; </t><t>Listen carefully and hear my words.</t><br/>aŽƒ;"<t>Now do not carry on as scoffers, </t><t>Or the bands which bind you will be made stronger; </t><t>For I have heard from the Lord GOD of hosts <n>[a decree]</n> </t><t>Of decisive destruction on all the earth.</t>wŽ
ƒg"<t>For the LORD will rise up as at Mount Perazim, </t><t>He will be stirred up as in the Valley of Gibeon, </t><t>To do His work, His unusual <i>and</i> incredible work, </t><t>And to accomplish His work, His extraordinary work.</t><br/>:Ž	‚m"<t>For the bed is too short to stretch out on, </t><t>And the blanket is too narrow to wrap around oneself <n>[and likewise all their preparations are inadequate]</n>.</t><br/>UŽƒ#"<t>"As often as it passes through, it will seize you; </t><t>For morning after morning it will pass through, by day and by night, </t><t>And it will be sheer terror to understand what it means."</t><br/>uŽƒc"<t>"Your covenant with death will be annulled, </t><t>And your agreement with Sheol (the place of the dead) will not stand; </t><t>When the overwhelming scourge passes through, </t><t>Then you will become its trampling ground.</t><br/>aŽƒ;"<t>"I will make justice the measuring line </t><t>And righteousness the mason's level; </t><t>Then hail will sweep away the refuge of lies </t><t>And waters will flood over the secret <n>[hiding]</n> place.</t><br/>‚zŽ…m"<pb/><t>Therefore the Lord GOD says this, </t><br/><t>"Listen carefully, I am laying in Zion a Stone, a tested Stone, </t><t>A precious Cornerstone for the <n>[secure]</n> foundation, firmly placed. </t><t>He who believes <n>[who trusts in, relies on, and adheres to that Stone]</n> will not<f>[2]</f> be disturbed <i>or</i> give way <n>[in sudden panic]</n>.</t><br/>‚2Ž„]"<t>Because you have said, "We have made a covenant with death, </t><t>And with Sheol (the place of the dead) we have made an agreement, </t><t>When the overwhelming scourge passes by, it will not reach us, </t><t>For we have made lies our refuge and we have concealed ourselves in deception."</t>~Žu"<t>Therefore, hear the word of the LORD, you arrogant men </t><t>Who rule this people who are in Jerusalem!</t><br/>‚HŽ…	"
<t>Therefore the word of the LORD to them will be <n>[merely monotonous repetitions]</n>: </t><t>"Precept upon precept, precept upon precept, </t><t>Rule upon rule, rule upon rule, </t><t>Here a little, there a little." </t><t>That they may go and stumble backward, and be broken, ensnared, and taken captive.</t><br/>$Ž‚A"<t>He who said to them, "This is the place of quiet, give rest to the weary," </t><t>And, "This is the resting place," yet they would not listen.</t><br/>"Ž ‚="<t>Indeed, the LORD will teach this people <n>[in a more humiliating way]</n> </t><t>By <n>[men with]</n> stammering lips and a foreign tongue,</t><br/>-‚S"
<t>"For <i>He says</i>, </t><t>'Precept upon precept, precept upon precept, </t><t>Rule upon rule, rule upon rule, </t><t>Here a little, there a little.'"</t><br/>Y~ƒ+"	<pb/><t><i>They say</i> "To whom would He teach knowledge? </t><t>And to whom would He explain the message? </t><t>Those <i>just</i> weaned from milk? </t><t>Those <i>just</i> taken from the breast?</t><br/>o}W"<t>For all the tables are full of filthy vomit, so that there is no place <n>[that is clean.]</n></t>‚+|„O"<t>But even these reel with wine and stagger from strong drink: </t><t>The priest and the prophet reel with strong drink; </t><t>They are confused by wine, they stagger from strong drink; </t><t>They reel while seeing visions, </t><t>They stagger <i>when pronouncing</i> judgment.</t><br/>({‚I"<t>A spirit of justice for him who sits in judgment <n>[administering the law]</n>, </t><t>A strength to those who drive back the battle at the gate.</t><br/>!z‚;"<t>In that day the LORD of hosts will become a magnificent crown </t><t>And a glorious diadem to the <n>[converted]</n> remnant of His people,</t><br/>‚\y…1"<t>And the fading flower of its glorious beauty, </t><t>Which is at the head of the rich valley, </t><t>Will be like the early fig before the summer, </t><t>Which one sees, </t><t>And as soon as it is in his hand </t><t>He <n>[greedily]</n> swallows it <n>[and so will the Assyrians rapidly devour Samaria, Israel's capital]</n>.</t><br/>rx]"<t>The splendid crown of the drunkards of Ephraim is trampled by <n>[the foreigners']</n> feet.</t><br/>‚w„"<t>Listen carefully, the Lord has a strong and mighty <i>agent</i> <n>[the Assyrian]</n>; </t><t>Like a tempest of hail, a disastrous storm, </t><t>Like a tempest of mighty overflowing waters, </t><t>He has cast it down to the earth with <i>His</i> hand.</t><br/>‚v	„!"<pb/><t>Woe (judgment is coming) to <n>[Samaria]</n> the splendid crown of the drunkards of<f>