It will come to pass in that day that a great trumpet will be blown, and those who were lost <i>and</i> perishing in the land of Assyria and who were scattered in the land of Egypt will come and worship the LORD on the holy mountain at Jerusalem.Otƒ"<pb/>In that day the LORD will thresh <n>[out His grain]</n> from the flowing stream of the River <n>[Euphrates]</n> to the Brook of Egypt, and you will be gathered up one by one, O sons of Israel.‚/s„W"<t>When its branches are dry, they are broken off; </t><t>The women come and<f>[6]</f> make a fire with them. </t><t>For they are not a people of understanding, </t><t>Therefore He who made them will not have compassion on them, </t><t>And He who created them will not be gracious to them.</t>]rƒ3"
<t>For the fortified city is isolated, </t><t>A settlement deserted and abandoned like the desert; </t><t>There the calf will graze, </t><t>And there it will lie down and<f>[5]</f> feed on its branches.</t><br/>ƒ)q†K"	<t>Therefore through this the wickedness <n>[the sin, the injustice, the wrongdoing]</n> of Jacob (Israel) will be atoned for <i>and</i> forgiven; </t><t>And this will be<f>[4]</f> the full price <n>[that God requires]</n> for taking away his sin: </t><t>When Israel makes all the stones of the <n>[pagan]</n> altars like crushed chalk stones; </t><t>When the Asherim and the incense altars will not stand.</t><br/>0p‚Y"<t>You contended with them by exile, by driving them away <n>[from Canaan]</n>; </t><t>He has expelled them with His fierce wind on the day of the east wind.</t><br/>'o‚G"<pb/><t>Like the striking<f>[3]</f> by Him who has struck them, has He struck them? </t><t>Or like the slaughter of His slain, have they been slain?</t><br/>2n‚]"<t><f>[2]</f> In the generations to come Jacob will take root; </t><t>Israel will blossom and sprout, </t><t>And they will fill the surface of the world with fruit.</t>?m‚w"<t>"Or let him (Israel) cling to My strength <i>and</i> rely on My protection <n>[My stronghold]</n>, </t><t>Let him make peace with Me, </t><t>Let him make peace with Me."</t><br/>#l‚?"<t>"I have no wrath. </t><t>Should anyone give Me briars <i>and</i> thorns in battle, </t><t>I would step on them, I would set them all on fire.</t><br/>k‚'"<t>"I, the LORD, am its Keeper; </t><t>I water it every moment. </t><t>So that no one will harm it, </t><t>I guard it night and day.</t><br/>j‚3"<pb/><t>In that day <n>[it will be said of the redeemed nation of Israel]</n>, </t><t>"A vineyard of<f>[1]</f> wine, sing in praise of it!</t><br/>‚i	„-"<pb/><t>In that day the Lord will punish Leviathan the fleeing serpent </t><t>With His fierce and great and mighty sword <n>[rescuing Israel from her enemy]</n>, </t><t>Even Leviathan the twisted serpent; </t><t>And He will kill the dragon who <i>lives</i> in the sea.</t>‚Kh…"<t>Listen carefully, the LORD is about to come out of His <n>[heavenly]</n> place </t><t>To punish the inhabitants of the earth for their wickedness <n>[their sin, their injustice, their wrongdoing]</n>; </t><t>The earth will reveal the <n>[innocent]</n> blood shed upon her </t><t>And will no longer cover her slain.</t>Fgƒ"<pb/><t>Come, my people, enter your chambers </t><t>And shut your doors behind you; </t><t>Hide for a little while </t><t>Until the <n>[<e>Lord's</e>]</n><f>[6]</f> wrath is past.</t><br/>‚(f„I"<t>Your dead will live; </t><t><f>[5]</f> Their dead bodies will rise. </t><t>You who lie in the dust, awake and shout for joy! </t><t>For your dew is a dew of <n>[celestial]</n> light <n>[heavenly, supernatural]</n>, </t><t>And the earth will give birth to the spirits of the dead.</t>‚
e„"<t>We have been with child, we have twisted <i>and</i> struggled <i>in labor</i>; </t><t>We gave birth, as it seems, <i>only</i> to wind. </t><t>We could not accomplish salvation for the earth, </t><t>Nor were inhabitants of the world<f>[4]</f> born.</t><br/>Bd‚}"<t>As a woman with child approaches <i>the time</i> to give birth, </t><t>She is in pain <i>and</i> struggles and cries out in her labor, </t><t>So we were before You, O LORD.</t><br/>c‚"<t>O LORD, they sought You in distress; </t><t>They managed only a prayerful whisper </t><t>When Your discipline was upon them.</t><br/>+b‚O"<t>You have increased the nation, O LORD; </t><t>You have increased the nation, You are glorified; </t><t>You have extended all the borders of the land.</t><br/>‚
