<t>O LORD our God, other masters besides You have ruled over us; </t><t>But through You alone we confess Your name.</t><br/>_w"<t>LORD, You will establish peace for us, </t><t>Since You have also performed for us all that we have done.</t><br/>‚^ƒ"<pb/><t><i>Though</i> Your hand is lifted up <n>[to strike]</n>, O LORD, the wicked do not see it. </t><t>Let them see Your zeal for <i>Your</i> people and be put to shame; </t><t>Indeed, let the fire reserved for Your enemies consume them.</t><br/>_]ƒ7"
<t><i>Though</i> the wicked is shown compassion <i>and</i> favor, </t><t>He does not learn righteousness; </t><t>In the land of uprightness he deals unjustly, </t><t>And refuses to see the majesty of the LORD.</t>‚
