¯	ë£ ª¡ŠÛ¿×1                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               !’‚;"3<pb/><t>Therefore, now hear this, you who are afflicted, </t><t>Who are drunk, but not with wine <n>[but overwhelmed by the wrath of God]</n>.</t><br/>c’ƒ?"3<t>Your sons have fainted; </t><t>They lie <i>helpless</i> at the head of every street, </t><t>Like an antelope in a net, </t><t>Full <n>[from drinking]</n> of the wrath of the LORD, </t><t>The rebuke of your God.</t>‚’„'"3<t>These two <i>tragedies</i> have befallen you; </t><t>Who will show sympathy for you <i>and</i> mourn with you? </t><t>The desolation and destruction <n>[on the land and city]</n>, famine and sword <n>[on the inhabitants]</n>; </t><t>How shall I comfort you?</t><br/>*’‚M"3<t>There is no one to guide her among all the sons she has borne, </t><t>Nor is there anyone to take her by the hand among all the sons she has reared.</t><br/>‚’„"3<pb/><t>Wake yourself up! Wake yourself up! Stand up, O Jerusalem, </t><t>You who have drunk at the hand of the LORD the cup of His wrath, </t><t>You who have drunk the cup of staggering <i>and</i> intoxication to the dregs <n>[leaving only sediment]</n>.</t><br/>‚’„"3<t>I have put My words in your mouth and have covered you with the shadow of My hand, to<f>[1]</f> establish the <n>[renewed]</n> heavens and lay the foundations of the <n>[renewed]</n> earth, and to say to Zion (Jerusalem), 'You are My people.'"</t>r’]"3For I am the LORD your God, who stirs up the sea so that its waves roarâ€”the LORD of hosts is His name.’ w"3<pb/>The <n>[captive]</n> exile will soon be set free, and will not die in the dungeon, nor will his food be lacking.‚C‘„"3
<t>That you have forgotten the LORD your Maker, </t><t>Who stretched out the heavens </t><t>And laid the foundations of the earth, </t><t>That you continually tremble with fear all day long because of the rage of the oppressor, </t><t>As he takes aim to destroy? </t><t>And where is the rage of the oppressor?</t>?‘~‚w"3<pb/><t>"I, even I, am He who comforts you. </t><t>Who are you that you are afraid of man who dies </t><t>And of a son of man who is made <n>[as destructible]</n> as grass,</t><br/>m‘}ƒS"3<t>So the redeemed of the LORD will return </t><t>And come with joyful shouting to Zion; </t><t>Everlasting joy will be on their heads. </t><t>They will obtain gladness and joy, </t><t>And sorrow and sighing will flee away.</t>C‘|‚"3
