<t>"I bring near My righteousness <n>[in the salvation of Israel]</n>, it is not far away; </t><t>And My salvation will not delay. </t><t>And I will grant salvation in Zion, </t><t>And My glory for Israel.</t>‘'‚".<pb/><t>"Listen to Me, you stiff-necked <i>people</i>, </t><t>You who are far from righteousness (right standing with God).</t><br/>e‘&ƒC".<t>Calling a bird of prey from the east, </t><t>From a far country, the man (Cyrus) of My purpose. </t><t>Truly I have spoken; truly I will bring it to pass. </t><t>I have planned it, <i>be assured</i> I will do it.</t>‚‘%„/".
<t>Declaring the end <i>and</i> the result from the beginning, </t><t>And from ancient times the things which have not <n>[yet]</n> been done, </t><t>Saying, 'My purpose will be established, </t><t>And I will do all that pleases Me <i>and</i> fulfills My purpose,'</t><br/>M‘$ƒ".	<t>"Remember <n>[carefully]</n> the former things <n>[which I did]</n> from ages past; </t><t>For I am God, and there is no one else; </t><t><i>I am</i> God, and there is no one like Me,</t><br/> ‘#y".<pb/><t>"Remember this, and take courage; </t><t>Take it to heart, you rebellious <i>and</i> disloyal people.</t><br/>‚S‘"…".<t>"They lift it on their shoulders <n>[in religious processions or into battle]</n> and carry it; </t><t>They set it in its place and <i>there</i> it remains standing. </t><t>It cannot move from its place. </t><t>Even if one cries to it <n>[for help]</n>, the idol cannot answer; </t><t>It cannot save him from his distress.</t>M‘!ƒ".<t>"Those who lavish gold from the bag </t><t>And weigh out silver on the scales </t><t>Hire a goldsmith, and he makes it <i>into</i> a god; </t><t>They bow down, indeed they worship it.</t><br/>|‘ q".<pb/><t>"To whom would you liken Me </t><t>And make Me equal and compare Me, </t><t>That we may be alike?</t><br/>y‘ƒk".<t>Even to <i>your</i> old age I am He, </t><t>And even to <i>your</i> advanced old age I will carry you! </t><t>I have made <i>you</i>, and I will carry <i>you</i>; </t><t>Be assured I will carry <i>you</i> and I will save <i>you</i>.</t>‚‘„".<pb/><t>"Listen to Me," <n>[says the LORD]</n>, "O house of Jacob, </t><t>And all the remnant of the house of Israel, </t><t>You who have been carried <i>by Me</i> from your birth </t><t>And have been carried <n>[in My arms]</n> from the womb,</t><br/>7‘‚g".<t>They stooped over, they have bowed down together; </t><t>They could not rescue the burden <n>[of their own idols]</n>, </t><t>But have themselves gone into captivi