<t>"For the mountains may be removed and the hills may shake, </t><t>But My lovingkindness will not be removed from you, </t><t>Nor will My covenant of peace be shaken," </t><t>Says the LORD who has compassion on you.</t>‚’-„!"6	<pb/><t>"For this is <i>like</i> the waters of Noah to Me, </t><t>As I swore <n>[an oath]</n> that the waters of Noah </t><t>Would not flood the earth again; </t><t>In the same way I have sworn that I will not be angry with you </t><t>Nor will I rebuke you.</t><br/>>’,‚u"6<t>"In an outburst of wrath </t><t>I hid My face from you for a moment, </t><t>But with everlasting kindness I will have compassion on you," </t><t>Says the LORD your Redeemer.</t>’+‚)"6<t>"For a brief moment I abandoned you, </t><t>But with great compassion <i>and</i> mercy I will gather you <n>[to Myself again]</n>.</t><br/>u’*ƒc"6<t>"For the LORD has called you, </t><t>Like a wife who has been abandoned, grieved in spirit, </t><t>And like a wife <n>[married]</n> in her youth when she is <n>[later]</n> rejected <i>and</i> scorned," </t><t>Says your God.</t><br/>A’)‚{"6<t>"For your husband is your Maker, </t><t>The LORD of hosts is His name; </t><t>And your Redeemer is the Holy One of Israel, </t><t>Who is called the God of the whole earth.</t><br/>‚’(„+"6<pb/><t>"Do not fear, for you will not be put to shame, </t><t>And do not feel humiliated <i>or</i> ashamed, for you will not be disgraced. </t><t>For you will forget the shame of your youth, </t><t>And you will no longer remember the disgrace of your widowhood.</t><br/>,’'‚Q"6<t>"For you will spread out to the right and to the left; </t><t>And your descendants will take possession of nations </t><t>And will inhabit deserted cities.</t>‚’&ƒ"6<t>"Enlarge the site of your tent <n>[to make room for more children]</n>; </t><t>Stretch out the curtains of your dwellings, do not spare them; </t><t>Lengthen your tent ropes </t><t>And make your pegs (stakes) firm <n>[in the ground]</n>.</t><br/>‚Q’%	…"6<pb/><t>"Shout for joy, O barren one, she who has not given birth; </t><t>Break forth into joyful shouting and rejoice, she who has not gone into labor <n>[with child]</n>! </t><t>For the <n>[spiritual]</n> sons of the desolate one <i>will be</i> more numerous </t><t>Than the sons of the married woman," says the LORD.</t><br/>ƒ"’$†="5<t>Therefore, I will divide <i>and</i> give Him a portion with the great <n>[kings and rulers]</n>, </t><t>And He shall divide the spoils with the mighty, </t><t>Because He <n>[willingly]</n> poured out His life to death, </t><t>And was counted among the transgressors; </t><t>Yet He Himself bore <i>and</i> took away the sin of many, </t><t>And interceded <n>[with the Father]</n> for the transgressors.</t>ƒ ’#…y"5<t>As a result of the<f>[7]</f> anguish of His soul, </t><t>He shall see it and be satisfied; </t><t>By His knowledge <n>[of what He has accomplished]</n> the Righteous One, </t><t>My Servant, shall justify the many <n>[making them righteousâ€”upright before God, in right standing with Him]</n>, </t><t>For He shall bear <n>[the responsibility for]</n> their sins.</t><br/>ƒ’"†!"5
<pb/><t>Yet the LORD was<f>[4]</f> willing </t><t>To crush Him,<f>[5]</f> causing Him to suffer; </t><t>If<f>[6]</f> He would give Himself as a guilt offering <n>[an atonement for sin]</n>, </t><t>He shall see <i>His</i> <n>[spiritual]</n> offspring, </t><t>He shall prolong <i>His</i> days, </t><t>And the will (good pleasure) of the LORD shall succeed <i>and</i> prosper in His hand.</t><br/>>’!‚u"5	<t>His grave was assigned with the wicked, </t><t>But He was with a rich man in His death, </t><t>Because He had done no violence, </t><t>Nor was there any deceit in His mouth.</t>ƒ’ †"5<t><f>[2]</f> After oppression and judgment He was taken away; </t><t>And<f>[3]</f> as for His generation <n>[His contemporaries]</n>, who <n>[among them]</n> concerned himself <i>with the fact</i> </t><t>That He was cut off from the land of the living <n>[by His death]</n> </t><t>For the transgression of my people, to whom the stroke <n>[of death]</n> <i>was due</i>?</t><br/>‚ ’„9"5<pb/><t>He was oppressed and He was afflicted, </t><t>Yet He did not open His mouth <n>[to complain or defend Himself]</n>; </t><t>Like a lamb that is led to the slaughter, </t><t>And like a sheep that is silent before her shearers, </t><t>So He did not open His mouth.</t><br/>~’ƒu"5<t>All of us like sheep have gone astray, </t><t>We have turned, each one, to his own way; </t><t>But the LORD has caused the wickedness of us all <n>[our sin, our injustice, our wrongdoing]</n> </t><t>To fall on Him <n>[instead of us]</n>.</t>‚’„/"5<t>But He was wounded for our transgressions, </t><t>He was crushed for our wickedness <n>[our sin, our injustice, our wrongdoing]</n>; </t><t>The punishment <n>[required]</n> for our well-being <i>fell</i> on Him, </t><t>And by His stripes (wounds) we are healed.</t><br/>‚’„"5<pb/><t>But <n>[in fact]</n> He has borne our griefs, </t><t>And He has carried our sorrows <i>and</i> pains; </t><t>Yet we <n>[ignorantly]</n> assumed that He was stricken, </t><t>Struck down by God and degraded <i>and</i> humiliated <n>[by Him]</n>.</t><br/>}’ƒs"5<t>He was despised and rejected by men, </t><t>A Man of sorrows <i>and</i> pain and acquainted with grief; </t><t>And like One from whom men hide their faces </t><t>He was despised, and we did not appreciate His worth <i>or</i> esteem Him.</t>‚J’…
"5<t>For He <n>[the Servant of God]</n> grew up before Him like a tender shoot (plant), </t><t>And like a root out of dry ground; </t><t>He has no <i>stately</i> form or <i>majestic</i> splendor </t><t>That we would look at Him, </t><t>Nor <n>[handsome]</n> appearance that we would<f>[1]</f> be attracted to Him.</t><br/>o’	ƒY"5<pb/><t>Who has believed <n>[confidently trusted in, relied on, and adhered to]</n> our message <n>[of salvation]</n>? </t><t>And to whom <n>[if not us]</n> has the arm <i>and</i> infinite power of the LORD been revealed?</t><br/>‚’ƒ}"4<t>So He will sprinkle many nations <n>[with His blood, providing salvation]</n>, </t><t>Kings will shut their mouths because of Him; </t><t>For what they had not been told they will see, </t><t>And what they had not heard they will understand.</t>U’ƒ#"4<t>Just as many were astonished <i>and</i> appalled at you, <i>My people</i>, </t><t>So His appearance was marred more than any man </t><t>And His form <n>[marred]</n> more than the sons of men.</t><br/>’‚%"4
<t>Indeed, My Servant (the Messiah) will act wisely <i>and</i> prosper; </t><t>He will be raised and lifted up and greatly exalted.</t><br/>‚	’„"4<t>For you will not go out in a hurry <n>[as when you left Egypt]</n>, </t><t>Nor will you go in flight <n>[fleeing, as you did from the Egyptians]</n>; </t><t>For the LORD will go before you, </t><t>And the God of Israel will be your rear guard.</t><br/>‚’„"4<pb/><t>Depart, depart, go out from there (the lands of exile), </t><t>Touch no unclean thing; </t><t>Go out of the midst of her (Babylon), purify yourselves, </t><t>You who carry the articles of the LORD <n>[on your journey from there]</n>.</t><br/>‚’„"4
<t>The LORD has bared His holy arm (His infinite power) </t><t>Before the eyes of all the nations <n>[revealing Himself as the One by Whom Israel is redeemed from captivity]</n>, </t><t>That all the ends of the earth may see </t><t>The salvation of our God.</t>*’‚M"4	<t>Break forth, shout joyfully together, </t><t>You ruins of Jerusalem; </t><t>For the LORD has comforted His people, </t><t>He has redeemed Jerusalem.</t><br/>2’‚]"4<t>Listen! Your watchmen lift up their voices, </t><t>Together they shout for joy; </t><t>For they will see face to face </t><t>The return of the LORD to Zion.</t><br/>‚’„3"4<pb/><t>How beautiful <i>and</i> delightful on the mountains </t><t>Are the feet of him who brings good news, </t><t>Who announces peace, </t><t>Who brings good news of good <n>[things]</n>, </t><t>Who announces salvation, </t><t>Who says to Zion, "Your God reigns!"</t><br/>’‚"4<t>Therefore My people shall know My Name <i>and</i> what it means. Therefore in that day I am the One who is speaking, 'Here I am.'"</t>‚’„"4But now, what do I have here," declares the LORD, "seeing that My people have been taken away without reason? Those who rule over them howl <n>[with taunting and mockery of salvation]</n>," declares the LORD, "and My name is continually blasphemed all day long.6’
‚e"4For the Lord GOD says this, "My people went down at the first into Egypt to live there; and <n>[many years later Sennacherib]</n> the Assyrian oppressed them without cause.p’Y"4<pb/>For the LORD says this, "You were sold for nothing and you will be redeemed, but not with money."(’‚I"4<t>Shake yourself from the dust, arise, </t><t>O captive Jerusalem; </t><t>Rid yourself of the chains around your neck, </t><t>O captive Daughter of Zion.</t>h’
