<pb/>Hear the word which the LORD speaks to you, O house of Israel.‚–„,	<f>[2]</f> Egypt and Judah, and Edom and the sons of Ammon, and Moab and all those who live in the desert who clip off the hair on their temples; for all these nations are uncircumcised (sinful, impure), and all the house of Israel are uncircumcised in heart."*–‚M,	<pb/>"Behold, the days are coming," says the LORD, "when I will punish all who are circumcised <n>[physically]</n> and yet uncircumcised <n>[spiritually]</n>â€”‚0– „Y,	but let the one who boasts boast in this, that he understands and knows Me <n>[and acknowledges Me and honors Me as God and recognizes without any doubt]</n>, that I am the LORD who practices lovingkindness, justice and righteousness on the earth, for in these things I delight," says the LORD.‚•„,	<pb/>Thus says the LORD, "Let not the one who is wise <i>and</i> skillful boast in his insight; let not the one who is mighty <i>and</i> powerful boast in his strength; let not the one who is rich boast in his <n>[temporal satisfactions and earthly]</n> abundance;U•~ƒ#,	<t>Speak, "Thus says the LORD, </t><t>'The dead bodies of men will fall like dung on the open field, </t><t>And like sheaves <n>[of grain]</n> behind the reaper, </t><t>And no one will gather them.'"</t>D•}ƒ,	<t>For death has come up through our windows; </t><t>It has entered our palaces, </t><t>Cutting off the children from the streets </t><t>And the young men from the town squares.</t><br/>^•|ƒ5,	<t>Now hear the word of the LORD, O you women, </t><t>And let your ear hear the word of His mouth; </t><t>Teach your daughters a song of mourning, </t><t>And each one <n>[teach]</n> her neighbor a dirge.</t><br/>‚•{ƒ{,	<t>"For a sound of wailing is heard <n>[coming]</n> from Zion: </t><t>'How we are ruined! </t><t>We are greatly perplexed <i>and</i> utterly shamed, </t><t>Because we have left the land, </t><t>Because they have torn down our dwellings.'"</t><br/>•z‚,	<t>"Let them hurry and take up a wailing for us, </t><t>That our eyes may shed tears </t><t>And our eyelids flow with water.</t><br/>!•y‚;,	<pb/><t>Thus says the LORD of hosts, </t><br/><t>"Consider and call for the mourning women to come; </t><t>Send for the wailing women to come.</t><br/>/•x‚W,	"I will <n>[also]</n> scatter them among nations that neither they nor their fathers have known, and I will send the sword after them until I have annihilated them."3•w‚_,	therefore thus says the LORD of hosts, the God of Israel, "behold, I will feed them, this people, with wormwood and give them bitter <i>and</i> poisonous water to drink.w•vg,	but have walked stubbornly after their <n>[own]</n> heart and after the Baals, as their fathers taught them,"<•u‚q,	
The LORD said, "Because they have<f>[1]</f> turned away from My law which I set before them, and have not listened to <i>and</i> obeyed My voice nor walked in accordance with it,p•tƒY,	<pb/>Who is the wise man who may understand this <n>[without any doubt]</n>? To whom has the mouth of the LORD spoken, so that he may declare it? Why is the land ruined, laid waste like a wilderness, so that no one passes through?;•s‚o,	<t>"I will make Jerusalem a heap of ruins, </t><t>A haunt <i>and</i> dwelling place of jackals; </t><t>And I will make the cities of Judah a desolation, without inhabitant."</t>‚z•r…m,	
<pb/><t>"I will take up a weeping and wailing for the mountains, </t><t>And a <n>[funeral]</n> dirge for the pastures of the wilderness, </t><t>Because they are burned up <i>and</i> desolated so that no one passes through <n>[them]</n>; </t><t>Nor can anyone hear the lowing of cattle. </t><t>Both the birds of the air and the beasts have fled; they are gone.</t><br/>•q‚,		<t>"Shall I not punish them for these things?" says the LORD. </t><t>"Shall I not avenge Myself </t><t>On such a nation as this?</t>T•pƒ!,	<t>"Their tongue is a murderous arrow; </t><t>It speaks deceit; </t><t>With his mouth one speaks peace to his neighbor, </t><t>But in his heart he lays traps <i>and</i> waits in ambush for him.</t><br/>U•oƒ#,	<pb/><t>Therefore thus says the LORD of hosts, </t><br/><t>"Behold, I will refine them <n>[through suffering]</n> and test them; </t><t>For how else should I deal with the daughter of My people?</t><br/>@•n‚y,	<t>"Your dwelling is in the midst of deceit <n>[oppression upon oppression and deceit upon deceit]</n>; </t><t>Through deceit they refuse to know (understand) Me," says the LORD.</t>[•mƒ/,	<t>"Everyone deceives <i>and</i> mocks his neighbor </t><t>And does not speak the truth. </t><t>They have taught their tongue to speak lies; </t><t>They exhaust themselves with sin <i>and</i> cruelty.</t><br/>‚•lƒ{,	<t>"Let everyone beware of his neighbor </t><t>And do not trust any brother. </t><t>For every brother is a supplanter <n>[like Jacob, a deceiver, ready to grab his brother's heel]</n>, </t><t>And every neighbor goes around as a slanderer.</t><br/>‚•k„-,	<t>"They bend their tongue like their bow; </t><t><n>[Their]</n> lies and not truth prevail <i>and</i> grow strong in the land; </t><t>For they proceed from evil to evil, </t><t>And they do not know <i>and</i> understand <i>and</i> acknowledge Me," says the LORD.</t><br/>‚o•j…W,	<t>Oh that I had in the wilderness </t><t>A lodging place (a mere shelter) for wayfaring men, </t><t>That I might leave my people </t><t>And go away from them! </t><t>For they are all adulterers <n>[worshiping idols instead of the LORD]</n>, </t><t><n>[They are]</n> an assembly of treacherous men <n>[of weak character, men without integrity]</n>.</t><br/>7•i	‚i,	<pb/><t>Oh that my head were waters </t><t>And my eyes a fountain of tears, </t><t>That I might weep day and night </t><t>For the slain of the daughter of my people!</t><br/><•h‚q,<t>Is there no balm in<f>[4]</f> Gilead? </t><t>Is there no physician there? </t><t>Why then has not the <n>[spiritual]</n> health of the daughter of my people been restored?</t>•g‚,<t>For the brokenness of the daughter of my people I (Jeremiah) am broken; </t><t>I mourn, anxiety has gripped me.</t><br/>7•f‚g,<t>"The harvest is past, the summer has ended <i>and</i> the gathering of fruit is over, </t><t>But we are not saved," <n>[comes the voice of the people again]</n>.</t><br/>‚A•e„{,<t>Behold, <n>[hear the sound of]</n> the cry of the daughter of my people from the distant land <n>[of Babylon]</n>: </t><t>"Is not the LORD in Zion? Is not her King within her?" </t><t><n>[But the LORD answers]</n> "Why have they provoked Me to anger with their carved images and with foreign idols?"</t><br/>6•d‚e,<pb/><t>Oh, that I (Jeremiah) could find comfort from my sorrow <n>[for my grief is beyond healing]</n>, </t><t>My heart is sick <i>and</i> faint <i>within me</i>!</t><br/>•c‚!,<t>"For behold, I am sending serpents among you, </t><t>Vipers which cannot be charmed, </t><t>And they will bite you," says the LORD.</t>‚E•b…,<t>The snorting of <n>[Nebuchadnezzar's]</n> horses is heard from Dan <n>[on Palestine's northern border]</n>. </t><t>At the sound of the neighing of his strong stallions </t><t>The whole land quakes; </t><t>For they come and devour the land and all that is in it, </t><t>The city and those who live in it.</t><br/>•a‚,<t>We waited for peace <i>and</i> salvation, but no good came, </t><t>And for a time of healing, but behold, terror!</t><br/>‚J•`…
,<t>Why are we sitting still <n>[the people wonder]</n>? </t><t>Assemble yourselves, and let us enter the fortified cities </t><t>And let us die there, </t><t>For the LORD our God has decreed our ruin </t><t>And given us bitter <i>and</i> poisonous water to drink, </t><t>Because we have sinned against the LORD.</t><br/>‚^•_…5,
<pb/><t>"I will gather <i>and</i> snatch them away <n>[utterly consuming them]</n>," says the LORD. </t><t>"There will be no grapes on the vine, </t><t>Nor figs on the fig tree, </t><t>And even the leaf will wither; </t><t>And the things that I have given them will pass away <n>[by the hand of those whom I have appointed]</n>."'"</t><br/>‚X•^…),<t>"Were they ashamed because of the extremely disgusting <i>and</i> shamefully vile things they had done? </t><t>They were not at all ashamed, </t><t>And they did not know how to blush. </t><t>Therefore, they shall fall among those who fall; </t><t>At the time of their punishment they shall be overthrown," </t><t>Says the LORD.</t>%•]‚C,<t>"For they have treated the brokenness of the daughter of My people superficially, </t><t>Saying, 'Peace, peace,' </t><t>When there is no peace.</t><br/>‚<•\„q,
<t>"Therefore I will give their wives to others </t><t>And their fields to new owners; </t><t>Because from the least even to the greatest </t><t>Everyone is greedy for <n>[unjust]</n> gain; </t><t>From the prophet even to the priest </t><t>Everyone practices deceit <i>and</i> deals in corruption.</t><br/>{•[ƒo,	<t>"The wise men are shamed, </t><t>They are dismayed and caught. </t><t>Behold, they have <n>[manipulated and]</n> rejected the <n>[truth in the]</n> word of the LORD, </t><t>And what kind of wisdom <i>and</i> insight do they have?</t><br/>‚:•Z„m,<pb/><t>"How can you say, 'We are wise, </t><t>And the law of the LORD is with us <n>[and we are learned in its language and teachings]</n>'? </t><t>Behold, <n>[the truth is that]</n> the lying pen of the scribes </t><t>Has made the law into a lie <n>[a mere code of ceremonial observances]</n>.</t><br/>v•Yƒe,<t>"Even the stork in the sky </t><t>Knows her seasons <n>[of migration]</n>, </t><t>And the turtledove, the swallow and the crane </t><t>Observe the time of their return. </t><t>But My people do not know </t><t>The law of the LORD.</t>‚•X„3,<t>"I have listened and heard, </t><t>But they have spoken what is not right; </t><t>No man repented of his wickedness, </t><t>Saying, 'What have I done?' </t><t>Everyone turns to his <n>[individual]</n> course, </t><t>As the horse rushes like a torrent into battle.</t><br/>x•Wƒi,<t>"Why then has this people of Jerusalem </t><t>Turned away with a perpetual turning away <n>[from Me]</n>? </t><t>They hold tightly to<f>[3]</f> deceit (idolatry); </t><t>They refuse to repent <i>and</i> return <n>[to God]</n>.</t><br/>l•VƒQ,<t>"Moreover <n>[Jeremiah]</n>, you shall say to them, 'Thus says the LORD, </t><br/><t>"Do men fall and not rise up again? </t><t>Does one turn away <n>[from God]</n> and not repent <i>and</i> return <n>[to Him]</n>?</t><br/>K•Uƒ,And death will be chosen rather than life by all the remnant of those who remain of this evil family (nation), who remain in all the places to which I have driven them," says the LORD of hosts.‚p•T…Y,They will <n>[carelessly scatter and]</n> spread them out before the sun and the moon and all the host of heaven, which the dead have loved and which they have served, and which they have walked after and which they have sought, and which they have worshiped. They will not be gathered or be buried; they will be like<f>[2]</f> dung on the face of the earth.‚•S	„-,<pb/>"At that time," says the LORD, "they <n>[the Babylonian army]</n> will bring out from their graves the<f>[1]</f> bones of the kings of Judah, the bones of its princes, the bones of the priests, the bones of the prophets, and the bones of the inhabitants of Jerusalem._•Rƒ7,"Then I will cause the voices of joy and gladness, and the voices of the bridegroom and the bride to vanish from the cities of Judah and from the streets of Jerusalem; for the land will become a ruinâ€”a wasteland.•Q‚%,!And the dead bodies of this people will be food for the birds of the air and for the beasts of the earth and no one will frighten them away.‚•P„/, <pb/>"Therefore, behold, the days are coming," declares the LORD, "when it will no longer be called Topheth or the Valley of Ben-hinnom, but the Valley of the Slaughter, for <n>[in bloody warfare]</n> they will bury <n>[the dead]</n> in Topheth until there is no more room.‚•O„,They have built the high places of Topheth, which is in the Valley of Ben-hinnom (son of Hinnom), to burn their sons and their daughters in the fire <n>[to honor Molech, the fire god]</n>â€”which I did not command, nor did it come into My heart (mind).M•Nƒ,<pb/>For the children of Judah have done evil in My sight," says the LORD; "they have set their disgusting <i>and</i> shamefully vile things in the house which is called by My Name, to defile it.i•MƒK,<pb/><t>'Cut off your hair <n>[your crown, O Jerusalem]</n> and throw it away, </t><t>And take up a mournful cry on the barren heights, </t><t>For the LORD has rejected and abandoned </t><t>The generation of His wrath.'</t>r•Lƒ],<t>You shall say to them, 'This is the nation that did not obey the voice of the LORD their God or accept correction <i>and</i> warning; truth <i>and</i> faithfulness have perished and have completely vanished from their mouths.</t>!•K‚;,<pb/>"You shall speak all these words to them, but they will not listen to you; and you shall <n>[also]</n> call to them, but they will not answer you.;•J‚o,Yet they did not listen to Me <i>and</i> obey Me or bend their ear <n>[to hear Me]</n>, but stiffened their neck; they did more evil <i>and</i> behaved worse than their fathers.H•Iƒ	,Since the day that your fathers came out of the land of Egypt until this day, I have <n>[persistently]</n> sent you all My servants the prophets, sending them daily, early <n>[and late]</n>.`•Hƒ9,But they did not obey Me or bend their ear <n>[to hear Me]</n>, but followed the counsels and the stubbornness of their <n>[own]</n> evil heart (mind), and <n>[they turned and]</n> went backward instead of forward.]•Gƒ3,But this thing I did command them: 'Listen to <i>and</i> obey My voice, and I will be your God, and you shall be My people; and you will walk in all the way which I command you, so that it may be well with you.'!•F‚;,"For in the day that I brought them out of the land of Egypt, I did not speak to your fathers or command them concerning burnt offerings or sacrifices.}•Es,<pb/>Thus says the LORD of hosts, the God of Israel, "Add your burnt offerings to your sacrifices and eat the meat.s•Dƒ_,Therefore thus says the Lord GOD, "Behold, My anger and My wrath will be poured out on this place, on man and beast, on the trees of the field and the fruit of the ground; and it will burn and <n>[the fire will]</n> not be quenched."	•C‚,Do they offend <i>and</i> provoke Me to anger?" says the LORD. "Is it not themselves <n>[they offend]</n>, to their own shame?"t•Bƒa,The children gather wood, the fathers kindle the fire, and the women knead the dough to make cakes for the<f>[2]</f> queen of heaven; and they pour out drink offerings to other gods that they may offend <i>and</i> provoke Me to anger.d•AA,Do you not see what they are doing in the cities of Judah and in the streets of Jerusalem?!•@‚;,<pb/>"Therefore, do not pray for this people <n>[of Judah]</n> or lift up a cry or entreaty for them or make intercession to Me, for I do not hear you.
