<t>'There is no one to plead your cause; </t><t>No <n>[device to close and allow the]</n> healing of your wound, </t><t>No recovery for you.</t><br/>}™`s,<pb/><t>"For thus says the LORD, </t><t>'Your wound is incurable </t><t>And your injury is beyond healing.</t><br/>‚P™_…,<t>'For I am with you,' says the LORD, 'to save you; </t><t>For I will destroy completely all the nations where I have scattered you, </t><t>But I will not destroy you completely. </t><t>But I will judge <i>and</i> discipline you fairly </t><t>And will by no means regard you as guiltless <i>and</i> leave you unpunished.'</t>‚f™^…E,
<pb/><t>'Fear not, O Jacob My servant,' says the LORD, </t><t>'Nor be dismayed <i>or</i> downcast, O Israel; </t><t>For behold, I will save you from a distant land <n>[of exile]</n> </t><t>And your descendants from the land of their captivity. </t><t>Jacob will return and will be quiet and at ease, </t><t>And no one will make him afraid.</t><br/>™]‚	,	<t>But they shall serve the LORD their God and <n>[the descendant of]</n> David their King, whom I will raise up for them.</t>‚™\ƒ,<pb/>'It shall come about on that day,' says the LORD of hosts, 'that I will break the yoke off your neck and I will tear off your bonds <i>and</i> force apart your shackles; and strangers will no longer make slaves of the people <n>[of Israel]</n>..™[‚U,<t>'Alas! for that day is great, </t><t>There is none like it; </t><t>It is the time of Jacob's <n>[unequaled]</n> trouble, </t><t>But he will be saved from it.</t>m™ZƒS,<t>'Ask now, and see </t><t>Whether a man can give birth <n>[to a child]</n>. </t><t>Why then do I see every man </t><t>With his hands on his<f>[1]</f> loins, as a woman in labor? </t><t>Why have all faces turned pale?</t><br/>™Y‚#,<pb/><t>"Thus says the LORD, </t><br/><t>'We have heard a terrified voice </t><t>Of panic <i>and</i> dread, and there is no peace.</t><br/>R™X,<pb/>Now these are the words the LORD spoke concerning Israel and Judah:‚™Wƒ,For behold (hear this), the days are coming,' says the LORD, 'when I will restore the fortunes of My people Israel and Judah,' says the LORD, 'and I will return them to the land that I gave to their forefathers and they will take possession of it.'"g™VG,"Thus says the LORD God of Israel, 'Write in a book all the words which I have spoken to you.;™U	s,<pb/>The word which came to Jeremiah from the LORD:‚F™T…, therefore thus says the LORD, "Behold, I am about to punish Shemaiah of Nehelam and his descendants. He will not have anyone <n>[born]</n> to live among this people, nor will he see the good that I am about to do to My people," says the LORD, "because he has spoken <i>and</i> preached rebellion against the LORD."'"_™Sƒ7,"Send <n>[this message]</n> to all the exiles, saying, 'Thus says the LORD concerning Shemaiah of Nehelam, "Because Shemaiah has prophesied to you, although I did not send him, and he has made you trust in a lie,"<™Rs,Then came the word of the LORD to Jeremiah, saying,M™Q,<pb/>Zephaniah the priest read this letter to Jeremiah the prophet.F™Pƒ,For he has sent <i>word</i> to us in Babylon, saying, <i>'This captivity</i> <n>[of yours]</n> will be long; build houses and live <i>in them</i> and plant gardens and eat their fruit.'"'"/™O‚W,now therefore <n>[continued the letter from Shemaiah in Babylon to Zephaniah in Jerusalem]</n>, why have you not rebuked Jeremiah of Anathoth, who prophesies to you?i™NƒK,"The LORD has made you <n>[Zephaniah]</n> priest instead of Jehoiada the <n>[deputy]</n> priest, to be the overseer in the house of the LORD over every madman who prophesies, to put him in the stocks and in the iron collar,d™MƒA,"Thus says the LORD of hosts, the God of Israel, 'Because you have sent letters in your own name to all the people who are in Jerusalem, and to Zephaniah the son of Maaseiah, the priest, and to all the priests, saying,h™LI,<pb/>Also you shall speak to Shemaiah of Nehelam <n>[among the exiles in Babylon]</n>, saying,™Kƒw,because they have acted foolishly in Israel and have committed adultery with their neighbors' wives and in My Name have spoken false <i>and</i> concocted words, which I did not command them. I am He who knows and I am a witness,' says the LORD."b™Jƒ=,Because of them, this curse shall be taken up <i>and</i> used by all the exiles from Judah who are in Babylon, saying, "May the LORD make you like Zedekiah and like Ahab, whom the king of Babylon roasted in the fire,‚t™I…a,<pb/>"Thus says the LORD of hosts, the God of Israel, concerning Ahab the son of Kolaiah and concerning Zedekiah the son of Maaseiah, who are prophesying lies to you in My Name, 'Behold, I will hand them over to Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon, and he will slaughter them before your eyes <n>[yes, all the false prophets in Babylon whom you follow shall die]</n>!p™HY,Hear, therefore, the word of the LORD, all you exiles whom I have sent away from Jerusalem to Babylon.i™GƒK,because they have not listened to <i>and</i> honored My words,' says the LORD, 'which I sent to them again and again by My servants the prophets. Moreover, you <n>[exiles]</n> did not listen <n>[either]</n>,' says the LORD.‚™Fƒ,I will pursue them with the sword, with famine and with virulent disease; and I will make them a terror (warning) to all the kingdoms of the earth, to be a curse, a horror, a hissing, and a disgrace among all the nations to which I have driven them,^™Eƒ5,thus says the LORD of hosts, 'Behold (listen very carefully), I am sending the sword, famine, and virulent disease (pestilence) on them, and I will make them like rotten figs that are so bad they cannot be eaten.W™Dƒ',thus says the LORD concerning the king who sits on the throne of David, and concerning all the people who live in this city, your brothers (fellow people of Judah) who did not go with you into captivityâ€”™C,<pb/>"Because you <n>[who have remained in Jerusalem]</n> have said, 'The LORD has raised up prophets for us in Babylon,'‚ ™B„9,I will be found by you,' says the LORD, 'and I will restore your fortunes and I will <n>[free you and]</n> gather you from all the nations and from all the places where I have driven you,' says the LORD, 'and I will bring you back to the place from where I sent you into exile.':™A‚m,
Then <n>[with a deep longing]</n> you will seek Me <i>and</i> require Me <n>[as a vital necessity]</n> and <n>[you will]</n> find Me when you search for Me with all your heart.	™@‚,Then you will call on Me and you will come and pray to Me, and I will hear <n>[your voice]</n> <i>and</i> I will listen to you.4™?‚a,For I know the plans <i>and</i> thoughts that I have for you,' says the LORD, 'plans for peace <i>and</i> well-being and not for disaster to give you a future and a hope.K™>ƒ,
<pb/>"For thus says the LORD, 'When seventy years <n>[of exile]</n> have been completed for Babylon, I will visit (inspect) you and keep My good promise to you, to bring you back to this place.\™=1,	for they prophesy falsely to you in My Name. I have not sent them,' says the LORD.}™<ƒs,For thus says the LORD of hosts, the God of Israel, 'Do not let your <n>[false]</n> prophets who are among you and your diviners deceive you; pay no attention <i>and</i> attach no significance to the dreams which they dream <i>or</i> to yours,1™;‚[,Seek peace <i>and</i> well-being for the city where I have sent you into exile, and pray to the LORD on its behalf; for in its peace (well-being) you will have peace.'M™:ƒ,Take wives and have sons and daughters; take wives for your sons and give your daughters in marriage, that they may bear sons and daughters; multiply there and do not decrease <n>[in number]</n>.S™9,'Build houses and live <i>in them</i>; plant gardens and eat their fruit.™8,"So says the LORD of hosts, the God of Israel, to all the captives whom I have sent into exile from Jerusalem to Babylon,A™7‚{,<i>The letter was</i> hand-carried by Elasah the son of Shaphan and Gemariah the son of Hilkiah, whom Zedekiah king of Judah sent to Babylon to Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon, saying,;™6‚o,(This was after King Jeconiah and the queen mother, the eunuchs, the princes (court officials) of Judah and Jerusalem, the craftsmen and the smiths had departed from Jerusalem.)‚™5	„,<pb/>Now these are the words of the letter which Jeremiah the prophet sent from Jerusalem to the rest of the elders in exile and to the priests, the prophets and all the people whom<f>[1]</f> Nebuchadnezzar had taken into captivity from Jerusalem to Babylon.z™4m,<pb/>So Hananiah the <n>[false]</n> prophet died <n>[two months later]</n>, the same year, in the seventh month.K™3ƒ,Therefore thus says the LORD, 'Behold, I am about to send you away from the face of the earth. This year you will die, because you have spoken <i>and</i> counseled rebellion against the LORD.'"!™2‚;,Then the prophet Jeremiah said to Hananiah the prophet, "Listen now, Hananiah, the LORD has not sent you, and you have made this people trust in a lie.‚™1„,For thus says the LORD of hosts, the God of Israel, "I have put the iron yoke <n>[of servitude]</n> on the neck of all these nations, that they may serve Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon; and they will serve him. And I have even given him the beasts of the field."'"™0‚,
"Go and tell Hananiah, 'The LORD says this, "You have broken yokes of wood, but you have made in their place bars of iron."$™/‚A,<pb/>The word of the LORD came to Jeremiah <n>[some time]</n> after Hananiah the prophet had broken the yoke off the neck of the prophet Jeremiah, saying,{™.ƒo,Hananiah spoke in the presence of all the people, saying, "Thus says the LORD, 'Even so within two full years I will break the yoke of Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon from the neck of all the nations.'" Then the prophet Jeremiah went his way.z™-m,
<pb/>Then Hananiah the <n>[false]</n> prophet took the yoke off the neck of the prophet Jeremiah and smashed it.A™,‚{,	But as for the prophet who <n>[on the contrary]</n> prophesies of peace, when that prophet's word comes to pass, <n>[only]</n> then will it be known that the LORD has truly sent him."5™+‚c,The prophets who were before me and before you from ancient times prophesied against many lands and against great kingdoms, of war and of disaster and of virulent disease.™*w,Nevertheless, listen now to this word which I am about to speak in your hearing and in the hearing of all the people!x™)ƒi,and the prophet Jeremiah said, "Amen! May the LORD do so; may the LORD confirm <i>and</i> fulfill your words which you have prophesied to bring back the articles of the <e>Lord's</e> house and all the captives, from Babylon to this place.™(‚1,<pb/>Then the prophet Jeremiah spoke to the prophet Hananiah in the presence of the priests and all the people who stood in the house of the LORD,_™'ƒ7,And I will also bring back to this place Jeconiah the son of Jehoiakim, king of Judah, along with all the exiles from Judah who went to Babylon,' says the LORD, 'for I will break the yoke of the king of Babylon.'"E™&ƒ,Within two years I am going to bring back to this place all the articles of the <e>Lord's</e> house, which Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon took away from this place and carried to Babylon.j™%M,"Thus says the LORD of hosts, the God of Israel, 'I have broken the yoke of the king of Babylon.‚p™$	…[,<pb/>In the same year, in the beginning of the reign of Zedekiah king of Judah, in the fourth year and the fifth month, the <n>[false]</n> prophet Hananiah the son of Azzur, who was from Gibeon <n>[one of the priests' cities]</n>, spoke <n>[without godly authority]</n> to me in the house of the LORD in the presence of the priests and all the people, saying:R™#ƒ,'They will be<f>[5]</f> carried to Babylon and they will be there until the day that I visit them <n>[with My favor]</n>,' says the LORD. 'Then I will bring them back and restore them to this place.'"2™"‚],"Yes, thus says the LORD of hosts, the God of Israel, concerning the articles which remain in the house of the LORD, in the house of the king of Judah and in Jerusalem,[™!ƒ/,which Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon did not take when he carried<f>[4]</f> Jeconiah the son of Jehoiakim, king of Judah, into exile from Jerusalem to Babylon, along with all the nobles of Judah and Jerusalem.‚2™ „],For thus says the LORD of hosts concerning the <n>[bronze]</n><f>[2]</f> pillars, the <n>[bronze]</n><f>[3]</f> Sea, the <n>[bronze]</n> bases <n>[of the ten basins in Solomon's temple used for washing sacrificial animals]</n>, and the rest of the articles that are left in this city (Jerusalem),‚+™„O,But if they are <n>[true]</n> prophets, and if the word of the LORD is <n>[really spoken]</n> by them, let them now entreat the LORD of hosts that the articles which are <n>[still]</n> left in the house of the LORD, in the house of the king of Judah and in Jerusalem may not go to Babylon.i™K,Do not listen to them; serve the king of Babylon, and live! Why should this city become a ruin?‚P™…,<pb/>Then I said to the priests and to all these people, saying, "Thus says the LORD: Do not listen to the words of your <n>[false]</n> prophets who are prophesying to you, saying, 'Behold, the articles of the <e>Lord's</e> house will now shortly be brought<f>[1]</f> back from Babylon'; for they are prophesying a lie to you.i™ƒK,for I have not sent them," says the LORD, "but they are prophesying falsely in My Name, in order that I may drive you out and that you may perish, you <n>[together]</n> with the <n>[false]</n> prophets who prophesy to you."7™‚g,Do not listen to <i>and</i> believe the words of the <n>[false]</n> prophets who are saying to you, 'You will not serve the king of Babylon,' for they prophesy a lie to you;0™‚Y,
Why will you die, you and your people, by the sword, by famine and by virulent disease, as the LORD has spoken to any nation which will not serve the king of Babylon?)™‚K,<pb/>I spoke to Zedekiah king of Judah in the same way, saying, "Bring your necks under the yoke of the king of Babylon and serve him and his people, and live!H™ƒ	,But the nation which will bow its neck under the yoke of the king of Babylon and serve him, that nation I will let remain on its own land," says the LORD, "to cultivate it and live in it."'"
™‚,
For they prophesy a lie to you which will cause you to be removed far from your land; and I will drive you out and you will perish.\™ƒ1,	And as for you, do not listen to your <n>[counterfeit]</n> prophets, your diviners, your dreams <i>and</i> dreamers, your soothsayers or your sorcerers, who say to you, 'You will not serve the king of Babylon.'‚B™„},<pb/>"But any nation or kingdom that will not serve this same Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon and put its neck under the yoke of the king of Babylon, that nation I will punish," says the LORD, "with the sword, with famine and with pestilence (virulent disease), until I have destroyed it by Nebuchadnezzar's hand.S™ƒ,All nations shall serve him and his son and his grandson until the <n>[appointed]</n> time <n>[of punishment]</n> for his own land comes; then many nations and great kings shall make him their servant.?™‚w,Now I have given all these lands into the hand of Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon, My servant <i>and</i> instrument, and I have also given the wild animals of the field to serve him.4™‚a,"I have made the earth, the men and the animals that are on the face of the earth by My great power and by My outstretched arm, and I will give it to whomever pleases Me.™‚,Command them to go to their masters, saying, 'Thus says the LORD of hosts, the God of Israel, you shall say this to your masters:T™ƒ!,and send word to the king of Edom, to the king of Moab, to the king of the sons of Ammon, to the king of Tyre, and to the king of Sidon by the messengers who come to Jerusalem to Zedekiah king of Judah.a™;,Thus says the LORD to me, "Make for yourself bonds and yokes and put them on your neck,™	‚,<pb/>In the beginning of the reign of Zedekiah the son of Josiah, king of Judah, this word came to Jeremiah from the LORD:™
‚%,<pb/>But the hand of Ahikam the son of Shaphan was with Jeremiah, so that he was not given into the hands of the people to put him to death.@™‚y,And they brought Uriah <n>[God's spokesman]</n> from Egypt and led him to King Jehoiakim, who executed him with a sword and threw his dead body among the graves of the common people.™‚,Then Jehoiakim the king sent men to Egypt: Elnathan the son of Achbor and certain <n>[other]</n> men with him <n>[went]</n> to Egypt.T™
ƒ!,And when Jehoiakim the king, with all his mighty men and all the princes, heard his words, the king sought to put Uriah to death; but when Uriah heard of it, he was afraid and fled and escaped to Egypt.^™	ƒ5,<pb/>And there was also a man who prophesied in the name of the LORD, Uriah the son of Shemaiah of Kiriath-jearim, who prophesied against this city and against this land in words similar to all those of Jeremiah.‚r™…],<pb/>"Did Hezekiah king of Judah and all Judah put Micah to death? Did he not <n>[reverently]</n> fear the LORD and entreat the favor of the LORD? And did not the LORD relent <i>and</i> reverse His decision concerning the misfortune which He had pronounced against them? But <n>[here]</n> we are <n>[thinking of]</n> committing a great evil against ourselves."ƒK™‡,<t>"Micah of Moresheth prophesied in the days of Hezekiah king of Judah; and he spoke to all the people of Judah, saying, 'Thus says the LORD of hosts, </t><br/><t>"Zion will be<f>[3]</f> plowed like a field, </t><t>And Jerusalem will become <n>[heaps of]</n> ruins, </t><t>And the mountain of the house <n>[of the LORDâ€”Mount Moriah, on which stands the temple, shall become covered not with buildings, but]</n> like a densely wooded height."'</t>k™O,Then some of the elders of the land stood up and spoke to all the assembly of the people, saying,D™ƒ,Then the princes and all the people said to the priests and to the <n>[false]</n> prophets, "This man is not deserving of death, for he has spoken to us in the name of the LORD our God."d™ƒA,But know for certain that if you put me to death, you will bring innocent blood on yourselves and on this city and on its inhabitants, for in truth the LORD has sent me to you to speak all these words in your hearing."^™5,As for me, behold, I am in your hands; do with me as seems good and suitable to you.Z™ƒ-,
Therefore, now change your ways and your deeds and obey the voice of the LORD your God; then the LORD will relent <i>and</i> reverse His decision concerning the misfortune which He has pronounced against you.>™‚u,<pb/>Then Jeremiah spoke to all the princes and to all the people, saying, "The LORD sent me to prophesy against this house and against this city all the words that you have heard.U™ ƒ#,Then the priests and the <n>[false]</n> prophets said to the princes and to all the people, "This man is deserving of death, for he has prophesied against this city as you have heard with your own ears."V˜ƒ%,
<pb/>When the<f>[2]</f> princes (court officials) of Judah heard these things, they came up from the king's house to the house of the LORD and sat in the entrance of the New Gate of the house of the LORD.‚Q˜~…,	Why have you prophesied in the name of the LORD saying, 'This house will be like Shiloh <n>[after the ark of the LORD had been taken by our enemies]</n> and this city <n>[Jerusalem]</n> will be desolate, without inhabitant'?" And all the people were gathered around Jeremiah in the <n>[outer area of the]</n> house of the LORD.Y˜}ƒ+,Now when Jeremiah finished proclaiming everything that the LORD had commanded him to speak to all the people, the priests and the <n>[false]</n> prophets and all the people seized him, saying, "You must die!˜|‚,The priests and the <n>[false]</n> prophets and all the people heard Jeremiah speaking these words in the house of the LORD.[˜{ƒ/,then I will make this house <n>[the temple]</n> like<f>[1]</f> Shiloh, and I will make this city <n>[subject to]</n> the curse of all nations of the earth <n>[because it will be so vile in their sight]</n>."'"-˜z‚S,and listen <i>and</i> follow <n>[carefully]</n> the words of My servants the prophets, whom I have been sending to you repeatedlyâ€”though you have not listenedâ€”˜y,And you will say to them, 'Thus says the LORD, "If you will not listen to Me and obey My law which I have set before you,p˜xƒY,It may be that they will listen and everyone will turn from his wickedness, so that I may relent <i>and</i> reverse <n>[My decision concerning]</n> the disaster which I am planning to do to them because of their malevolent deeds.'‚˜w„5,"Thus says the LORD, 'Stand in the court of the <e>Lord's</e> house <n>[Jeremiah]</n>, and speak to all <n>[the people of]</n> the cities of Judah who have come to worship in the <e>Lord's</e> house all the words that I have commanded you to speak to them. Do not omit a word! ˜v	{,<pb/>In the beginning of the reign of Jehoiakim the son of Josiah, king of Judah, this word came from the LORD, saying,H˜uƒ	,&<t>"He has left His lair like the lion; </t><t>For their land has become a horror </t><t>Because of the fierceness of the oppressor </t><t>And because of the <e>Lord's</e> fierce anger."</t>˜t,%<t>"And the peaceful folds are devastated <i>and</i> made silent </t><t>Because of the fierce anger of the LORD.</t><br/>˜s‚3,$<t>"A voice! The cry of the shepherds </t><t>And the wailing of the masters of the flock! </t><t>For the LORD is destroying their pasture,</t><br/>~˜ru,#<t>"The shepherds will have no way to flee, </t><t>Nor the masters of the flock any <n>[way of]</n> escape.</t><br/>‚˜q„,"<pb/><t>"Wail, you shepherds, and cry; </t><t>And roll in ashes, you masters of the flock. </t><t>For the days of your slaughter and of your dispersions have come in full, </t><t>And you will fall <i>and</i> be broken into pieces like a choice vessel.</t><br/>˜pƒw,!<pb/><t>"And those slain by the LORD on that day will be from one end of the earth to the other end of the earth. They will not be lamented (mourned over with expressions of grief) or gathered or buried; they will be like dung on the ground.</t>N˜oƒ, <pb/><t>Thus says the LORD of hosts, </t><t>"Behold, evil is going forth </t><t>From nation to nation, </t><t>And a great whirling tempest is rising </t><t>From the remotest part of the earth.</t>‚˜n„#,<t>'A noise has come to the end of the earth, </t><t>For the LORD has a controversy with <i>and</i> an indictment against the nations. </t><t>He is entering into judgment with all mankind; </t><t>As for the wicked, He has given them to the sword,' says the LORD."</t>ƒ˜m†,<pb/><t>"Therefore prophesy all these words against them and say to them: </t><br/><t>'The LORD will roar from on high </t><t>And utter His voice from His holy dwelling; </t><t>He will roar mightily against His fold <i>and</i> pasture. </t><t>He will jubilantly shout like those who tread <i>the grapes</i> <n>[in the wine press]</n>, </t><t>Against all the inhabitants of the earth.</t><br/>‚˜lƒ,For behold, I am beginning to work disaster in the city which is called by My Name, and shall you go unpunished? You will not be exempt from punishment, for I am calling for a sword against all the inhabitants of the earth," says the LORD of hosts.'˜k‚',And if they refuse to take the cup from your hand to drink, then you will say to them, 'Thus says the LORD of hosts, "You shall surely drink!B˜j‚},<pb/>"Then you shall say to them, 'Thus says the LORD of hosts, the God of Israel, "Drink, be drunk, vomit, and fall to rise no more because of the sword which I will send among you."'H˜iƒ	,all the kings of the north, far and near, one after anotherâ€”and all the kingdoms of the world which are on the face of the earth. And the king of Sheshach (Babylon) shall drink after them.]˜h3,all the kings of Zimri, all the kings of Elam (Persia), and all the kings of Media;e˜gC,all the kings of Arabia and all the kings of the foreign population who live in the desert;˜f‚,Dedan, Tema, Buz <n>[the neighboring tribes north of Arabia]</n>, and all who clip off the side-growth <i>of their hair</i>;˜e‚%,all the kings of Tyre, all the kings of Sidon, and the kings of the islands <i>and</i> the coastlands across the <n>[Mediterranean]</n> Sea;/˜dY,Edom, Moab, and the children of Ammon;T˜cƒ!,and all the foreign (mixed) population, all the kings of the land of Uz, and all the kings of the land of the Philistines (and <n>[their cities of]</n> Ashkelon, Gaza, Ekron, and the remnant of Ashdod);K˜b,Pharaoh king of Egypt, his servants, his princes, all his people,Q˜aƒ,Jerusalem and the cities of Judah <n>[being most guilty because their privileges were greatest]</n>, its kings and princes, to make them a horror, a ruin, a hissing and a curse, as it is to this day;	˜`‚,<pb/>Then I (Jeremiah) took the cup from the <e>Lord's</e> hand and made all the nations to whom the LORD had sent me drink it:c˜_?,They will drink and stagger and go mad because of the sword that I will send among them."+˜^‚O,<pb/>For thus says the LORD, the God of Israel, to me, "Take this cup of the wine of wrath from My hand and cause all the nations to whom I send you to drink it.v˜]ƒe,(For many nations and great kings will make slaves of them, even the Chaldeans <n>[who enslaved other nations]</n>; and I will repay <n>[all of]</n> them according to their deeds and according to the work of their <n>[own]</n> hands.)'",˜\‚Q,
I will bring on that land all My words which I have pronounced against it, all that is written in this book which Jeremiah has prophesied against all the nations.v˜[ƒe,'Then when seventy years are completed, I will punish the king of Babylon and that nation, the land of the Chaldeans (Babylonia),' says the LORD, 'for their wickedness, and will make the land <n>[of the Chaldeans]</n> a perpetual waste.˜Z{,This whole land will be a waste and a horror, and these nations will serve the king of Babylon<f>[1]</f> seventy years.w˜Yƒg,
Moreover, I will take from them the voice of joy and the voice of gladness, the voice of the bridegroom and the voice of the bride, the sound of the millstones <n>[grinding meal]</n> and the light of the lamp <n>[to light the night]</n>.ƒE˜X‡,	behold (hear this), I will send for all the families of the north,' says the LORD, 'and <i>I will send</i> for Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon, My servant <n>[to enact My plan]</n>, and I will bring them against this land and against its inhabitants and against all these surrounding nations; and I will utterly destroy them and make them a horror and a hissing <n>[that is, an object of warning and ridicule]</n> and an everlasting desolation.]˜W3,<pb/>"Therefore thus says the LORD of hosts, 'Because you have not obeyed My words,˜V‚',Yet you have not listened to Me," says the LORD, "so that you have provoked Me to anger with the work (idols) of your hands to your own harm.#˜U‚?,and do not go after other gods to serve them and to worship them, and do not provoke Me to anger with the work of your hands, and I will do you no harm.'Y˜Tƒ+,saying, 'Turn now everyone from his evil way and the evil of your actions <n>[that you may not forfeit the right to]</n> live in the land that the LORD has given to you and your forefathers forever and ever;/˜S‚W,Although the LORD has persistently sent to you all His servants the prophets, you have not listened nor <n>[even]</n> inclined your ear to hear <n>[His message]</n>,l˜RƒQ,"For these twenty-three yearsâ€”from the thirteenth year of Josiah the son of Amon, king of Judah, even to this dayâ€”the word of the LORD has come to me and I have spoken to you over and over again, but you have not listened.v˜Qe,which Jeremiah the prophet spoke to all the people of Judah and to all the inhabitants of Jerusalem, saying,i˜P	ƒM,<pb/>The word that came to Jeremiah in regard to all the people of Judah in the fourth year of the reign of Jehoiakim the son of Josiah, king of Judah (that was the first year of the reign of Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon),˜O‚-,
I will send the sword, famine and virulent disease among them until they are consumed from the land which I gave to them and to their fathers.'"r˜Nƒ],	I will make them a focus of ridicule <i>and</i> disappointment <n>[tossed back and forth]</n> among all the kingdoms of the earth, a <n>[notorious]</n> disgrace, a byword, a taunt and a curse in all places where I will scatter them.‚˜M„,<pb/>'And as for the bad figs, which are so rotten that they cannot be eaten,' surely thus says the LORD, 'so I will abandon Zedekiah king of Judah and his princes, and the remnant of Jerusalem who remain in this land and those who live in the land of Egypt.G˜Lƒ,I will give them a heart to know Me, <n>[understanding fully]</n> that I am the LORD; and they will be My people, and I will be their God, for they will return to Me with their whole heart.8˜K‚i,For I will set My eyes on them for good, and I will bring them again to this land; and I will build them up and not overwhelm them, and I will plant them and not uproot them.9˜J‚k,"Thus says the LORD, the God of Israel, 'Like these good figs, so I will regard as good the captives of Judah, whom I have sent from this place into the land of the Chaldeans.<˜Is,<pb/>Again the word of the LORD came to me, saying,6˜H‚e,Then the LORD said to me, "What do you see, Jeremiah?" And I said, "Figs, the good figs, very good; and the bad <i>figs</i>, very bad, so rotten that they cannot be eaten."#˜G‚?,One basket had very good figs, like the figs that are the first to ripen; but the other basket had very bad figs, so rotten that they could not be eaten.‚h˜F	…K,<pb/>After Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon had taken Jeconiah <n>[who was also called Coniah and Jehoiachin]</n> the son of Jehoiakim, king of Judah, and the princes of Judah <n>[along]</n> with the craftsmen and smiths into exile from Jerusalem to Babylon, the LORD showed me <n>[in a vision]</n> two baskets of figs set before the temple of the LORD.{˜Eo,(And I will bring an everlasting disgrace on you and a perpetual humiliation (shame) which will not be forgotten."+˜D‚O,'"Therefore behold, I, even I, will assuredly forget you and send you away from My presence, you and the city (Jerusalem) which I gave to you and to your fathers.[˜Cƒ/,&For if you say, 'The oracle of the LORD!' surely thus says the LORD, 'Because you said this word, "The oracle of the LORD!" when I have also sent to you, saying, "You shall not say, 'The oracle of the LORD!'"'˜B},%Thus you will <n>[reverently]</n> say to the prophet, 'What has the LORD answered you?' and, 'What has the LORD spoken?'ƒ˜A…},$For you will no longer remember the oracle of the LORD, because every man's own word will become the oracle, <n>[for as they mockingly call all prophecies oracles, whether good or bad, so will it prove to be to them; God will take them at their own word]</n>; and you have perverted the words <n>[not of a lifeless idol, but]</n> of the living God, the LORD of hosts, our God.
