	u	°Gá-Ên 6Z¤ú                                                                                                                                                                  %ŸJ‚C6<t>Those who feasted on delicacies </t><t>Are perishing in the streets; </t><t>Those reared in purple <n>[as nobles]</n> </t><t>Embrace ash heaps.</t><br/>1ŸI‚[6<t>The tongue of the infant clings </t><t>To the roof of its mouth because of thirst; </t><t>The little ones ask for food, </t><t>But no one gives it to them.</t><br/>WŸHƒ'6<t>Even the jackals offer the breast, </t><t>They nurse their young; </t><t>But the daughter of my people has become cruel </t><t>Like ostriches in the wilderness <n>[that desert their young]</n>.</t><br/>\ŸGƒ16<t>The <n>[noble and]</n> precious sons of Zion, </t><t><n>[Once]</n> worth their weight in fine gold, </t><t>How they are regarded <n>[merely]</n> as earthen jars, </t><t>The work of a potter's hands!</t><br/>dŸF	ƒC6<pb/><t>How dark <i>and</i> dim the gold has become, </t><t>How the pure gold has changed! </t><t>The sacred stones <n>[of the temple]</n> are poured out <i>and</i> scattered </t><t>At the head of every street.</t><br/>jŸEM6B<t>You will pursue them in anger and destroy them </t><t>From under the heavens of the LORD.</t>XŸD)6A<t>You will harden their hearts; </t><t>Your curse will be upon them.</t><br/>_ŸC76@<t>You will repay them, O LORD, </t><t>According to the work of their hands.</t><br/>/ŸB‚W6?<t>Look at their sitting and their rising <n>[their actions and secret counsels]</n>; </t><t>I am their mocking song <n>[the subject of their ridicule]</n>.</t><br/>bŸA=6><t>The lips and whispering of my assailants </t><t>Are against me all day long.</t><br/>eŸ@C6=<t>You have heard their reproach, O LORD, </t><t>And all their schemes against me.</t><br/>]Ÿ?36<<t>You have seen all their vengeance, </t><t>All their schemes against me.</t><br/>`Ÿ>96;<t>O LORD, You have seen the wrong <n>[done to me]</n>; </t><t>Judge my case.</t><br/>%Ÿ=‚C6:<t>O Lord, You have pleaded my soul's cause <n>[You have guided my way and protected me]</n>; </t><t>You have rescued <i>and</i> redeemed my life.</t><br/>_Ÿ<769<t>You drew near on the day I called to You; </t><t>You said, "Do not fear."</t><br/>Ÿ;‚68<t>You have heard my voice, </t><t>"Do not hide Your ear from my <i>prayer</i> for relief, </t><t>From my cry for help."</t><br/>RŸ:67<t>I called on Your name, O LORD, </t><t>Out of the lowest pit.</t><br/>`Ÿ9966<t>The waters ran down on my head; </t><t>I said, "I am cut off (destroyed)!"</t><br/>TŸ8!65<t>They silenced me in the pit </t><t>And placed a stone over me.</t><br/>QŸ764<t>Without cause my enemies </t><t>Hunted me down like a bird;</t><br/>|Ÿ6q63<t>My eyes <n>[see things that]</n> bring pain to my soul </t><t>Because of all the daughters of my city.</t><br/>LŸ562<t>Until the LORD looks down </t><t>And sees from heaven.</t><br/>LŸ461<t>My eyes overflow unceasingly, </t><t>Without stopping,</t><br/>Ÿ3‚	60<t>My eyes overflow with streams of tears </t><t>Because of the destruction of the daughter of my people (Jerusalem).</t><br/>lŸ2Q6/<t>Panic and pitfall (traps, danger) have come on us, </t><t>Devastation and destruction.</t><br/>6Ÿ1g6.<t>All our enemies have gaped at us.</t><br/>bŸ0=6-<t>You have made us scum and refuse </t><t>Among the peoples (Gentile nations).</t><br/>gŸ/G6,<t>You have covered Yourself with a cloud </t><t>So that no prayer can pass through.</t><br/>Ÿ.‚+6+<t>You have covered <i>Yourself</i> with anger </t><t>And pursued us; </t><t>You have slain <n>[without pity]</n> and have not spared.</t><br/>VŸ-%6*<t>We have transgressed and rebelled, </t><t>You have not pardoned.</t><br/>mŸ,S6)<t>Let us lift up our hearts and our hands <n>[in prayer]</n> </t><t>Toward God in heaven;</t><br/>]Ÿ+36(<t>Let us test and examine our ways, </t><t>And let us return to the LORD.</t><br/> Ÿ*y6'<pb/><t>Why should any living mortal, or any man, </t><t>Complain <n>[of punishment]</n> in view of his sins?</t><br/>Ÿ)‚6&<t>Is it not from the mouth of the Most High </t><t>That both adversity (misfortune) and good (prosperity, happiness) proceed?</t>Ÿ(}6%<t>Who is there who speaks and it comes to pass, </t><t>Unless the Lord has authorized <i>and</i> commanded it?</t><br/>jŸ'M6$<t>To defraud a man in his lawsuitâ€” </t><t>The Lord does not approve of these things.</t><br/>ZŸ&-6#<t>To deprive a man of justice </t><t>In the presence of the Most High,</t><br/>fŸ%E6"<t>To trample <i>and</i> crush under His feet </t><t>All the prisoners of the land,</t><br/>wŸ$g6!<t>For He does not afflict willingly <i>and</i> from His heart </t><t>Or grieve the children of men.</t><br/>Ÿ#‚-6 <t>For if He causes grief, </t><t>Then He will have compassion </t><t>According to His abundant lovingkindness <i>and</i> tender mercy.</t><br/>:Ÿ"o6<t>For the Lord will not reject forever,</t><br/>pŸ!Y6<t>Let him give his cheek to the one who strikes him; </t><t>Let him be filled with reproach.</t><br/>Ÿ }6<t>Let him put his mouth in the dust <n>[in recognition of his unworthiness]</n>; </t><t>There may yet be hope.</t><br/>Ÿ‚	6<t>Let him sit alone <n>[in hope]</n> and keep quiet, </t><t>Because God has laid it on him <n>[for his benefit]</n>.</t><br/>yŸk6<t>It is good for a man that he should bear </t><t>The yoke <n>[of godly discipline]</n> in his youth.</t><br/>]Ÿ36<t>It is good that one waits quietly </t><t>For the salvation of the LORD.</t><br/>Ÿ‚16<t>The LORD is good to those who wait <n>[confidently]</n> for Him, </t><t>To those who seek Him <n>[on the authority of God's word]</n>.</t><br/>"Ÿ‚=6<t>"The LORD is my portion <i>and</i> my inheritance," says my soul; </t><t>"Therefore I have hope in Him <i>and</i> wait expectantly for Him."</t><br/>nŸU6<t>They are new every morning; </t><t>Great <i>and</i> beyond measure is Your faithfulness.</t><br/>Ÿ‚56<t>It is because of the <e>Lord's</e> lovingkindnesses that we are not consumed, </t><t>Because His <n>[tender]</n> compassions never fail.</t><br/>LŸ6<t>But this I call to mind, </t><t>Therefore I have hope.</t><br/>cŸ?6<t>My soul <i>continually</i> remembers them </t><t>And is bowed down within me.</t><br/>vŸe6<t>Remember <n>[O LORD]</n> my affliction and my wandering, the wormwood and the gall (bitterness).</t><br/>zŸm6<t>So I say, "My strength has perished </t><t>And so has my hope <i>and</i> expectation from the LORD."</t><br/>cŸ?6<t>My soul has been cast far away from peace; </t><t>I have forgotten happiness.</t><br/>Ÿ‚6<t>He has broken my teeth with gravel; </t><t>He has <n>[covered me with ashes and]</n> made me cower in the dust.</t><br/>oŸW6<t>He has filled me with bitterness; </t><t>He has made me drunk with wormwood (bitterness).</t><br/>Ÿ‚76<t>I have become the <n>[object of]</n> ridicule to all my people, </t><t>And <n>[the subject of]</n> their <i>mocking</i> song all the day.</t><br/>\Ÿ16
<t>He has caused the arrows of His quiver </t><t>To enter my inner parts.</t><br/>VŸ%6<t>He has bent His bow </t><t>And set me as a target for the arrow.</t><br/>hŸI6<t>He has turned aside my ways and torn me in pieces; </t><t>He has made me desolate.</t><br/>uŸ
c6
<t>He is to me like a bear lying in wait, </t><t>And like a lion <n>[hiding]</n> in secret places.</t><br/>aŸ;6	<t>He has blocked my ways with cut stone; </t><t>He has made my paths crooked.</t><br/>\Ÿ16<t>Even when I cry out and shout for help, </t><t>He shuts out my prayer.</t><br/>eŸ
C6<t>He walled me in so that I cannot get out; </t><t>He has weighted down my chain.</t><br/>cŸ	?6<t>He has made me live in dark places </t><t>Like those who have long been dead.</t><br/>UŸ#6<t>He has besieged and surrounded me with bitterness and hardship.</t><br/>iŸK6<t>He has caused my flesh and my skin to waste away; </t><t>He has shattered my bones.</t><br/>]Ÿ36<t>Surely He has turned His hand against me </t><t>Repeatedly all the day.</t><br/>YŸ+6<t>He has led me and made me walk </t><t>In darkness and not in light.</t><br/>xŸ	k6<pb/><t>I am <n>[Jeremiah]</n> the man who has seen affliction </t><t>Because of the rod of His wrath.</t><br/>‚:Ÿ„m6<t>You <n>[LORD]</n> called as in the day of an appointed feast </t><t>My terrors (dangers) on every side; </t><t>And there was no one who escaped or survived </t><t>In the day of the <e>Lord's</e> anger. </t><t>Those I have cared for and brought up with tenderness, </t><t>My enemy annihilated them.</t>xŸƒi6<t>The young and the old </t><t>Lie on the ground in the streets; </t><t>My virgins and my young men </t><t>Have fallen by the sword. </t><t>You have killed them in the day of Your anger, </t><t>You have slaughtered, not sparing.</t><br/>‚Ÿ„6<t>See, O LORD, and look! </t><t>With whom have You dealt this way? </t><t>Should women eat their offspring, </t><t>The little ones <i>who were born</i> healthy and beautiful? </t><t>Should priest and prophet be killed </t><t>In the sanctuary of the Lord?</t><br/>‚@Ÿ „y6<t>"Arise, cry aloud in the night, </t><t>At the beginning of the night watches; </t><t>Pour out your heart like water </t><t>Before the presence of the Lord; </t><t>Lift up your hands to Him </t><t>For the life of your little ones </t><t>Who are faint from hunger </t><t>At the head of every street."</t><br/>_žƒ76<t>Their hearts cried out to the Lord. </t><t>"O wall of the Daughter of Zion, </t><t>Let your tears run down like a river day and night; </t><t>Give yourself no relief, </t><t>Let your eyes have no rest.</t><br/>‚%ž~„C6<t>The LORD has done what He planned; </t><t>He has accomplished His word </t><t>Which He commanded<f>[2]</f> from days of old. </t><t>He has demolished without sparing, </t><t>And He has caused the enemy to rejoice over you; </t><t>He has exalted the power of your enemies.</t><br/>‚*ž}„M6<t>All your enemies </t><t>Have opened their mouths wide against you; </t><t>They <n>[scornfully]</n> hiss and gnash <i>their</i> teeth. </t><t>They say, "We have swallowed her up! </t><t>Certainly this is the day for which we waited; </t><t>We have reached it, we have seen it!"</t><br/>‚&ž|„E6<t>All who pass along the way </t><t>Clap their hands <i>in derision</i> at you; </t><t>They scoff and shake their heads </t><t>At the Daughter of Jerusalem, saying, </t><t>"Is this the city that was called </t><t>'The perfection of beauty, </t><t>The joy of all the earth'?"</t><br/>‚Až{„{6<t>Your prophets have seen (imagined) for you </t><t>False and foolish <i>visions</i>; </t><t>And they have not exposed your wickedness </t><t>To restore you from captivity <n>[by teaching you to repent]</n>, </t><t>But they have seen (imagined) <i>and</i> declared to you false and misleading oracles.</t><br/>‚žz„-6
<t>How shall I console you? </t><t>To what shall I compare you, </t><t>O Daughter of Jerusalem? </t><t>With what shall I compare you, so that I may comfort you, </t><t>O Virgin Daughter of Zion? </t><t>For your ruin is as vast as the sea; </t><t>Who can heal you?</t><br/>wžyƒg6<t>They cry to their mothers, </t><t>"Where is grain and wine?" </t><t>As they faint like a wounded man </t><t>In the streets of the city, </t><t>As their life <n>[slips away and]</n> is poured out </t><t>In their mothers' arms.</t><br/>‚Pžx…6<t>My eyes fail because of tears <n>[mourns Jeremiah]</n>, </t><t>My spirit is deeply disturbed; </t><t>My heart is poured out on the earth <n>[in grief]</n> </t><t>Because of the destruction of the daughter of my people <n>[Jerusalem]</n>, </t><t>When little ones and infants faint </t><t>In the streets of the city.</t><br/>‚žw„6
<t>The elders of the Daughter of Zion </t><t>Sit on the ground keeping silent; </t><t>They have thrown dust on their heads, </t><t>They have covered themselves with sackcloth. </t><t>The virgins of Jerusalem </t><t>Have bowed their heads to the ground.</t><br/>‚žv„6	<t>Her gates have sunk into the ground; </t><t>He has destroyed and broken her bars. </t><t>Her king and her princes are <n>[exiled]</n> among the nations; </t><t>The law is no more. </t><t>Also, her prophets no longer find </t><t>Vision from the LORD.</t><br/>‚8žu„i6<t>The LORD determined to lay in ruins </t><t>The <n>[city]</n> wall of the Daughter of Zion. </t><t>He has stretched out a line, </t><t>He has not stopped His hand from destroying. </t><t>He has caused the rampart and the wall to lament (mourn in grief); </t><t>They have languished together.</t><br/>‚žt„6<t>The Lord has rejected His altar; </t><t>He has abandoned His sanctuary. </t><t>He has given into the hand of the enemy </t><t>The walls of her palaces; </t><t>They have made a noise in the house of the LORD </t><t>As on a day of an appointed feast.</t><br/>‚ižs…K6<t>And He has violently broken down His temple like a <n>[fragile]</n> garden <i>hedge</i>; </t><t>He has destroyed His appointed meeting place. </t><t>The LORD has caused the appointed feast and Sabbath </t><t>To be forgotten in Zion </t><t>And has despised <i>and</i> rejected the king and the priest </t><t>In the indignation of His anger.</t><br/>‚žr„%6<t>The Lord has become like an enemy; </t><t>He has swallowed up Israel. </t><t>He has swallowed up all its palaces; </t><t>He has destroyed its strongholds </t><t>And multiplied in the Daughter of Judah </t><t>Mourning and lamentation (expressions of grief).</t><br/>‚žq„6<t>He has bent His bow like an enemy; </t><t>He has set His right hand like an adversary </t><t>And slain all that were delightful <i>and</i> pleasing to the eye; </t><t>In the tent of the Daughter of Zion </t><t>He has poured out His wrath like fire.</t><br/>‚žp„6<t>In fierce anger He has cut off <i>and</i> destroyed </t><t>Every<f>[1]</f> horn of Israel. </t><t>He has withdrawn His right hand </t><t>From the presence of the enemy. </t><t>And He has burned in Jacob like a flaming fire </t><t>Consuming all around.</t><br/>‚Ežo…6<t>The Lord has swallowed up; He has not spared </t><t>All the country places of Jacob. </t><t>In His wrath He has thrown down </t><t>The strongholds of the Daughter of Judah (Jerusalem). </t><t>He has brought them down to the ground <n>[in disgrace]</n>; </t><t>He has debased the kingdom and its princes.</t><br/>‚!žn	„=6<pb/><t>How the Lord has covered the Daughter of Zion (Jerusalem) </t><t>With a cloud in His anger! </t><t>He has cast down from heaven to the earth </t><t>The glory <i>and</i> splendor of Israel </t><t>And has not remembered His footstool </t><t>In the day of His anger.</t><br/>Mžm	ƒ6<t>"Let all their wickedness come before You; </t><t>And deal with them as You have dealt with me </t><t>Because of all my transgressions; </t><t>For my groans are many and my heart is faint."</t>‚[žl	…16<t>"People have heard that I groan, </t><t>That I have no comforter <n>[in You]</n>. </t><t>All my enemies have heard of my desperation; </t><t>They are delighted <n>[O LORD]</n> that You have done it. </t><t>Oh, that You would bring the day <n>[of judgment]</n> which You have proclaimed </t><t>So that they will become like me.</t><br/>‚@žk	„{6<t>"See, O LORD, how distressed I am! </t><t>My spirit is deeply disturbed; </t><t>My heart is overturned within me <i>and</i> cannot rest, </t><t>For I have been very rebellious. </t><t>In the street the sword kills <i>and</i> bereaves; </t><t>In the house there is <n>[famine, disease and]</n> death!</t><br/>Zžj	ƒ/6<t>"I <n>[Jerusalem]</n> called to my lovers (political allies), but they deceived me. </t><t>My priests and my elders perished in the city </t><t>While they looked for food to restore their strength.</t><br/>}ži	ƒu6<t>"The LORD is righteous <i>and</i> just; </t><t>For I have rebelled against His commandment (His word). </t><t>Hear now, all you peoples, </t><t>And look at my pain; </t><t>My virgins and my young men </t><t>Have gone into captivity.</t><br/>‚žh	„6<t>Zion stretches out her hands, </t><t>But there is no comforter for her. </t><t>The LORD has commanded concerning Jacob </t><t>That his neighbors should be his enemies; </t><t>Jerusalem has become a filthy thing <n>[an object of contempt]</n> among them.</t><br/>‚žg	„6<t>"I weep for these things; </t><t>My eyes overflow with tears, </t><t>Because a comforter, </t><t>One who could restore my soul, is far away from me. </t><t>My children are desolate <i>and</i> perishing, </t><t>For the enemy has prevailed."</t><br/>‚žf	ƒ6<t>"The Lord has rejected all the strong men </t><t>In my midst; </t><t>He has proclaimed an established time against me </t><t>To crush my young men. </t><t>The Lord has trampled down as in a wine press </t><t>The Virgin Daughter of Judah.</t><br/>‚že	„96<t>"The yoke of my transgressions is bound; </t><t>By His hand they are knit <i>and</i> woven together. </t><t>They have come upon my neck. </t><t>He has made my strength fail; </t><t>The Lord has put me into the hand </t><t>Of <i>those against whom</i> I cannot stand.</t><br/>‚
