JAlso take some of them and bind them in the edges of your robes.‚ E„)JYou shall burn one third with fire in the center of the city, when the days of the siege are completed. Then you shall take one third and strike it with the sword all around the city, and one third you shall scatter to the wind; and I will unsheathe a sword behind them.W D	ƒ)J<pb/>"And you <n>[Ezekiel]</n>, son of man, take a sharp sword and use it as a barber's razor and shave your head and your beard. Then take scales for weighing and divide the hair <n>[into three parts]</n>. C‚+Jbecause bread and water will be scarce; and they will look at one another in dismay and waste away <n>[in punishment]</n> for their wickedness.‚c B…?JMoreover, He said to me, "Son of man, behold (listen carefully), I am going to break the staff of bread <n>[that supports life]</n> in Jerusalem; and they shall eat bread <n>[rationed]</n> by weight and <n>[eat it]</n> with anxiety <i>and</i> fear, and drink water by measure and <n>[drink it]</n> in horror <n>[of the impending starvation]</n>,  AyJThen He said to me, "See, I will let you use cow's dung instead of human dung over which you shall prepare your food."] @ƒ3JBut I said, "Ah, Lord GOD! Behold (hear me), I have never been defiled; for from my youth until now I have never eaten what died on its own or was torn by beasts, nor has any unclean meat ever entered my mouth." ?‚'J
