He also said to me, "Yet again you will see even greater repulsive acts which they are committing."o¡	ƒWJThen He said to me, "Son of man, do you see what the elders of the house of Israel do in the dark, each man in his <n>[secret]</n> room of carved images? For they say, 'The LORD does not see us; the LORD has abandoned the land.'"‚*¡„MJStanding before these <n>[images]</n> were seventy elders of the house of Israel, and among them stood Jaazaniah the son of Shaphan <n>[the scribe]</n>, each man with his censer in his hand and a thick <i>and</i> fragrant cloud of incense was rising <n>[as they prayed to these gods]</n>.2¡‚]J
So I entered and looked, and saw every kind of creeping things and beasts and loathsome things, and all the idols of the house of Israel, carved all around on the wall.f¡EJ	And He said to me, "Go in and see the wicked, repulsive acts that they are committing here."~¡uJHe said to me, "Son of man, now dig into the wall." And when I had dug into the wall, behold, there was an entrance.¡‚J<pb/>Then He brought me to the entrance of the courtyard; and when I looked, behold, <n>[there was]</n> a hole in the wall.q¡ƒ[JFurthermore, He said to me, "Son of man, do you see what they are doing, the great repulsive acts which the house of Israel is committing here, to drive Me far away from My sanctuary? But you will again see greater repulsive acts."R¡ƒJ<pb/>Then He said to me, "Son of man, now raise your eyes toward the north." So I looked toward the north, and behold, to the north of the altar gate was this idol (image) of jealousy at the entrance.&¡‚EJAnd behold, the glory <i>and</i> brilliance of the God of Israel <n>[who had loved and chosen them]</n> was there, like the vision which I saw in the plain.‚j¡ …MJHe stretched out the form of a hand and took me by a lock of hair on my head; and the Spirit lifted me up between earth and heaven and brought me in the visions of God to Jerusalem, to the entrance of the north gate of the inner <i>courtyard</i>, where the seat of the idol (image) of<f>[4]</f> jealousy, which provokes to jealousy, was <i>located</i>.o ƒWJThen I looked, and behold, a likeness <n>[of a man]</n> with the appearance of fire; from His<f>[3]</f> loins downward He was like fire, and from His loins upward He had the appearance of brightness, like gleaming metal (bronze).‚ ~	„1J<pb/>It came about in the<f>[1]</f> sixth year <n>[of the captivity of King Jehoiachin]</n>, on the fifth day of the sixth month, as I sat in my house <n>[near Babylon]</n> with the elders of Judah sitting before me, that the hand of the Lord<f>[2]</f> GOD fell on me there.‚ }…wJThe king <n>[of Judah]</n> will mourn and the prince (Zedekiah) will be clothed with <n>[garments of]</n> despair <i>and</i> anguish, and the hands of the people of the land shall tremble <n>[in terror]</n>. I will deal with them in accordance with their conduct, and by their judgments I will judge them. And they will know <n>[without any doubt]</n> that I am the LORD.'"x |ƒiJDisaster will come upon disaster and rumor will be <i>heaped</i> on rumor; they will seek a vision from a prophet, but the law <i>and</i> guidance will be lost from the priest and <n>[wise]</n> counsel <n>[will cease]</n> from the elders.
