therefore thus says the Lord GOD, "I will also stretch out My hand against Edom and I will cut off <i>and</i> destroy man and beast. I will make it desolate; from Teman even to Dedan they will fall by the sword.P¤hƒJ'Thus says the Lord GOD, "Because<f>[3]</f> Edom has acted against the house of Judah by taking vengeance, and has greatly offended <i>and</i> has incurred grievous guilt by taking revenge on them,"¤g‚	JThus I will execute judgment <i>and</i> punishment on Moab, and they will know <n>[without any doubt]</n> that I am the LORD."B¤f‚}J
I will give it, along with the children of Ammon, to the people of the East as a possession, so that the children of Ammon will not be remembered among the nations <n>[any longer]</n>.(¤e‚IJ	therefore, behold, I will deprive the flank of Moab of its cities which are on its frontiers, the glory of the land, Beth-jeshimoth, Baal-meon and Kiriathaim.¤d‚!J'Thus says the Lord GOD, "Because<f>[2]</f> Moab and Seir (Edom) say, 'Behold, the house of Judah is like all the <n>[pagan]</n> nations,'‚6¤c„eJtherefore, behold, I have stretched out My hand against you and will hand you over as prey <i>and</i> spoil to the nations. And I will cut you off from the peoples and will cause you to perish from the countries; I will destroy you. Then you shall know <n>[without any doubt]</n> that I am the LORD."Q¤bƒJFor thus says the Lord GOD, "Because you have clapped your hands and stamped your feet and rejoiced with all the contempt, <i>and</i> malice, <i>and</i> spite of your soul against the land of Israel,c¤aƒ?JI will make Rabbah <n>[your chief city]</n> a pasture for camels and <n>[the cities of]</n> the Ammonites a resting place for flocks <n>[of sheep]</n>. And you will know <n>[without any doubt]</n> that I am the LORD."^¤`ƒ5Jtherefore, behold, I am going to give you to the people of the East as a possession, and they will set their encampments among you and make their dwellings among you; they will eat your fruit and drink your milk.‚¤_„%JAnd say to the Ammonites, 'Hear the word of the Lord GOD, for thus says the Lord GOD, "Because you said, 'Aha!' against My sanctuary when it was profaned and against the land of Israel when it was made desolate and against the house of Judah when they went into exile,^¤^5J"Son of man, set your face toward the<f>[1]</f> Ammonites and prophesy against them.;¤]	sJ<pb/>The word of the LORD came to me again, saying,d¤\ƒAJOn that day<f>[4]</f> your mouth will be opened to him who escaped, and you will speak and no longer be mute. In this way you shall be a sign to them, and they will know <n>[without any doubt]</n> that I am the LORD.'"¤[‚Jthat on that day a survivor will come to you to let you hear <n>[of the destruction of Jerusalem]</n> with your <n>[own]</n> ears.‚¤Z„+J<pb/>'As for you, son of man, on the day when I take their strength <i>and</i> their stronghold from them, their joy and their glory, the desire of their eyes and<f>[3]</f> their heart's <n>[chief]</n> delight (the temple), and I also take their sons and their daughters,`¤Yƒ9JSo Ezekiel will be a sign to you; in accordance with all that he has done you will do. And when this <n>[destruction of the temple]</n> comes, then you will know <n>[without any doubt]</n> that I am the Lord GOD.'".¤X‚UJ'Your turbans will be on your heads and your sandals on your feet. You will not mourn or weep, but you will rot away in your sins and you will groan to one another.¤W‚1JYou will do as I <n>[Ezekiel]</n> have done; you shall not cover your mustache nor eat the bread of <n>[mourning brought to you by other]</n> men.‚-¤V„SJ'Speak to the house of Israel, "Thus says the Lord GOD, 'Behold, I will<f>[2]</f> profane My sanctuary, the pride of your strength, the desire of your eyes, and the delight of your soul; and your sons and your daughters whom you have left behind <n>[in Jerusalem]</n> will fall by the sword.I¤UJThen I answered them, "The word of the LORD came to me, saying,g¤TGJThe people said to me, "These things that you are doingâ€”tell us, what do they mean for us?"¤S‚JSo I spoke to the people in the morning, and<f>[1]</f> in the evening my wife died. And the next morning I did as I was commanded.[¤Rƒ/JSigh <i>and</i> groan in silence; do not mourn for the dead. Bind on your turban and put your sandals on your feet, and do not cover your mustache or eat the bread of <n>[mourners furnished by other]</n> men."Y¤Qƒ+J"Son of man, listen carefully, I am about to take away from you the desire of your eyes <n>[your wife]</n> with a single stroke. Yet you shall not mourn and you shall not weep, and your tears shall not flow.6¤PgJAlso the word of the LORD came to me, saying,‚¤O„J<pb/>I the LORD have spoken; it is coming and I will act. I will not relent, and I will not have compassion and I will not be sorry; in accordance with your ways and in accordance with your deeds I will judge <i>and</i> punish you," says the Lord GOD.'"‚ ¤N„9J
<t>"In your filthiness are lewdness <i>and</i> outrage. </t><t>Therefore I <i>would</i> have cleansed you, </t><t>Yet you were not <n>[willing to be]</n> cleansed, </t><t>You will not be cleansed from your filthiness again </t><t>Until I have satisfied My wrath against you.</t>M¤MƒJ<t>"She has wearied Me with toil, </t><t>Yet her great rust has not left her; </t><t>Her thick rust <i>and</i> filth will not be burned away by fire <n>[no matter how hot the flame]</n>.</t><br/>[¤Lƒ/J<t>"Then set the empty pot (Jerusalem) back on the coals </t><t>So that it may be hot </t><t>And its bronze may glow </t><t>And its filthiness may be melted </t><t>And its rust (scum) may be consumed.</t><br/>¤K‚7J
<t>"Heap on wood, kindle the fire, </t><t>Boil the meat well <n>[done]</n> </t><t>And mix in the spices, </t><t>And let the bones be burned.</t><br/>¤J‚J	<t>'Therefore, thus says the Lord GOD, </t><t>"Woe to the bloody city! </t><t>I will also make the pile <n>[of wood]</n> high.</t><br/>S¤IƒJ<t>"That it may cause wrath to come up to take vengeance, </t><t>I have put her blood <n>[guilt for her children sacrificed to Molech]</n> on the bare rock, </t><t>That it may not be covered."</t><br/>@¤H‚yJ<t>"For her blood <n>[that she has shed]</n> remains in her midst; </t><t>She put it on the bare rock; </t><t>She did not pour it on the ground </t><t>To cover it with dust.</t><br/>‚¤G„J<pb/><t>'Therefore, thus says the Lord GOD, </t><t>"Woe (judgment is coming) to the bloody city, </t><t>To the pot in which there is rust </t><t>And whose rust has not gone out of it! </t><t>Take out of it piece by piece, </t><t>Without making any choice.</t><br/> ¤F‚9J<t>"Take the choicest of the flock, </t><t>And also pile wood under the pot. </t><t>Make it boil vigorously </t><t>And boil its bones in the pot."</t>.¤E‚UJ<t>"Put in it the pieces <n>[of meat]</n>, </t><t>Every good piece (the people of Jerusalem), the thigh and the shoulder; </t><t>Fill it with choice bones.</t><br/>@¤D‚yJ<t>Speak a parable against the rebellious house <n>[of Judah]</n> and say to them, 'Thus says the Lord GOD, </t><br/><t>"Put on a pot; put it on and also pour water into it;</t><br/> ¤CyJ"Son of man, record the name of the day, this very day. The king of Babylon has laid siege to Jerusalem this very day.P¤B	ƒJ<pb/>Again in the ninth year <n>[of King Jehoiachin's captivity by Nebuchadnezzar of Babylon]</n>, in the tenth month, on the tenth <n>[day]</n> of the month, the word of the LORD came to me, saying,=¤A‚sJ1Thus your lewdness will be repaid to you, and you will suffer the penalty for your <n>[sinful]</n> idolatry; and you will know <n>[without any doubt]</n> that I am the Lord GOD.'"¤@‚)J0Thus I will make lewdness cease from the land, that all women may be admonished <i>and</i> taught not to commit immoral acts as you have done.,¤?‚QJ/And the horde will stone them with stones and cut them down with their swords; they will kill their sons and their daughters and burn down their houses with fire.z¤>mJ.<pb/>"For thus says the Lord GOD, 'Bring up a horde (mob) against them and hand them over to terror and plunder.^¤=ƒ5J-And they, righteous men, will judge <i>and</i> condemn them with the judgment (punishment) of adulteresses and with the judgment of women who shed blood, because they are adulteresses and blood is on their hands.¤<‚/J,But they committed adultery with her as they would with a prostitute. So they went in to Oholah (Israel) and to Oholibah (Judah), the lewd women.¤;‚J+<pb/>"Then I said concerning the one (Oholah) worn out by adulteries, 'Will they now commit adultery with her when she is like this?'_¤:ƒ7J*The sound of a carefree crowd was with her; and drunkards were brought from the wilderness with men of a common sort, who put bracelets on the hands of the women (both sisters) and beautiful crowns on their heads.u¤9cJ)and you sat on a splendid couch with a table arranged before it on which you had set My incense and My oil.G¤8ƒJ(<pb/>"Furthermore, you have even sent a messenger for men to come from far away; and behold, they cameâ€”those for whom you bathed, painted your eyes, and decorated yourself with ornaments;p¤7ƒYJ'For when they had killed their children <n>[as offerings]</n> to their idols, then they came the same day to My sanctuary to profane it <n>[by daring to offer a sacrifice there also]</n>. And behold, this they did within My house.¤6‚+J&Moreover, they have done this to Me: they have defiled My sanctuary on the same day <n>[of their idolatries]</n> and have profaned My Sabbaths.‚¤5„J%For they have committed adultery, and blood is on their hands. They have committed adultery <n>[against Me]</n> with their idols and have even forced their sons, whom they bore to Me, to pass through the fire as <n>[an offering of]</n> food to them (idols).o¤4ƒWJ$<pb/>Moreover, the LORD said to me, "Son of man, will you judge Oholah (Samaria, capital of Israel) and Oholibah (Jerusalem, capital of Judah)? Then inform them of their atrocities <n>[the detestable and vile things they do]</n>.;¤3‚oJ#Therefore, thus says the Lord GOD, 'Because you have forgotten Me and cast Me behind your back, therefore bear now <n>[the consequences of]</n> your lewdness and prostitution.'"#¤2‚?J"<t>'You will drink it and drain it, </t><t>Then you will gnaw its fragments </t><t>And tear your breasts; </t><pb/>for I have spoken,' says the Lord GOD.!¤1‚;J!<t>'You shall be filled with drunkenness and sorrow, </t><t>With the cup of horror and desolation, </t><t>With the cup of your sister Samaria.</t><br/>|¤0ƒqJ <t>Thus says the Lord GOD, </t><br/><t>'You will drink your sister's cup, </t><t>Which is deep and wide <n>[and filled to the brim]</n>. </t><t>You shall be laughed at and derided; </t><t>It contains much <n>[too much to endure]</n>.</t><br/>¤/}JYou have walked in the way of your sister (Samaria); therefore I will give her cup <n>[of judgment]</n> into your hand.''¤.‚GJThese things will be done to you because you have prostituted yourself with the <n>[Gentile]</n> nations, because you have defiled yourself with their idols.H¤-ƒ	JThey will deal with you in hatred, take all your property, and leave you naked and bare. And the nakedness of your depravity will be uncovered, both your lewdness and your obscene practices.$¤,‚AJFor thus says the Lord GOD, 'Behold, I will place you into the hands of those whom you hate, into the hands of those from whom you turned away in disgust.O¤+ƒJThus I will put an end to your lewdness and your prostitution <i>brought</i> from the land of Egypt, so that you will not lift up your eyes to them or remember Egypt <n>[with longing]</n> anymore.'_¤*7JThey will also strip you (Judah) of your clothes and take away your beautiful jewels.‚G¤)…JI will set My jealous indignation against you <n>[demanding what is rightfully and uniquely mine]</n>, and they will deal with you in fury. They will remove your nose and your ears, and your survivors will fall by the sword. They will take your sons and your daughters; and the survivors will be devoured by the fire.‚j¤(…MJThey will come against you with weapons, chariots, and wagons, and with a company of people (infantry) who will array themselves against you on every side with large shield and small, and helmet; and I will commit the judgment <i>and</i> the punishment to them, and they will judge <i>and</i> punish you in accordance with their <n>[pagan]</n> customs.f¤'ƒEJthe Babylonians and all the Chaldeans, Pekod and Shoa and Koa, and all the Assyrians with them, desirable young men, governors and officials all of them, princes, officers and men of renown, all of them riding on horses.Q¤&ƒJ<pb/>"Therefore, O Oholibah, thus says the Lord GOD, 'Behold, I will stir up your lovers (allies) against you, from whom you turned away in disgust, and I will bring them against you from every side:¤%‚3JThus you longed for the lewdness <i>and</i> vulgarity of your youth, when the Egyptians handled your bosom on account of the breasts of your youth.¤$‚JFor she lusted after her lovers <n>[there]</n>, whose flesh is like the flesh of donkeys and whose issue is like the issue of horses.¤#‚JYet she multiplied her depravities, remembering the days of her youth, when she was actively immoral in the land of Egypt.L¤"ƒJSo she flaunted her acts of prostitution and exposed her nakedness; then I became disgusted with her <n>[and turned away]</n>, as I had become disgusted with her sister <n>[and turned away]</n>.d¤!ƒAJThe Babylonians came to her to the bed of love and they defiled her with their evil desire; and when she had been defiled by them, she (Jerusalem) broke the relationship <i>and</i> pushed them away from her in disgust.s¤ _JWhen she saw <n>[the sketches of]</n> them, she lusted after them and sent messengers to them in Chaldea.4¤‚aJgirded with belts on their<f>[5]</f> loins, with flowing turbans on their heads, all of them looking like officers, like the Babylonian men whose native land was Chaldea.F¤ƒJBut Oholibah carried her depravity further, for she saw men pictured on the wall, the images of the Chaldeans (Babylonians) sketched <i>and</i> portrayed in vermilion (bright red pigment),T¤!J
I saw that she had defiled herself; they both <i>behaved</i> the same way.%¤‚CJShe lusted after the Assyriansâ€”governors and officials, her neighbors, magnificently clothed, horsemen riding on horses, all of them desirable young men.<¤‚qJ<pb/>"Now her sister Oholibah saw this, yet she was more corrupt in her lust than she, and her acts of prostitution were more <n>[wanton]</n> than the immoralities of her sister.C¤‚J
They uncovered her nakedness; they took her sons and her daughters and they killed her with the sword. So she became<f>[4]</f> notorious among women, and they executed judgments on her.u¤cJ	Therefore, I placed her in the hand of her lovers (allies), into the hand of the Assyrians whom she adored.b¤ƒ=JShe did not<f>[3]</f> give up the acts of prostitution that originated <i>during her time in</i> Egypt; for in her youth men had lain with her, and they handled her virgin bosom and poured out their depravity on her.F¤ƒJShe bestowed <n>[freely]</n> her immoralities on them, the choicest men of Assyria, all of them; and with all whom she adored <i>and</i> lusted after, she defiled herself with their idols.{¤oJwho were clothed in purple, governors and officials, all of them attractive young men, horsemen riding on horses.¤‚-J<pb/>"Oholah played the prostitute while she was Mine; and she adored <i>and</i> lusted after her lovers (allies), the Assyrians, her neighbors,‚'¤„GJTheir names were Oholah the elder and Oholibah her sister, and they became Mine and they gave birth to sons and daughters. And as for <n>[the identity of]</n> their names, Oholah is Samaria (capital city of<f>[1]</f> Israel) and Oholibah is Jerusalem (capital city of<f>[2]</f> Judah).-¤‚SJand they prostituted themselves in Egypt. From their youth they were grossly immoral; in that place their breasts were embraced and their virgin bosom was grasped.q¤[J"Son of man, there were two women (Israel and Judah), the daughters of one mother (the united kingdom);;¤	sJ<pb/>The word of the LORD came to me again, saying,G¤ƒJTherefore I have poured out My indignation on them; I have consumed them with the fire of My wrath; I have repaid their way <n>[by bringing it]</n> upon their own heads," says the Lord GOD.N¤ƒJI searched for a man among them who would build up the wall and stand in the gap before Me for <n>[the sake of]</n> the land, that I would not destroy it, but I found no one <n>[not even one]</n>.F¤ƒJThe people of the land have practiced oppression <i>and</i> extortion and have committed robbery; they have wronged the poor and needy and they have oppressed the stranger without justice.)¤
‚KJHer prophets have smeared whitewash for them, seeing false visions and divining lies for them, saying, 'Thus says the Lord GOD'â€”when the LORD has not spoken.¤‚/JHer princes within her are like wolves tearing <i>and</i> devouring the prey, shedding blood and destroying lives in order to get dishonest gain.‚G¤…JHer priests have done violence to My law and have profaned My holy things. They have made no distinction between the holy (sacred) and the profane (secular), they have not taught <n>[people]</n> the difference between the unclean and the clean; and they hide their eyes from My Sabbaths, and I am profaned among them.‚¤
„JThere is a conspiracy of her <n>[false]</n> prophets in her midst, like a roaring lion tearing the prey. They have devoured <n>[human]</n> life; they have taken <n>[in their greed]</n> treasure and precious things; they have made many widows among her.¤	‚	J"Son of man, say to her, 'You <n>[Israel]</n> are a land that is not pronounced clean or rained on in the day of indignation.':¤oJ<pb/>And the word of the LORD came to me, saying,I¤ƒJAs silver is melted in the furnace, so will you be melted in the midst of it; and you will know <n>[without any doubt]</n> that I the LORD have poured out My wrath on you <n>[O Israel]</n>.'"q¤[JI will gather you and blow on you with the fire of My wrath, and you will be melted in the midst of it.V¤ƒ%JAs they gather silver and bronze and iron and lead and tin into the furnace to blow fire on it in order to melt it, so I will gather you in My anger and in My wrath, and I will put you there and melt you.$¤‚AJTherefore, thus says the Lord GOD, 'Because you have all become dross, therefore, behold, I will gather you <n>[O Israel]</n> into the midst of Jerusalem.7¤‚gJ"Son of man, the house of Israel has become dross (metallic waste) to Me. All of them are (useless) bronze, tin, iron, and lead in the furnace; they are the dross of silver.:¤oJ<pb/>And the word of the LORD came to me, saying,¤‚!JYou will defile yourself in the sight of the <n>[Gentile]</n> nations, and you will know <n>[without any doubt]</n> that I am the LORD."'"z¤ mJI will scatter you among the nations and disperse you through the countries, and I will destroy your filthiness.£‚JCan your heart (courage) endure, or can your hands be strong in the days that I will deal with you? I the LORD have spoken, and will act.£~‚5J
<pb/>"Behold, therefore, I strike My hands <n>[together]</n> at your dishonest gain which you have acquired and at the bloodshed which is among you.‚
