J%And I looked, and behold, there were sinews on the bones, and flesh grew and skin covered them; but there was no breath in them.5§‚cJ%<pb/>So I prophesied as I was commanded; and as I prophesied, there was a <n>[thundering]</n> noise, and behold, a rattling; and the bones came together, bone to its bone.6§‚eJ%I will put sinews on you, make flesh grow back on you, cover you with skin, and I will put breath in you so that you may come alive; and you will know that I am the LORD.'"~§uJ%Thus says the Lord GOD to these bones, 'Behold, I will make<f>[1]</f> breath enter you so that you may come to life.r§]J%Again He said to me, "Prophesy to these bones and say to them, 'O dry bones, hear the word of the LORD.'h§IJ%And He said to me, "Son of man, can these bones live?" And I answered, "O Lord GOD, You know."#§‚?J%He caused me to pass all around them, and behold, <i>there were</i> very many <n>[human bones]</n> in the open valley; and lo, <i>they were</i> very dry.&§	‚GJ%<pb/>The hand of the LORD was upon me, and He brought me out in the Spirit of the LORD and set me down in the middle of the valley; and it was full of bones.k§ƒOJ$&Like the flock for sacrifices, like the flock at Jerusalem during her appointed feasts, so will the desolate cities be filled with flocks of people. Then they will know <n>[with confident assurance]</n> that I am the LORD."'"§‚J$%<pb/>'Thus says the Lord GOD, "This too I will let the house of Israel ask Me to do for them: I will increase their people like a flock.:§‚mJ$$Then the nations that are left around you will know that I the LORD have rebuilt the ruined places and planted that which was desolate. I the LORD have spoken, and will do it.";§‚oJ$#Then they will say, 'This land that was deserted <i>and</i> desolate has become like the garden of Eden; and the waste, desolate, and ruined cities are fortified and inhabited.'t§aJ$"The desolate land will be cultivated instead of being a desolation in the sight of everyone who passes by.9§‚kJ$!<pb/>'Thus says the Lord GOD, "On the day that I cleanse you from all your sins I will also cause the cities <n>[of Israel]</n> to be inhabited, and the ruins will be rebuilt.(§‚IJ$ I am not doing this for your sake," says the Lord GOD. "Let that be known to you. Be ashamed and humiliated for your <n>[wicked]</n> ways, O house of Israel!"S§ƒJ$Then you will remember <n>[clearly]</n> your <n>[own]</n> evil ways and your deeds that were not good, and you will loathe yourselves in your own sight for your sins and for your outrageous atrocities.§‚+J$I will multiply the fruit of the tree and the produce of the field, so that you will not suffer again the disgrace of famine among the nations.§
‚J$I will also save you from all your uncleanness, and I will call for the grain and make it abundant, and I will not bring famine on you.s§_J$You will live in the land that I gave to your fathers; and you will be My people, and I will be your God.|§qJ$I will put my Spirit within you and cause you to walk in My statutes, and you will keep My ordinances and do them.$§
‚AJ$Moreover, I will give you a new heart and put a new spirit within you, and I will remove the heart of stone from your flesh and give you a heart of flesh.§	‚J$Then I will sprinkle clean water on you, and you will be clean; I will cleanse you from all your uncleanness and from all your idols. §yJ$For I will<f>[1]</f> take you from the nations and gather you from all the countries and bring you into your own land.‚§„+J$I will vindicate the holiness of My great name which has been profaned among the nations, which you have profaned among them. Then the nations will know <n>[without any doubt]</n> that I am the LORD," says the Lord GOD, "when I prove Myself holy among you in their sight.^§ƒ5J$"Therefore say to the house of Israel, 'Thus says the Lord GOD, "It is not for your sake, O house of Israel, that I am about to act, but for My holy name, which you have profaned among the nations where you went.w§gJ$But I had concern for My holy name, which the house of Israel had profaned among the nations where they went.<§‚qJ$When they came to the nations wherever they went, they profaned My holy name, because it was said of them, 'These are the people of the LORD; yet they have come out of His land.'N§ƒJ$Also I scattered them among the nations and they were dispersed throughout the countries. I judged <i>and</i> punished them in accordance with their conduct and their <n>[idolatrous]</n> behavior.
§‚
J$So I poured out My wrath on them for the blood which they had shed on the land and because they had defiled it with their idols.‚	§„J$"Son of man, when the house of Israel was living in their own land, they defiled it by their <n>[own]</n> behavior and by their <n>[idolatrous]</n> actions. Their conduct before Me was like the uncleanness of a woman during her <n>[physical]</n> impurity.@§ {J$<pb/>Moreover, the word of the LORD came to me, saying,a¦ƒ;J$I will not let you hear insults from the nations anymore, nor will you bear disgrace from the peoples any longer, nor will you cause your nation to stumble <n>[through idolatry]</n> any longer," says the Lord GOD.'"x¦~iJ$therefore you will no longer devour people, and no longer bereave your nation of children,' says the Lord GOD.¦}‚/J$
<pb/>"Thus says the Lord GOD, 'Because they say to you, "You <n>[O land]</n> are a devourer of people and have bereaved your nation of children,"S¦|ƒJ$Yes, <n>[O mountains of Israel]</n> I will cause menâ€”My people Israelâ€”to walk on you and take possession of you, so that you will become their inheritance and never again bereave them of children.'‚¦{„5J$I will multiply on you man and animal; and they will increase and be fruitful. And I will cause you to be inhabited as you were formerly, and I will do better <n>[things]</n> for you than at your beginning. Then you will know <n>[with great confidence]</n> that I am the LORD.¦z‚+J$
I will multiply people on you, all the house of Israel, <n>[indeed]</n> all of it; the cities shall be inhabited and the ruins will be rebuilt.t¦yaJ$	For, behold, I am for you, and I will turn to you <n>[in favor]</n>, and you shall be cultivated and sown.¦x‚!J$But you, O mountains of Israel, will put out your branches and bear your fruit to My people Israel; for they will soon come <n>[home]</n>.E¦wƒJ$"Therefore thus says the Lord GOD, 'I have lifted up My hand <i>and</i> sworn <n>[an oath]</n> that the nations that are around you will themselves endure their <n>[shameful]</n> insults.‚=¦v„sJ$Therefore prophesy concerning the land of Israel and say to the mountains and to the hills, to the ravines and to the valleys, "Thus says the Lord GOD, 'Behold, I have spoken in My jealousy (love for that which is Mine) and in My wrath because you have endured the <n>[shameful]</n> insults of the nations.'‚e¦u…CJ$therefore thus says the Lord GOD, "Most certainly in the fire of My jealousy (love for that which is Mine) I have spoken against the rest of the nations and against all Edom, who appropriated My land for themselves as a possession with wholehearted joy and with uttermost contempt, so that they might empty it out <n>[and possess it]</n> as prey."‚,¦t„QJ$Therefore, O mountains of Israel, hear the word of the Lord GOD. Thus says the Lord GOD to the mountains and to the hills, to the ravines and to the valleys, to the desolate ruins and to the deserted cities which have become prey and a mockery to the rest of the nations which surround you,‚¦s„)J$therefore prophesy and say, 'Thus says the Lord GOD, "For good reason they have made you a desolation, and they crushed you from every side so that you would become a possession of the rest of the nations and you have become the talk and the whispering of the people."'"¦r{J$Thus says the Lord GOD, "Because the enemy has said of you, 'Aha!' and, 'The ancient heights have become our property,'¦q	‚J$<pb/>"And you, son of man, prophesy to the mountains of Israel and say, 'You mountains of Israel, hear the word of the LORD.}¦pƒsJ#As you rejoiced over the inheritance of the house of Israel because it was desolate, so I will do to you; you will be a desolate waste, O Mount Seir, and all Edom, all of it. Then they will know <n>[without any doubt]</n> that I am the LORD."'`¦o9J#'Thus says the Lord GOD, "While the whole earth rejoices, I will make you a wasteland.¦nJ#
So you have boasted <i>and</i> spoken arrogantly against Me, and have multiplied your words against Me; I have heard it."‚¦mƒ}J#Then you will know <n>[without any doubt]</n> that I am the LORD, and that I have heard all your scornful speeches which you have spoken against the mountains of Israel, saying, 'They have been made a wasteland; they have been given to us as food.'y¦lƒkJ#therefore, as I live," says the Lord GOD, "I will deal with you in accordance with the anger and envy you showed because of your hatred for them; and I will make Myself known among them <n>[as Judge]</n> when I judge <i>and</i> punish you.V¦kƒ%J#
<pb/>"Because you <n>[descendants of Esau]</n> have said, 'These two nations <n>[Israel and Judah]</n> and these two lands shall be mine, and we will take possession of them,' although the LORD was there,&¦j‚EJ#	I will make you an everlasting desolation and your<f>[1]</f> cities will not be inhabited. Then you will know <n>[without any doubt]</n> that I am the LORD.¦i‚!J#I will fill its mountains with its slain; those killed by the sword will fall on your hills, and in your valleys, and in all your ravines.¦h‚+J#I will make Mount Seir (Edom) a ruin and a desolate wasteland and I will cut off from it the one who passes through it and the one who returns.4¦g‚aJ#therefore, as I live," says the Lord GOD, "I will hand you over to bloodshed, and bloodshed will pursue you since you have not hated bloodshed, bloodshed will pursue you.‚¦f„+J#<pb/>Because you <n>[descendants of Esau]</n> have had an everlasting hatred <n>[for Jacob (Israel)]</n> and you handed over the sons of Israel to the power of the sword at the time of their tragedy, at the time of their final punishment <n>[the Babylonian conquest]</n>,¦e‚5J#<t>"I will destroy your cities </t><t>And you will become a wasteland. </t><t>Then you shall know <n>[without any doubt]</n> that I am the LORD.</t>K¦dƒJ#<t>and say to it, 'Thus says the Lord GOD, </t><br/><t>"Behold, Mount Seir, I am against you, </t><t>And I will stretch out My hand against you </t><t>And make you completely desolate.</t><br/>W¦c'J#"Son of man, set your face against Mount Seir (Edom), and prophesy against it?¦b	{J#<pb/>Moreover, the word of the LORD came to me, saying,m¦aSJ""As for you, My flock, the flock of My pasture, you are men, and I am your God," says the Lord GOD.$¦`‚AJ"Then they will know <n>[with assurance]</n> that I the LORD their God, am with them and that they, the house of Israel, are My people," says the Lord GOD.I¦_ƒJ"I will prepare for them a place renowned for planting <n>[crops]</n>, and they will not again be victims of famine in the land, and they will not endure the insults of the nations any longer.\¦^ƒ1J"They will no longer be prey to the nations, and the predators of the earth will not devour them; but they will live safely, and no one will make them afraid <n>[in the<f>[2]</f> day of the Messiah's reign]</n>.‚9¦]„kJ"Also the tree of the field will yield its fruit and the earth will yield its produce; and My people will be secure on their land. Then they will know <n>[with confidence]</n> that I am the LORD, when I have broken the bars of their yoke and have rescued them from the hand of those who made them slaves.M¦\ƒJ"I will make them and the places around My hill (Jerusalem, Zion) a blessing. And I will make showers come down in their season; there will be <n>[abundant]</n> showers of blessing (divine favor).I¦[ƒJ"<pb/>"I will make a covenant of peace with them and will eliminate the predatory animals from the land so that they may live securely in the wilderness and sleep <n>[safely]</n> in the woods.u¦ZcJ"And I the LORD will be their God, and My servant David will be a prince among them; I the LORD have spoken.,¦Y‚QJ"<pb/>"Then I will appoint over them one shepherd and he will feed them, <n>[a ruler like]</n> My servant<f>[1]</f> David; he will feed them and be their shepherd.¦X‚5J"therefore, I will rescue My flock, and they shall no longer be prey; and I will judge between one sheep <n>[ungodly]</n> and another <n>[godly]</n>.¦W‚7J"Because you push with side and shoulder, and gore with your horns all those that have become weak <i>and</i> sick until you have scattered them away,¦V‚J"<pb/>Therefore thus says the Lord GOD to them, "Behold, I Myself will judge between the <n>[well-fed]</n> fat sheep and the lean sheep.¦U‚J"As for My flock (the righteous), they must feed on what you trample with your feet and drink what you muddy with your feet!'"‚Z¦T…-J"Is it too little a thing for you that you <n>[unrighteous ones who are well-fed]</n> feed in the best pasture, yet you must trample down with your feet <n>[of wickedness]</n> the rest of your pastures? Or that you drink clear <n>[still]</n> water, yet you must muddy with your feet <n>[of wickedness]</n> the rest <n>[of the water]</n>?I¦SƒJ"<pb/>"And as for you, My flock, thus says the Lord GOD, 'Behold, I judge between one sheep and another, between the rams and the male goats <n>[between the righteous and the unrighteous]</n>.‚¦R„J""I will seek the lost, bring back the scattered, bandage the crippled, and strengthen the weak <i>and</i> the sick; but I will destroy the fat and the strong <n>[who have become hard-hearted and perverse]</n>. I will feed them with judgment <i>and</i> punishment.a¦Q;J"I will feed My flock and I will let them lie down <n>[to rest]</n>," says the Lord GOD.V¦Pƒ%J"I will feed them in a good pasture, and their grazing ground will be on the mountain heights of Israel. There they will lie down on good grazing ground and feed in rich pasture on the mountains of Israel.c¦Oƒ?J"
I will bring them out from the nations and gather them from the countries and bring them to their own land; and I will feed them on the mountains of Israel, by the streams, and in all the inhabited places of the land.]¦Nƒ3J"As a shepherd cares for his sheep on the day that he is among his scattered flock, so I will care for My sheep; and I will rescue them from all the places to which they were scattered on a cloudy and gloomy day.c¦M?J"For thus says the Lord GOD, "Behold, I Myself will search for My flock and seek them out.‚¦L„1J"
'Thus says the Lord GOD, "Behold, I am against the shepherds, and I will demand My flock from them and make them stop tending the flock, so that the shepherds cannot feed themselves anymore. I will rescue My flock from their mouth, so that they will not be food for them."'"Q¦KJ"	therefore, you <n>[spiritual]</n> shepherds, hear the word of the LORD:‚$¦J„AJ""As I live," says the Lord GOD, "certainly because My flock has become prey, My flock has even become food for every predator of the field for lack of a shepherd, and My shepherds did not search for My flock, but <i>rather</i> the shepherds fed themselves and did not feed My flock;V¦I%J"<pb/>Therefore, you <n>[spiritual]</n> shepherds, hear the word of the LORD:*¦H‚MJ"My flock wandered through all the mountains and on every high hill; My flock was scattered over all the face of the earth and no one searched or sought them."'"¦G‚J"They were scattered because there was no shepherd, and when they were scattered they became food for all the predators of the field.y¦FƒkJ"You have not strengthened those who are weak, you have not healed the sick, you have not bandaged the crippled, you have not brought back those gone astray, you have not looked for the lost; but you have ruled them with force and violence.%¦E‚CJ"You eat the fat <n>[the choicest of meat]</n>, and clothe yourselves with the wool, you slaughter the best of the livestock, but you do not feed the flock.‚(¦D„IJ""Son of man, prophesy against the shepherds of Israel. Prophesy and say to them, the <n>[spiritual]</n> shepherds, 'Thus says the Lord GOD, "Woe (judgment is coming) to the <n>[spiritual]</n> shepherds of Israel who have been feeding themselves! Should not the shepherds feed the flock?9¦C	oJ"<pb/>And the word of the LORD came to me, saying,¦B‚!J!!So when it comes to passâ€”as it most certainly willâ€”then they will know <n>[without any doubt]</n> that a prophet has been among them."P¦AƒJ! Behold, you are to them like a love song by one who has a pleasant voice and plays well on a stringed instrument <n>[merely to entertain them]</n>; for they hear your words but do not practice them.u¦@ƒcJ!They come to you as people come, and they sit before you as My people, and they hear your words, but they do not practice them; for with their mouth they <i>express</i> loving devotion, but their heart goes after their (unlawful) gain.i¦?ƒKJ!<pb/>"But as for you, son of man, your people who talk about you by the walls and in the doorways of the houses say one to another, every one to his brother, 'Come now and hear what the message is that comes from the LORD.'4¦>‚aJ!Then they will know <n>[without any doubt]</n> that I am the LORD, when I make the land a desolation and a ruin because of all the atrocities which they have committed."'S¦=ƒJ!And I will make the land <n>[of Israel]</n> a desolation and a ruin, and her pride in her power will be brought to an end; and the mountains of Israel will be so deserted that no one will pass through.‚3¦<„_J!You shall say this to them, 'Thus says the Lord GOD, "As I live, those who are in the ruins certainly will fall by the sword, and I will give whoever is in the open field to the <n>[predatory]</n> animals to be devoured, and those who are in strongholds and in caves will die of virulent diseases.I¦;ƒJ!You rely on your sword <n>[as your security]</n>; you commit outrageous <i>and</i> disgraceful acts and each of you defiles his neighbor's wife. Should you then take possession of the land?"'=¦:‚sJ!Therefore say to them, 'Thus says the Lord GOD, "You eat meat with the blood <i>in it</i> and raise your eyes to your idols and shed blood. Should you take possession of the land?‚!¦9„;J!"Son of man, those <n>[back in Palestine]</n> who inhabit these ruins in the land of Israel are saying, 'Abraham was <n>[only]</n> one man and he took possession of the land, but we are many; the land has <n>[most certainly]</n> been given to us <n>[to possess]</n> as property.';¦8qJ!<pb/>Then the word of the LORD came to me, saying,o¦7ƒWJ!Now the hand of the LORD had been upon me in the evening, before the survivor came. And He<f>[1]</f> opened my mouth at the time he came to me in the morning; so my mouth was opened <n>[in readiness]</n> and I was no longer mute.,¦6‚QJ!In the twelfth year of our exile <n>[in Babylon]</n>, on the fifth of the tenth month, a survivor from Jerusalem came to me, saying, "The city has been captured."¦5‚/J!Yet you say, 'The way of the Lord is not right.' O house of Israel, I will judge you, every one <n>[of you]</n> in accordance with his own ways!"¦4‚J!But when a wicked man turns back from his wickedness and practices what is just (fair) and right, he will live because of it.u¦3cJ!When the righteous turns back from his righteousness and commits injustice, he will also die because of it.%¦2‚CJ!<pb/>"Yet your people <n>[who are in exile in Babylon]</n> say, 'The way of the Lord is not right;' but as for them, it is their own way that is not right.#¦1‚?J!None of his sins that he has committed will be remembered against him. He has practiced that which is just (fair) and right; he will most certainly live.\¦0ƒ1J!if a wicked man returns <n>[what he took as]</n> a pledge, pays back what he had taken by robbery, walks in the statutes which ensure life, without committing injustice, he will certainly live; he will not die.¦/‚J!But when I say to the wicked, 'You will certainly die,' and he turns from his sin and practices that which is just (fair) and rightâ€”‚¦.„#J!
When I say to the righteous that he will most certainly live, and he trusts in his <n>[previous acts of]</n> righteousness <n>[to save him]</n> and commits injustice, none of his righteous deeds will be remembered; but he will die for his injustice that he committed.ƒ¦-†/J!And you, son of man, say to the sons of your people, 'The righteousness of the righteous man will not save him in the day of his transgression; and as for the wickedness of the wicked, he will not stagger because of it in the day that he turns from his wickedness, whereas a righteous man will not be able to live because of his <n>[previous acts of]</n> righteousness on the day when he commits sin.'‚(¦,„IJ!Say to them, 'As I live,' says the Lord GOD, 'I take no pleasure in the death of the wicked, but rather that the wicked turn from his way and live. Turn back (change your way of thinking), turn back <n>[in repentance]</n> from your evil ways! For why should you die, O house of Israel?'O¦+ƒJ!
<pb/>"Now as for you, son of man, say to the house of Israel, 'Thus you have said, "Truly our transgressions and our sins are on us, and we are rotting away because of them; how then can we live?"'?¦*‚wJ!	But if you on your part warn the wicked man to turn from his <n>[evil]</n> way and he does not turn from his <n>[evil]</n> way, he will die in his sin; but you have saved your life.[¦)ƒ/J!When I say to the wicked, 'O wicked man, you will certainly die,' and you do not speak to warn the wicked from his way, that wicked man will die because of his sin; but I will require his blood from your hand.*¦(‚MJ!<pb/>"Now as for you, son of man, I have made you a watchman for the house of Israel; so you shall hear a message from My mouth and give them a warning from Me.‚¦'„J!But if the watchman sees the sword coming and does not blow the trumpet and the people are not warned, and the sword comes and takes any one of them, he is taken away because of his corruption <i>and</i> sin; but I will require his blood from the watchman's hand.'¦&‚7J!He heard the sound of the trumpet but did not take warning; his blood shall be on himself. But if he had taken warning, he would have saved his life."¦%‚=J!then whoever hears the sound of the trumpet and does not take warning, and a sword comes and takes him away, his blood will be on his <n>[own]</n> head.b¦$=J!and he sees the sword coming on the land, and he blows the trumpet and warns the people,_¦#ƒ7J!"Son of man, speak to the sons of your people <n>[who are exiled in Babylon]</n> and say to them, 'If I bring a sword on a land, and the people of the land take one man from among them and make him their watchman,9¦"	oJ!<pb/>And the word of the LORD came to me, saying,Z¦!ƒ-J  "Though I instilled a terror of him in the land of the living, yet he will be made to lie down among the uncircumcised along with those slain by the sword, even Pharaoh and all his hordes," says the Lord GOD.¦ ‚#J <pb/>"Pharaoh will see them, and he will be comforted for all his hordes slain by the swordâ€”Pharaoh and all his army," says the Lord GOD.‚3¦„_J <pb/>"The princes of the north are there also, all of them, and all the Sidonians, who in spite of the terror resulting from their power, have gone down in shame with the slain. So they lay down uncircumcised with those slain by the sword and bore their disgrace with those who go down to the pit.‚¦„	J <pb/>"Edom is there also, her kings and all her princes, who for all their power <i>and</i> strength are laid with those who were slain by the sword; they will lie <n>[in shame and defeat]</n> with the uncircumcised and with those who go down to the pit.¦‚J But you will be broken in the midst of the uncircumcised and you will lie <n>[without honors]</n> with those who are slain by the sword.‚8¦„iJ Nor do they lie beside the fallen heroes of the uncircumcised, who went down to Sheol with their weapons of war, whose swords were laid <n>[with honors]</n> under their heads. The punishment for their sins rested on their bones, for the terror of these heroes <i>was once</i> in the land of the living.L¦ƒJ <pb/>"Meshech, Tubal, and all their hordes are there; their graves<f>[2]</f> surround them. All of them uncircumcised, slain by the sword, for they spread their terror in the land of the living.‚M¦…J They have made a bed for her among the slain with all her hordes. Her graves are around it; they are all uncircumcised (barbaric, boorish, crude), slain by the sword (for their terror had been spread in the land of the living), and they bore their disgrace with those who go down to the pit; they were laid among the slain.‚Y¦…+J <pb/>"<f>[1]</f> Elam <n>[a conquest of Assyria]</n> is there and all her hordes around her grave; all of them slain, fallen by the sword, who have gone down uncircumcised to the lower parts of the earth, who made their terror spread in the land of the living and bore their shame <i>and</i> defeat with those who went down to the pit.>¦‚uJ whose graves are set in the remotest parts of the pit and her army is all around her grave. All of them are slain, fallen by the sword, who spread terror in the land of the living.¦‚J <pb/>"Assyria is there with all her warriors; their graves are all around her. All of them are slain, fallen by the sword,N¦ƒJ The strong among the mighty rulers will say of him (Pharaoh) and his allies from the midst of Sheol, 'They have gone down <n>[defeated]</n>; they lie still, the uncircumcised, slain by the sword.'0¦‚YJ <pb/>They will fall among those who are slain by the sword. She (Egypt) is handed over to the sword; they have drawn her and all her hordes away <n>[to judgment]</n>.*¦‚MJ <pb/><t>'Whom <n>[among them]</n> do you surpass in beauty? </t><t>Go down and make your bed with the uncircumcised (the barbaric, the boorish, the crude).'</t>g¦ƒGJ <t>"Son of man, wail over the hordes of Egypt and cast them down, both her and the daughters of the powerful <i>and</i> majestic nations, to the nether world (the place of the dead), with those who go down to the pit;</t>(¦‚IJ <pb/>In the twelfth year <n>[after King Jehoiachin of Judah was taken into exile]</n>, on the fifteenth of the month, the word of the LORD came to me, saying,X¦ƒ)J <pb/>This is the dirge (funeral poem to be sung) and they shall sing it <n>[for her]</n>. The daughters of the nations shall sing it; for Egypt and for all her hordes they shall sing it," says the Lord GOD.‚¦„J <t>"When I make the land of Egypt desolate, </t><t>And the country is stripped <i>and</i> deprived of all that which filled it, </t><t>When I strike all those who live in it, </t><t>Then they will know <n>[without any doubt]</n> that I am the LORD.</t>2¦‚]J <t>"Then I will make their waters quiet <i>and</i> clear; </t><t>I will make their rivers run <n>[slowly and smoothly]</n> like oil," </t><t>Says the Lord GOD.</t><br/>C¦‚J 
<t>"I will also destroy all its cattle from beside its great waters; </t><t>And the foot of man will not muddy them anymore </t><t>Nor will the hoofs of the animals muddy them.</t><br/>‚	¦
„J <t>I will make your horde <n>[of people]</n> fall by the swords of the mightyâ€”all of them are tyrants among the nations, </t><br/><t>And they will devastate the pride <i>and</i> presumption of Egypt, </t><t>And all its hordes will be destroyed.</t><br/>^¦5J <pb/>For thus says the Lord GOD, "The sword of the king of Babylon will come on you.‚4¦„aJ 
I will make many peoples appalled at you <n>[at your judgment and your defeat]</n>, and their kings will be horribly afraid of you when I brandish My sword <n>[of judgment]</n> before them; they will tremble <i>and</i> shudder every moment, every man for his own life, on the day of your downfall."4¦
‚aJ 	<pb/>I will also put fear into the hearts of many peoples when I bring your destruction <n>[and captivity]</n> among the nations, into countries which you have not known.¦	‚5J <t>"All the bright lights in the heavens </t><t>I will darken over you </t><t>And I will place darkness on your land," </t><t>Says the Lord GOD.</t>Q¦ƒJ <t>"And when I extinguish you, </t><t>I will cover the heavens <n>[of Egypt]</n> and darken their stars; </t><t>I will cover the sun with a cloud </t><t>And the moon will not give its light.</t><br/>¦‚#J <t>"I will also water the land with your flowing blood </t><t>As far as the mountains, </t><t>And the ravines will be full of you.</t><br/>¦‚+J <t>"And I will scatter your flesh on the mountains </t><t>And fill the valleys with your debris <n>[your corpses and their worms]</n>.</t><br/>j¦ƒMJ <t>"Then I will leave you (Egypt) on the land; </t><t>I will hurl you on the open field. </t><t>And I will make all the birds of the sky dwell on you, </t><t>And I will satisfy the animals of all the earth with you.</t><br/>5¦‚cJ <pb/><t>Thus says the Lord GOD, </t><br/><t>"I will spread out My net over you </t><t>With a company of many nations, </t><t>And they will bring you up in My net.</t><br/>ƒ¦†-J <t>"Son of man, take up a dirge (funeral poem to be sung) over Pharaoh king of Egypt and say to him, </t><br/><t>'You have compared yourself to a young lion among the nations, </t><t>But you are like a monster in the seas; </t><t>You burst into your rivers </t><t>And disturbed <i>and</i> muddied the waters with your feet </t><t>And fouled their rivers <n>[the source of their prosperity]</n>.'"</t>P¦	ƒJ <pb/>In the twelfth year <n>[after King Jehoiachin of Judah was taken into exile by the king of Babylon]</n>, in the twelfth month, on the first of the month, the word of the LORD came to me, saying,
