*	3ÃVé{:‹	GÆ/´øV                  ©k		‚7T<pb/>In the third year of the reign of<f>[1]</f> Jehoiakim king of Judah,<f>[2]</f> Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon came to Jerusalem and besieged it.7©j‚gJ0#The distance around the city shall be 18,000 (4 x 4,500) <i>cubits</i>; and the name of the city from that day <n>[and ever after]</n> <i>shall be</i>, 'The LORD is There.'"w©igJ0"On the west side, 4,500 <i>cubits</i>, three gates: one gate of Gad, one gate of Asher, one gate of Naphtali.©h‚J0!On the south side, 4,500 <i>cubits</i>, by measurement, also three gates: one gate of Simeon, one gate of Issachar, one gate of Zebulun.}©gsJ0 On the east side, 4,500 <i>cubits</i>, also three gates: one gate of Joseph, one gate of Benjamin, one gate of Dan.=©f‚sJ0there shall also be gates of the city, <i>named</i> after the names of the tribes of Israel, three gates toward the north: one gate of Reuben, one gate of Judah, one gate of Levi.~©euJ0"These are the exits of the city: on the north side, <n>[which is to extend]</n> 4,500 <i>cubits</i> by measurement,*©d‚MJ0This is the land which you shall divide by lot among the tribes of Israel as their inheritance, and these are their <i>several</i> portions," says the Lord GOD.S©cƒJ0And beside the border of Gad, at the south side, southward, the border shall extend from Tamar to the waters of Meribath-kadesh, to the Brook <n>[of Egypt]</n>, to the Great <n>[Mediterranean]</n> Sea.e©bCJ0Beside the border of Zebulun, from the east side to the west side, Gad, one <i>portion</i>.j©aMJ0Beside the border of Issachar, from the east side to the west side, Zebulun, one <i>portion</i>.i©`KJ0Beside the border of Simeon, from the east side to the west side, Issachar, one <i>portion</i>.i©_KJ0Beside the border of Benjamin, from the east side to the west side, Simeon, one <i>portion</i>.l©^QJ0"As for the rest of the tribes: from the east side to the west side, Benjamin, one <i>portion</i>.r©]ƒ]J0Exclusive of the property of the Levites and of the property of the city, which are in the middle of that which belongs to the prince, <i>everything</i> between the border of Judah and the border of Benjamin shall be for the prince.ƒ0©\†YJ0"The remainder, on both sides of the holy allotment and of the property possessed by the city, <i>shall belong</i> to the prince. In front of the 25,000 <i>cubits</i> of the allotment toward the east border and westward in front of the 25,000 toward the west border, alongside the <n>[tribal]</n> portions, <i>it shall be</i> for the prince. The holy allotment with the sanctuary of the temple shall be in the midst of it.©[‚5J0The whole allotment <i>shall be</i> 25,000 by 25,000 <i>cubits</i>; you shall set apart the holy allotment, a square, with the property of the city.T©Z!J0The workers of the city, from all the tribes of Israel shall cultivate it.n©YƒUJ0The remainder of the length alongside the holy allotment shall be 10,000 <i>cubits</i> to the east and 10,000 to the west; and it shall be beside the holy allotment. The produce from it shall be food for the workers of the city.©X‚'J0The city shall have open country: toward the north 250 <i>cubits</i>, and toward the south 250, toward the east 250, and toward the west 250.©W‚7J0These <i>shall be</i> the measurements of it: the north side 4,500 <i>cubits</i>, the south side 4,500, the east side 4,500, and the west side 4,500.h©VƒIJ0<pb/>"The remaining <n>[strip of]</n> 5,000 <i>cubits</i> in width and 25,000 in length shall be for the city's common (secular) use, for a place in which to live and for open country. The city shall be in the midst of it.©U‚3J0And they shall not sell any of it or exchange it, or allow this choice <i>portion</i> of land to pass <i>to others</i>; for it is holy to the LORD.[©Tƒ/J0
Alongside the border of the priests, the <n>[other]</n> Levites <i>shall have</i> 25,000 <i>cubits</i> in length and 10,000 in width. The whole length <i>shall be</i> 25,000 <i>cubits</i> and the width 10,000.,©S‚QJ0And this <n>[land offering]</n> shall be an allotment to them from the allotment of the land, a most holy portion beside the border of the <n>[other]</n> Levites.a©Rƒ;J0<i>It shall be</i> for the priests who are sanctified of the sons of Zadok, who have kept My charge, and who did not go astray when the children (descendants) of Israel went astray as the <n>[other]</n> Levites did.‚,©Q„QJ0
The holy allotment shall be for these, <i>namely</i> for the priests, toward the north 25,000 <i>cubits in length</i>, and toward the west 10,000 in width, and toward the east 10,000 in width, and toward the south 25,000 in length; and the sanctuary of the LORD shall be in the midst of it."©P‚=J0	The allotment <n>[of land]</n> that you shall set apart <i>and</i> offer to the LORD <i>shall be</i> 25,000 <i>cubits</i> in length and 10,000 in width.‚b©O…=J0<pb/>"And beside the border of Judah, from the east side to the west side, shall be the allotment <i>and</i> contribution of land which you shall set apart <i>and</i> offer, 25,000 <i>cubits</i> in width, and in length like one of the <n>[tribal]</n> portions, from the east side to the west side; and the sanctuary shall be in the midst of it.f©NEJ0Beside the border of Reuben, from the east side to the west side, Judah, one <i>portion</i>.h©MIJ0Beside the border of Ephraim, from the east side to the west side, Reuben, one <i>portion</i>.j©LMJ0Beside the border of Manasseh, from the east side to the west side, Ephraim, one <i>portion</i>.k©KOJ0Beside the border of Naphtali, from the east side to the west side, Manasseh, one <i>portion</i>.h©JIJ0Beside the border of Asher, from the east side to the west side, Naphtali, one <i>portion</i>.c©I?J0Beside the border of Dan, from the east side to the west side, Asher, one <i>portion</i>.‚©H	„J0<pb/>"Now these are the names of the tribes: from the north end, beside the way of Hethlon to Lebo-hamath, as far as Hazar-enan, which is on the northern border of Damascus, beside Hamath, and running from the east to the west, Dan, one <i>portion</i>.p©GYJ/In whatever tribe the foreigner resides, there shall you give him his inheritance," says the Lord GOD.‚M©F…J/You shall divide it by lot as an inheritance among yourselves and among the foreigners who stay among you, who give birth to sons among you. They shall be to you as the native-born <n>[in the country]</n> among the children (descendants) of Israel; they shall be allotted an inheritance with you among the tribes of Israel.a©E;J/<pb/>"So you shall divide this land among yourselves according to the tribes of Israel.G©DƒJ/<pb/>"The west side <i>shall be</i> the Great <n>[Mediterranean]</n> Sea, from the <i>south</i> border to a point opposite Lebo-hamath <n>[north of Mount Hermon]</n>. This is the west side.y©CƒkJ/<pb/>"The south side, southward, from Tamar <n>[near the Dead Sea]</n> <i>shall extend</i> as far as the waters of Meribath-kadesh, to the Brook of Egypt and to the Great <n>[Mediterranean]</n> Sea. This is the south side toward the south.S©BƒJ/<pb/>"The east side, from between Hauran, Damascus, Gilead, and the land of Israel, <i>shall be</i> the Jordan; from the <i>north</i> border to the eastern sea you shall measure. This is the east side.@©A‚yJ/So the boundary will extend from the <n>[Mediterranean]</n> Sea to Hazar-enan at the border of Damascus, and on the north, northward, is the border of Hamath. This is the north side.+©@‚OJ/Hamath, Berothah, Sibraim, which is between the border of Damascus and the border of Hamath; <n>[as far as]</n> Hazer-hatticon, which is on the border of Hauran.#©?‚?J/<pb/>"And this shall be the boundary of the land on the north side: from the Great <n>[Mediterranean]</n> Sea by way of Hethlon to the entrance of Zedad,E©>ƒJ/You shall divide it as an inheritance, each one equally with the other. I lifted up My hand <i>and</i> swore to give it to your fathers, and this land shall fall to you as an inheritance.C©=‚J/
Thus says the Lord GOD, "This <i>shall be</i> the boundary by which you shall divide the land as an inheritance among the twelve tribes of Israel; Joseph <i>shall have</i> two portions.‚5©<„cJ/By the river on its bank, on one side and on the other, will grow all <i>kinds of</i> trees for food. Their leaves will not wither and their fruit will not fail. They shall bear every month because their water flows from the sanctuary, and their fruit will be for food and their leaves for healing."(©;‚IJ/But its swamps and marshes will not become fresh <n>[and wholesome for animal life]</n>; they will <n>[as the river subsides]</n> be left encrusted with salt.‚
