<t>Therefore, he who is prudent <i>and</i> has insight will keep silent at such a <n>[corrupt and evil]</n> time, for it is an evil time <n>[when people will not listen to truth and will disregard those of good character]</n>.</t>‚¯$„r<t>For I know your transgressions are many and your sins are great (shocking, innumerable), </t><t>You who distress the righteous and take bribes, </t><t>And turn away from the poor in the <n>[court of the city]</n> gate <n>[depriving them of justice]</n>.</t><br/>‚?¯#„wr<t>Therefore, because you impose heavy rent on the poor </t><t>And demand a tribute (food-tax) of grain from them, </t><t>Though you have built <n>[luxurious]</n> houses of square stone, </t><t>You will not live in them; </t><t>You have planted beautiful vineyards, but you will not drink their wine.</t><br/>‚ ¯"„9r
<pb/><t>They hate the one who reprimands <n>[the unrighteous]</n> in the <n>[court held at the city]</n> gate <n>[regarding him as unreasonable and rejecting his reprimand]</n>, </t><t>And they detest him who speaks <n>[the truth]</n> with integrity <i>and</i> honesty.</t><br/>¯!‚r	<t>It is He who causes <n>[sudden]</n> destruction to flash forth on the strong </t><t>So that destruction comes on the fortress.</t>‚P¯ …r<pb/><t>He who made the <n>[cluster of stars called]</n> Pleiades and <n>[the constellation]</n> Orion, </t><t>Who turns deep darkness into the morning </t><t>And darkens the day into night, </t><t>Who calls for the waters of the sea </t><t>And pours them out on the surface of the earth, </t><t>The LORD is His name.</t><br/>¯‚!r<t>"For those <n>[shall be consumed]</n> who turn justice into wormwood (bitterness) </t><t>And cast righteousness down to the earth."</t>‚A¯„{r<t>"Seek the LORD <n>[search diligently for Him and long for Him as your most essential need]</n> so that you may live, </t><t>Or He will rush down like a <n>[devouring]</n> fire, O<f>[1]</f> house of Joseph, </t><t>And there will be no one to quench the flame for <n>[idolatrous]</n><f>[2]</f> Bethel,</t><br/>‚+¯„Or<t>"But do not resort to Bethel <n>[to worship the golden calf]</n> </t><t>Nor enter <n>[idolatrous]</n> Gilgal, </t><t>Nor cross over to Beersheba <n>[and its idols]</n>; </t><t>For Gilgal will certainly go into captivity <i>and</i> exile, </t><t>And Bethel will come to nothing.</t><br/>@¯‚yr<pb/><t>For thus says the LORD to the house of Israel, </t><br/><t>"Seek Me <n>[search diligently for Me and regard Me as more essential than food]</n> so that you may live.</t><br/>w¯ƒgr<t>For thus says the Lord GOD, </t><t>"The city which goes forth a thousand <i>strong</i> </t><t>Will have a hundred left, </t><t>And the one which goes forth a hundred <i>strong</i> </t><t>Will have ten left to the house of Israel."</t>