<pb/>On the twenty-fourth day of the ninth month (Dec 18, 520 <e>b.c</e>.), in the second year of Darius, the word of the LORD came to Haggai the prophet, saying,^²Qƒ5¸	'The latter<f>[3]</f> glory of this house will be greater than the former,' says the LORD of hosts, 'and in this place I shall give <n>[the ultimate]</n> peace <i>and</i> prosperity,' declares the LORD of hosts."P²P¸'The silver is Mine and the gold is Mine,' declares the LORD of hosts.M²Oƒ¸'I will shake all the nations; and they will come with the desirable <i>and</i> precious things of all nations, and I will fill this house with glory <i>and</i> splendor,' says the LORD of hosts.²N‚¸"For thus says the LORD of hosts, 'Once more, in a little while, I am going to shake the heavens and the earth, the sea and the dry land.)²M‚K¸'As for the promise which I made with you when you came out of Egypt, My Spirit stands <n>[firm and immovable]</n> <i>and</i> continues with you; do not fear!'‚²Lƒ{¸But now be courageous, Zerubbabel,' declares the LORD, 'be courageous also, Joshua the son of Jehozadak, the high priest, and be courageous, all you people of the land,' declares the LORD, 'and work; for I am with you,' declares the LORD of hosts.*²K‚M¸'Who is left among you who saw this<f>[2]</f> house (temple) in its former glory? And how do you see it now? Does it not seem to you like nothing in comparison?
