	e´û‘6ÓqÌÿ+lª                                                                                                                                                                                     ¶/‚%Ö<J>And everyone who hears these words of Mine and does not do them, will be like a foolish (stupid) man who built his house on the sand.</J>=¶.‚sÖ<J>And the rain fell, and the floods <i>and</i> torrents came, and the winds blew and slammed against that house; yet it did not fall, because it had been founded on the rock.</J>:¶-‚mÖ<J>"So everyone who hears these words of Mine and acts on them, will be like a wise man <n>[a far-sighted, practical, and sensible man]</n> who built his house on the rock.</J>O¶,ƒÖ<J>And then I will declare to them publicly, 'I never knew you; <e>depart from Me</e> <n>[you are banished from My presence]</n>, <e>you who act wickedly</e> <n>[disregarding My commands]</n>.'</J>H¶+ƒ	Ö<J>Many will say to Me on that day <n>[when I judge them]</n>, 'Lord, Lord, have we not prophesied in Your name, and driven out demons in Your name, and done many miracles in Your name?'</J> ¶*‚9Ö<pb/><J>"Not everyone who says to Me, 'Lord, Lord,' will enter the kingdom of heaven, but only he who does the will of My Father who is in heaven.</J>^¶)5Ö<J>Therefore, by their fruit you will recognize them <n>[as false prophets]</n>.</J>_¶(7Ö<J>Every tree that does not bear good fruit is cut down and thrown into the fire.</J>W¶''Ö<J>A good tree cannot bear bad fruit, nor can a bad tree bear good fruit.</J>f¶&EÖ<J>Even so, every healthy tree bears good fruit, but the unhealthy tree bears bad fruit.</J>4¶%‚aÖ<J>By their fruit you will recognize them <n>[that is, by their contrived doctrine and self-focus]</n>. Do people pick grapes from thorn bushes or figs from thistles?</J>,¶$‚QÖ<J>"Beware of the false prophets, <n>[teachers]</n> who come to you dressed as sheep <n>[appearing gentle and innocent]</n>, but inwardly are ravenous wolves.</J>,¶#‚QÖ<J>But small is the gate and narrow <i>and</i> difficult to travel is the path that leads the way to <n>[everlasting]</n> life, and there are few who find it.</J>Y¶"ƒ+Ö
<J>"Enter through the narrow gate. For wide is the gate and broad <i>and</i> easy to travel is the path that leads the way to destruction <i>and</i> eternal loss, and there are many who enter through it.</J>:¶!‚mÖ<pb/><J>"So then, in everything treat others the same way you want them to treat you, for this is <n>[the essence of]</n> the Law and the <n>[writings of the]</n> Prophets.</J>‚¶ „1Ö<J>If you then, evil (sinful by nature) as you are, know how to give good <i>and</i> advantageous gifts to your children, how much more will your Father who is in heaven <n>[perfect as He is]</n> give what is good <i>and</i> advantageous to those who keep on asking Him.</J>R¶Ö
<J>Or if he asks for a fish, will <n>[instead]</n> give him a snake?</J>w¶gÖ	<J>Or what man is there among you who, if his son asks for bread, will <n>[instead]</n> give him a stone?</J>¶‚Ö<J>For everyone who keeps on asking receives, and he who keeps on seeking finds, and to him who keeps on knocking, it will be opened.</J>P¶ƒÖ<J>"<f>[3]</f> Ask <i>and</i> keep on asking and it will be given to you; seek <i>and</i> keep on seeking and you will find; knock <i>and</i> keep on knocking and the door will be opened to you.</J>@¶‚yÖ<pb/><J>"Do not give that which is holy to<f>[2]</f> dogs, and do not throw your pearls before pigs, for they will trample them under their feet, and turn and tear you to pieces.</J>)¶‚KÖ<J>You hypocrite (play-actor, pretender), first get the log out of your own eye, and then you will see clearly to take the speck out of your brother's eye.</J>¶{Ö<J>Or how can you say to your brother, 'Let me get the speck out of your eye,' when there is a log in your own eye?</J>@¶‚yÖ<J>Why do you look at the <n>[insignificant]</n> speck that is in your brother's eye, but do not notice <i>and</i> acknowledge the <n>[egregious]</n> log that is in your own eye?</J>‚ ¶ƒyÖ<J>For just as you <n>[hypocritically]</n> judge others <n>[when you are sinful and unrepentant]</n>, so will you be judged; and in accordance with your standard of measure <n>[used to pass out judgment]</n>, judgment will be measured to you.</J>y¶	ƒmÖ<pb/><J>"<f>[1]</f> Do not judge <i>and</i> criticize <i>and</i> condemn <n>[others unfairly with an attitude of self-righteous superiority as though assuming the office of a judge]</n>, so that you will not be judged <n>[unfairly]</n>.</J>¶‚Ö"<pb/><J>"So do not worry about tomorrow; for tomorrow will worry about itself. Each day has enough trouble of its own.</J>s¶ƒ_Ö!<J>But first <i>and</i> most importantly seek (aim at, strive after) His kingdom and His righteousness <n>[His way of doing and being rightâ€”the attitude and character of God]</n>, and all these things will be given to you also.</J>¶‚3Ö <J>For the <n>[pagan]</n> Gentiles eagerly seek all these things; <n>[but do not worry,]</n> for your heavenly Father knows that you need them.</J>C¶‚Ö<J>Therefore do not worry <i>or</i> be anxious (perpetually uneasy, distracted), saying, 'What are we going to eat?' or 'What are we going to drink?' or 'What are we going to wear?'</J>t¶ƒaÖ<J>But if God so clothes the grass of the field, which is alive <i>and</i> green today and tomorrow is <n>[cut and]</n> thrown <n>[as fuel]</n> into the furnace, <i>will He</i> not much more <i>clothe</i> you? You of little faith!</J>¶wÖ<J>yet I say to you that not even Solomon in all his glory <i>and</i> splendor dressed himself like one of these.</J>7¶‚gÖ<J>And why are you worried about clothes? See how the lilies <i>and</i> wildflowers of the field grow; they do not labor nor do they spin <n>[wool to make clothing]</n>,</J>k¶OÖ<J>And who of you by worrying can add one<f>[12]</f> hour to <n>[the length of]</n> his life?</J>m¶
ƒSÖ<J>Look at the birds of the air; they neither sow <n>[seed]</n> nor reap <n>[the harvest]</n> nor gather <n>[the crops]</n> into barns, and yet your heavenly Father keeps feeding them. Are you not worth much more than they?</J>‚¶„-Ö<J>"Therefore I tell you, stop being worried <i>or</i> anxious (perpetually uneasy, distracted) about your life, as to what you will eat or what you will drink; nor about your body, as to what you will wear. Is life not more than food, and the body more than clothing?</J>‚¶„#Ö<pb/><J>"No one can serve two masters; for either he will hate the one and love the other, or he will be devoted to the one and despise the other. You cannot serve God and mammon <n>[money, possessions, fame, status, or whatever is valued more than the Lord]</n>.</J>‚+¶
„OÖ<J>But if your eye is bad <n>[spiritually blind]</n>, your whole body will be full of darkness <n>[devoid of God's precepts]</n>. So if the <n>[very]</n> light inside you <n>[your inner self, your heart, your conscience]</n> is darkness, how great <i>and</i> terrible is that darkness!</J>?¶	‚wÖ<pb/><J>"The eye is the lamp of the body; so if your eye is clear <n>[spiritually perceptive]</n>, your whole body will be full of light <n>[benefiting from God's precepts]</n>.</J>¶‚Ö<J>for where your treasure is, there your heart <n>[your wishes, your desires; that on which your life centers]</n> will be also.</J>¶‚!Ö<J>But store up for yourselves treasures in heaven, where neither moth nor rust destroys, and where thieves do not break in and steal;</J>¶‚5Ö<pb/><J>"Do not store up for yourselves <n>[material]</n> treasures on earth, where moth and rust destroy, and where thieves break in and steal.</J>3¶‚_Ö<J>so that your fasting will not be noticed by people, but by your Father who is in secret; and your Father who sees <n>[what is done]</n> in secret will reward you.</J>}¶sÖ<J>But when you fast, put oil on your head <n>[as you normally would to groom your hair]</n> and wash your face</J>‚K¶…Ö<J>"And whenever you are fasting, do not look gloomy like the hypocrites, for they put on a sad and dismal face <n>[like actors, discoloring their faces with ashes or dirt]</n> so that their fasting may be seen by men. I assure you <i>and</i> most solemnly say to you, they <n>[already]</n> have their reward in full.</J>O¶ƒÖ<J>But if you do not forgive others <n>[nurturing your hurt and anger with the result that it interferes with your relationship with God]</n>, then your Father will not forgive your trespasses.</J>!¶‚;Ö<pb/><J>For if you forgive<f>[11]</f> others their trespasses <n>[their reckless and willful sins]</n>, your heavenly Father will also forgive you.</J>B¶ ‚}Ö
<t><J>'And do not<f>[8]</f> lead us into temptation, but deliver us from<f>[9]</f> evil.<f>[10]</f><n>[For Yours is the kingdom and the power and the glory forever. Amen.]</n>'</J></t>µ‚/Ö<t><J>'And forgive us our<f>[7]</f> debts, as we have forgiven our debtors <n>[letting go of both the wrong and the resentment]</n></J>.</t><br/>Iµ~Ö<t><J>'Give us this day our<f>[6]</f> daily bread.</J></t><br/>µ}‚Ö
<t>'<J><f>[4]</f> Your kingdom come,</J> </t><t><J>Your<f>[5]</f> will be done</J> </t><t><J>On earth as it is in heaven.</J></t><br/>&µ|‚EÖ	<pb/><t><J>"Pray, then,<f>[2]</f> in this way:</J> </t><br/><t><J>'Our Father who is in heaven,</J> </t><t><J><f>[3]</f> Hallowed be Your name.</J></t><br/>|µ{qÖ<J>So do not be like them <n>[praying as they do]</n>; for your Father knows what you need before you ask Him.</J>µz‚5Ö<pb/><J>"And when you pray, do not use meaningless repetition as the Gentiles do, for they think they will be heard because of their many words.</J>FµyƒÖ<J>But when you pray, go into your most private room, close the door and pray to your Father who is in secret, and your Father who sees <n>[what is done]</n> in secret will reward you.</J>‚3µx„_Ö<pb/><J>"Also, when you pray, do not be like the hypocrites; for they love to pray <n>[publicly]</n> standing in the synagogues and on the corners of the streets so that they may be seen by men. I assure you <i>and</i> most solemnly say to you, they <n>[already]</n> have their reward in full.</J>µw‚Ö<J>so that your charitable acts will be done in secret; and your Father who sees <n>[what is done]</n> in secret will reward you.</J>.µv‚UÖ<J>But when you give to the poor <i>and</i> do acts of kindness, do not let your left hand know what your right hand is doing <n>[give in complete secrecy]</n>,</J>ƒ$µu†AÖ<pb/><J>"So whenever you give to the poor <i>and</i> do acts of kindness, do not blow a trumpet before you <n>[to advertise it]</n>, as the hypocrites do <n>[like actors acting out a role]</n> in the synagogues and in the streets, so that they may be honored <i>and</i> recognized <i>and</i> praised by men. I assure you <i>and</i> most solemnly say to you, they <n>[already]</n> have their reward in full.</J>Wµt	ƒ)Ö<pb/><J>"Be <n>[very]</n> careful not to do your<f>[1]</f> good deeds publicly, to be seen by men; otherwise you will have no reward <n>[prepared and awaiting you]</n> with your Father who is in heaven.</J>QµsƒÖ0<J>You, therefore, will be perfect <n>[growing into spiritual maturity both in mind and character, actively integrating godly values into your daily life]</n>, as your heavenly Father is perfect.</J>Vµrƒ%Ö/<J>And if you greet only your brothers <n>[wishing them God's blessing and peace]</n>, what more <n>[than others]</n> are you doing? Do not even the Gentiles <n>[who do not know the Lord]</n> do that?</J>µqÖ.<J>For if you love <n>[only]</n> those who love you, what reward do you have? Do not even the tax collectors do that?</J>‚Lµp…Ö-<J>so that you may <n>[show yourselves to]</n> be the children of your Father who is in heaven; for He makes His sun rise on those who are evil and on those who are good, and makes the rain fall on the righteous <n>[those who are morally upright]</n> and the unrighteous <n>[the unrepentant, those who oppose Him]</n>.</J>%µo‚CÖ,<J>"But I say to you,<f>[14]</f> love <n>[that is, unselfishly seek the best or higher good for]</n> your enemies and pray for those who persecute you,</J>µnwÖ+<pb/><J>"You have heard that it was said, '<e>You shall love your neighbor</e> (fellow man) and hate your enemy.'</J>iµmKÖ*<J>Give to him who asks of you, and do not turn away from him who wants to borrow from you.</J>SµlÖ)<J>And whoever<f>[13]</f> forces you to go one mile, go with him two.</J>µk‚Ö(<J>If anyone wants to sue you and take your shirt,<f>[12]</f> let him have your coat also <n>[for the Lord repays the offender]</n>.</J>‚[µj…/Ö'<J>But I say to you, do not resist an evil person <n>[who insults you or violates your rights]</n>; but whoever<f>[11]</f> slaps you on the right cheek, turn the other toward him also <n>[simply ignore insignificant insults or trivial losses and do not bother to retaliateâ€”maintain your dignity, your self-respect, your poise]</n>.</J>µi‚%Ö&<pb/><J>"You have heard that it was said, '<e>An eye for an eye, and a tooth for a tooth</e> <n>[punishment that fits the offense]</n>.'</J>µh‚Ö%<J>But let your statement be, 'Yes, yes' or 'No, no' <n>[a firm yes or no]</n>; anything more than that comes from the evil one.</J>tµgaÖ$<J>Nor shall you make an oath by your head, for you are not able to make a single hair white or black.</J>µf‚Ö#<J>or by the earth, for it is the footstool of His feet; or by Jerusalem, for it is <e>the city of the Great King</e>.</J>mµeSÖ"<J>But I say to you, do not make an oath at all, either by heaven, for it is the throne of God;</J>Bµd‚}Ö!<pb/><J>"Again, you have heard that it was said to the men of old, '<e>You shall not make false vows, but you shall fulfill your vows to the Lord</e> <n>[as a religious duty]</n>.'</J>LµcƒÖ <J>but I say to you that whoever divorces his wife, except on grounds of sexual immorality, causes her to commit adultery; and whoever marries a woman who has been divorced commits adultery.</J>yµbkÖ<pb/><J>"It has also been said, '<e>Whoever divorces his wife is to give her a certificate of divorce</e>';</J>‚µa„+Ö<J>If your right hand makes you stumble <i>and</i> leads you to sin, cut it off and throw it away <n>[that is, remove yourself from the source of temptation]</n>; for it is better for you to lose one of the parts of your body than for your whole body to go into hell.</J>‚!µ`„;Ö<J>If your right eye makes you stumble <i>and</i> leads you to sin, tear it out and throw it away <n>[that is, remove yourself from the source of temptation]</n>; for it is better for you to lose one of the parts of your body, than for your whole body to be thrown into hell.</J> µ_‚9Ö<J>but I say to you that everyone who <n>[so much as]</n> looks at a woman with lust for her has already committed adultery with her in his heart.</J>_µ^7Ö<pb/><J>"You have heard that it was said, '<e>You shall not commit adultery</e>';</J>µ]‚Ö<J>I assure you <i>and</i> most solemnly say to you, you will not come out of there until you have paid the last<f>[10]</f> cent.</J>‚µ\„Ö<J>Come to terms quickly <n>[at the earliest opportunity]</n> with your opponent at law while you are with him on the way <n>[to court]</n>, so that your opponent does not hand you over to the judge, and the judge to the guard, and you are thrown into prison.</J>µ[‚Ö<J>leave your offering there at the altar and go. First make peace with your brother, and then come and present your offering.</J>KµZƒÖ<J>So if you are presenting your offering at the altar, and <i>while</i> there you remember that your brother has something <n>[such as a grievance or legitimate complaint]</n> against you,</J>ƒµY†-Ö<J>But I say to you that everyone who continues to be angry with his brother <i>or</i> harbors malice against him shall be guilty before the court; and whoever speaks <n>[contemptuously and insultingly]</n> to his brother,<f>[8]</f> Raca (You empty-headed idiot)!' shall be guilty before the supreme court (Sanhedrin); and whoever says, 'You fool!' shall be in danger of the<f>[9]</f> fiery hell.</J>%µX‚CÖ<J>"You have heard that it was said to the men of old, '<e>You shall not murder</e>,' and 'Whoever murders shall be<f>[7]</f> guilty before the court.'</J>?µW‚wÖ<pb/><J>"For I say to you that unless your righteousness (uprightness, moral essence) is more than that of the scribes and Pharisees, you will never enter the kingdom of heaven.</J>‚µV„1Ö<J>So whoever breaks one of the least <n>[important]</n> of these commandments, and teaches others to do the same, will be called least <n>[important]</n> in the kingdom of heaven; but whoever practices and teaches them, he will be called great in the kingdom of heaven.</J>vµUƒeÖ<J>For I assure you <i>and</i> most solemnly say to you, until heaven and earth pass away, not the smallest letter or stroke <n>[of the pen]</n> will pass from the Law until all things <n>[which it foreshadows]</n> are accomplished.</J>FµTƒÖ<pb/><J>"Do not think that I came to do away with <i>or</i> undo the<f>[6]</f> Law <n>[of Moses]</n> or the <n>[writings of the]</n> Prophets; I did not come to destroy but to fulfill.</J>HµSƒ	Ö<J>Let your light shine before men in such a way that they may see your good deeds <i>and</i> moral excellence, and <n>[recognize and honor and]</n> glorify your Father who is in heaven.</J>µR‚Ö<J>nor does <i>anyone</i> light a lamp and put it under a basket, but on a lampstand, and it gives light to all who are in the house.</J>pµQYÖ<pb/><J>"You are the light of <n>[Christ to]</n> the world. A city set on a hill cannot be hidden;</J>‚
µP„Ö
<J>"You are the<f>[4]</f> salt of the earth; but if the salt has<f>[5]</f> lost its taste (purpose), how can it be made salty? It is no longer good for anything, but to be thrown out and walked on by people <n>[when the walkways are wet and slippery]</n>.</J>=µO‚sÖ<J>Be glad and exceedingly joyful, for your reward in heaven is great <n>[absolutely inexhaustible]</n>; for in this same way they persecuted the prophets who were before you.</J>‚µN„Ö<pb/><J>"Blessed <n>[morally courageous and spiritually alive with life-joy in God's goodness]</n> are you when <i>people</i> insult you and persecute you, and falsely say all kinds of evil things against you because of <n>[your association with]</n> Me.</J>`µMƒ9Ö
<pb/><J>"Blessed <n>[comforted by inner peace and God's love]</n> are those who are persecuted for<f>[3]</f> doing that which is morally right, for theirs is the kingdom of heaven <n>[both now and forever]</n>.</J>QµLƒÖ	<pb/><J>"Blessed <n>[spiritually calm with life-joy in God's favor]</n> are the makers <i>and</i> maintainers of peace, for they will <n>[express His character and]</n> be called the sons of God.</J>GµKƒÖ<pb/><J>"Blessed <n>[anticipating God's presence, spiritually mature]</n> are the pure in heart <n>[those with integrity, moral courage, and godly character]</n>, for they will see God.</J>{µJoÖ<pb/><J>"Blessed <n>[content, sheltered by God's promises]</n> are the merciful, for they will receive mercy.</J>gµIƒGÖ<pb/><J>"Blessed <n>[joyful, nourished by God's goodness]</n> are those who hunger and thirst for righteousness <n>[those who actively seek right standing with God]</n>, for they will be <n>[completely]</n> satisfied.</J>^µHƒ5Ö<pb/><J>"Blessed <n>[inwardly peaceful, spiritually secure, worthy of respect]</n> are the<f>[2]</f> gentle <n>[the kind-hearted, the sweet-spirited, the self-controlled]</n>, for they will inherit the earth.</J>IµGƒÖ<pb/><J>"Blessed <n>[forgiven, refreshed by God's grace]</n> are those who mourn <n>[over their sins and repent]</n>, for they will be comforted <n>[when the burden of sin is lifted]</n>.</J>‚
