Ö<pb/><J>"Blessed <n>[spiritually prosperous, happy, to be admired]</n> are the poor in spirit <n>[those devoid of spiritual arrogance, those who regard themselves as insignificant]</n>, for theirs is the kingdom of heaven <n>[both now and forever]</n>.</J>4µEcÖThen He <i>began</i> to teach them, saying,µD	}Ö<pb/>When Jesus saw the crowds, He went up on the mountain; and when He was seated, His<f>[1]</f> disciples came to Him.µC‚ÖLarge crowds followed Him from Galilee and the<f>[4]</f> Decapolis and Jerusalem and Judea and the other side of the Jordan.nµBƒUÖ<pb/>So the news about Him spread throughout all Syria; and they brought to Him all who were sick, those suffering with various diseases and pains, those under the power of demons, and epileptics, paralytics; and He healed them.‚µA„/ÖAnd He went throughout all Galilee, teaching in their synagogues and preaching the good news (gospel) of the kingdom, and healing every kind of disease and every kind of sickness among the people <n>[demonstrating and revealing that He was indeed the promised Messiah]</n>.%µ@‚CÖImmediately they left the boat and their father, and followed Him <n>[becoming His disciples, believing and trusting in Him and following His example]</n>.‚	µ?„ÖAnd going on <n>[further]</n> from there He noticed two other brothers, James the <i>son</i> of Zebedee, and his brother John, in the boat with their father<f>[3]</f> Zebedee, mending their nets; and He called them <n>[to follow Him as His disciples]</n>.µ>‚#ÖImmediately they left their nets and followed Him <n>[becoming His disciples, believing and trusting in Him and following His example]</n>.Qµ=ƒÖAnd He said to them, <J>"<f>[2]</f> Follow Me <n>[as My disciples, accepting Me as your Master and Teacher and walking the same path of life that I walk]</n>, and I will make you fishers of men."</J>7µ<‚gÖAs Jesus was walking by the Sea of Galilee, He noticed tw