Ö<pb/>Then the devil took Him into the holy city <n>[Jerusalem]</n> and placed Him on the pinnacle (highest point) of the temple.9µ.‚kÖBut Jesus replied, <J>"It is written <i>and</i> forever remains written, '<e>Man shall not live by bread alone, but by every word that comes out of the mouth of God</e>.'"</J>tµ-aÖAnd the tempter came and said to Him, "If You are the Son of God, command that these stones become bread."[µ,/ÖAfter He had gone without food for forty days and forty nights, He became hungry.lµ+	SÖ<pb/>Then Jesus was led by the <n>[Holy]</n> Spirit into the wilderness to be tempted by the devil.µ*‚Öand behold, a<f>[13]</f> voice from heaven said, "This is My beloved Son, in whom I am well-pleased <i>and</i> delighted!"Rµ)ƒÖAfter Jesus was baptized, He came up immediately out of the water; and behold, the heavens were opened, and he (John) saw the<f>[12]</f> Spirit of God descending as a dove and lighting on Him (Jesus),>µ(‚uÖBut Jesus replied to him, <J>"Permit it just now; for this is the fitting way for us<f>[11]</f> to fulfill all righteousness."</J> Then John permitted <n>[it and baptized]</n> Him.µ'‚ÖBut John tried to prevent Him <n>[vigorously protesting]</n>, saying, "It is I who need to be baptized by You, and do You come to me?"cµ&?Ö
Then Jesus came from Galilee to John at the Jordan <n>[River]</n>, to be baptized by him.xµ%ƒiÖHis<f>[10]</f> winnowing fork is in His hand, and He will thoroughly clear out His threshing floor; and He will gather His wheat (believers) into His barn (kingdom), but He will burn up the chaff (the unrepentant) with unquenchable fire."„µ$ˆ1Ö<pb/>"As for me, I baptize you<f>[8]</f> with water because of <n>[your]</n> repentance <n>[that is, because you are willing to change your inner selfâ€”your old way of thinking, regret your sin and live a changed life]</n>, but He (the Messiah) who is coming after me is mightier <n>[more powerful, more noble]</n> than I, whose sandals I am not worthy to remove <n>[even as His slave]</n>; He will baptize you <n>[who truly repent]</n> with the Holy Spirit and <n>[you who remain unrepentant]</n> with<f>[9]</f> fire (judgment).Eµ#ƒÖ
And already the axe <n>[of God's judgment]</n> is<f>[7]</f> swinging toward the root of the trees; therefore every tree that does not bear good fruit is cut down and thrown into the fire.‚µ"ƒ}Ö	and do not presume to say to yourselves <n>[as a defense]</n>, 'We have Abraham for our father <n>[so our inheritance assures us of salvation]</n>'; for I say to you that from these stones God is able to raise up children (descendants) for Abraham.0µ!‚YÖSo produce fruit that is consistent with repentance <n>[demonstrating new behavior that proves a change of heart, and a conscious decision to turn away from sin]</n>;dµ ƒAÖ<pb/>But when he saw many of the<f>[5]</f> Pharisees and<f>[6]</f> Sadducees coming for baptism, he said to them, "You brood of vipers, who warned you to flee from the <n>[divine]</n> wrath <i>and</i> judgment to come?`µ9Öand they were being baptized by him in the Jordan River, as they confessed their sins.lµQÖAt that time Jerusalem was going out to him, and all Judea and all the district around the Jordan;)µ‚KÖ<pb/>Now this same John had clothing made of camel's hair and a <n>[wide]</n> leather<f>[4]</f> band around his waist; and his food was locusts and wild honey.‚µ„Ö<t>This is the one who was mentioned by the prophet Isaiah when he said, </t><br/><t>"<e>The voice of one shouting in the wilderness</e>, </t><t>'<e>Prepare the road for the Lord</e>, </t><t><f>[3]</f><e>Make His highways straight</e> (level, direct)!'"</t>cµƒ?Ö"<f>[2]</f> Repent <n>[change your inner selfâ€”your old way of thinking, regret past sins, live your life in a way that proves repentance; seek God's purpose for your life]</n>, for the kingdom of heaven is at hand."!µ	‚=Ö<pb/>In those days<f>[1]</f> John the Baptist appeared, preaching in the Wilderness of Judea <n>[along the western side of the Dead Sea]</n> and saying,&µ‚EÖand went and settled in a city called Nazareth. <i>This was</i> to fulfill what was spoken through the prophets: "He shall be called a<f>[10]</f> Nazarene."eµƒCÖBut when he heard that Archelaus was ruling over Judea<f>[9]</f> in place of his father Herod <n>[the Great]</n>, he was afraid to go there. Then being warned <i>by God</i> in a dream, he left for the region of Galilee,bµ=ÖThen Joseph got up, and took the Child and His mother, and came into the land of Israel. µyÖ"Get up! Take the Child and His mother, and go to the land of Israel; for those who sought the Child's life are dead."tµaÖ<pb/>But when<f>[8]</f> Herod died, an angel of the Lord appeared in a dream to Joseph in Egypt, and said,‚µƒ{Ö<pb/><t>"<e>A voice was heard in</e><f>[6]</f><e>Ramah</e>, </t><t><e>Weeping and great mourning</e>, </t><t><f>[7]</f><e>Rachel weeping for her children</e>; </t><t><e>She refused to be comforted</e>, </t><t><e>Because they were no more</e>."</t>Vµ%Ö<t>Then what had been spoken through Jeremiah the prophet was fulfilled:</t>‚$µ„AÖThen Herod, when he realized that he had been tricked by the magi, was extremely angry, and he sent <n>[soldiers]</n> and put to death all the male children in Bethlehem and in all that area who were two years old and under, according to the date which he had learned from the magi./µ‚WÖHe remained there until the death of Herod. <i>This was</i> to fulfill what the Lord had spoken by the prophet <n>[Hosea]</n>: "<e>Out of Egypt I called My Son</e>."oµWÖ<pb/>So Joseph got up and took the Child and His mother while it was still night, and left for Egypt.µƒwÖ
