W	´¬­sÀ'>ŠŠÊ                                                                            ;·j‚oÖ(<J>for just as <e>Jonah was three days and three nights in the belly of the sea monster</e>, so will the Son of Man be three days and three nights in the heart of the earth.</J>{·iƒoÖ'But He replied and said to them, <J>"An evil and adulterous generation <n>[that is morally unfaithful to God]</n> craves <i>and</i> demands a <n>[miraculous]</n> sign; but no sign will be given to it except the sign of the prophet Jonah;</J>/·h‚WÖ&Then some of the scribes and Pharisees said to Him, "Teacher, we want to see a sign (attesting miracle) from You <n>[proving that You are what You claim to be]</n>."d·gƒAÖ%<J>For by your words <n>[reflecting your spiritual condition]</n> you will be justified <i>and</i> acquitted of the guilt of sin; and by your words <n>[rejecting Me]</n> you will be condemned <i>and</i> sentenced."</J>·f‚!Ö$<J>But I tell you, on the day of judgment people will have to give an accounting for every careless <i>or</i> useless word they speak.</J>.·e‚UÖ#<J>The good man, from his <n>[inner]</n> good treasure, brings out good things; and the evil man, from his <n>[inner]</n> evil treasure, brings out evil things.</J>·d‚Ö"<J>You brood of vipers, how can you speak good things when you are evil? For the mouth speaks out of that which fills the heart.</J>"·c‚=Ö!<J>"Either make the tree good and its fruit good, or make the tree bad and its fruit bad; for the tree is recognized <i>and</i> judged by its fruit.</J>z·bƒmÖ <J>Whoever speaks a word against the Son of Man will be forgiven; but whoever speaks against the Holy Spirit <n>[by attributing the miracles done by Me to Satan]</n> will not be forgiven, either in this age or in the <i>age</i> to come.</J>‚·aƒÖ<pb/><J>"Therefore I say to you, every sin and blasphemy <n>[every evil, abusive, injurious speaking, or indignity against sacred things]</n> will be forgiven people, but<f>[6]</f> blasphemy against the <n>[Holy]</n> Spirit will not be forgiven.</J>·`‚5Ö<J>He who is not with Me <n>[once and for all on My side]</n> is against Me; and he who does not <n>[unequivocally]</n> gather with Me scatters.</J>C·_‚Ö<J>Or how can anyone go into a strong man's house and steal his property unless he first overpowers <i>and</i> ties up the strong man? Then he will ransack <i>and</i> rob his house.</J>·^‚+Ö<J>But if it is by the Spirit of God that I cast out the demons, then the kingdom of God has come upon you <n>[before you expected it]</n>.</J>#·]‚?Ö<J>If I cast out the demons by <n>[the help of]</n> Beelzebul (Satan), by whom do your sons drive them out? For this reason they will be your judges.</J>$·\‚AÖ<J>If Satan casts out Satan <n>[that is, his demons]</n>, he has become divided against himself <i>and</i> disunited; how then will his kingdom stand?</J>N·[ƒÖ<pb/>Knowing their thoughts Jesus said to them, <J>"Any kingdom that is divided against itself is being laid waste; and no city or house divided against itself will <n>[continue to]</n> stand.</J>·Z‚3ÖBut the Pharisees heard it and said, "This man<f>[5]</f> casts out demons only by <n>[the help of]</n> Beelzebul (Satan) the prince of the demons."i·YKÖAll the people wondered in amazement, and said, "Could this be the Son of David (the Messiah)?"
·X‚ÖThen a demon-possessed man who was blind and mute was brought to Jesus, and He healed him, so that the mute man both spoke and saw.·W‚Ö<t>"<e>And in His name the Gentiles</e> (all the nations of the world) <e>will hope</e> <n>[with confidence]</n>."</t><br/>-·V‚SÖ<t>"<e>A battered reed He will not break</e>, </t><t><e>And a smoldering wick He will not extinguish</e>, </t><t><e>Until He leads justice to victory</e>.</t><br/>·UÖ<t>"<e>He will not quarrel, nor cry out loudly</e>; </t><t><e>Nor will anyone hear His voice in the streets</e>.</t><br/>k·TƒOÖ<pb/><t>"<e>Behold, My Servant whom I have chosen</e>; </t><t><e>My Beloved in whom My soul is well-pleased</e>; </t><t><e>I will put My Spirit upon Him</e>, </t><t><e>And He will proclaim justice to the nations</e>.</t><br/>R·SÖ<t><i>This was</i> to fulfill what was spoken by the prophet Isaiah:</t>B·RÖand warned them not to tell <n>[publicly]</n> who He was.z·QmÖ<pb/>Being aware of this, Jesus left there. Many followed Him, and He healed all of them <n>[who were sick]</n>,m·PSÖBut the Pharisees went out and conspired against Him, <i>discussing</i> how they could destroy Him.·O‚!Ö
