ÖBut Jesus, aware of this, said, <J>"You men of little faith, why are you discussing among yourselves that you have no bread?</J>t¹ aÖThey began to discuss this among themselves, saying, "<i>He said that</i> because we did not bring bread."¸}ÖJesus said to them, <J>"Watch out and be on your guard against the<f>[2]</f> leaven of the Pharisees and Sadducees."</J>¸~{Ö<pb/>When the disciples reached the other side <i>of the sea</i>, they realized that they had forgotten to bring bread.X¸}ƒ)Ö<J>An evil and <n>[morally]</n> unfaithful generation craves a <n>[miraculous]</n> sign; but no sign will be given to it, except the sign of <n>[the prophet]</n> Jonah."</J> Then He left them and went away.W¸|ƒ'Ö<J>And in the morning, '<i>It will be</i> stormy today, for the sky is red and has a threatening look.' You know how to interpret the appearance of the sky, but cannot interpret the signs of the times?</J>¸{‚ÖBut He replied to them, <J>"<f>[1]</f> When it is evening, you say, '<i>It will be</i> fair weather, for the sky is red.'</J>X¸z	ƒ+Ö<pb/>Now the Pharisees and Sadducees came up, and testing Jesus <n>[to get something to use against Him]</n>, they asked Him to show them a sign from heaven <n>[which would support His divine authority]</n>.p¸yYÖ'<pb/>Then Jesus sent the crowds away, got into the boat and went to the district of<f>[7]</f> Magadan.W¸x'Ö&<n>[Among]</n> those who ate were 4,000 men, not counting women and children. ¸wyÖ%And they all ate and were satisfied, and they gathered up seven full baskets of the broken pieces that were left over.>¸v‚uÖ$and He took the seven loaves and the fish; and when He had given thanks, He broke them and started giving them to the disciples, and the disciples <n>[gave them]</n> to the people.9¸umÖ#He directed the crowd to sit down on the ground,¸t‚Ö"And Jesus asked them, <J>"How many loaves <n>[of bread]</n> do you