sº0_Ö<J>And he answered, 'I will not'; but afterward he regretted it <i>and</i> changed his mind and went.</J>º/‚Ö<J>"What do you think? There was a man who had two sons, and he came to the first and said, 'Son, go and work in the vineyard today.'</J>º.‚7ÖSo they answered Jesus, "We do not know." And He said to them, <J>"Neither will I tell you by what <n>[kind of]</n> authority I do these things."</J>º-{ÖBut if we say, 'From men,' we are afraid of the <n>[response of the]</n> crowd; for they all regard John as a prophet."‚<º,„qÖ<J>The baptism of Johnâ€”from where did it come? From heaven <n>[that is, ordained by God]</n> or from men?"</J> And they <i>began</i> debating among themselves <n>[considering the implications of their answer]</n>, saying, "If we say, 'From heaven,' He will say to us, 'Then why did you not believe John?'!º+‚;ÖJesus replied to them, <J>"I will also ask you a question, and if you tell Me the answer, then I will tell you by what authority I do these things.</J>‚º*„ÖWhen He entered the temple <i>area</i>, the<f>[5]</f> chief priests and elders of the people came to Him as He was teaching and said, "By what <n>[kind of]</n> authority are You doing these things, and who gave You this authority <n>[to exercise this power]</n>?"Rº)Ö<J>And whatever you ask for in prayer, believing, you will receive."</J>ƒº(†ÖJesus replied to them, <J>"I assure you <i>and</i> most solemnly say to you, if you have faith <n>[personal trust and confidence in Me]</n> and do not doubt <i>or</i> allow yourself to be drawn in two directions, you will not only do what was done to the fig tree, but even if you say to this mountain, 'Be taken up and thrown into the sea,' it will happen <n>[if God wills it]</n>.</J>º'‚Ö<pb/>When the disciples saw it, they were astonished and asked, "How is it that the fig tree has withered away all at once?"Hº&ƒ	ÖSeeing a lone fig tree at the roadside, He went to it and found nothing but leaves on it; and He said to it, <J>"Never again will fruit come from you."</J> And at once the fig tree withered.Xº%)ÖNow early in the morning, as Jesus was coming back to the city, He was hungry.[º$/ÖThen He left them and went out of the city to Bethany, and spent the night there.‚'º#„GÖand they said to Him, "Do You hear what these <i>children</i> are saying?" And Jesus replied to them, <J>"Yes; have you never read <n>[in the Scripture]</n>, '<e>Out of the mouths of infants and nursing babies You have prepared</e> <i>and</i> <e>provided praise for Yourself</e>'?"</J>‚Fº"…ÖBut when the chief priests and the scribes saw the wonderful <i>and</i> miraculous things that Jesus had done, and <i>heard</i> the<f>[4]</f> boys who were shouting in <n>[the porticoes and courts of]</n> the temple <n>[in praise and adoration]</n>, "Hosanna to the Son of David (the Messiah)," they became indignant	º!‚Ö<pb/>And the blind and the lame came to Him in <n>[the porticoes and courts of]</n> the temple <i>area</i>, and He healed them.-º ‚SÖ
