<pb/>The disciples said to Jesus, "If the relationship of a man with his wife is like this, it is better not to marry."¹\‚Ö	<J>I say to you, whoever divorces his wife, except for sexual immorality, and marries another woman commits adultery<f>[1]</f>."</J>0¹[‚YÖHe said to them, <J>"Because your hearts were hard <i>and</i> stubborn Moses permitted you to divorce your wives; but from the beginning it has not been this way.</J>¹ZÖThe Pharisees said to Him, "Why then did Moses command us to <e>give her a certificate of divorce and send her away</e>?"y¹YkÖ<J>So they are no longer two, but one flesh. Therefore, what God has joined together, let no one separate."</J>,¹X‚QÖ<J>and said, '<e>For this reason a man shall leave his father and mother and shall be joined inseparably to his wife, and the two shall become one flesh</e>'?</J>¹WwÖHe replied, <J>"Have you never read that He who created them from the beginning <e>made them male and female</e>,</J>¹V‚Ö<pb/>And Pharisees came to Jesus, testing Him and asking, "Is it lawful for a man to divorce his wife for just any reason?"A¹U}Öand large crowds followed Him, and He healed them there.	¹T	‚
Ö<pb/>Now when Jesus had finished saying these things, He left Galilee and went into the part of Judea that is beyond the Jordan;¹S‚#Ö#<J>My heavenly Father will also do the same to <n>[every one of]</n> you, if each of you does not forgive his brother from your heart."</J>s¹R_Ö"<J>And in wrath his master turned him over to the torturers (jailers) until he paid all that he owed.</J>¹Q‚Ö!<J>Should you not have had mercy on your fellow slave <n>[who owed you little by comparison]</n>, as I had mercy on you?'</J>.¹P‚UÖ <J>Then his master called him and said to him, 'You wicked <i>and</i> contemptible slave, I forgave all that <n>[great]</n> debt of yours because you begged me.</J>G¹OƒÖ<J>When his fellow slaves saw what had happened, they were deeply grieved and they went and reported to their master <n>[with clarity and in detail]</n> everything that had taken place.</J>k¹NOÖ<J>But he was unwilling and he went and had him thrown in prison until he paid back the debt.</J>~¹MuÖ<J>So his fellow slave fell on his knees and begged him earnestly, 'Have patience with me and I will repay you.'</J>G¹LƒÖ<J>But that same slave went out and found one of his fellow slaves who owed him<f>[10]</f> a hundred denarii; and he seized him and <i>began</i> choking him, saying, 'Pay what you owe!'</J>¹K}Ö<J>And his master's heart was moved with compassion and he released him and forgave him <n>[canceling]</n> the debt.</J> ¹JyÖ<J>So the slave fell on his knees and begged him, saying, 'Have patience with me and I will repay you everything.'</J>-¹I‚SÖ<J>"But because he could not repay, his master ordered him to be sold, with his wife and his children and everything that he possessed, and payment to be made.</J>l¹HQÖ<J>When he began the accounting, one who owed him 10,000<f>[9]</f> talents was brought to him.</J>t¹GaÖ<pb/><J>"Therefore the kingdom of heaven is like a king who wished to settle accounts with his slaves.</J>c¹F?ÖJesus answered him, <J>"I say to you, not up to seven times, but seventy times seven.</J>¹E‚1ÖThen Peter came to Him and asked, "Lord, how many times will my brother sin against me and I forgive him <i>and</i> let it go? Up to seven times?"¹D}Ö<J>For where two or three are gathered in My name <n>[meeting together as My followers]</n>, I am there among them."</J>v¹CƒeÖ<pb/><J>"Again I say to you, that if two<f>[8]</f> believers on earth agree <n>[that is, are of one mind, in harmony]</n> about anything that they ask <n>[within the will of God]</n>, it will be done for them by My Father in heaven.</J>‚K¹B…Ö<J>I assure you <i>and</i> most solemnly say to you, whatever you bind <n>[forbid, declare to be improper and unlawful]</n> on earth<f>[6]</f> shall have <n>[already]</n> been bound in heaven, and whatever you loose <n>[permit, declare lawful]</n> on earth<f>[7]</f> shall have <n>[already]</n> been loosed in heaven.</J>h¹AƒIÖ<J>If he pays no attention to them <n>[refusing to listen and obey]</n>, tell it to the<f>[5]</f> church; and if he refuses to listen even to the church, let him be to you as a Gentile (unbeliever) and a tax collector.</J>)¹@‚KÖ<J>But if he does not listen, take along with you one or two others, so that <e>every word may be confirmed by the testimony of two or three witnesses</e>.</J>'¹?‚GÖ<J>"If your brother sins<f>[4]</f>, go and show him his fault in private; if he listens <i>and</i> pays attention to you, you have won back your brother.</J>m¹>SÖ<J>So it is not the will of your Father who is in heaven that one of these little ones be lost.</J>2¹=‚]Ö
