<pb/><J>"See that you do not despise <i>or</i> think less of one of these little ones, for I say to you that their angels in heaven <n>[are in the presence of and]</n> continually look upon the face of My Father who is in heaven.</J>‚¹9„-Ö	<J>If your eye causes you to stumble <i>and</i> sin, pluck it out and throw it away from you <n>[that is, remove yourself from the source of temptation]</n>; it is better for you to enter life with only one eye, than to have two eyes and be thrown into the fiery hell.</J>‚:¹8„mÖ<pb/><J>"If your hand or your foot causes you to stumble <i>and</i> sin, cut it off and throw it away from you <n>[that is, remove yourself from the source of temptation]</n>; it is better for you to enter life crippled or lame, than to have two hands or two feet and be thrown into everlasting fire.</J>x¹7ƒiÖ<J>"Woe (judgment is coming) to the world because of stumbling blocks <i>and</i> temptations to sin! It is inevitable that stumbling blocks come; but woe to the person on whose account <i>or</i> through whom the stumbling block comes!</J>‚8¹6„iÖ<J>but whoever causes one of these little ones who believe in Me to stumble <i>and</i> sin <n>[by leading him away from My teaching]</n>, it would be better for him to have a heavy millstone <n>[as large as one turned by a donkey]</n> hung around his neck and to be drowned in the depth of the sea.</J>k¹5OÖ<J>Whoever receives <i>and</i> welcomes one<f>[2]</f> child like this in My name receives Me;</J>s¹4_Ö<J>Therefore, whoever<f>[1]</f> humbles himself like this child is greatest in the kingdom of heaven.</J>‚&¹3„EÖand said, <J>"I assure you <i>and</i> most solemnly say to you, unless you repent <n>[that is, change your inner selfâ€”your old way of thinking, live changed lives]</n> and become like children <n>[trusting, humble, and forgiving]</n>, you will never enter the kingdom of heaven.</J>:¹2oÖHe called a little child and set him before them,