Ö7<pb/>At that moment Jesus said to the crowds, <J>"Have you come out with swords and clubs to arrest Me as <i>you would</i> against a robber? Day after day I used to sit in the porches <i>and</i> courts of the temple teaching, and you did not arrest Me.</J>Z¼--Ö6<J>How then will the Scriptures be fulfilled, that it must happen this way?"</J>¼,‚'Ö5<J>Do you think that I cannot appeal to My Father, and He will immediately provide Me with more than twelve<f>[22]</f> legions of angels?</J>¼+‚#Ö4Then Jesus said to him, <J>"Put your sword back in its place; for all those who <i>habitually</i> draw the sword will die by the sword.</J>,¼*‚QÖ3<pb/>And<f>[21]</f> one of those who were with Jesus reached out and drew his sword, and struck <n>[Malchus]</n> the slave of the high priest and cut off his ear.w¼)gÖ2Jesus said to Judas, <J>"Friend, do what you came for."</J> Then they came and seized Jesus and arrested Him.¼(‚)Ö1Immediately Judas went to Jesus and said, "Greetings (rejoice), Rabbi!" And he<f>[20]</f> kissed Him <n>[in a deliberate act of betrayal]</n>.f¼'EÖ0Now the betrayer had given them a sign, saying, "Whomever I kiss, He is the one; seize Him."w¼&ƒgÖ/As Jesus was still speaking, Judas <n>[Iscariot]</n>, one of the twelve <n>[disciples]</n>, came up accompanied by a large crowd with swords and clubs, <n>[who came as representatives]</n> from the chief priests and elders of the people.>¼%wÖ.<J>Get up, let us go. Look, My betrayer is near!"</J>‚¼$„)Ö-Then He returned to the disciples and said to them, <J>"Are you still sleeping and resting? Listen,<f>[19]</f> the hour <n>[of My sacrifice]</n> is at hand and the Son of Man is being betrayed into the hands of sinners <n>[whose way and nature is to oppose God]</n>.</J>n¼#UÖ,So, leaving them again, He went away and prayed for the third time, saying the same words once more.K¼"Ö+Again He came and found them sleeping, for their eyes were heavy.¼!‚Ö*<pb/>He went away a second time and prayed, saying, <J>"My Father, if this cannot pass away unless I drink it, Your will be done."</J>¼ ‚-Ö)<J>Keep <i>actively</i> watching and praying that you may not come into temptation; the spirit is willing, but the<f>[18]</f> body is weak."</J>.¼‚UÖ(And He came to the disciples and found them sleeping, and said to Peter, <J>"So, you <i>men</i> could not stay awake <i>and</i> keep watch with Me for one hour?</J>s¼ƒ_Ö'<pb/>And after going a little farther, He fell face down and prayed, saying, <J>"My Father, if it is possible <n>[that is, consistent with Your will]</n>, let this cup<f>[17]</f> pass from Me; yet not as I will, but as You will."</J>'¼‚GÖ&Then He said to them, <J>"My soul is deeply grieved, so that I am almost dying <i>of sorrow</i>. Stay here and stay awake <i>and</i> keep watch with Me."</J>¼‚Ö%And taking with Him Peter and the two sons of Zebedee <n>[James and John]</n>, He began to be grieved and greatly distressed.'¼‚GÖ$Then Jesus came with them to a place called<f>[16]</f> Gethsemane (olive-press), and He told His disciples, <J>"Sit here while I go over there and pray."</J> ¼yÖ#Peter said to Jesus, "Even if I have to die with You, I will not deny You!" And all the disciples said the same thing.-¼‚SÖ"Jesus said to him, <J>"I assure you <i>and</i> most solemnly say to you, this night, before a rooster crows, you will <n>[completely]</n> deny Me three times."</J>¼‚Ö!Peter replied to Him, "Though they all fall away because of You <n>[and doubt and disown You]</n>, I will never fall away!"u¼cÖ <J>But after I am raised <n>[to life]</n>, I will go ahead of you <n>[leading the way]</n> to Galilee."</J>‚(¼„IÖ<pb/>Then Jesus said to them, <J>"You will all fall away because of Me this night <n>[disillusioned about Me, confused, and some even ashamed of Me]</n>, for it is written <n>[in the Scriptures]</n>, '<e>I will strike the Shepherd, and the sheep of the flock will be scattered</e>.'</J>U¼#Ö<pb/>After singing a<f>[15]</f> hymn, they went out to the Mount of Olives.¼‚5Ö<J>But I say to you, I will not drink of this fruit of the vine from now on until that day when I drink it new with you in My Father's kingdom."</J>k¼ƒOÖ<J>for this is My blood of the <n>[new and better]</n> covenant, which <n>[ratifies the agreement and]</n> is being poured out for many <n>[as a<f>[14]</f></J>substitutionary atonement]</n> <J>for the forgiveness of sins.</J>¼{ÖAnd when He had taken a cup and<f>[13]</f> given thanks, He gave it to them, saying, <J>"Drink from it, all of you;</J>.¼‚UÖNow as they were eating Jesus took bread, and after<f>[12]</f> blessing it, He broke it and gave it to the disciples, and said, <J>"Take, eat; this is My body."</J>¼‚	ÖAnd Judas, the betrayer, said, "Surely it is not I, Rabbi?" Jesus said to him, <J>"<f>[11]</f> You have said it yourself."</J>‚¼ƒ{Ö<J>The Son of Man is to go <n>[to the cross]</n>, just as it is written <n>[in Scripture]</n> of Him; but woe (judgment is coming) to that man by whom the Son of Man is betrayed! It would have been good for that man if he had never been born."</J>¼‚%ÖJesus answered, <J>"He who has dipped his hand in the bowl with Me <n>[as a<f>[10]</f></J>pretense of friendship]</n> <J>will betray Me.</J>{¼
