e bystanders there heard it, they <i>began</i> saying, "This man is calling for<f>[11]</f> Elijah."M¼pƒÖ.About the ninth hour Jesus cried out with a loud <n>[agonized]</n> voice, <J><f>[10]</f>"<e>Eli, Eli, lama sabachthani</e>?"</J> that is, <J>"<e>My God, My God, why have You forsaken Me</e>?"</J>t¼oaÖ-<pb/>Now from the sixth hour (noon) there was darkness over all the land until the ninth hour (3:00 p.m.)._¼n7Ö,The robbers who had been crucified with Him also began to insult Him in the same way.¼m‚Ö+<e>He trusts in God; let God rescue</e> <i>Him</i> now, <e>if He delights in Him</e>; for He said, 'I am the Son of God.'">¼l‚uÖ*"He saved others <n>[from death]</n>; He cannot save Himself. He is the King of Israel; let Him now come down from the cross, and we will believe in Him <i>and</i> acknowledge Him.h¼kIÖ)In the same way the chief priests also, along with the scribes and elders, mocked Him, saying,E¼jƒÖ(and they said <n>[tauntingly]</n>, "You who would destroy the temple and rebuild it in three days, save Yourself <n>[from death]</n>! If You are the Son of God, come down from the cross."¼i‚Ö'Those who passed by were hurling abuse at Him <i>and</i> jeering at Him, wagging their heads <n>[in scorn and ridicule]</n>,l¼hQÖ&<pb/>At the same time two robbers were crucified with Jesus, one on the right and one on the left.}¼gsÖ%And above His head they put the accusation against Him which read, "<f>[9]</f> THIS IS JESUS THE KING OF THE JEWS."y¼fkÖ$Then sitting down there, they <i>began</i> to keep watch over Him <n>[to guard against any rescue attempt]</n>.n¼eUÖ#<pb/>And when they had crucified Him, they divided His clothes among them by casting<f>[8]</f> lots.
