And He told them, <J>"Wherever you go into a house, stay there until you leave that town.</J>Z¾a-à	but to wear sandals; and <n>[He told them]</n> not to wear<f>[4]</f> two tunics.¾`‚#àHe told them to take nothing for the journey except a mere walking stickâ€”no bread, no <n>[traveler's]</n> bag, no money in their beltsâ€”B¾_‚}àAnd He called the twelve <n>[disciples]</n> and began to send them out <n>[as His special messengers]</n> two by two, and gave them authority <i>and</i> power over the unclean spirits.f¾^Eà<t>He wondered at their unbelief. </t><br/>And He was going around in the villages teaching.¾]‚/àAnd He could not do a miracle there at all <n>[because of their unbelief]</n> except that He laid His hands on a few sick people and healed them.¾\‚)àJesus said to them, <J>"A prophet is not without honor (respect) except in his hometown and among his relatives and in his own household."</J>‚@¾[„yàIs this not the carpenter,<f>[1]</f> the son of Mary, and the brother of<f>[2]</f> James and Joses and<f>[3]</f> Judas and Simon? Are His sisters not here with us?" And they were <n>[deeply]</n> offended by Him <n>[and their disapproval blinded them to the fact that He was anointed by God as the Messiah]</n>.‚h¾Z…IàWhen the Sabbath came, He began to teach in the synagogue; and many who listened to Him were astonished, saying, "Where did this man get these things <n>[this knowledge and spiritual insight]</n>? What is this wisdom <n>[this confident understanding of the Scripture]</n> that has been given to Him, and such miracles as these performed by His hands?j¾Y	Oà<pb/>Jesus left there and came to His hometown <n>[Nazareth]</n>; and His disciples followed Him.y¾Xkà+He gave strict orders that no one should know about this, and He told them to give her <i>something</i> to eat.e¾WƒCà*The little girl immediately got up and <i>began</i> to walk, for she was twelve years old. And immediately they <n>[who witnessed the child's resurrection]</n> were overcome with great wonder <i>and</i> utter amazement.6¾V‚eà)Taking the child's hand, He said <n>[tenderly]</n> to her, <J>"Talitha kum!"</J>â€”which translated <n>[from Aramaic]</n> means, <J>"Little girl, I say to you, get up!"</J>‚¾U„5à(They <i>began</i> laughing <n>[scornfully]</n> at Him <n>[because they knew the child was dead]</n>. But He made them all<f>[5]</f> go outside, and took along the child's father and mother and His own <n>[three]</n> companions, and entered <i>the room</i> where the child was. ¾Tyà'When He had gone in, He said to them, <J>"Why make a commotion and weep? The child has not died, but is sleeping."</J>E¾Sƒà&They came to the house of the synagogue official; and He looked <n>[with understanding]</n> at the uproar <i>and</i> commotion, and people loudly weeping and wailing <n>[in mourning]</n>.¾R‚à%And He allowed no one to go with Him <n>[as witnesses]</n>, except Peter and<f>[4]</f> James and John the brother of James.¾Q‚7à$Overhearing what was being said, Jesus said to the synagogue official, <J>"Do not be afraid; only keep on believing <n>[in Me and my power]</n>."</J>9¾P‚kà#<pb/>While He was still speaking, some people came from the synagogue official's house, saying <n>[to Jairus]</n>, "Your daughter has died; why bother the Teacher any longer?"N¾Oƒà"Then He said to her, <J>"Daughter, your faith <n>[your personal trust and confidence in Me]</n> has restored you to health; go in peace and be <n>[permanently]</n> healed from your suffering."</J>¾N‚1à!And the woman, though she was afraid and trembling, aware of what had happened to her, came and fell down before Him and told Him the whole truth.H¾M	à Still He kept looking around to see the woman who had done it.¾L‚àHis disciples said to Him, "You see the crowd pressing in around You <n>[from all sides]</n>, and You ask, 'Who touched Me?'"¾K‚1àImmediately Jesus, recognizing in Himself that power had gone out from Him, turned around in the crowd and asked, <J>"Who touched My clothes?"</J>¾J‚)àImmediately her flow of blood was dried up; and she felt in her body <n>[and knew without any doubt]</n> that she was healed of her suffering.K¾IàFor she thought, "If I just touch His clothing, I will get well."y¾HkàShe had heard <n>[reports]</n> about Jesus, and she came up behind Him in the crowd and touched His outer robe.*¾G‚Màand had endured much <n>[suffering]</n> at the hands of many physicians. She had spent all that she had and was not helped at all, but instead had become worse.f¾FEà<pb/>A woman <n>[in the crowd]</n> had <n>[suffered from]</n> a hemorrhage for twelve years,t¾EaàAnd Jesus went with him; and a large crowd followed Him and pressed in around Him <n>[from all sides]</n>.4¾D‚aàand begged anxiously with Him, saying, "My little daughter is at the point of death; <n>[please]</n> come and lay Your hands on her, so that she will be healed and live."_¾C7àOne of the synagogue officials named Jairus came up; and seeing Him, fell at His feet#¾B‚?àWhen Jesus had again crossed over in the boat to the other side <n>[of the sea]</n>, a large crowd gathered around Him; and so He stayed by the seashore.a¾Aƒ;àSo he <n>[obeyed and]</n> went away and began to publicly proclaim in Decapolis <n>[the region of the ten Hellenistic cities]</n> all the great things that Jesus had done for him; and all the people were astonished.W¾@ƒ'àJesus did not let him <n>[come]</n>, but <n>[instead]</n> He said to him, <J>"Go home to your family and tell them all the great things that the Lord has done for you, and how He has had mercy on you."</J>8¾?‚iàAs He was stepping into the boat, the <n>[Gentile]</n> man who had been demon-possessed was begging with Him <n>[asking]</n> that he might go with Him <n>[as a disciple]</n>.F¾>àSo the people began to beg with Jesus to leave their region.#¾=‚?àThose who had seen it described <n>[in detail]</n> to the people what had happened to the demon-possessed man, and <n>[told them all]</n> about the pigs.Y¾<ƒ+àThey came to Jesus and saw the man who had been demon-possessed sitting down, clothed and in his right mind, the man who had <n>[previously]</n> had the "legion" <n>[of demons]</n>; and they were frightened.#¾;‚?à<pb/>The herdsmen <n>[tending the pigs]</n> ran away and reported it in the city and in the country. And <i>the people</i> came to see what had happened.‚ ¾:ƒyà
