And he <i>began</i> begging Him repeatedly not to send them out of the region.n¾6Uà	He was asking him, <J>"What is your name?"</J> And he replied, "My name is Legion; for we are many."]¾53àFor Jesus had been saying to him, <J>"Come out of the man, you unclean spirit!"</J>S¾4ƒàand screaming with a loud voice, he said, "<f>[3]</f> What business do we have in common with each other, Jesus, Son of the Most High God? I implore you by God <n>[swear to me]</n>, do not torment me!"_¾37àSeeing Jesus from a distance, he ran up and bowed down before Him <n>[in homage]</n>;¾2‚5àNight and day he was constantly screaming <i>and</i> shrieking among the tombs and on the mountains, and cutting himself with <n>[sharp]</n> stones.W¾1ƒ'àFor he had often been bound with shackles <n>[for the feet]</n> and with chains, and he tore apart the chains and broke the shackles into pieces, and no one was strong enough to subdue <i>and</i> tame him.l¾0Qàand the man lived in the<f>[2]</f> tombs, and no one could bind him anymore, not even with chains.j¾/MàWhen Jesus got out of the boat, immediately a man from the tombs with an unclean spirit met Him,_¾.	9à<pb/>They came to the<f>[1]</f> other side of the sea, to the region of the Gerasenes. ¾-yà)They were filled with great fear, and said to each other, "Who then is this, that even the wind and the sea obey Him?"{¾,oà(Jesus said to them, <J>"Why are you afraid? Do you still have no faith <i>and</i> confidence <n>[in Me]</n>?"</J>{¾+ƒoà'And He got up and <n>[sternly]</n> rebuked the wind and said to the sea, <J>"Hush, be still (muzzled)!"</J> And the wind died down <n>[as if it had grown weary]</n> and there was <n>[at once]</n> a great calm <n>[a perfect peacefulness]</n>.E¾*ƒà&But Jesus was in the stern, asleep <n>[with His head]</n> on the <n>[sailor's leather]</n> cushion. And they woke Him and said to Him, "Teacher, do You not care that we are about to die?"¾)‚à%And a<f>[5]</f> fierce windstorm began to blow, and waves were breaking over the boat, so that it was already being swamped.t¾(aà$So leaving the crowd, they took Him with them, just as He was, in the boat. And other boats were with Him.¾'‚%à#On that <n>[same]</n> day, when evening had come, He said to them, <J>"Let us go over to the other side <n>[of the Sea of Galilee]</n>."</J>¾&‚-à"and He did not say <i>anything</i> to them without <n>[using]</n> a parable; He did, however, explain everything privately to His own disciples.y¾%kà!<pb/>With many such parables, Jesus spoke the word to them, as they were able to hear <i>and</i> understand it;j¾$ƒMà <J>yet when it is sown, it grows up and becomes larger than all the garden herbs; and it puts out large branches, so that <e>the birds of the sky</e> are able to <e>make nests</e> <i>and</i> <e>live under its shade</e>."</J>;¾#‚oà<J>It is like a mustard seed, which, when it is sown on the ground, even though it is<f>[4]</f> smaller than all the <n>[other]</n> seeds that are <n>[sown]</n> on the soil,</J>¾"‚àAnd He said, <J>"How shall we<f>[3]</f> picture the kingdom of God, or what parable shall we use to illustrate <i>and</i> explain it?</J>¾!‚à<J>But when the crop ripens, he immediately puts in the sickle <n>[to reap]</n>, because <n>[the time for]</n> the harvest has come."</J>	¾ ‚à<J>The earth produces crops by itself; first the blade, then the head <n>[of grain]</n>, then the mature grain in the head.</J>)¾‚Kà<J>and he goes to bed at night and gets up every day, and <n>[in the meantime]</n> the seed sprouts and grows; how <n>[it does this]</n>, he does not know.</J>_¾7àThen He said, <J>"The kingdom of God is like a man who throws seed on the ground;</J>g¾ƒGà<J>For<f>[2]</f> whoever has <n>[a teachable heart]</n>, to him <i>more</i> <n>[understanding]</n> will be given; and whoever does not have <n>[a yearning for truth]</n>, even what he has will be taken away from him."</J>‚D¾…àThen He said to them, <J>"Pay attention to what you hear. By your own standard of measurement <n>[that is, to the extent that you study spiritual truth and apply godly wisdom]</n> it will be measured to you <n>[and you will be given even greater ability to respond]</n>â€”and more will be given to you besides.</J>T¾!à<J>If anyone has ears to hear, let him hear <i>and</i> heed My words."</J>n¾ƒUà<J>For nothing is hidden, except to be revealed; nor has anything been kept secret, but that it would come to light <n>[that is, things are hidden only temporarily, until the appropriate time comes for them to be known]</n>.</J>*¾‚Mà<pb/>He said to them, <J>"A lamp is not brought in to be put under a basket or under a bed, is it? Is it not <n>[brought in]</n> to be put on the lampstand?</J>‚ ¾„9à<J>And those <n>[in the last group]</n> are the ones on whom seed was sown on the good soil; and they hear the word <n>[of God, the good news regarding the way of salvation]</n> and accept it and bear fruitâ€”thirty, sixty, and a hundred times as much <n>[as was sown]</n>."</J>‚M¾…à<J>but the worries <i>and</i> cares of the world <n>[the distractions of this age with its worldly pleasures]</n>, and the deceitfulness <n>[and the false security or glamour]</n> of wealth <n>[or fame]</n>, and the passionate desires for all the other things creep in and choke out the word, and it becomes unfruitful.</J>|¾qà<J>And others are the ones on whom seed was sown among the thorns; these are the ones who have heard the word,</J>‚¾„à<J>and they have no real root in themselves, so they endure only for a little while; then, when trouble or persecution comes because of the word, immediately they <n>[are offended and displeased at being associated with Me and]</n> stumble <i>and</i> fall away.</J>a¾ƒ;à<J>In a similar way these <n>[in the second group]</n> are the ones on whom seed was sown on rocky ground, who, when they hear the word, immediately receive it with joy <n>[but accept it only superficially]</n>;</J>G¾ƒà<J>These <n>[in the first group]</n> are the ones along the road where the word is sown; but when they hear, Satan immediately comes and takes away the word which has been sown in them.</J>g¾Gà<J>The sower sows the word <n>[of God, the good news regarding the way of salvation]</n>.</J>¾‚#à
