e prayed."</J>ÁR‚àBut Peter kept saying insistently, "If I have to die with You, I will not deny You!" And they all were saying the same thing as well.@ÁQ‚yàJesus said to him, <J>"I assure you <i>and</i> most solemnly say to you, this very night, before a rooster crows twice, you will deny <n>[that you even know]</n> Me three times."</J>&ÁP‚EàBut Peter said to Him, "Even if they all fall away <n>[and desert You, ashamed and afraid of being associated with You]</n>, yet I will not <n>[do so]</n>!"iÁOKà<J>But after I have been raised <n>[from the dead]</n>, I will go ahead of you to Galilee."</J>kÁNƒOà<pb/>Jesus said to them, <J>"You will all fall away <n>[and be ashamed and be afraid to be associated with Me as disciples]</n>, because it is written, '<e>I will strike the Shepherd, and the sheep will be scattered</e>.'</J>[ÁM/à<pb/>After they had sung a<f>[10]</f> hymn, they went out to the Mount of Olives.-ÁL‚Sà<J>I assure you <i>and</i> most solemnly say to you, I will not drink again of the fruit of the vine until that day when I drink it new in the kingdom of God."</J>0ÁK‚YàAnd He said to them, <J>"This is My blood of the <n>[new]</n> covenant, <n>[My blood]</n> which is being poured out for many <n>[for the forgiveness of sins]</n>.</J>ÁJ}àAnd when He had taken a cup <n>[of wine]</n> and<f>[9]</f> given thanks, He gave it to them, and they all drank from it.@ÁI‚yàWhile they were eating, Jesus took bread and<f>[8]</f> blessed it <n>[giving thanks and praise]</n>, and He broke it, and gave it to them and said, <J>"Take it. This is My body."</J>pÁHƒYà<J>For the Son of Man goes <n>[to the cross]</n> just as it is written <n>[in Scripture]</n> of Him; but woe to that man by whom the Son of Man is betrayed! <i>It would have been</i> good for that man if he had not been born."</J>ÁG}àAnd He replied, <J>"It is one of the twelve <n>[disciples]</n>, one who is 