rself</e>.' There is no other commandment greater than these."</J>LÁ ƒà<J><e>and you shall love the Lord your God with all your heart, and with all your soul</e> (life), <e>and with all your mind</e> (thought, understanding), <e>and with all your strength</e>.'</J>À‚àJesus answered, <J>"The first <i>and</i> most important <i>one</i> is: '<e>Hear</e>, O <e>Israel, the Lord our God is one Lord</e>;</J>}À~ƒsà<pb/>Then one of the scribes <n>[an expert in Mosaic Law]</n> came up and listened to them arguing <n>[with one another]</n>, and noticing that Jesus answered them well, asked Him, "Which commandment is first <i>and</i> most important of all?"À}‚à<J>He is not the God of the dead, but of the living; you are greatly mistaken <i>and</i> you are deceiving yourselves!"</J>‚À|ƒ{à<J>But concerning the raising of the dead, have you not read in the book of Moses, in the <i>passage</i> about the <i>burning</i> bush, how God spoke to him, saying, '<e>I am the God of Abraham, and the God of Isaac, and the God of Jacob</e>'?</J>À{à<J>For when they rise from the dead, they do not marry nor are they given in marriage, but are like angels in heaven.</J>NÀzƒàJesus said to them, <J>"Is this not why you are wrong, because you know neither the Scriptures <n>[that teach the resurrection]</n> nor the power of God <n>[who is able to raise the dead]</n>?</J>lÀyQàIn the resurrection, whose wife will she be? For all seven <n>[brothers]</n> were married to her."pÀxYàand so all seven <n>[married her and died, and]</n> left no children. Last of all the woman died also._Àw7àThe second brother married her, and died leaving no children; and the third likewise;fÀvEàThere were seven brothers; the first <n>[one]</n> took a wife, and died leaving no children.`Àuƒ9à"Teacher, Moses wrote for us <n>[a law]</n> that <e>if a man's brother dies</e> and leaves a wife <e>but leaves no child, 