/>So with many other appeals <i>and</i> various admonitions John preached the good news (gospel) to the people.eÃSƒCêHis<f>[10]</f> winnowing fork is in His hand to thoroughly clear His threshing floor, and to gather the wheat (believers) into His barn (kingdom); but He will burn up the chaff (the unrepentant) with unquenchable fire."ƒÃR†êJohn answered them all by saying, "As for me, I baptize you <n>[only]</n><f>[8]</f> with water; but One who is mightier <n>[more powerful, more noble]</n> than I is coming, and I am not fit to untie the strap of His sandals <n>[even as His slave]</n>. He will baptize you <n>[who truly repent]</n> with the Holy Spirit and <n>[you who remain unrepentant]</n> with<f>[9]</f> fire.-ÃQ‚Sê<pb/>Now the people were in a state of expectation, and all were wondering in their hearts about John, as to whether he was the Christ (the Messiah, the Anointed).kÃPƒOê<i>Some</i> soldiers asked him, "And <i>what about</i> us, what are we to do?" And he replied to them, "Do not<f>[7]</f> extort money from anyone or harass <i>or</i> blackmail <i>anyone</i>, and be satisfied with your wages."uÃOcê
And he told them, "Collect no more than the <i>fixed amount</i> you have been ordered to <n>[collect]</n>."lÃNQêEven <i>some</i> tax collectors came to be baptized, and they asked, "Teacher, what are we to do?"ÃM}êAnd John replied, "The man who has two tunics is to share with him who has none; and he who has food is to do the same."=ÃLuê
<pb/>The crowds asked him, "Then what are we to do?";ÃK‚oê	Even now the axe <n>[of God's judgment]</n> is swinging toward the root of the trees; so every tree that does not produce good fruit is being cut down and thrown into the fire."„$ÃJˆAêTherefore produce fruit that is worthy of <n>[and consistent with your]</n> repentance <n>[that is, live changed lives, turn from sin and seek God and His righteousness]</n>. And do not <i>even</i> begin to say to yourselves <n>[as a defense]</n>, 'We have Abraham for our father <n>[and so our heritage assures us of salvation]</n>'; for I say to you that from these stones God is able to raise up children (descendants) for Abraham <n>[for God can replace the unrepentant, regardless of their heritage, with those who are obedient]</n>.HÃIƒ	ê<pb/>So he <i>began</i> saying to the crowds who were coming out to be baptized by him, "You brood of<f>[6]</f> vipers, who warned you to flee from the wrath <n>[of God that is]</n> to come?YÃH+ê<t><e>and</e><f>[5]</f><e>all mankind shall see the salvation of God</e>.'"</t>qÃGƒ[ê<t>'<e>Every ravine shall be filled up</e>, </t><t><e>And every mountain and hill shall be leveled</e>; </t><t><e>And the crooked</e> <n>[places]</n> <e>shall be made straight</e>, </t><t><e>And the rough roads smooth</e>;</t><br/>‚ÃF„'ê<t>as it is written <i>and</i> forever remains written in the book of the words of Isaiah the prophet, </t><br/><t>"<e>The voice of one shouting in the wilderness</e>, </t><t>'<e>Prepare the way of the Lord</e>, </t><t><f>[4]</f><e>Make His paths straight</e>.</t><br/>{ÃEoêAnd he went into all the country around the Jordan, preaching a baptism of repentance for the forgiveness of sin;*ÃD‚Mêin the high<f>[2]</f> priesthood of Annas and<f>[3]</f> Caiaphas <n>[his son-in-law]</n>, the word of God came to John, the son of Zacharias, in the wilderness.‚4ÃC	„cê<pb/>Now in the fifteenth year of <n>[Emperor]</n><f>[1]</f> Tiberius Caesar's reignâ€”when Pontius Pilate was governor of Judea, and Herod <n>[Antipas]</n> was tetrarch of Galilee, and his brother Philip was tetrarch of the region of Ituraea and Trachonitis, and Lysanias was tetrarch of Abileneâ€”aÃB;ê4<pb/>And Jesus kept increasing in wisdom and in stature, and in favor with God and men.!ÃA‚;ê3He went down to Nazareth with them, and was continually submissive <i>and</i> obedient to them; and His mother treasured all these things in her heart.>Ã@wê2But they did not understand what He had said to them.Ã?‚ê1And He answered, <J>"Why did you have to look for Me? Did you not know that I had to be<f>[12]</f> in My Father's <i>house</i>?"</J>cÃ>ƒ?ê0When they saw Him, they were overwhelmed; and His mother said to Him, "Son, why have You treated us like this? Listen, Your<f>[11]</f> father and I have been <n>[greatly distressed and]</n> anxiously looking for You."iÃ=Kê/All who heard Him were amazed by His intelligence <i>and</i> His understanding and His answers.Ã<‚1ê.Three days later they found Him in the <n>[court of the]</n> temple, sitting among the teachers, both listening to them and asking them questions.fÃ;Eê-When they did not find Him, they went back to Jerusalem looking for Him <n>[everywhere]</n>.@Ã:‚yê,but supposed Him to be in the caravan, and traveled a day's journey; and <n>[then]</n> they <i>began</i> searching <n>[anxiously]</n> for Him among their relatives and acquaintances.VÃ9ƒ%ê+and as they were returning <n>[to<f>[10]</f> Nazareth]</n>, after spending the required number of days <n>[at the Feast]</n>, the boy Jesus remained behind in Jerusalem. Now His parents did not know this,sÃ8_ê*And when He was twelve years old, they went up <i>to Jerusalem</i>, according to the custom of the Feast;NÃ7ê)Now His parents went to Jerusalem every year for the Passover Feast."Ã6‚=ê(And the Child continued to grow and beco