ÂY	‚êto a virgin<f>[10]</f> betrothed to a man whose name was Joseph, a descendant of the house of David; and the virgin's name was Mary.ÂX	‚êNow in the sixth month <n>[of Elizabeth's pregnancy]</n> the angel Gabriel was sent from God to a city in Galilee called Nazareth,ÂW	‚!ê"This is how the Lord has dealt with me in the days when He looked with favor on <i>me</i>, to take away my<f>[9]</f> disgrace among men."}ÂV	uê<pb/>Now after this his wife Elizabeth became pregnant, and for five months she secluded herself completely, saying,QÂU	êWhen his time of priestly service was finished, he returned to his home..ÂT	‚WêBut when he did come out, he was unable to speak to them. They realized that he had seen a vision in the temple; and he kept making signs to them, and remained mute.ÂS	‚ê<pb/>The people <n>[outside in the court]</n> were waiting for Zacharias, and were wondering about his <i>long</i> delay in the temple.nÂR	ƒWê<f>[8]</f> Listen carefully, you will be <i>continually</i> silent and unable to speak until the day when these things take place, because you did not believe what I told you; but my words will be fulfilled at their proper time."RÂQ	ƒêThe angel replied and said to him, "I am Gabriel; I stand <i>and</i> minister in the <n>[very]</n> presence of God, and I have been sent <n>[by Him]</n> to speak to you and to bring you this good news.ÂP	‚ê<pb/>And Zacharias said to the angel, "How will I be certain of this? For I am an old man and my wife is advanced in age."‚|ÂO	…sêIt is he who will go <i>as a forerunner</i> before Him in the spirit and power of Elijah, <e>to turn the hearts of the fathers back to the children</e>, and the disobedient to the attitude of the righteous <n>[which is to seek and submit to the will of God]</n>â€”in order to make ready a people <n>[perfectly]</n> prepared <n>[spiritually and morally]</n> for the Lord."vÂN	gêHe will turn many of the sons of Israel back <n>[from sin]</n> to <n>[love and serve]</n> the Lord their God.aÂM	ƒ=êfor he will be great <i>and</i> distinguished in the sight of the Lord; and will never drink wine or liquor, and he will be filled with <i>and</i> empowered to act by the Holy Spirit while still in his mother's womb.SÂL	!êYou will have great joy and delight, and many will rejoice over his birth,HÂK	ƒê
But the angel said to him, "Do not be afraid, Zacharias, because your petition <n>[in prayer]</n> was heard, and your wife Elizabeth will bear you a son, and you will name him<f>[7]</f> John.UÂJ	%êWhen Zacharias saw <i>the angel</i>, he was troubled and overcome with fear.aÂI	=êAnd an angel of the Lord appeared to him, standing to the right of the altar of incense.~ÂH	wê
And all the congregation was praying outside <n>[in the court of the temple]</n> at the hour of the incense offering.9ÂG	‚mê	as was the custom of the priesthood, he was chosen by lot to enter <n>[the sanctuary of]</n> the temple of the Lord and<f>[6]</f> burn incense <n>[on the altar of incense]</n>.ÂF	‚ê<pb/>Now it happened while Zacharias was serving as priest before God in the <i>appointed</i> order of his priestly division,iÂE	MêBut they were childless, because Elizabeth was barren, and they were both far advanced in years.ÂD	‚êThey both were righteous (approved) in the sight of God, walking blamelessly in all the commandments and requirements of the Lord.‚ÂC	„)êIn the days of Herod <n>[the Great]</n>, king of Judea, there was a certain priest whose name was<f>[3]</f> Zacharias, of<f>[4]</f> the division of Abijah. His wife was<f>[5]</f> a descendant of Aaron <n>[the first high priest of Israel]</n>, and her name was Elizabeth.ÂB	‚'êso that you may know the exact truth about the things you have been<f>[2]</f> taught <n>[that is, the history and doctrine of the faith]</n>.‚
ÂA	„êit seemed fitting for<f>[1]</f> me as well, <n>[and so I have decided]</n> after having carefully searched out <i>and</i> investigated all the events accurately, from the <i>very</i> beginning, to write an orderly account for you, most excellent Theophilus;‚Â@	„êexactly as they were handed down to us by those <n>[with personal experience]</n> who from the beginning <n>[of Christ's ministry]</n> were eyewitnesses and ministers of the word <n>[that is, of the teaching concerning salvation through faith in Christ]</n>,!Â?		‚?ê<pb/>Since <n>[as is well known]</n> many have undertaken to compile an orderly account of the things which have been fulfilled among us <n>[by God]</n>,Â>‚àAnd they went out and preached everywhere, while the Lord was working with them and confirming the word by the signs that followed.]Â=}à<pb/>So then, when the Lord Jesus had spoken to them, He was taken up into heaven and sat down at the right hand of God.
