¸	û	k„rÉB&šñ)                                                                                                                                                                                     CÆo‚ê1<J>For this reason also the wisdom of God said <n>[in the Scriptures]</n>, 'I will send them prophets and apostles, some of whom they will put to death and some they will persecute,</J>$Æn‚Aê0<J>So you are witnesses and approve the deeds of your fathers, because they <n>[actually]</n> killed them, and you repair <i>or</i> build their tombs.</J>Æm‚ê/<J>Woe to you! For you repair <i>or</i> build<f>[15]</f> tombs for the prophets, and it was your fathers who killed them.</J>‚Æl„'ê.But He said, <J>"Woe to you lawyers as well, because you weigh men down with burdens <n>[man-made rules, unreasonable requirements]</n> which are hard to bear, and you yourselves will not even touch the burdens with one of your fingers <n>[to lighten the load]</n>.</J>Æk}ê-<pb/>One of the lawyers <n>[an expert in the Mosaic Law]</n> answered Him, "Teacher, by saying this, You insult us too!"$Æj‚Aê,<J>Woe to you! For you are like graves which are unmarked, and people walk over them without being aware of it <n>[and are ceremonially unclean]</n>."</J>Æi‚)ê+<J>Woe to you Pharisees, because you love the<f>[14]</f> best seats in the synagogues and to be respectfully greeted in the market places.</J>‚pÆh…Yê*<pb/><J>"But woe (judgment is coming) to you Pharisees, because you <n>[self-righteously]</n><f>[12]</f> tithe mint and<f>[13]</f> rue and every <n>[little]</n> garden herb <n>[tending to all the minutiae]</n>, and yet disregard <i>and</i> neglect justice and the love of God; but these are the things you should have done, without neglecting the others.</J>bÆgƒ=ê)<J>But give that which is within as charity <n>[that is, acts of mercy and compassion, not as a public display, but as an expression of your faithfulness to God]</n>, and then indeed all things are clean for you.</J>Æf‚ê(<J>You foolish ones <n>[acting without reflection or intelligence]</n>! Did not He who made the outside make the inside also?</J>8Æe‚iê'But the Lord said to him, <J>"Now you Pharisees clean the outside of the cup and plate <n>[as required by tradition]</n>; but inside you are full of greed and wickedness.</J>qÆd[ê&The Pharisee noticed this and was surprised that Jesus did not first ceremonially wash before the meal.LÆcƒê%Now after Jesus had spoken, a Pharisee asked Him to have lunch with him. He went in <n>[the Pharisee's home]</n> and reclined <i>at the table</i> <n>[without ceremonially washing His hands]</n>.1Æb‚[ê$<J>So if your whole body is illuminated, with no dark part, it will be entirely bright <n>[with light]</n>, as when the lamp gives you light with its bright rays."</J>VÆa%ê#<J>Be careful, therefore, that the light that is in you is not darkness.</J>‚:Æ`„mê"<J>The eye is the lamp of your body. When your eye is clear <n>[spiritually perceptive, focused on God]</n>, your whole body also is full of light <n>[benefiting from God's precepts]</n>. But when it is bad <n>[spiritually blind]</n>, your body also is full of darkness <n>[devoid of God's word]</n>.</J>TÆ_ƒ!ê!<pb/><J>"No one lights a lamp and then puts it in a cellar nor under a basket <n>[hiding the light]</n>, but <n>[instead it is put]</n> on the lampstand, so that those who come in may see the light.</J>]Æ^ƒ3ê <J>The men of Nineveh will stand up <n>[as witnesses]</n> at the judgment with this generation and condemn it, because they repented at the preaching of Jonah, and look, something greater than Jonah is here.</J>‚Æ]„ê<J>The Queen of the South (the kingdom of Sheba) will rise up in the judgment with the men of this generation and condemn them, because she came from the ends of the earth to listen to the wisdom of Solomon, and look, something greater than Solomon is here.</J>Æ\‚)ê<J>For just as<f>[11]</f> Jonah became a sign to the people of Nineveh, so will the Son of Man also be <n>[a sign]</n> to this generation.</J>‚Æ[„êNow as the crowds were increasing <n>[in number]</n>, He began to say, <J>"This <n>[present]</n> generation is a wicked generation; it seeks a sign (attesting miracle), but no sign will be given to it except the sign of Jonah <n>[the prophet]</n>.</J>ÆZ‚êBut He said, <J>"On the contrary, blessed (happy, favored by God) are those who hear the word of God and continually observe it."</J>aÆYƒ;ê<pb/>Now while Jesus was saying these things, one of the women in the crowd raised her voice and said to Him, "Blessed (happy, favored by God) is the womb that gave birth to You and the breasts at which You nursed!"GÆXƒê<J>Then it goes and brings seven other spirits more evil than itself, and they go in <n>[the person]</n> and live there; and the last state of that person becomes worse than the first."</J>NÆWê<J>And when it comes, it finds the place swept and put in order.</J>eÆVƒCê<pb/><J>"When the unclean spirit comes out of a person, it roams through waterless places in search <n>[of a place]</n> of rest; and not finding any, it says, 'I will go back to my house (person) from which I came.'</J>YÆUƒ+ê<J>He who is not with Me <n>[believing in Me as Lord and Savior]</n> is against Me <n>[there is no impartial position]</n>; and he who does not gather with Me <n>[assisting in My ministry]</n>, scatters.</J>+ÆT‚Oê<J>But when someone stronger than he attacks and overpowers him, he robs him of all his armor on which he had relied and divides his <n>[goods as]</n> spoil.</J>zÆSmê<J>When the strong man, fully armed, guards his own house, his belongings are undisturbed <i>and</i> secure.</J>ÆR}ê<J>But if I drive out the demons by the finger of God, then<f>[10]</f> the kingdom of God has already come upon you.</J>)ÆQ‚Kê<J>Now if I drive out the demons by Beelzebul, by whom do your sons <n>[the Jewish exorcists]</n> drive them out? For this reason they will be your judges.</J>DÆPƒê<J>If Satan also is divided against himself, how will his kingdom stand <i>and</i> continue to survive? For you are saying that I drive out demons by <n>[the power of]</n> Beelzebul.</J>OÆOƒêBut He, <i>well</i> aware of their thoughts <i>and</i> purpose, said to them, <J>"Every kingdom divided against itself is doomed to destruction; and a house <i>divided</i> against itself falls.</J>OÆNêOthers, trying to test Him, were demanding of Him a sign from heaven.ÆM‚êBut some of them said, "He drives out demons by <n>[the power of]</n><f>[9]</f> Beelzebul (Satan), the ruler of the demons."NÆLƒêAnd <n>[at another time]</n> Jesus was casting out a demon, and it was <n>[controlling a man so as to make him]</n> mute; when the demon had gone out, the mute man spoke. And the crowds were awed.jÆKƒMê
