êAnd those who heard it said, "<f>[2]</f> Then who can be saved?"3Èr‚_ê<J>For it is easier for a camel to go through the eye of a needle than for a rich man <n>[who places his faith in wealth or status]</n> to enter the kingdom of God."</J>zÈqmêJesus looked at him and said, <J>"How difficult it is for those who are wealthy to enter the kingdom of God!</J>XÈp)êBut when he heard these things, he became very sad, for he was extremely rich.‚NÈo…êWhen Jesus heard this, He said to him, <J>"You still lack one thing; sell everything that you have and distribute the money to the poor, and you will have <n>[abundant]</n> treasure in heaven; and come, follow Me <n>[becoming My disciple, believing and trusting in Me and walking the same path of life that I walk]</n>."</J>BÈnêHe replied, "I have kept all these things from my youth."%Èm‚Cê<J>You know the commandments: '<e>Do not commit adultery, Do not murder, Do not steal, Do not testify falsely, Honor your father and your mother</e>.'"</J>ÈlwêJesus said to him, <J>"Why do you call Me good? No one is <n>[essentially and morally]</n> good except God alone.</J>LÈkƒêA certain ruler asked Him, "Good Teacher <n>[You who are essentially and morally good]</n>, what shall I do to inherit eternal life <n>[that is, eternal salvation in the Messiah's kingdom]</n>?"7Èj‚gê<J>I assure you <i>and</i> most solemnly say to you, whoever does not receive the kingdom of God <n>[with faith and humility]</n> like a child will not enter it at all."</J>?Èi‚wêBut Jesus called them to Himself, saying <n>[to the apostles]</n>, <J>"Allow the children to come to Me, and do not forbid them, for the kingdom of God belongs to such as these.</J>5Èh‚cê<pb/>Now they were also bringing their babies to Him, so that He would touch <i>and</i> bless them, and when the disciples noticed it, they <i>began</i> reprimanding them.‚-Èg„Sê<J>I tell you, this man went to his home justified <n>[forgiven of the guilt of sin and placed in right standing with God]</n> rather than the other man; for everyone who exalts himself will be humbled, but he who humbles himself <n>[forsaking self-righteous pride]</n> will be exalted."</J>‚Èf„1ê
<J>But the tax collector, standing at a distance, would not even raise his eyes toward heaven, but was striking his chest <n>[in humility and repentance]</n>, saying, 'God, be merciful <i>and</i> gracious to me, the <n>[especially wicked]</n> sinner <n>[that I am]</n>!'</J>FÈeê<J>I fast twice a week; I pay tithes of all that I get.'</J>‚Èd„ê<J>The Pharisee stood <n>[ostentatiously]</n> and began praying to himself <n>[in a self-righteous way, saying]</n>: 'God, I thank You that I am not like the rest of menâ€”swindlers, unjust (dishonest), adulterersâ€”or even like this tax collector.</J>{Ècoê
<J>"Two men went up into the temple <n>[enclosure]</n> to pray, one a Pharisee and the other a tax collector.</J>iÈbƒKê	He also told this parable to some people who trusted in themselves <i>and</i> were confident that they were righteous <n>[posing outwardly as upright and in right standing with God]</n>, and who viewed others with contempt:6Èa‚eê<J>I tell you that He will defend <i>and</i> avenge them quickly. However, when the Son of Man comes, will He find <n>[this kind of persistent]</n> faith on the earth?"</J>NÈ`ƒê<J>And will not <n>[our just]</n> God defend <i>and</i> avenge His elect <n>[His chosen ones]</n> who cry out to Him day and night? Will He delay <n>[in providing justice]</n> on their behalf?</J>KÈ_êThen the Lord said, <J>"Listen to what the unjust judge says!</J>oÈ^ƒWê<J>yet because this widow <i>continues</i> to bother me, I will give her justice <i>and</i> legal protection; otherwise<f>[1]</f> by continually coming she <n>[will be an intolerable annoyance and she]</n> will wear me out.'"</J>wÈ]gê<J>For a time he would not; but later he said to himself, 'Even though I do not fear God nor respect man,</J>*È\‚Mê<J>There was a <n>[desperate]</n> widow in that city and she kept coming to him and saying, 'Give me justice <i>and</i> legal protection from my adversary.'</J>nÈ[Uêsaying, <J>"In a certain city there was a judge who did not fear God and had no respect for man.</J>ÈZ	‚-ê<pb/>Now Jesus was telling the disciples a parable to make the point that at all times they ought to pray and not give up <i>and</i> lose heart,|ÈYqê%And they asked Him, "Where, Lord?" He answered, <J>"Where the corpse is, there the vultures will be gathered."</J>}ÈXsê$<J><f>[12]</f><n>["Two men will be in the field;<f>[13]</f> one will be taken and the other will be left."]</n></J>IÈWƒê#<J>There will be two women grinding <n>[at the mill]</n> together; the<f>[11]</f> one (the non-believer) will be taken <n>[away in judgment]</n> and the other (the believer) will be left.</J>ÈVƒwê"<J>I tell you, on that night <n>[when Messiah comes again]</n> there will be two <n>[sleeping]</n> in one bed; the<f>[9]</f> one (the non-believer) will be taken <n>[away in judgment]</n> and the<f>[10]</f> other (the believer) will be left.</J>wÈUƒgê!<J>Whoever seeks to save his<f>[8]</f> life will <n>[eventually]</n> lose it <n>[through death]</n>, and whoever loses <i>his life</i> <n>[in this world]</n> will keep it <n>[from the consequences of sin and separation from God]</n>.</J>]ÈT3ê <J>Remember <n>[what happened to]</n> Lot's wife <n>[when she looked back]</n>!</J>PÈSƒê<J>On that day, whoever is on the housetop, with his belongings in the house, must not come down <n>[and go inside]</n> to take them out; and likewise whoever is in the field must not turn back.</J>UÈR#ê<J>It will be just the same on the day that the Son of Man is revealed.</J>ÈQ‚ê<J>but on the <n>[very]</n> day that Lot left Sodom it rained fire and brimstone (burning sulfur) from heaven and destroyed them all.</J>yÈPƒkê<J>It was the same as it was in the days of Lot. People were eating, they were drinking, they were buying, they were selling, they were planting, they were building <n>[carrying on business as usual, without regard for their sins]</n>;</J>yÈOƒkê<J>the people were<f>[7]</f> eating, they were drinking, they were marrying, they were being given in marriage, <n>[they were indifferent to God]</n> until the day that Noah went into the ark, and the flood came and destroyed them all.</J>
ÈN‚ê<J>And just as it was in the days of Noah, so it will be in the<f>[6]</f> time of <n>[the second coming of]</n> the Son of Man:</J>;ÈM‚oê<J>But first He must suffer many things and be repudiated <i>and</i> rejected <i>and</i> considered unfit <n>[to be the Messiah]</n> by this <n>[unbelieving]</n> generation.</J>NÈLƒê<J>For just like the lightning, when it flashes out of one part<f>[4]</f> of the sky, gives light to the other part<f>[5]</f> of the sky, so <n>[visible]</n> will the Son of Man be in His day.</J>8ÈK‚iê<J>They will say to you, 'Look <n>[the Messiah is]</n> there!' <i>or</i> 'Look <n>[He is]</n> here!' Do not go away <n>[to see Him]</n>, and do not run after <i>them</i>.</J>'ÈJ‚GêThen He said to the disciples, <J>"The time will come when you will long to see <n>[even]</n> one of the days of the Son of Man, and you will not see it.</J>ÈI‚ê<J>nor will people say, 'Look! Here it is!' or, 'There it is!' For the kingdom of God is among you <n>[because of My presence]</n>."</J>JÈHƒ
