ƒcê%<J>For I tell you that this <n>[Scripture]</n> which is written must be completed <i>and</i> fulfilled in Me: '<e>And He was counted with the criminals</e>'; for that which refers to Me has its fulfillment <n>[and is settled]</n>."</J>;Ê-‚oê$Then He said to them, <J>"But now, he who has a money belt is to take it along, and also his <n>[provision]</n> bag, and he who has no sword is to sell his coat and buy one.</J>=Ê,‚sê#<pb/>And He said to them, <J>"When I sent you out without a money belt and <n>[provision]</n> bag and <n>[extra]</n> sandals, did you lack anything?"</J> They answered, "Nothing."Ê+‚ê"Jesus said, <J>"I say to you, Peter, before the rooster crows today, you will <n>[utterly]</n> deny three times that you know Me."</J>_Ê*7ê!And Peter said to Him, "Lord, I am ready to go with You both to prison and to death!"‚Ê)„ê <J>but I have prayed <n>[especially]</n> for you <n>[Peter]</n>, that your faith <n>[and confidence in Me]</n> may not fail; and you, once you have turned back again <n>[to Me]</n>, strengthen <i>and</i> support your brothers <n>[in the faith]</n>."</J>Ê({ê<pb/><J>"Simon, Simon (Peter), listen! Satan has demanded <i>permission</i> to sift <n>[all of]</n> you like grain;</J>Ê'‚ê<J>that you may eat and drink at My table in My kingdom, and you will sit on thrones judging the twelve tribes of Israel.</J>cÊ&?ê<J>and just as My Father has granted Me a kingdom, I grant you <n>[the privilege]</n></J>`Ê%9ê<pb/><J>"You are those who have remained <i>and</i> have stood by Me in My trials;</J>FÊ$ƒê<J>For who is the greater, the one who reclines <i>at the table</i> or the one who serves? Is it not the one who reclines <i>at the table</i>? But I am among you as the one who serves.</J>eÊ#ƒCê<J>But it is not to be this way with you; on the contrary, the one who is the greatest among you must become like the youngest <n>[and least privileged]</n>, and the <n>[one who is the]</n> leader, like the servant.</J>,Ê"‚QêJesus said to them, <J>"The kings of the Gentiles have absolute power <i>and</i> lord it over them; and those in authority over them are called 'Benefactors.'</J>bÊ!=êNow a dispute also arose among them as to which of them was regarded to be the greatest.lÊ QêAnd they began to discuss among themselves which one of them it might be who was going to do this.(Ê‚Iê<J>For indeed, the Son of Man is going as it has been determined; but woe (judgment is coming) to that man by whom He is betrayed <i>and</i> handed over!"</J>XÊ)ê<J>But listen, the hand of the one betraying Me is with Mine on the table.</J>4Ê‚aêAnd in the same way <i>He took</i> the cup after they had eaten, saying, <J>"This cup, which is poured out for you, is the new covenant <n>[ratified]</n> in My blood.</J>/Ê‚WêAnd when He had taken bread and given thanks, He broke it and gave it to them, saying, <J>"This is My body which is given for you; do this in remembrance of Me."</J>yÊkê<J>for I say to you, I will not drink of the fruit of the vine from now on until the kingdom of God comes."</J>{ÊoêAnd when He had taken a cup and<f>[3]</f> given thanks, He said, <J>"Take this and share it among yourselves;</J>hÊIê<J>for I say to you, I will not eat it again until it is fulfilled in the kingdom of God."</J>iÊKêHe said to them, <J>"I have earnestly wanted to eat this Passover with you before I suffer;</J>vÊeêWhen the hour <n>[for the meal]</n> had come, Jesus reclined <i>at the table</i>, and the apostles with Him.ZÊ-ê
