	?ê<pb/>Now the Festival of Unleavened Bread, which is called the Passover, was approaching.cÊ	?ê&And early in the morning all the people would come to Him in the temple to listen to Him.;Ê‚oê%<pb/>Now in the daytime Jesus was teaching in <n>[the porches and courts of]</n> the temple, but at night He would go out and spend the night on the mount that is called Olivet.‚(Ê„Iê$<J>But keep alert at all times <n>[be attentive and ready]</n>, praying that you may have the strength <i>and</i> ability <n>[to be found worthy and]</n> to escape all these things that are going to take place, and to stand in the presence of the Son of Man <n>[at His coming]</n>."</J>WÊ'ê#<J>for it will come upon all those who live on the face of all the earth.</J>‚(Ê„Iê"<pb/><J>"But be on guard, so that your hearts are not weighed down <i>and</i> depressed with the giddiness of debauchery and the nausea of self-indulgence and the worldly worries of life, and then that day <n>[when the Messiah returns]</n> will not come on you suddenly like a trap;</J>RÊê!<J>Heaven and earth will pass away, but My words will not pass away.</J>_Êƒ7ê <J>I assure you <i>and</i> most solemnly say to you, this generation <n>[those living at that definite period of time preceding the second coming]</n> will not pass away until<f>[4]</f> everything takes place.</J>Ê}ê<J>So you too, when you see these things happening, know <n>[without any doubt]</n> that the kingdom of God is near.</J>hÊIê<J>as soon as they put out leaves, you see it and know for yourselves that summer is near.</J>VÊ %êThen He told them a parable: <J>"Look at the fig tree and all the trees;</J>.É‚Uê<J>Now when these things begin to occur, stand tall and lift up your heads <n>[in joy]</n>, because <n>[suffering ends as]</n> your redemption is drawing near."</J>.É~‚Uê<J>Then they will see <e>the Son of Man coming in a cloud</e> with <n>[transcendent, overwhelming]</n> power <n>[subduing the nations]</n> and with great glory.</J>+É}‚Oê<J>people fainting from fear and expectation of the <n>[dreadful]</n> things coming on the world; for the <n>[very]</n> powers of the heavens will be shaken.</J>vÉ|ƒeê<J>"There will be signs (attesting miracles) in the sun and moon and stars; and on the earth <n>[there will be]</n> distress <i>and</i> anguish among nations, in perplexity at the roaring <i>and</i> tossing of the sea and the waves,</J>[É{ƒ/ê<J>And they will fall by the edge of the sword, and will be led captive into all nations; and Jerusalem will be trampled underfoot by the Gentiles until the times of the Gentiles are fulfilled (completed).</J>bÉzƒ=ê<J>Woe to those women who are pregnant and to those who are nursing babies in those days! For great trouble <i>and</i> anguish will be on the land, and wrath <i>and</i> retribution on this people <n>[Israel]</n>.</J>Éy‚1ê<J>for these are days of vengeance <n>[of rendering full justice or satisfaction]</n>, so that all things which are written will be fulfilled.</J>TÉxƒ!ê<J>At that time, those who are in Judea must flee to the mountains, and those who are inside the city (Jerusalem) must get out, and those who are <n>[out]</n> in the country must not enter the city;</J>1Éw‚[ê<pb/><J>"But when you see Jerusalem surrounded by <n>[hostile]</n> armies, then understand <n>[with confident assurance]</n> that her complete destruction is near.</J>sÉv_ê<J>By your <n>[patient]</n> endurance <n>[empowered by the Holy Spirit]</n> you will gain your souls.</J>8Éukê<J>But not a hair of your head will perish.</J>xÉtiê<J>and you will be <i>continually</i> hated by everyone because of <n>[your association with]</n> My name.</J>'És‚Gê<J>But you will be betrayed <i>and</i> handed over even by parents and brothers and relatives and friends, and they will put <i>some</i> of you to death,</J>Ér‚ê<J>for I will give you <n>[skillful]</n> words and wisdom which none of your opponents will be able to resist or refute.</J>VÉq%ê<J>So make up your minds not to prepare beforehand to defend yourselves;</J>dÉpAê
<J>This will be a time <i>and</i> an opportunity for you to testify <n>[about Me]</n>.</J>\Éoƒ1ê<pb/><J>"But before all these things, they will lay their hands on you and will persecute you, turning you over to the synagogues and prisons, and bringing you before kings and governors for My name's sake.</J>VÉnƒ%ê<J>There will be violent earthquakes, and in various places famines and <n>[deadly and devastating]</n> pestilences (plagues, epidemics); and there will be terrible sights and great signs from heaven.</J>dÉmAê
