­	÷	HÉÌßxÇ,uÕÊ                                                                    2Í‚]ô%<J>And the Father who sent Me has Himself testified about Me. You have never heard His voice nor seen His form <n>[His majesty and greatnessâ€”what He is like]</n>.</J>‚OÍ…ô$<J>But the testimony which I have is far greater than <i>the testimony of</i> John; for the works that the Father has given Me to finishâ€”the very same works <n>[that is, the miracles and proofs of My deity]</n> that I am <n>[now]</n> doingâ€”testify about Me, <n>[by providing evidence]</n> that the Father has sent Me.</J>Í‚/ô#<J>John was the lamp that kept on burning and shining <n>[to show you the way]</n>, and you were willing for a while to rejoice in his light.</J>2Í‚]ô"<J>But the testimony I receive is not from man <n>[a merely human witness]</n>; but I say these things so that you may be saved <n>[that is, have eternal life]</n>.</J>Í‚%ô!<J>You have sent <n>[an inquiry]</n> to<f>[7]</f> John <n>[the Baptist]</n> and he has testified <n>[as an eyewitness]</n> to the truth.</J>,Í‚Qô <J>There is another <n>[My Father]</n> who testifies about Me, and I know <n>[without any doubt]</n> that His testimony on My behalf is true <i>and</i> valid.</J>cÍ?ô<pb/><J>"If I <i>alone</i> testify about Myself, My testimony is not<f>[6]</f> valid.</J>hÍƒIô<pb/><J>"I can do nothing on my own initiative <i>or</i> authority. Just as I hear, I judge; and My judgment is just (fair, righteous, unbiased), because I do not seek My own will, but only the will of Him who sent Me.</J>xÍ ƒiô<J>and they will come outâ€”those who did good things <n>[will come out]</n> to a resurrection of <n>[new]</n> life, but those who did evil things <n>[will come out]</n> to a resurrection of judgment <n>[that is, to be sentenced]</n>.</J>{Ìoô<J>Do not be surprised at this; for a time is coming when all those who are in the tombs will hear His voice,</J>*Ì~‚Mô<J>And He has given Him authority to execute judgment, because He is a Son of Man <n>[sinless humanity, qualifying Him to sit in judgment over mankind]</n>.</J>1Ì}‚[ô<J>For just as the Father has life in Himself <n>[and is self-existent]</n>, even so He has given to the Son to have life in Himself <n>[and be self-existent]</n>.</J>CÌ|‚ô<J>I assure you <i>and</i> most solemnly say to you, a time is coming and is <n>[here]</n> now, when the dead will hear the voice of the Son of God, and those who hear it will live.</J>ƒÌ{†-ô<pb/><J>"I assure you <i>and</i> most solemnly say to you, the person who hears My word <n>[the one who heeds My message]</n>, and believes <i>and</i> trusts in Him who sent Me, has (possesses now) eternal life <n>[that is, eternal life actually beginsâ€”the believer is transformed]</n>, and does not come into judgment <i>and</i> condemnation, but has passed <n>[over]</n> from death into life.</J>RÌzƒô<J>so that all will give honor (reverence, homage) to the Son just as they give honor to the Father. <n>[In fact]</n> the one who does not honor the Son does not honor the Father who has sent Him.</J>.Ìy‚Uô<J>For the Father judges no one, but has given all judgment <n>[that is, the prerogative of judging]</n> to the Son <n>[placing it entirely into His hands]</n>,</J>Ìx‚7ô<J>Just as the Father raises the dead and gives them life <n>[and allows them to live on]</n>, even so the Son also gives life to whom He wishes.</J>TÌwƒ!ô<J>For the Father <i>dearly</i> loves the Son and shows Him everything that He Himself is doing; and <i>the Father</i> will show Him greater works than these, so that you will be filled with wonder.</J>‚@Ìv„yô<pb/>So Jesus answered them by saying, <J>"I assure you <i>and</i> most solemnly say to you, the Son<f>[5]</f> can do nothing of Himself <n>[of His own accord]</n>, unless it is something He sees the Father doing; for whatever things the Father does, the Son <n>[in His turn]</n> also does in the same way.</J>VÌuƒ%ôThis made the Jews more determined than ever to kill Him, for not only was He breaking the Sabbath <n>[from their viewpoint]</n>, but He was also calling God His own Father, making Himself equal with God.Ìt‚ôBut Jesus answered them, <J>"My Father has been working until now <n>[He has never ceased working]</n>, and I too am working."</J> ÌsyôFor this reason the Jews began to persecute Jesus <i>continually</i> because He was doing these things on the Sabbath.VÌr%ôThe man went away and told the Jews that it was Jesus who had made him well.Ìq‚ôAfterward, Jesus found him in the temple and said to him, <J>"See, you are well! Stop sinning or something worse may happen to you."</J>Ìp‚'ô
Now the man who had been healed did not know who it was, for Jesus had slipped away <n>[unnoticed]</n> since there was a crowd in that place.fÌoEôThey asked him, "Who is the Man who told you, <J>'Pick up <i>your pallet</i> and walk'?"</J>Ìn‚-ôHe answered them, "The Man who healed me <i>and</i> gave me back my strength was the One who said to me, <J>'Pick up your pallet and walk.'"</J>2Ìm‚]ô
So the Jews kept saying to the man who had been healed, "It is the Sabbath, and you are not<f>[4]</f> permitted to pick up your pallet <n>[because it is unlawful]</n>."$Ìl‚Aô	<t>Immediately the man was healed <i>and</i> recovered his strength, and<f>[3]</f> picked up his pallet and walked. </t><br/>Now that day was the Sabbath.KÌkôJesus said to him, <J>"Get up; pick up your pallet and walk."</J>CÌj‚ôThe invalid answered, "Sir, I have no one to put me in the pool when the water is stirred up, and while I am coming <n>[to get into it myself]</n>, someone else steps down ahead of me."0Ìi‚YôWhen Jesus noticed him lying there <n>[helpless]</n>, knowing that he had been <i>in that condition</i> a long time, He said to him, <J>"Do you want to get well?"</J>PÌhôThere was a certain man there who had been ill for thirty-eight years.8Ìg‚iôfor an angel of the Lord went down into the pool at appointed seasons and stirred up the water; the first one to go in after the water was stirred was healed of his disease.]Ìf‚)ôIn these <i>porticoes</i> lay a great number of people who were sick, blind, lame, withered,<f>[2]</f> [waiting for the stirring of the water;2Ìe‚]ô<pb/>Now in Jerusalem, near the Sheep Gate, there is a<f>[1]</f> pool, which is called in Hebrew (Jewish Aramaic) Bethesda, having five porticoes (alcoves, colonnades).[Ìd	1ô<pb/>Later on there was a Jewish feast (festival), and Jesus went up to Jerusalem..Ìc‚Uô6This is the second sign (attesting miracle) that Jesus performed <n>[in Cana]</n> after He had come from Judea to Galilee <n>[revealing that He is the Messiah]</n>._Ìbƒ7ô5Then the father realized that it was at that <i>very</i> hour when Jesus had said to him, <J>"Your son lives";</J> and he and his entire household believed <i>and</i> confidently trusted <n>[in Him as Savior]</n>.Ìa}ô4So he asked them at what time he began to get better. They said, "Yesterday during the seventh hour the fever left him."
Ì`‚ô3As he was already going down <n>[the road]</n>, his servants met him and reported that his son was living <n>[and was healthy]</n>.sÌ__ô2Jesus said to him, <J>"Go; your son lives!"</J> The man believed what Jesus said to him and started home.iÌ^Kô1The royal official pleaded with Him, "Sir, do come down <n>[at once]</n> before my child dies!"Ì]‚%ô0Then Jesus said to him, <J>"Unless you <n>[people]</n> see <n>[miraculous]</n> signs and wonders, you <n>[simply]</n> will not believe."</J>AÌ\‚{ô/Having heard that Jesus had come back from Judea to Galilee, he<f>[9]</f> went to <i>meet</i> Him and began asking Him to come down and heal his son; for he was at the point of death.,Ì[‚Qô.So Jesus came again to Cana of Galilee, where He had turned the water into wine. And there was a<f>[8]</f> certain royal official whose son was sick in Capernaum.8ÌZ‚iô-So when He arrived in Galilee, the Galileans<f>[7]</f> welcomed Him, since they had seen all the things that He did in Jerusalem at the feast; for they too came to the feast.TÌY!ô,For Jesus Himself declared that a prophet has no honor in his own country.EÌXô+<pb/>After the two days He went on from there into Galilee.ÌWƒwô*and they told the woman, "We no longer believe <i>just</i> because of what you said; for <n>[now]</n> we have heard <i>Him</i> for ourselves and know <n>[with confident assurance]</n> that this One is truly the Savior of <n>[all]</n> the world."ÌV}ô)Many more believed in Him <n>[with a deep, abiding trust]</n> because of His word <n>[His personal message to them]</n>;qÌU[ô(So when the Samaritans came to Jesus, they asked Him to remain with them; and He stayed there two days.GÌTƒô'Now many Samaritans from that city believed in Him <i>and</i> trusted Him <n>[as Savior]</n> because of what the woman said when she testified, "He told me all the things that I have done."&ÌS‚Eô&<J>I sent you to reap <n>[a crop]</n> for which you have not worked. Others have worked and you have been privileged to reap the results of their work."</J>jÌRMô%<J>For in this <i>case</i> the saying is true, 'One <n>[person]</n> sows and another reaps.'</J>*ÌQ‚Mô$<J>Already the reaper is receiving <i>his</i> wages and he is gathering fruit for eternal life; so that he who plants and he who reaps may rejoice together.</J>:ÌP‚mô#<J>Do you not say, 'It is still four months until the harvest comes?' Look, I say to you, raise your eyes and look at the fields <i>and</i> see, they are white for harvest.</J>uÌOcô"Jesus said to them, <J>"My food is to do the will of Him who sent Me and to completely finish His work.</J>aÌN;ô!So the disciples said to one another, "Has anyone brought Him <i>something</i> to eat?"SÌMô But He told them, <J>"I have food to eat that you do not know about."</J>rÌL]ô<pb/>Meanwhile, the disciples were urging Jesus <n>[to have a meal]</n>, saying, "Rabbi (Teacher), eat."<ÌKsôSo the people left the city and were coming to Him.|ÌJqô"Come, see a man who told me all the things that I have done! Can this be the Christ (the Messiah, the Anointed)?"aÌI;ôThen the woman left her water jar, and went into the city and began telling the people,;ÌH‚oô<pb/>Just then His disciples came, and they were surprised to find Him talking with a woman. However, no one said, "What are You asking about?" or, "Why are You talking to her?"UÌG#ôJesus said to her, <J>"I who speak to you, am <i>He</i> (the Messiah)."</J>4ÌF‚aôThe woman said to Him, "I know that Messiah is coming (He who is called Christâ€”the Anointed); when that One comes, He will tell us everything <n>[we need to know]</n>."ÌE‚ô<J>God is spirit <n>[the Source of life, yet invisible to mankind]</n>, and those who worship Him must worship in spirit and truth."</J>aÌDƒ;ô<J>But a time is coming and is already here when the true worshipers will worship the Father in spirit <n>[from the heart, the inner self]</n> and in truth; for the Father seeks such people to be His worshipers.</J>ÌC‚ô<J>You <n>[Samaritans]</n> do not know what you worship; we <n>[Jews]</n> do know what we worship, for salvation is from the Jews.</J>2ÌB‚]ôJesus replied, <J>"Woman, believe Me, a time is coming <n>[when God's kingdom comes]</n> when you will worship the Father neither on this mountain nor in Jerusalem.</J>ÌA‚1ôOur fathers worshiped on this mountain, but you <i>Jews</i> say that the place where one ought to worship is in Jerusalem <n>[at the temple]</n>."DÌ@ôThe woman said to Him, "Sir, I see that You are a prophet.Ì?‚ô<J>for you have had five husbands, and the man you are now living with is not your<f>[6]</f> husband. You have said this truthfully."</J>Ì>‚ôThe woman answered, "I do not have a husband." Jesus said to her, <J>"You have correctly said, 'I do not have a husband';</J>LÌ=ôAt this, Jesus said, <J>"Go, call your husband and come back."</J>Ì<‚7ô<pb/>The woman said to Him, "Sir, give me this water, so that I will not get thirsty nor <n>[have to continually]</n> come all the way here to draw."‚Ì;„ô<J>But whoever drinks the water that I give him will never be thirsty again. But the water that I give him will become in him a spring of water <n>[satisfying his thirst for God]</n> welling up <n>[continually flowing, bubbling within him]</n> to eternal life."</J>[Ì:/ô
Jesus answered her, <J>"Everyone who drinks this water will be thirsty again.</J>Ì9‚-ôAre You greater than our father<f>[5]</f> Jacob, who gave us the well, and who used to drink from it himself, and his sons and his cattle also?"#Ì8‚?ôShe said to Him, "Sir,<f>[4]</f> You have nothing to draw with <n>[no bucket and rope]</n> and the well is deep. Where then do You get that living water?uÌ7ƒcô
Jesus answered her, <J>"If you knew <n>[about]</n> God's gift <n>[of eternal life]</n>, and who it is who says, 'Give Me a drink,' you would have asked Him <n>[instead]</n>, and He would have given you living water (eternal life)."</J>,Ì6‚Qô	The Samaritan woman asked Him, "How is it that You, being a Jew, ask me, a<f>[3]</f> Samaritan woman, for a drink?" (For Jews have nothing to do with Samaritans.)EÌ5ôFor His disciples had gone off into the city to buy foodâ€”fÌ4EôThen a woman from Samaria came to draw water. Jesus said to her, <J>"Give Me a drink"â€”</J>Ì3‚ôand Jacob's well was there. So Jesus, tired as He was from His journey, sat down by the well. It was then about the sixth hour (noon).tÌ2aôSo He arrived at a Samaritan town called Sychar, near the tract of land that Jacob gave to his son Joseph;>Ì1wôNow<f>[1]</f> He had to go through<f>[2]</f> Samaria.5Ì0eôHe left Judea and returned again to Galilee.MÌ/ô(although Jesus Himself was not baptizing, but His disciples were),Ì.	‚ô<pb/>So when the Lord learned that the Pharisees had been told that Jesus was making and baptizing more disciples than John‚Ì-…wô$He who believes <i>and</i> trusts in the Son <i>and</i> accepts Him <n>[as Savior]</n> has eternal life <n>[that is, already possesses it]</n>; but he who does not believe the Son <i>and</i> chooses to reject Him, <n>[disobeying Him and denying Him as Savior]</n> will not see <n>[eternal]</n> life, but <n>[instead]</n> the wrath of God hangs over him <i>continually</i>."_Ì,7ô#The Father loves the Son and has given <i>and</i> entrusted all things into His hand.LÌ+ƒô"For He whom God has sent speaks the words of God <n>[proclaiming the Father's own message]</n>; for God gives the <n>[gift of the]</n> Spirit without measure <n>[generously and boundlessly]</n>!Ì*‚ô!Whoever receives His testimony has set his seal <n>[of approval]</n> to this: God is true <n>[and he knows that God cannot lie]</n>.Ì)‚ô What He has <n>[actually]</n> seen and heard, of that He testifies; and yet no one accepts His testimony <n>[as true]</n>.‚Ì(„ô<pb/>"He who comes from <n>[heaven]</n> above is above all <i>others</i>; he who is of the earth is from the earth and speaks <n>[about things]</n> of the earth <n>[his viewpoint and experience are earthly]</n>. He who comes from heaven is above all.GÌ'ôHe must increase <n>[in prominence]</n>, but I must decrease.bÌ&ƒ=ôHe who has the bride is the bridegroom; but the friend of the bridegroom, who stands by and listens to him, rejoices greatly because of the bridegroom's voice. So this pleasure <i>and</i> joy of mine is now complete.vÌ%ƒeôYou yourselves are my witnesses that I stated, 'I am not the Christ (the Messiah, the Anointed),' but, 'I have <n>[only]</n> been sent ahead of Him <n>[as His appointed forerunner and messenger to announce and proclaim His coming]</n>.'KÌ$ƒôJohn replied, "A man can receive nothing <n>[he can claim nothing at all]</n> unless it has been granted to him from heaven <n>[for there is no other source than the sovereign will of God]</n>.}Ì#ƒsôSo they came to John and said to him, "Rabbi (Teacher), the Man who was with you on the other side of the Jordan <n>[at the Jordan River crossing]</n>â€”and to whom you have testifiedâ€”look, He is baptizing too, and everyone is going to Him!"Ì"‚ô<pb/>Therefore there arose a controversy between John's disciples and a Jew in regard to<f>[4]</f> purification (ceremonial washing).6Ì!gôfor John had not yet been thrown into prison."Ì ‚=ôNow John was also baptizing at Aenon near Salim, because there was an abundance of water there; and <i>people</i> were coming and were being baptizedâ€”Ì{ôAfter these things Jesus and His disciples went into the land of Judea, and there He spent time with them and baptized.‚Ì„1ô<J>But whoever practices truth <n>[and does what is rightâ€”morally, ethically, spiritually]</n> comes to the Light, so that his works may be plainly shown to be what they areâ€”accomplished in God <n>[divinely prompted, done with God's help, in dependence on Him]</n>."</J>OÌƒô<J>For every wrongdoer hates the Light, and does not come to the Light <n>[but shrinks from it]</n> for fear that his <n>[sinful, worthless]</n> activities will be exposed <i>and</i> condemned.</J>‚Ì„ô<J>This is the judgment <n>[that is, the cause for indictment, the test by which people are judged, the basis for the sentence]</n>: the Light has come into the world, and people loved the<f>[3]</f> darkness rather than the Light, for their deeds were evil.</J>„GÌ‰ô<J>Whoever believes <i>and</i> has decided to trust in Him <n>[as personal Savior and Lord]</n> is not judged <n>[for this one, there is no judgment, no rejection, no condemnation]</n>; but the one who does not believe <n>[and has decided to reject Him as personal Savior and Lord]</n> is judged already <n>[that one has been convicted and sentenced]</n>, because<f>[2]</f> he has not believed <i>and</i> trusted in the name of the <n>[One and]</n> only begotten Son of God <n>[the One who is truly unique, the only One of His kind, the One who alone can save him]</n>.</J>PÌƒô<J>For God did not send the Son into the world to judge <i>and</i> condemn the world <n>[that is, to initiate the final judgment of the world]</n>, but that the world might be saved through Him.</J>‚Ì„'ô<pb/><J>"For God so <n>[greatly]</n> loved <i>and</i> dearly prized the world, that He <n>[even]</n> gave His <n>[One and]</n><f>[1]</f> only begotten Son, so that whoever believes <i>and</i> trusts in Him <n>[as Savior]</n> shall not perish, but have eternal life.</J>Ì‚ô<J>so that whoever believes will in Him have eternal life <n>[after physical death, and will actually live forever]</n>.</J>!Ì‚;ô<J>Just as Moses lifted up the <n>[bronze]</n> serpent in the desert <n>[on a pole]</n>, so must the Son of Man be lifted up <n>[on the cross]</n>,</J>Ì‚'ô
<J>No one has gone up into heaven, but there is One who came down from heaven, the Son of Man <n>[Himselfâ€”whose home is in heaven]</n>.</J>FÌƒô<J>If I told you earthly things <n>[that is, things that happen right here on earth]</n> and you do not believe, how will you believe <i>and</i> trust Me if I tell you heavenly things?</J>‚Ì„+ô<J>I assure you <i>and</i> most solemnly say to you, we speak only of what we <n>[absolutely]</n> know and testify about what we have <n>[actually]</n> seen <n>[as eyewitnesses]</n>; and <n>[still]</n> you <n>[reject our evidence and]</n> do not accept our testimony.</J>1Ì‚[ô
Jesus replied, <J>"You are the <n>[great and well-known]</n> teacher of Israel, and yet you do not know <i>nor</i> understand these things <n>[from Scripture]</n>?</J>PÌô	<pb/>Nicodemus said to Him, "How can these things be <i>possible</i>?"=Ì‚sô<J>The wind blows where it wishes and you hear its sound, but you do not know where it is coming from and where it is going; so it is with everyone who is born of the Spirit."</J>Ì‚5ô<J>Do not be surprised that I have told you, 'You must be born again <n>[reborn from aboveâ€”spiritually transformed, renewed, sanctified]</n>.'</J>Ì‚ô<J>That which is born of the flesh is flesh <n>[the physical is merely physical]</n>, and that which is born of the Spirit is spirit.</J>0Ì‚YôJesus answered, <J>"I assure you <i>and</i> most solemnly say to you, unless one is born of water and the Spirit he cannot <n>[ever]</n> enter the kingdom of God.</J>Ì
