Now the Passover of the Jews was approaching, so Jesus went up to Jerusalem.Ë|‚	ô<pb/>After this He went down to Capernaum, He and His mother and brothers and His disciples; and they stayed there a few days.‚,Ë{„QôThis, the first of His signs (attesting miracles), Jesus did in Cana of Galilee, and revealed His glory <n>[displaying His deity and His great power openly]</n>, and His disciples believed <n>[confidently]</n> in Him <n>[as the Messiahâ€”they adhered to, trusted in, and relied on Him]</n>.[Ëzƒ/ô
and said to him, "Everyone else serves his best wine first, and when <i>people</i> have<f>[3]</f> drunk freely, <i>then he serves</i> that which is not so good; but you have kept back the good wine until now.":Ëy‚mô	And when the headwaiter tasted the water which had turned into wine, not knowing where it came from (though the servants who had drawn the water knew) he called the bridegroom,Ëx‚'ôThen He said to them, <J>"Draw <i>some</i> out now and take it to the headwaiter <n>[of the banquet]</n>."</J> So they took it <i>to him</i>.qËw[ôJesus said to the servants, <J>"Fill the waterpots with water."</J> So they filled them up to the brim.Ëv‚1ôNow there were six stone waterpots set there for the Jewish custom of purification (ceremonial washing), containing twenty or thirty gallons each.LËuôHis mother said to the servants, "Whatever He says to you, do it." Ët‚9ôJesus said to her, "<n>[Dear]</n> <J>woman,<f>[2]</f> what is that to you and to Me? My time <n>[to act and to be revealed]</n> has not yet come."</J>rËs]ôWhen the wine was all gone, the mother of Jesus said to Him, "<f>[1]</f> They have no <i>more</i> wine."GËrôand both Jesus and His disciples were invited to the wedding.iËq	Mô<pb/>On the third day there was a wedding at Cana of Galilee, and the mother of Jesus was there;bËp	ƒ?ô3Then He said to him, <J>"I assure you <i>and</i> most solemnly say to you, you will see heaven opened and the angels of God ascending and descending on the Son of Man <n>[the bridge between heaven and earth]</n>."</J>Ëo	‚9ô2Jesus replied, <J>"Because I said to you that I saw you under the fig tree, do you believe <n>[in Me]</n>? You will see greater things than this."</J>cËn	Aô1Nathanael answered, "Rabbi (Teacher), You are the Son of God; You are the King of Israel."9Ëm	‚mô0Nathanael said to Jesus, "How do You know <n>[these things about]</n> me?" Jesus answered, <J>"Before Philip called you, when you were still under the fig tree, I saw you."</J>LËl	ƒô/Jesus saw Nathanael coming toward Him, and said of him, <J>"Here is an Israelite indeed <n>[a true descendant of Jacob]</n>, in whom there is no guile <i>nor</i> deceit <i>nor</i> duplicity!"</J>jËk	Oô.Nathanael answered him, "Can anything good come out of Nazareth?" Philip replied, "Come and see."FËj	ƒô-Philip found Nathanael and told him, "We have found the One Moses in the Law and also the Prophets wrote aboutâ€”Jesus from Nazareth, the son of Joseph <n>[according to public record]</n>."EËi	ô,Now Philip was from Bethsaida, the city of Andrew and Peter.eËh	ƒEô+<pb/>The next day Jesus decided to go into Galilee, and He found Philip and said to him, <J>"Follow Me <n>[as My disciple, accepting Me as your Master and Teacher, and walking the same path of life that I walk]</n>."</J>0Ëg	‚[ô*Andrew brought Simon to Jesus. Jesus looked at him and said, <J>"You are Simon the son of John. You shall be called Cephas</J> (which is translated<f>[17]</f> Peter)."Ëf	‚5ô)He first looked for <i>and</i> found his own brother Simon and told him, "We have found the<f>[16]</f> Messiah" (which translated means the Christ).{Ëe	qô(One of the two who heard what John said and <n>[as a result]</n> followed Jesus was Andrew, Simon Peter's brother.FËd	ƒô'He said to them, <J>"Come, and you will see."</J> So they went <n>[with Him]</n> and saw where He was staying; and they stayed with Him that day, for it was about the<f>[15]</f> tenth hour.4Ëc	‚cô&And Jesus turned and saw them following Him, and asked them, <J>"What do you want?"</J> They answered Him, "Rabbi (which translated means Teacher), where are You staying?"RËb	ô%The two disciples heard him say this, and they<f>[14]</f> followed Jesus.VËa	'ô$and he looked at Jesus as He walked along, and said, "Look! The Lamb of God!"HË`	ô#Again the next day John was standing with two of his disciples,uË_	eô"I myself have <n>[actually]</n> seen <n>[that happen]</n>, and my testimony is that this is the Son of God!"_Ë^	ƒ9ô!I did not recognize Him <n>[as the Messiah]</n>, but He who sent me to baptize<f>[13]</f> in water said to me, 'He upon whom you see the Spirit descend and remain, this One is He who baptizes with the Holy Spirit.'aË]	ƒ=ô John gave <n>[further]</n> evidence <n>[testifying officially for the record, with validity and relevance]</n>, saying, "I have seen the<f>[12]</f> Spirit descending as a dove out of heaven, and He remained upon Him.)Ë\	‚Mô<f>[10]</f> I did not recognize Him <n>[as the Messiah]</n>; but I came baptizing<f>[11]</f> in water so that He would be <n>[publicly]</n> revealed to Israel."Ë[	‚3ôThis is He on behalf of whom I said, 'After me comes a Man who has a higher rank than I <i>and</i> has priority over me, for He existed before me.'ËZ	‚ô<pb/>The next day he saw Jesus coming to him and said, "Look! The Lamb of God<f>[9]</f> who takes away the sin of the world!|ËY	sôThese things occurred in Bethany across the Jordan <n>[at the Jordan River crossing]</n>, where John was baptizing.ËX	‚1ôIt is He <n>[the preeminent One]</n> who comes after me, the<f>[8]</f> strap of whose sandal I am not worthy to untie <n>[even as His slave]</n>."'ËW	‚IôJohn answered them, "I baptize <n>[only]</n><f>[7]</f> in water, but among you there stands One whom you do not recognize <i>and</i> of whom you know nothing.nËV	WôThey asked him, "Why then are you baptizing, if you are not the Christ, nor Elijah, nor the Prophet?"7ËU	kô<pb/>Now they had been sent from the Pharisees.
ËT	‚ôHe said, "I am <e>the voice of one shouting in the wilderness, 'Make straight the way of the Lord</e>,' as the prophet Isaiah said."ËS	‚ôThen they said to him, "Who are you? <i>Tell us</i>, so that we may give an answer to those who sent us. What do you say about yourself?"ËR	‚ôThey asked him, "What then? Are you Elijah?" And he said, "I am not." "Are you the <n>[promised]</n> Prophet?" And he answered, "No."$ËQ	‚CôAnd he confessed <n>[truthfully]</n> and did not deny <n>[that he was only a man]</n>, but acknowledged, "I am not the Christ (the Messiah, the Anointed)!"ËP	‚!ôThis is the testimony of John <n>[the Baptist]</n> when the Jews sent priests and Levites to him from Jerusalem to ask him, "Who are you?"‚%ËO	„EôNo one has seen God <n>[His essence, His divine nature]</n> at any time; the <n>[One and]</n> only begotten God <n>[that is, the unique Son]</n> who is in the intimate presence of the Father, He has explained Him <n>[and interpreted and revealed the awesome wonder of the Father]</n>.ËN	‚ôFor the Law was given through Moses, but grace <n>[the unearned, undeserved favor of God]</n> and truth came through Jesus Christ.[ËM	ƒ1ôFor out of His fullness <n>[the superabundance of His grace and truth]</n> we have all received grace upon grace <n>[spiritual blessing upon spiritual blessing, favor upon favor, and gift heaped upon gift]</n>.‚1ËL	„]ôJohn testified <n>[repeatedly]</n> about Him and<f>[5]</f> has cried out <n>[testifying officially for the record, with validity and relevance]</n>, "This was He of whom I said, 'He who comes after me<f>[6]</f> has a higher rank than I <i>and</i> has priority over me, for He existed before me.'"‚8ËK	„kôAnd the Word (Christ) became flesh, and lived among us; and we <n>[actually]</n> saw His glory, glory as belongs to the <n>[One and]</n> only begotten <i>Son</i> of the Father, <n>[the Son who is truly unique, the only One of His kind, who is]</n>