So they said to him, "How were your eyes opened?"tÎRaô		Some said, "It is he." Still others said, "No, but he looks like him." But he kept saying, "I am the man."|ÎQqô	So the neighbors, and those who used to know him as a beggar, said, "Is not this the man who used to sit and beg?"ÎP‚5ô	And He said to him, <J>"Go, wash in the pool of<f>[2]</f> Siloam"</J> (which is translated, Sent). So he went away and washed, and came back seeing.ÎO‚'ô	When He had said this, He spat on the ground and made mud with His saliva, and He spread the mud <n>[like an ointment]</n> on the man's eyes.ÎNwô	<J>As long as I am in the world, I am the Light of the world <n>[giving guidance through My word and works]</n>."</J>qÎM[ô	<J>We must work the works of Him who sent Me while it is day; night is coming when no one can work.</J> ÎL‚9ô	Jesus answered, <J>"Neither this man nor his parents sinned, but it was so that the works of God might be displayed <i>and</i> illustrated in him.</J>ÎK{ô	His disciples asked Him, "Rabbi (Teacher), who<f>[1]</f> sinned, this man or his parents, that he would be born blind?"_ÎJ	9ô	<pb/>While He was passing by, He noticed a man <n>[who had been]</n> blind from birth.dÎIAô;So they picked up stones to throw at Him, but Jesus concealed Himself and left the temple.|ÎHqô:Jesus replied, <J>"I assure you <i>and</i> most solemnly say to you, before Abraham was born,<f>[8]</f> I Am."</J>uÎGcô9Then the Jews said to Him, "You are not even fifty years old, and You <n>[claim to]</n> have seen Abraham?"ÎF‚ô8<J>Your father Abraham <n>[greatly]</n> rejoiced to see My day (My incarnation).<f>[7]</f> He saw it and was delighted."</J>ÎE‚5ô7<J>Yet you do not know Him, but I know Him fully. If I said I did not know Him, I would be a liar like you. But I do know Him and keep His word.</J>ÎD‚5ô6Jesus answered, <J>"If I glorify Myself, My glory is <n>[worth]</n> nothing. It is My Father who glorifies Me, of whom you say, 'He is our God.'</J>yÎCkô5Are You greater than our father Abraham, who died? The prophets died too! Whom do You make Yourself out to be?"\ÎBƒ1ô4The Jews said to Him, "Now we know that You have a demon <n>[and are under its power]</n>. Abraham died, and also the prophets; yet You say, <J>'If anyone keeps My word, he will never, ever taste of death.'</J>RÎAƒô3<J>I assure you <i>and</i> most solemnly say to you, if anyone keeps My word <n>[by living in accordance with My message]</n> he will indeed never, ever see <i>and</i> experience<f>[6]</f> death."</J>Î@‚!ô2<J>However, I am not seeking glory for Myself. There is One who seeks <n>[glory for Me]</n> and judges <n>[those who dishonor Me]</n>.</J>qÎ?[ô1Jesus answered, <J>"I do not have a demon. On the contrary, I honor My Father, and you dishonor Me.</J>'Î>‚Gô0<pb/>The Jews answered Him, "Are we not right when we say You are a<f>[5]</f> Samaritan and <n>[that You]</n> have a demon <n>[and are under its power]</n>?"VÎ=ƒ%ô/<J>Whoever is of God <i>and</i> belongs to Him hears <n>[the truth of]</n> God's words; for this reason you do not hear them: because you are not of God <i>and</i> you are not in fellowship with Him."</J>yÎ<kô.<J>Which one of you <n>[has proof and]</n> convicts Me of sin? If I speak truth, why do you not believe Me?</J>mÎ;Sô-<J>But because I speak the truth, you do not believe Me <n>[and continue in your unbelief]</n>.</J>‚oÎ:…Wô,<J>You are of <i>your</i> father the devil, and it is your will to practice the desires <n>[which are characteristic]</n> of your father. He was a murderer from the beginning, and does not stand in the truth because there is no truth in him. When he lies, he speaks what it natural to him, for he is a liar and the father of lies <i>and</i> half-truths.</J>)Î9‚Kô+<J>Why do you misunderstand what I am saying? It is because <n>[your spiritual ears are deaf and]</n> you are unable to hear <n>[the truth of]</n> My word.</J>‚CÎ8„ô*Jesus said to them, <J>"If God were your Father <n>[but He is not]</n>, you would love <i>and</i> recognize Me, for I came from God <n>[out of His very presence]</n> and have arrived <i>here</i>. For I have not even come on My own initiative <n>[as self-appointed]</n>, but He <n>[is the One who]</n> sent Me.</J>(Î7‚Iô)<J>You are doing the works of your <n>[own]</n> father."</J> They said to Him, "We are not illegitimate children; we have one <n>[spiritual]</n> Father: God."Î6‚ô(<J>But as it is, you want to kill Me, a Man who has told you the truth, which I heard from God. This is not the way Abraham acted.</J><Î5‚qô'<pb/>They answered, "Abraham is our father." Jesus said to them, <J>"If you are <n>[truly]</n> Abraham's children, then do the works of Abraham <i>and</i> follow his example.</J>"Î4‚=ô&<J>I tell the things that I have seen at My Father's side <n>[in His very presence]</n>; so you also do the things that you heard from your father."</J>8Î3‚iô%<J>I know that you are Abraham's descendants; yet you plan to kill Me, because My word has no place <n>[to grow]</n> in you <n>[and it makes no change in your heart]</n>.</J>PÎ2ô$<J>So if the Son makes you free, then you are unquestionably free.</J>zÎ1mô#<J>Now the slave does not remain in a household forever; the son <n>[of the master]</n> does remain forever.</J>Î0‚)ô"<pb/>Jesus answered, <J>"I assure you <i>and</i> most solemnly say to you, everyone who practices sin <i>habitually</i> is a slave of sin.</J>(Î/‚Iô!They answered Him, "We are Abraham's descendants and have never been enslaved to anyone.<f>[4]</f> What do You mean by saying, <J>'You will be set free'?"</J>
Î.‚ô <J>And you will know the truth <n>[regarding salvation]</n>, and the truth will set you free <n>[from the penalty of sin]</n>."</J>NÎ-ƒôSo Jesus was saying to the Jews who had believed Him, <J>"If you abide in My word <n>[continually obeying My teachings and living in accordance with them, then]</n> you are truly My disciples.</J>AÎ,}ôAs He said these things,<f>[3]</f> many believed in Him. Î+yô<J>And He who sent Me is <n>[always]</n> with Me; He has not left Me alone, because I always do what pleases Him."</J>yÎ*ƒkôSo Jesus said, <J>"When you lift up the Son of Man <n>[on the cross]</n>, you will know then <n>[without any doubt]</n> that I am <i>He</i>, and that I do nothing on My own authority, but I say these things just as My Father taught Me.</J>Î)}ôThey did not realize <n>[or have the spiritual insight to understand]</n> that He was speaking to them about the Father.-Î(‚Sô<J>I have many things to say and judge concerning you, but He who sent Me is true; and I say to the world <n>[only]</n> the things that I have heard from Him."</J>Î'‚ôSo they said to Him, "Who are You <n>[anyway]</n>?" Jesus replied, <J>"What have I been saying to you from the beginning?</J>PÎ&ƒô<J>That is why I told you that you will die <n>[unforgiven and condemned]</n> in your sins; for if you do not believe that I am <i>the One</i> <n>[I claim to be]</n>, you will die in your sins."</J>vÎ%eôHe said to them, <J>"You are from below, I am from above; you are of this world, I am not of this world.</J>Î$‚#ôSo the Jews were asking <n>[among themselves]</n>, "Will He kill Himself? Is that why He says, <J>'Where I am going, you cannot come'?"</J>AÎ#‚{ô<pb/>Then He said again to them, <J>"I am going away, and you will look for Me, and you will die <n>[unforgiven and condemned]</n> in your sin. Where I am going, you cannot come."</J>Î"‚/ôJesus said these things in the treasury, as He taught in the temple <n>[courtyard]</n>; and no one seized Him, because His time had not yet come.5Î!‚côThen the Pharisees said to Him, "Where is this Father of Yours?" Jesus answered, <J>"You know neither Me nor My Father; if you knew Me, you would know My Father also."</J>xÎ iô<J>I am One <n>[of the Two]</n> who testifies about Myself, and My Father who sent Me testifies about Me."</J>|Îqô<J>Even in your own law it is written that the testimony of two persons is true <n>[valid and admissible]</n>.</J>IÎƒô<J>But even if I do judge, My judgment is true <i>and</i> My decision is right; for I am not alone <n>[in making it]</n>, but I and the Father who sent Me <n>[make the same judgment]</n>.</J>wÎgô<J>You judge according to<f>[2]</f> human standards <n>[just by what you see]</n>. I do not judge anyone.</J>PÎƒôJesus replied, <J>"Even if I do testify on My own behalf, My testimony is valid, because I know where I came from and where I am going; but you do not know where I come from or where I am going.</J>lÎQô
Then the Pharisees told Him, "You are testifying on Your own behalf; Your testimony is not valid.":Î‚môOnce more Jesus addressed the crowd. He said, <J>"<f>[1]</f> I am the Light of the world. He who follows Me will not walk in the darkness, but will have the Light of life."</J>{ÎoôShe answered, "No one, Lord!" And Jesus said, <J>"I do not condemn you either. Go. From now on sin no more."]</J>fÎEô
Straightening up, Jesus said to her, <J>"Woman, where are they? Did no one condemn you?"</J>gÎƒGô	They listened <n>[to His reply]</n>, and they <i>began</i> to go out one by one, starting with the oldest ones, until He was left alone, with the woman <n>[standing there before Him]</n> in the center <i>of the court</i>.GÎôThen He stooped down again and started writing on the ground.<Î‚qôHowever, when they persisted in questioning Him, He straightened up and said, <J>"He who is without <n>[any]</n> sin among you, let him be the first to throw a stone at her."</J>#Î‚?ôThey said this to test Him, hoping that they would have grounds for accusing Him. But Jesus stooped down and began writing on the ground with His finger.Î‚'ôNow in the Law Moses commanded us to stone such women <n>[to death]</n>. So what do You say <n>[to do with herâ€”what is Your sentence]</n>?"aÎ;ôand they said to Him, "Teacher, this woman has been caught in the very act of adultery.Î‚ôNow the scribes and Pharisees brought a woman who had been caught in adultery. They made her stand in the center <i>of the court</i>,Î‚5ôEarly in the morning He came back into the temple <n>[court]</n>, and all the people were coming to Him. He sat down and <i>began</i> teaching them.3Î	cô<pb/>But Jesus went to the Mount of Olives.7Îiô5<f>[8]</f>[And everyone went to his own house.!Î
