_ô1But this <n>[ignorant, contemptible]</n> crowd that does not know the Law is accursed <i>and</i> doomed!"<Î	sô0Has any of the rulers or Pharisees believed in Him?fÎEô/Then the Pharisees said to them, "Have you also been deluded <i>and</i> swept off your feet?cÎ?ô.The guards replied, "Never <n>[at any time]</n> has a man talked the way this Man talks!"Î‚+ô-<pb/>Then the guards went <n>[back]</n> to the chief priests and Pharisees, who asked them, "Why did you not bring Him <n>[here with you]</n>?"JÎ
ô,Some of them wanted to arrest Him, but no one laid hands on Him.1Î]ô+So the crowd was divided because of Him.
Î‚ô*Does the Scripture not say that the Christ comes from the descendants of David, and from Bethlehem, the village where David lived?"Î‚)ô)Others said, "This is the Christ (the Messiah, the Anointed)!" But others said, "Surely the Christ is not going to come out of Galilee, is He?]Î3ô(Listening to these words, some of the people said, "This is certainly the Prophet!"hÎ ƒIô'But He was speaking of the <n>[Holy]</n> Spirit, whom those who believed in Him <n>[as Savior]</n> were to receive <i>afterward</i>. The Spirit had not yet been given, because Jesus was not yet glorified (raised to honor).HÍƒ	ô&<J>He who believes in Me <n>[who adheres to, trusts in, and relies on Me]</n>, as the Scripture has said, 'From his innermost being will flow <i>continually</i> rivers of living water.'"</J>4Í~‚aô%<pb/>Now on the last and most important day of the feast, Jesus stood and called out <n>[in a loud voice]</n>, <J>"If anyone is thirsty, let him come to Me and drink!</J>Í}‚-ô$What does this statement of His mean, <J>'You will look for Me, and will not <n>[be able to]</n> find Me; and where I am, you cannot come'?"</J>`Í|ƒ9ô#Then the Jews said among themselves, "Where does this Man intend to go that we will not find Him? Does He intend to go to the Dispersion <n>[of Jews scattered and living]</n> among the Greeks, and teach the Greeks?rÍ{]ô"<J>You will look for Me, and will not <n>[be able to]</n> find Me; and where I am, you cannot come."</J>Íz{ô!Therefore Jesus said, <J>"For a little while longer I am <n>[still]</n> with you, and then I go to Him who sent Me.</J>3Íy‚_ô <pb/>The Pharisees heard the crowd muttering these things <n>[under their breath]</n> about Him, and the chief priests and Pharisees sent<f>[7]</f> guards to arrest Him.%Íx‚CôBut many from the crowd believed in Him. And they kept saying, "When the Christ comes, will He do more signs <i>and</i> exhibit more proofs than this Man?"mÍwSôSo they were eager to arrest Him; but no one laid a hand on Him, because His time had not yet come.Ív‚ô<J>I know Him Myself because I am from Him <n>[I came from His very presence]</n> and it was He <n>[personally]</n> who sent Me."</J>cÍuƒ?ôThen Jesus called out as He taught in the temple, <J>"You know Me and know where I am from; and I have not come on my own initiative <n>[as self-appointed]</n>, but He who sent Me is true, and Him you do not know.</J>lÍtQôBut we know where this Man is from; whenever the Christ comes, no one will know where He is from."	Ís‚ôLook, He is speaking publicly, and they say nothing to Him! Is it possible that the rulers really know that this is the Christ?aÍr;ô<pb/>Then some of the people of Jerusalem said, "Is this not the Man they want to kill?|Íqqô<J>Do not judge by appearance <n>[superficially and arrogantly]</n>, but judge fairly <i>and</i> righteously."</J><Íp‚qô<J>If, to avoid breaking the Law of Moses, a man undergoes<f>[6]</f> circumcision on the Sabbath, why are you angry with Me for making a man's whole body well on the Sabbath?</J>RÍoƒô<J>For this reason Moses has given you <n>[God's law regarding]</n> circumcision (not that it originated with Moses, but with the patriarchs) and you circumcise a man <n>[even]</n> on the Sabbath.</J>UÍn#ôJesus replied, <J>"I did one<f>[5]</f> work, and you are all astounded.</J>jÍmMôThe crowd answered, "You have a demon <n>[You are out of Your mind]</n>! Who wants to kill You?"Íl‚#ô<pb/><J>"Did not Moses give you the Law? And yet not one of you keeps the Law. Why do you want to kill Me <n>[for not keeping it]</n>?"</J>kÍkƒOô<J>He who speaks on his own accord seeks glory <i>and</i> honor for himself. But He who seeks the glory <i>and</i> the honor of the One who sent Him, He is true, and there is no unrighteousness <i>or</i> deception in Him.</J>%Íj‚Cô<J>If anyone is willing to do His will, he will know whether the teaching is of God or whether I speak on My own accord <i>and</i> by My own authority.</J>`Íi9ôJesus answered them by saying, <J>"My teaching is not My own, but His who sent Me.</J>3Íh‚_ôThen the Jews were perplexed. They said, "How<f>[3]</f> did this man become learned <n>[so versed in the Scriptures and theology]</n><f>[4]</f> without formal training?"|Ígqô<pb/>When the feast was already half over, Jesus went up into the temple <n>[court]</n> and <i>began to</i> teach.vÍfeô
Yet no one was speaking out openly <i>and</i> freely about Him for fear of <n>[the leaders of]</n> the Jews.eÍeƒCôThere was a lot of whispered discussion <i>and</i> murmuring among the crowds about Him. Some were saying, "He is a good man"; others said, "No, on the contrary, He misleads the people <n>[giving them false ideas]</n>."RÍdôSo the Jews kept looking for Him at the feast and asking, "Where is He?"DÍcƒô
<pb/>But <n>[afterward]</n>, when His brothers had gone up to the feast, He went up too, not publicly <n>[with a caravan]</n>, but quietly <n>[because He did not want to be noticed]</n>.HÍb	ô	Having said these things to them, He stayed behind in Galilee.xÍaiô<J>Go up to the feast yourselves. I am not going up to this feast because My time has not yet fully come."</J>#Í`‚?ô<J>The world cannot hate you <n>[since you are part of it]</n>, but it does hate Me because I denounce it <i>and</i> testify that its deeds are evil.</J>aÍ_;ôSo Jesus said to them, <J>"My time has not yet come; but any time is right for you.</J>3Í^aôFor not even His brothers believed in Him.<Í]‚qôNo one does anything in secret when he wants to be <i>known</i> publicly. If You <n>[must]</n> do these things, show Yourself openly to the world <i>and</i> make Yourself known!"Í\‚'ôSo His<f>[2]</f> brothers said to Him, "Leave here and go to Judea, so that Your disciples <n>[there]</n> may also see the works that You do.QÍ[ôNow the Jewish<f>[1]</f> Feast of Tabernacles (Booths) was approaching.ÍZ	‚-ô<pb/>After this, Jesus walked <n>[from place to place]</n> in Galilee, for He would not walk in Judea because the Jews were seeking to kill Him.ÍY‚ôGNow He was speaking of Judas, <i>the son</i> of Simon Iscariot; for he, one of the twelve <n>[disciples]</n>, was about to betray Him.ÍX‚ôFJesus answered them, <J>"Did I not choose you, the twelve <n>[disciples]</n>? And yet one of you is a devil (ally of Satan)."</J>hÍWƒIôEWe have believed <i>and</i> confidently trusted, and <n>[even more]</n> we have come to know <n>[by personal observation and experience]</n> that You are the Holy One of God <n>[the Christ, the Son of the living God]</n>."
ÍV‚ôDSimon Peter answered, "Lord, to whom shall we go? You <n>[alone]</n> have the words of eternal life <n>[you are our only hope]</n>.hÍUIôCSo Jesus said to the twelve <n>[disciples]</n>, <J>"You do not want to leave too, do you?"</J>kÍTOôBAs a result of this<f>[8]</f> many of His disciples abandoned Him, and no longer walked with Him.EÍSƒôAAnd He was saying, <J>"This is the reason why I have told you that no one can come to Me unless it has been granted him <n>[that is, unless he is enabled to do so]</n> by the Father."</J>5ÍR‚cô@<J>But <n>[still]</n> there are some of you who do not believe <i>and</i> have faith."</J> For Jesus knew from the beginning who did not believe, and who would betray Him.@ÍQ‚yô?<J>It is the Spirit who gives life; the flesh conveys no benefit <n>[it is of no account]</n>. The words I have spoken to you are spirit and life <n>[providing eternal life]</n>.</J>ÍP‚	ô><J><i>What</i> then <n>[will you think]</n> if you see the Son of Man ascending to <n>[the realm]</n> where He was before?</J>ÍO‚!ô=But Jesus, aware that His disciples were complaining about it, asked them, <J>"Does this cause you to stumble <i>and</i> take offense?</J><ÍN‚qô<<pb/>When many of His disciples heard <i>this</i>, they said, "This is a difficult <i>and</i> harsh <i>and</i> offensive statement. Who can <n>[be expected to]</n> listen to it?"QÍMô;He said these things in a synagogue while He was teaching in Capernaum.yÍLƒkô:<J>This is the Bread which came down out of heaven. It is not like <n>[the manna that]</n> our fathers ate and they <n>[eventually]</n> died; the one who eats this Bread <n>[believes in Me, accepts Me as Savior]</n> will live forever."</J>AÍK‚{ô9<J>Just as the living Father sent Me, and I live because of the Father, even so the one who feeds on Me <n>[believes in Me, accepts Me as Savior]</n> will also live because of Me.</J>$ÍJ‚Aô8<J>He who eats My flesh and drinks My blood <n>[believes in Me, accepts Me as Savior]</n> remains in Me, and I <n>[in the same way remain]</n> in him.</J>mÍISô7<J>For My flesh is true <n>[spiritual]</n> food, and My blood is true <n>[spiritual]</n> drink.</J>aÍHƒ;ô6<J>The one who eats My flesh and drinks My blood <n>[believes in Me, accepts Me as Savior]</n> has eternal life <n>[that is, now possesses it]</n>, and I will raise him up <n>[from the dead]</n> on the last day.</J>‚2ÍG„]ô5And Jesus said to them, <J>"I assure you <i>and</i> most solemnly say to you, unless you eat the flesh of the Son of Man and drink His blood <n>[unless you believe in Me as Savior and believe in the saving power of My blood which will be shed for you]</n>, you do not have life in yourselves.</J>yÍFkô4<pb/>Then the Jews <i>began</i> to argue with one another, saying, "How can this man give us His flesh to eat?"tÍEƒaô3<J>I am the Living Bread that came down out of heaven. If anyone eats of this Bread <n>[believes in Me, accepts Me as Savior]</n>, he will live forever. And the Bread that I will give for the life of the world is My flesh (body)."</J>hÍDIô2<J>This is the Bread that comes down out of heaven, so that one may eat of it and not die.</J>MÍCô1<J>Your fathers ate the manna in the wilderness, and they died.</J>`ÍB9ô0<J>I am the Bread of Life <n>[the Living Bread which gives and sustains life]</n>.</J>jÍAƒMô/<J>I assure you <i>and</i> most solemnly say to you, he who believes <n>[in Me as Saviorâ€”whoever adheres to, trusts in, relies on, and has faith in Meâ€”already]</n> has eternal life <n>[that is, now possesses it]</n>.</J>Í@‚1ô.<J>Not that anyone has seen the Father, except He <n>[who was with the Father and]</n> who is from God; He <n>[alone]</n> has seen the Father.</J>#Í?‚?ô-<J>It is written in the prophets, '<e>And they will all be taught of God</e>.' Everyone who has listened to and learned from the Father, comes to Me.</J><Í>‚qô,<J>No one can come to Me unless the Father who sent Me draws him <n>[giving him the desire to come to Me]</n>; and I will raise him up <n>[from the dead]</n> on the last day.</J>EÍ=ô+So Jesus answered, <J>"Stop murmuring among yourselves.</J>AÍ<‚{ô*They kept saying, "Is this not Jesus, the son of Joseph, whose father and mother we know? How does He now <n>[have the arrogance to]</n> say, <J>'I have come down out of heaven'?"</J>Í;‚ô)Now the Jews murmured <i>and</i> found fault with Him because He said, <J>"I am the Bread that came down out of heaven."</J>`Í:ƒ9ô(<J>For this is My Father's will <i>and</i> purpose, that everyone who sees the Son and believes in Him <n>[as Savior]</n> will have eternal life, and I will raise him up <n>[from the dead]</n> on the last day."</J>)Í9‚Kô'<J>This is the will of Him who sent Me, that of all that He has given Me I lose nothing, but that I <n>[give new life and]</n> raise it up at the last day.</J>pÍ8Yô&<J>For I have come down from heaven, not to do My own will, but to do the will of Him who sent Me.</J>7Í7‚gô%<J>All that My Father gives Me will come to Me; and the one who comes to Me I will most certainly not cast out <n>[I will never, never reject anyone who follows Me]</n>.</J>RÍ6ô$<J>But as I told you, you have seen Me and still you do not believe.</J>{Í5ƒoô#<pb/>Jesus replied to them, <J>"<f>[7]</f> I am the Bread of Life. The one who comes to Me will never be hungry, and the one who believes in Me <n>[as Savior]</n> will never be thirsty <n>[for that one will be sustained spiritually]</n>.</J>BÍ4ô"Then they said to Him, "Lord, always give us this bread."gÍ3Gô!<J>For the Bread of God is He who comes down out of heaven, and gives life to the world."</J>aÍ2ƒ;ô Then Jesus said to them, <J>"I assure you <i>and</i> most solemnly say to you, it is not Moses who has given you the bread out of heaven, but it is My Father who gives you the true<f>[6]</f> bread out of heaven.</J>Í1‚ôOur fathers ate the manna in the wilderness; as it is written <n>[in Scripture]</n>, '<e>He gave them bread out of heaven to eat</e>.'",Í0‚QôSo they said to Him, "What sign (attesting miracle) will You do that we may see it and believe You? What <n>[supernatural]</n> work will You do <n>[as proof]</n>?Í/‚7ôJesus answered, <J>"This is the work of God: that you believe <n>[adhere to, trust in, rely on, and have faith]</n> in the One whom He has sent."</J>oÍ.WôThen they asked Him, "What are we to do, so that we may <i>habitually</i> be doing the works of God?"]Í-ƒ3ô<J>Do not work for food that perishes, but for food that endures <n>[and leads]</n> to eternal life, which the Son of Man will give you; for God the Father has authorized Him <i>and</i> put His seal on Him."</J>WÍ,ƒ'ôJesus answered, <J>"I assure you <i>and</i> most solemnly say to you, you have been searching for Me, not because you saw the signs (attesting miracles), but because you ate the loaves and were filled.</J>oÍ+WôAnd when they found Him on the other side of the sea, they asked Him, "Rabbi, when did You get here?"!Í*‚;ôSo when the crowd saw that neither Jesus nor His disciples were there, they boarded the small boats themselves and came to Capernaum looking for Jesus.Í)‚-ô<n>[Now some]</n> other small boats from<f>[5]</f> Tiberias had come in near the place where they ate the bread after the Lord had given thanks.mÍ(ƒSô<pb/>The next day the crowd that stood on the other side of the sea realized that there had been only one small boat there, and that Jesus had not boarded the boat with His disciples, but that His disciples had gone away alone.Í'‚+ôThen they were willing to take Him on board the boat, and immediately the boat reached the <n>[shore of the]</n> land to which they were going.SÍ&ôBut Jesus said to them, <J>"It is I (<e>I Am</e>); do not be afraid."</J>aÍ%ƒ;ôThen, when they had rowed<f>[3]</f> three or four miles <n>[and were near the<f>[4]</f> center of the sea]</n>, they saw Jesus walking on the sea and approaching the boat; and they were <n>[terribly]</n> frightened.]Í$3ôThe sea was getting rough <i>and</i> rising high because a strong wind was blowing.Í#‚%ôand they got into a boat and started to cross the sea to Capernaum. It was already dark, and Jesus had still not come <n>[back]</n> to them.EÍ"ô<pb/>When evening came, His disciples went down to the sea,Í!‚ôThen Jesus, knowing that they were going to come and take Him by force to make Him king, withdrew again to the mountainside by Himself.4Í ‚aôWhen the people saw the sign (attesting miracle) that He had done, they <i>began</i> saying, "This is without a doubt the promised Prophet who is to come into the world!"Í‚3ô
So they gathered them up, and they filled twelve large baskets with pieces from the five barley loaves which were left over by those who had eaten.Í‚ôWhen they had eaten enough, He said to His disciples, <J>"Gather up the leftover pieces so that nothing will be lost."</J>&Í‚EôThen Jesus took the loaves, and when He had given thanks, He distributed them to those who were seated; the same also with the fish, as much as they wanted.LÍƒô
Jesus said, <J>"Have the people sit down <n>[to eat]</n>."</J> Now <n>[the ground]</n> there was <n>[covered with]</n> an abundance of grass, so the men sat down, about<f>[2]</f>5,000 in number.vÍeô	"There is a little boy here who has five barley loaves and two fish; but what are these for so many people?"KÍôOne of His disciples, Andrew, Simon Peter's brother, said to Him,Í‚ôPhilip answered, "Two hundred denarii (200 days' wages) worth of bread is not enough for each one to receive even a little."SÍôBut He said this to test Philip, because He knew what He was about to do.#Í‚?ôJesus looked up and saw that a large crowd was coming toward Him, and He said to Philip, <J>"Where will we buy bread for these <i>people</i> to eat?"</J>BÍôNow the Passover, the feast of the Jews, was approaching.VÍ%ôAnd Jesus went up on the mountainside and sat down there with His disciples.Í‚1ôA large crowd was following Him because they had seen the signs (attesting miracles) which He <i>continually</i> performed on those who were sick.lÍ	Sô<pb/>After this, Jesus went to the other side of the Sea of Galilee (or<f>[1]</f> Sea of Tiberias).XÍ)ô/<J>But if you do not believe his writings, how will you believe My words?"</J>$Í‚Aô.<J>For if you believed <i>and</i> relied on <n>[the Scriptures written by]</n> Moses, you would believe Me, for he wrote about Me <n>[personally]</n>.</J>eÍƒCô-<J>Do not think that I <n>[am the One who]</n> will accuse you before the Father. There <n>[already]</n> is one who accuses you: Moses, <n>[the very one]</n> in whom you have placed your hope <n>[for salvation]</n>.</J>gÍƒGô,<J>How can you believe <n>[in Me]</n>, when you <n>[seek and]</n> receive glory <i>and</i> approval from one another, and yet you do not seek the glory <i>and</i> approval which comes from the <i>one and</i> only God?</J>‚+Í„Oô+<J>I have come in My Father's name <i>and</i> with His power, and you do not receive Me <n>[because your minds are closed]</n>; but if another comes in his own name <i>and</i> with no authority or power except his own, you will receive him <i>and</i> give your approval to an imposter.</J>hÍ
Iô*<J>but I know you <i>and</i> recognize that you do not have the love of God in yourselves.</J>EÍô)<J>I do not receive glory <i>and</i> approval from men;</J>UÍ#ô(<J>and still you are unwilling to come to Me so that you may have life.</J>aÍ
ƒ;ô'<J><f>[8]</f> You search <i>and</i> keep on searching <i>and</i> examining the Scriptures because you think that in them you have eternal life; and yet it is those <n>[very Scriptures]</n> that testify about Me;</J>+Í	‚Oô&<J>You do not have His word (Scripture) abiding in you <n>[actually living in your hearts and minds]</n>, because you do not believe in Him whom He has sent.</J>
