<pb/>Now before the Passover Feast, Jesus knew that His hour had come <n>[and it was time]</n> for Him to leave this world <i>and</i> return to the Father. Having <n>[greatly]</n> loved His own who were in the world, He loved them <n>[and continuously loves them with His perfect love]</n> to the end (eternally).0Ð‚Yô2<J>I know that His commandment is eternal life. So the things I speak, I speak <n>[in accordance with His exact instruction,]</n> just as the Father has told Me."</J>@Ð‚yô1<J>For I have never spoken on My own initiative <i>or</i> authority, but the Father Himself who sent Me has given Me a commandment <i>regarding</i> what to say and what to speak.</J>4Ð‚aô0<J>Whoever rejects Me and refuses to accept My teachings, has one who judges him; the <i>very</i> word that I spoke will judge <i>and</i> condemn him on the last day.</J>dÐƒAô/<J>If anyone hears My words and does not keep them, I do not judge him; for I did not come to judge <i>and</i> condemn the world <n>[that is, to initiate the final judgment of the world]</n>, but to save the world.</J>qÐƒ[ô.<J>I have come as Light into the world, so that everyone who believes <i>and</i> trusts in Me <n>[as Saviorâ€”all those who anchor their hope in Me and rely on the truth of My message]</n> will not continue to live in darkness.</J>=Ðuô-<J>And whoever sees Me sees the One who sent Me.</J>2Ð‚]ô,<pb/>But Jesus loudly declared, <J>"The one who believes <i>and</i> trusts in Me does not believe <n>[only]</n> in Me but <n>[also believes]</n> in Him who sent Me.</J>KÐ ô+for they loved the approval of men more than the approval of God.‚Ï„ô*Nevertheless, even many of the leading men believed in Him <n>[as Savior and Messiah]</n>, but because of the Pharisees they would not confess it, for fear that <n>[if they acknowledged Him openly]</n> they would be put out of the synagogue (excommunicated);PÏ~ô)Isaiah said these things because he saw His glory and spoke about Him.bÏ}ƒ=ô("<e>He has blinded their eyes and He hardened their heart, to keep them from seeing with their eyes and understanding with their heart and being converted; otherwise</e>, I <n>[their God]</n> <e>would heal them</e>."AÏ|}ô'Therefore they could not believe, for Isaiah said again,NÏ{ƒô&<i>This was</i> to fulfill what Isaiah the prophet said: "<e>Lord, who has believed our message</e>? <e>And to whom has the arm</e> (the power) <e>of the Lord been shown</e> (unveiled, revealed)?"Ïz‚)ô%Even though He had done so many signs (attesting miracles) right before them, yet they still did not believe <i>and</i> failed to trust Himâ€”‚3Ïy„_ô$<t><J>While you have the Light, believe <i>and</i> trust in the Light <n>[have faith in it, hold on to it, rely on it]</n>, so that you may become sons of Light <n>[being filled with Light as followers of God]</n>."</J> </t><br/>Jesus said these things, and then He left and hid Himself from them.‚)Ïx„Kô#So Jesus said to them, <J>"The Light is among you <n>[only]</n> a little while longer. Walk while you have the Light <n>[keep on living by it]</n>, so that darkness will not overtake you. He who walks in the darkness does not know where he is going <n>[he is drifting aimlessly]</n>.</J>PÏwƒô"At this the crowd answered Him, "<f>[5]</f> We have heard from the Law that the Christ is to remain forever; how then can You say, <J>'The Son of Man must be lifted up'?</J> Who is this Son of Man?"LÏvô!He said this to indicate the kind of death by which He was to die.*Ïu‚Mô <J>And I, if <i>and</i> when I am lifted up from the earth <n>[on the cross]</n>, will draw all <i>people</i> to Myself <n>[Gentiles, as well as Jews]</n>."</J>
Ït‚ô<J>Now judgment is upon this world <n>[the sentence is being passed]</n>. Now the ruler of this world (Satan) will be cast out.</J>RÏsôJesus answered, <J>"This voice has come for your sake, not for mine.</J>Ïr‚ôThe crowd <i>of people</i> who stood nearby and heard the voice said that it had thundered; others said, "An angel has spoken to Him!"AÏq‚{ô<n>[Rather, I will say,]</n> <J>'Father, glorify (honor, extol) Your name!'"</J> Then a<f>[4]</f> voice came from heaven saying, "I have both glorified it, and will glorify it again."|Ïpƒqô<J>"Now My soul is troubled <i>and</i> deeply distressed; what shall I say? 'Father, save Me from this hour <n>[of trial and agony]</n>'? But it is for this <n>[very]</n> purpose that I have come to this hour <n>[this time and place]</n>.</J>‚sÏo…_ô<J>If anyone serves Me, he must <n>[continue to faithfully]</n> follow Me <n>[without hesitation, holding steadfastly to Me, conforming to My example in living and, if need be, suffering or perhaps dying because of faith in Me]</n>; and wherever I am <n>[in heaven's glory]</n>, there will My servant be also. If anyone serves Me, the Father will honor him.</J>XÏnƒ)ô<J>The one who loves his life <n>[eventually]</n> loses it <n>[through death]</n>, but the one who hates his life in this world <n>[and is concerned with pleasing God]</n> will keep it for life eternal.</J>sÏmƒ_ô<J>I assure you <i>and</i> most solemnly say to you, unless a grain of wheat falls into the earth and dies, it remains alone <n>[just one grain, never more]</n>. But if it dies, it produces much grain <i>and</i> yields a harvest.</J>sÏl_ôAnd Jesus answered them, <J>"The hour has come for the Son of Man to be glorified <i>and</i> exalted.</J>RÏkôPhilip came and told Andrew; then Andrew and Philip went and told Jesus.wÏjgôthese came to Philip, who was from Bethsaida in Galilee, with a request, saying, "Sir, we wish to see Jesus."fÏiEôNow there were some Greeks (Gentiles) among those who were going up to worship at the feast;(Ïh‚IôThen the Pharisees <n>[argued and]</n> said to one another, "You see that your efforts are futile. Look! The whole world has gone <n>[running]</n> after Him!"}ÏgsôFor this reason the crowd went to meet Him, because they heard that He had performed this <n>[miraculous]</n> sign.Ïf‚-ôSo the people, who were with Him when He called Lazarus out of the tomb and raised him from the dead, continued to tell others <i>about Him</i>.aÏeƒ;ôHis disciples did not understand <n>[the meaning of]</n> these things at first; but when Jesus was glorified <i>and</i> exalted, they remembered that these things had been written about Him and had been done to Him.iÏdKô"<e>Do not fear, Daughter of Zion; Behold, Your King is coming, seated on a donkey's colt</e>."dÏcAôAnd Jesus, finding a young donkey, sat on it; just as it is written <n>[in Scripture]</n>,‚Ïb„'ô
