cusation]</n>.‚cÑG…?ô%So Pilate said to Him, "Then You are a King?" Jesus answered, <J>"You say <n>[correctly]</n> that I am a King. This is why I was born, and for this I have come into the world, to testify to the truth. Everyone who is of the truth <n>[who is a friend of the truth and belongs to the truth]</n> hears <i>and</i> listens carefully to My voice."</J>‚!ÑF„;ô$Jesus replied, <J>"My kingdom is not of this world <n>[nor does it have its origin in this world]</n>. If My kingdom were of this world, My servants would be fighting <n>[hard]</n> to keep Me from being handed over to the Jews; but as it is, My kingdom is not of this world."</J>+ÑE‚Oô#Pilate answered, "I am not a Jew, am I? Your own people and their chief priests have handed You over to me. What have You done <n>[that is worthy of death]</n>?"nÑDUô"Jesus replied, <J>"Are you saying this on your own initiative, or did others tell you about Me?"</J>xÑCiô!<pb/>So Pilate went into the Praetorium again, and called Jesus and asked Him, "Are You the King of the Jews?"}ÑBsô <i>This was</i> to fulfill the word which Jesus had spoken to indicate by what manner of death He was going to die. ÑA‚9ôThen Pilate said to them, "Take Him yourselves and judge Him according to your own law." The Jews said, "We are not permitted to put anyone to death."uÑ@côThey answered, "If He were not a criminal, we would not have handed Him over to you <n>[for judgment]</n>."`Ñ?9ôSo Pilate came out to them and asked, "What accusation do you bring against this Man?"‚`Ñ>…9ôThen the Jews led Jesus from Caiaphas to the Praetorium (governor's palace). Now it was early and the Jews did not enter the Praetorium so that they would not be <n>[ceremonially]</n> unclean, but might <n>[be able to]</n> eat <n>[and participate in the Feast of Unleavened Bread which began after]</n> the<f>[6]</f> Passover <n>[supper]</n>.EÑ=ôSo Peter denied it again, and immediately a rooster crowed.
Ñ<‚ôOne of the high priest's servants, a relative of the one whose ear Peter cut off, said, "Did I not see you with Him in the garden?"/Ñ;‚WôNow Simon Peter was <n>[still]</n> standing and warming himself. So they said to him, "You are not one of His disciples, are you?" He denied it and said, "I am not."=Ñ:uôSo Annas sent Him bound to Caiaphas the high priest.)Ñ9‚KôJesus replied, <J>"If I have said <i>anything</i> wrong, make a formal statement about the wrong; but if <n>[I spoke]</n> properly, why did you strike Me?"</J>+Ñ8‚OôBut when He said this, one of the officers who was standing nearby<f>[5]</f> struck Jesus <n>[in the face]</n>, saying, "Is that how You answer the high priest?"lÑ7Qô<J>Why question Me? Question those who have heard what I said to them. They know what I said."</J>WÑ6ƒ'ôJesus answered him, <J>"I have spoken openly to the world. I always taught in a synagogue and in the temple <n>[area]</n>, where all the Jews <i>habitually</i> congregate; and I said nothing in secret.</J>`Ñ59ô<pb/>Then the high priest questioned Jesus about His disciples and about His teaching.@Ñ4‚yôNow the servants and the officers had made a fire of coals, because it was cold, and they were standing and warming themselves. And Peter was with them, standing and warming himself.	Ñ3‚ôThen the servant girl who kept the door said to Peter, "You are not one of this Man's disciples, are you?" He said, "I am not."5Ñ2‚côbut Peter was standing outside at the door. So the other disciple (John), who was known to the high priest, went out and spoke to the doorkeeper, and brought Peter inside.VÑ1ƒ%ô<pb/>Simon Peter and<f>[4]</f> another disciple were following Jesus. Now that disciple was known to the high priest, so he went with Jesus into the courtyard of the <n>[residence of the]</n> high priest;tÑ0aôIt was Caiaphas who had advised the Jews that it was expedient for one 