Then Simon Peter, who had a sword, drew it and struck the high priest's servant, cutting off his right ear. The servant's name was Malchus.Ñ+‚ô	<i>This was</i> to fulfill <i>and</i> verify the words He had spoken, <J>"Of those whom You have given Me, I have not lost even one."</J>tÑ*aôJesus answered, <J>"I told you that I am <i>He</i>; so if you want Me, let these men go on their way."</J>^Ñ)5ôAgain He asked them, <J>"Whom do you want?"</J> And they said, "Jesus the Nazarene."ZÑ(-ôWhen Jesus said, <J>"I am <i>He</i>,"</J> they drew back and fell to the ground.Ñ'‚%ôThey answered Him, "Jesus the Nazarene." Jesus said, <J>"I am <i>He</i>."</J> And Judas, who was betraying Him, was also standing with them.uÑ&côThen Jesus, knowing all that was about to happen to Him, went to them and asked, <J>"Whom do you want?"</J>2Ñ%‚]ôSo Judas, having obtained the <i>Roman</i><f>[2]</f> cohort and some officers from the high priests and the Pharisees, came there with lanterns and torches and weapons.qÑ$[ôNow Judas, who was betraying Him, knew the place, because Jesus had often met there with His disciples.7Ñ#	‚iô<pb/>Having said these things, Jesus left with His disciples and went across the<f>[1]</f> ravine of the Kidron. There was a garden there, which He and His disciples entered.dÑ"ƒAô<J>and I have made Your name known to them, and will <i>continue to</i> make it known, so that the love with which You have loved Me may be in them <n>[overwhelming their heart]</n>, and I <n>[may be]</n> in them."</J>‚#Ñ!„?ô<pb/><J>"O just <i>and</i> righteous Father, although the world has not known You <i>and</i> has never acknowledged You <n>[and the revelation of Your mercy]</n>, yet I have <i>always</i> known You; and these <n>[believers]</n> know <n>[without any doubt]</n> that You sent Me;</J>sÑ ƒ_ô<J>Father, I desire that they also, whom You have given to Me <n>[as Your gift to Me]</n>, may be with Me where I am, so that they may see My glory which You have given Me, because You loved Me before the foundation of the world.</J>mÑƒSô<J>I in them and You in Me, that they may be perfected <i>and</i> completed into one, so that the world may know <n>[without any doubt]</n> that You sent Me, and <n>[that You]</n> have loved them, just as You have loved Me.</J>Ñô<J>I have given to them the glory <i>and</i> honor which You have given Me, that they may be one, just as We are one;</J>CÑ‚ô<J>that they all may be one; just as You, Father, are in Me and I in You, that they also may be one in Us, so that the world may believe <n>[without any doubt]</n> that You sent Me.</J>bÑƒ=ô<pb/><J>"I do not pray for these alone <n>[it is not for their sake only that I make this request]</n>, but also for <n>[all]</n> those who <n>[will ever]</n> believe <i>and</i> trust in Me through their message,</J>:Ñ‚mô<J>For their sake<f>[5]</f> I sanctify Myself <n>[to do Your will]</n>, so that they also may be sanctified <n>[set apart, dedicated, made holy]</n> in <n>[Your]</n> truth.</J>Ñ‚%ô<J>Just as You commissioned <i>and</i> sent Me into the world, I also have commissioned <i>and</i> sent them (believers) into the world.</J>zÑmô<J>Sanctify them in the truth <n>[set them apart for Your purposes, make them holy]</n>; Your word is truth.</J>JÑ
ô<J>They are not of the world, just as I am not of the world.</J>Ñ}ô<J>I do not ask You to take them out of the world, but that You keep them <i>and</i> protect them from the evil one.</J>uÑƒcô<J>I have given to them Your word <n>[the message You gave Me]</n>; and the world has hated them because they are not of the world <i>and</i> do not belong to the world, just as I am not of the world <i>and</i> do not belong to it.</J>yÑƒkô
<J>But now I am coming to You; and I say these things <n>[while I am still]</n> in the world so that they may experience My joy made full <i>and</i> complete <i>and</i> perfect within them <n>[filling their hearts with My delight]</n>.</J>~Ñƒuô<J>While I was with them, I was keeping them in Your name which You have given Me; and I guarded them <i>and</i> protected them, and not one of them was lost except<f>[4]</f> the son of destruction, so that the Scripture would be fulfilled.</J>\Ñƒ1ô<J>I am no longer in the world; yet they are still in the world, and I am coming to You. Holy Father, keep them in Your name, <i>the name</i> which You have given Me, so that they may be one just as We are.</J>Ñ‚ô
<J>and all things that are Mine are Yours, and <n>[all things that are]</n> Yours are Mine; and I am glorified in them.</J>{Ñoô	<J>I pray for them; I do not pray for the world, but for those You have given Me, because they belong to You;</J>‚Ñ„%ô<J>For the words which You gave Me I have given them; and they received <i>and</i> accepted them and truly understood <n>[with confident assurance]</n> that I came from You <n>[from Your presence]</n>, and they believed <n>[without any doubt]</n> that You sent Me.</J>Ñ‚7ô<J>Now <n>[at last]</n> they know <n>[with confident assurance]</n> that all You have given Me is from You <n>[it is really and truly Yours]</n>.</J>wÑƒgô<pb/><J>"I have manifested Your name <n>[and revealed Your very self, Your real self]</n> to the people whom You have given Me out of the world; they were Yours and You gave them to Me, and they have kept <i>and</i> obeyed Your word.</J>Ñ
‚ô<J>Now, Father, glorify Me together with Yourself, with the glory <i>and</i> majesty that I had with You before the world existed.</J>~Ñuô<J>I have glorified You <n>[down here]</n> on the earth by<f>[3]</f> completing the work that You gave Me to do.</J>JÑƒ
ô<J>Now this is eternal life: that they may know You, the only true <n>[supreme and sovereign]</n> God, and <n>[in the same manner know]</n> Jesus <n>[as the]</n> Christ whom You have sent.</J>iÑ
ƒKô<J>Just as You have given Him power <i>and</i> authority over all mankind, <n>[now glorify Him]</n> so that He may give eternal life<f>[2]</f> to all whom You have given Him <n>[to be Hisâ€”permanently and forever]</n>.</J>LÑ		ƒô<pb/>When Jesus had spoken these things, He raised His eyes to heaven <n>[in prayer]</n> and said, <J>"Father, the<f>[1]</f> hour has come. Glorify Your Son, so that Your Son may glorify You.</J>‚NÑ…ô!<J>I have told you these things, so that in Me you may have <n>[perfect]</n> peace. In the world you have tribulation <i>and</i> distress <i>and</i> suffering, but be courageous <n>[be confident, be undaunted, be filled with joy]</n>; I have overcome the world." <n>[My conquest is accomplished, My victory abiding.]</n></J>OÑƒô <J>Take careful notice: an hour is coming, and has arrived, when you will all be scattered, each to his own <i>home</i>, leaving Me alone; and yet I am not alone, because the Father is with Me.</J>KÑôJesus answered them, <J>"Do you now <n>[at last]</n> believe?</J>+Ñ‚OôNow we know that You know all things, and have no need for anyone to question You; because of this we believe <n>[without any doubt]</n> that you came from God."hÑIô<pb/>His disciples said, "Ah, now You are speaking plainly to us and not in figures of speech!}Ñsô<J>I came from the Father and have come into the world; again, I am leaving the world and going to the Father."</J>
Ñ‚ô<J>for the Father Himself <n>[tenderly]</n> loves you, because you have loved Me and have believed that I came from the Father.</J>#Ñ‚?ô<J>In that day you will ask in My name, and I am not saying to you that I will ask the Father on your behalf <n>[because it will be unnecessary]</n>;</J>eÑ ƒCô<pb/><J>"I have told you these things in figurative language (veiled language, proverbs); the hour is now coming when I will no longer speak to you in figures of speech, but I will tell you plainly about the Father.</J>HÐƒ	ô<J>Until now you have not asked <n>[the Father]</n> for anything in My name; but now ask <i>and</i> keep on asking and you will receive, so that your joy may be full <i>and</i> complete.</J>[Ð~ƒ/ô<J>In that day you will not <n>[need to]</n> ask Me about anything. I assure you <i>and</i> most solemnly say to you, whatever you ask the Father in My name <n>[as My representative]</n>, He will give you.</J>/Ð}‚Wô<J>So for now you are in grief; but I will see you again, and <n>[then]</n> your hearts will rejoice, and no one will take away from you your <n>[great]</n> joy.</J>rÐ|ƒ]ô<J>A woman, when she is in labor, has pain because her time <n>[to give birth]</n> has come; but when she has given birth to the child, she no longer remembers the anguish because of her joy that a child has come into the world.</J>XÐ{ƒ)ô<J>I assure you <i>and</i> most solemnly say to you, that you will weep and grieve <n>[in great mourning]</n>, but the world will rejoice. You will be sorrowful, but your sorrow will be turned into joy.</J>jÐzƒMôJesus knew that they wanted to ask Him, so He said to them, <J>"Are you wondering among yourselves about what I meant when I said, 'A little while, and you will not see Me, and again a little while, and you will see Me'?</J>Ðy}ôSo they were saying, "What does He mean when He says, <J>'A little while'?</J> We do not know what He is talking about."jÐxƒMôSome of His disciples said to one another, "What does He mean when He tells us, <J>'A little while, and you will not see Me; and again a little while, and you will see Me';</J> and, <J>'because I am going to My Father'?"</J>pÐwYô<J>"A little while, and you will no longer see Me; and again a little while, and you will see Me."</J>#Ðv‚?ô<J>All things that the Father has are Mine. Because of this I said that He <n>[the Spirit]</n> will take from what is Mine and will reveal it to you.</J>Ðu‚ô<J>He will glorify <i>and</i> honor Me, because He (the Holy Spirit) will take from what is Mine and will disclose it to you.</J>‚OÐt…ô
<J>But when He, the Spirit of Truth, comes, He will guide you into all the truth <n>[full and complete truth]</n>. For He will not speak on His own initiative, but He will speak whatever He hears <n>[from the Fatherâ€”the message regarding the Son]</n>, and He will disclose to you what is to come <n>[in the future]</n>.</J>lÐsQô<pb/><J>"I have many more things to say to you, but you cannot bear <n>[to hear]</n> them now.</J>Ðr‚ô<J>about judgment <n>[the certainty of it]</n>, because the ruler of this world (Satan) has been judged <i>and</i> condemned.</J>Ðq‚!ô
<J>about righteousness <n>[personal integrity and godly character]</n>, because I am going to My Father and you will no longer see Me;</J>yÐpkô	<J>about sin <n>[and the true nature of it]</n>, because they do not believe in Me <n>[and My message]</n>;</J>/Ðo‚Wô<J>And He, when He comes, will convict the world about <n>[the guilt of]</n> sin <n>[and the need for a Savior]</n>, and about righteousness, and about judgment:</J>‚?Ðn„wô<J>But I tell you the truth, it is to your advantage that I go away; for if I do not go away, the<f>[1]</f> Helper (Comforter, Advocate, Intercessorâ€”Counselor, Strengthener, Standby) will not come to you; but if I go, I will send Him (the Holy Spirit) to you <n>[to be in close fellowship with you]</n>.</J>Ðm‚ô<J>But because I have said these things to you, sorrow has filled your hearts <n>[and taken complete possession of them]</n>.</J>hÐlIô<J>"But now I am going to Him who sent Me; and none of you asks Me, 'Where are You going?'</J>TÐkƒ!ô<J>I have told you these things <n>[now]</n>, so that when their time comes, you will remember that I told you about them. I did not say these things to you at the beginning, because I was with you.</J>\Ðj1ô<J>And they will do these things because they have not known the Father or Me.</J>1Ði‚[ô<J>They will put you out of the synagogues <i>and</i> make you outcasts. And a time is coming when whoever kills you will think that he is offering service to God.</J>Ðh	‚ô<pb/><J>"I have told you these things so that you will not stumble <i>or</i> be caught off guard <i>and</i> fall away.</J>xÐgiô<J>But you will testify also <i>and</i> be My witnesses, because you have been with Me from the beginning.</J>‚Ðf„-ô<pb/><J>"But when the<f>[4]</f> Helper (Comforter, Advocate, Intercessorâ€”Counselor, Strengthener, Standby) comes, whom I will send to you from the Father, <i>that is</i> the Spirit of Truth who comes from the Father, He will testify <i>and</i> bear witness about Me.</J>Ðe‚%ô<J>But <n>[this is so]</n> that the word which has been written in their Law would be fulfilled, '<e>They hated Me without a cause</e>.'</J>‚;Ðd„oô<J>If I had not done among them the works (attesting miracles) which no one else <n>[ever]</n> did, they would not have <n>[the guilt of their]</n> sin; but now <n>[the fact is that]</n> they have both seen <n>[these works]</n> and have hated Me <n>[and continue to hate Me]</n> and My Father as well.</J>:Ðcoô<J>The one who hates Me also hates My Father.</J>Ðb‚%ô<J>If I had not come and spoken to them, they would not have <n>[the guilt of their]</n> sin; but now they have no excuse for their sin.</J>EÐaƒô<J>But they will do all these <n>[hurtful]</n> things to you for My name's sake <n>[because you bear My name and are identified with Me]</n>, for they do not know the One who sent Me.</J>^Ð`ƒ5ô<J>Remember <n>[and continue to remember]</n> that I told you, 'A servant is not greater than his master.' If they persecuted Me, they will also persecute you. If they kept My word, they will keep yours also.</J>‚Ð_„+ô<J>If you belonged to the world, the world would love <n>[you as]</n> its own <i>and</i> would treat you with affection. But you are not of the world <n>[you no longer belong to it]</n>, but I have chosen you out of the world. And because of this the world hates you.</J>tÐ^aô<J>"If the world hates you <n>[and it does]</n>, know that it has hated Me before <i>it hated</i> you.</J>yÐ]kô<J>This <n>[is what]</n> I command you: that you love <i>and</i> unselfishly seek the best for one another.</J>‚eÐ\…Cô<J>You have not chosen Me, but I have chosen you and I have appointed <i>and</i> placed <i>and</i> purposefully planted you, so that you would go and bear fruit <i>and</i> keep on bearing, and that your fruit will remain <i>and</i> be lasting, so that whatever you ask of the Father in My name <n>[as My representative]</n> He may give to you.</J>fÐ[ƒEô<J>I do not call you servants any longer, for the servant does not know what his master is doing; but I have called you <n>[My]</n> friends, because I have revealed to you everything that I have heard from My Father.</J>LÐZô<J>You are my friends if you keep on doing what I command you.</J>xÐYiô
<J>No one has greater love <n>[nor stronger commitment]</n> than to lay down his own life for his friends.</J>ÐX‚ô<J>"This is My commandment, that you<f>[3]</f> love <i>and</i> unselfishly seek the best for one another, just as I have loved you.</J>-ÐW‚Sô<J>I have told you these things so that My joy <i>and</i> delight may be in you, and that your joy may be made full <i>and</i> complete <i>and</i> overflowing.</J>*ÐV‚Mô
<J>If you keep My commandments <i>and</i> obey My teaching, you will remain in My love, just as I have kept My Father's commandments and remain in His love.</J>ÐUwô	<J>I have loved you just as the Father has loved Me; remain in My love <n>[and do not doubt My love for you]</n>.</J>ÐT‚!ô<J>My Father is glorified <i>and</i> honored by this, when you bear much fruit, and prove yourselves to be My <n>[true]</n> disciples.</J>AÐS‚{ô<J>If you remain in Me and My words remain in you <n>[that is, if we are vitally united and My message lives in your heart]</n>, ask whatever you wish and it will be done for you.</J>SÐRƒô<J>If anyone does not remain in Me, he is thrown out like a <n>[broken off]</n> branch, and withers <i>and</i> dies; and they gather such branches and throw them into the fire, and they are burned.</J>eÐQƒCô<J><f>[2]</f> I am the Vine; you are the branches. The one who remains in Me and I in him bears much fruit, for <n>[otherwise]</n> apart from Me <n>[that is, cut off from vital union with Me]</n> you can do nothing.</J>jÐPƒMô<J>Remain in Me, and I <n>[will remain]</n> in you. Just as no branch can bear fruit by itself without remaining in the vine, neither can you <n>[bear fruit, producing evidence of your faith]</n> unless you remain in Me.</J>	ÐO‚ô<J>You are already clean because of the word which I have given you <n>[the teachings which I have discussed with you]</n>.</J>gÐNƒGô<J>Every branch in Me that does not bear fruit, He takes away; and every <i>branch</i> that continues to bear fruit, He <n>[repeatedly]</n> prunes, so that it will bear more fruit <n>[even richer and finer fruit]</n>.</J>VÐM	'ô<pb/><J>"<f>[1]</f> I am the true Vine, and My Father is the vinedresser.</J>XÐLƒ)ô<J>but so that the world may know <n>[without any doubt]</n> that I love the Father, I do exactly as the Father has commanded Me <n>[and act in full agreement with Him]</n>. Get up, let us go from here.</J>BÐK‚}ô<J>I will not speak with you much longer, for the ruler of the world (Satan) is coming. And he has no claim on Me <n>[no power over Me nor anything that he can use against Me]</n>;</J>ÐJ‚ô<J>I have told you now before it happens, so that when it does take place, you may believe <i>and</i> have faith <n>[in Me]</n>.</J>tÐIƒaô<J>You heard Me tell you, 'I am going away, and I am coming <i>back</i> to you.' If you <n>[really]</n> loved Me, you would have rejoiced, because I am going <n>[back]</n> to the Father, for<f>[5]</f> the Father is greater than I.</J>‚'ÐH„Gô<J>Peace I leave with you; My <n>[perfect]</n> peace I give to you; not as the world gives do I give to you. Do not let your heart be troubled, nor let it be afraid. <n>[Let My perfect peace calm you in every circumstance and give you courage and strength for every challenge.]</n></J>‚?ÐG„wô<J>But the<f>[4]</f> Helper (Comforter, Advocate, Intercessorâ€”Counselor, Strengthener, Standby), the Holy Spirit, whom the Father will send in My name <n>[in My place, to represent Me and act on My behalf]</n>, He will teach you all things. And He will help you remember everything that I have told you.</J>NÐFô<pb/><J>"I have told you these things while I am still with you.</J>&ÐE‚Eô<J>One who does not <n>[really]</n> love Me does not keep My words. And the word (teaching) which you hear is not Mine, but is the Father's who sent Me.</J>AÐD‚{ôJesus answered, <J>"If anyone <n>[really]</n> loves Me, he will keep My word (teaching); and My Father will love him, and We will come to him and make Our dwelling place with him.</J>ÐC‚ôJudas (not Iscariot) asked Him, "Lord, what has happened that You are going to reveal Yourself to us and not to the world?"‚ÐBƒô<J>The person who has My commandments and keeps them is the one who <n>[really]</n> loves Me; and whoever <n>[really]</n> loves Me will be loved by My Father, and I will love him and reveal Myself to him <n>[I will make Myself real to him]</n>."</J>!ÐA‚;ô<J>On that day <n>[when that time comes]</n> you will know for yourselves that I am in My Father, and you <i>are</i> in Me, and I <i>am</i> in you.</J>Ð@wô<J>After a little while the world will no longer see Me, but you will see Me; because I live, you will live also.</J>Ð?‚ô<pb/><J>"I will not leave you as orphans <n>[comfortless, bereaved, and helpless]</n>; I will come <n>[back]</n> to you.</J>xÐ>ƒiô<J>the Spirit of Truth, whom the world cannot receive <n>[and take to its heart]</n> because it does not see Him or know Him, <i>but</i> you know Him because He (the Holy Spirit) remains with you <i>continually</i> and will be in you.</J>:Ð=‚mô<J>And I will ask the Father, and He will give you another<f>[3]</f> Helper (Comforter, Advocate, Intercessorâ€”Counselor, Strengthener, Standby), to be with you foreverâ€”</J>eÐ<Cô<pb/><J>"If you <n>[really]</n> love Me, you will keep <i>and</i> obey My commandments.</J>_Ð;7ô<J>If you ask Me anything in My name <n>[as My representative]</n>, I will do it.</J>AÐ:‚{ô
<J>And I will do whatever you ask in My name</J> <n>[<f>[2]</f> as My representative]</n>, <J>this I will do, so that the Father may be glorified <i>and</i> celebrated in the Son.</J>‚Ð9ƒô<J>I assure you <i>and</i> most solemnly say to you, anyone who believes in Me <n>[as Savior]</n> will also do the things that I do; and he will do even greater things than these <n>[in extent and outreach]</n>, because I am going to the Father.</J>;Ð8‚oô<J>Believe Me that I am in the Father and the Father is in Me; otherwise believe <n>[Me]</n> because of the <n>[very]</n> works themselves <n>[which you have witnessed]</n>.</J>‚Ð7„'ô
<J>Do you not believe that I am in the Father, and the Father is in Me? The words I say to you I do not say on My own initiative <i>or</i> authority, but the Father, abiding <i>continually</i> in Me, does His works <n>[His attesting miracles and acts of power]</n>.</J>kÐ6ƒOô	Jesus said to him, <J>"Have I been with you for so long a time, and you do not know Me yet, Philip, <i>nor</i> recognize clearly who I am? Anyone who has seen Me has seen the Father. How can you say, 'Show us the Father?'</J>\Ð51ô<pb/>Philip said to Him, "Lord, show us the Father and then we will be satisfied."Ð4‚	ô<J>If you had <n>[really]</n> known Me, you would also have known My Father. From now on you know Him, and have seen Him."</J>=Ð3‚sôJesus said to him, <J>"<f>[1]</f> I am the <n>[only]</n> Way <n>[to God]</n> and the <n>[real]</n> Truth and the <n>[real]</n> Life; no one comes to the Father but through Me.</J>eÐ2CôThomas said to Him, "Lord, we do not know where You are going; so how can we know the way?"OÐ1ô<J>And <n>[to the place]</n> where I am going, you know the way."</J>Ð0‚ô<J>And if I go and prepare a place for you, I will come back again and I will take you to Myself, so that where I am you may be also.</J>Ð/‚5ô<J>In My Father's house are many dwelling places. If it were not so, I would have told you, because I am going there to prepare a place for you.</J>[Ð.	ƒ1ô<pb/><J>"Do not let your heart be troubled (afraid, cowardly). Believe <n>[confidently]</n> in God <i>and</i> trust in Him, <n>[have faith, hold on to it, rely on it, keep going and]</n> believe also in Me.</J>YÐ-ƒ+ô
&Jesus answered, <J>"Will you <n>[really]</n> lay down your life for Me? I assure you <i>and</i> most solemnly say to you, before a rooster crows you will deny <i>and</i> completely disown Me three times.</J>bÐ,=ô
