ôThen Jesus said to them again, <J>"Peace to you; as the Father has sent Me, I also send you <n>[as My representatives]</n>."</J>Ò‚ôAfter He said this, He showed them His hands and His side. When the disciples saw the Lord, they were filled with great joy.vÒƒeôSo when it was evening on that <i>same</i> day, the first day of the week, though the disciples were <n>[meeting]</n> behind barred doors for fear of the Jews, Jesus came and stood among them, and said, <J>"<f>[9]</f> Peace to you."</J>~ÒuôMary Magdalene came, reporting to the disciples that she had seen the Lord and that He had said these things to her.[Òƒ/ôJesus said to her, <J>"<f>[8]</f> Do not hold Me, for I have not yet ascended to the Father; but go to My brothers and tell them, 'I am ascending to My Father and your Father, and to My God and your God.'"</J>~ÒuôJesus said to her, <J>"Mary!"</J> She turned and said to Him in<f>[7]</f> Hebrew, "Rabboni!" (which means, Teacher).‚
