ôJesus said to her, <J>"Woman, why are you crying? For whom are you looking?"</J> Supposing that He was the gardener, she replied, "Sir, if you are the one who has carried Him away <i>from here</i>, tell me where you have put Him, and I will take Him away."{ÒoôAfter saying this, she turned around and saw Jesus standing <i>there</i>, but she did not know that it was Jesus.Ò‚7ô
And they said to her, "Woman, why are you crying?" She told them, "Because they have taken away my Lord, and I do not know where they have laid Him."Ò ‚ôand she saw two angels in white sitting <i>there</i>, one at the head and one at the feet, where the body of Jesus had lain.Ñ‚)ô<pb/>But Mary <n>[who had returned]</n> was standing outside the tomb sobbing; and so, as she wept, she stooped down and looked into the tomb;?Ñ~yô
Then the disciples went back again to their own homes.\Ñ}1ô	For as yet they did not understand the Scripture, that He must rise from the dead.XÑ|ƒ)ôSo the other disciple, who had reached the tomb first, went in too; and he saw <n>[the wrappings and the face-cloth]</n> and<f>[6]</f> believed <n>[without any doubt that Jesus had risen from the dead]</n>.6Ñ{‚eôand the <n>[burial]</n><f>[4]</f> face-cloth which had been on Jesus' head, not lying with the <n>[other]</n> linen wrappings, but<f>[5]</f> rolled up in a place by itself.	Ñz‚ôThen Simon Peter came up, following him, and went into the tomb and saw the linen wrappings <n>[neatly]</n> lying <i>there</i>;Ñy‚ôStooping down and looking in, he saw the linen<f>[3]</f> wrappings <n>[neatly]</n> lying <i>there</i>; but he did not go in.oÑxWôAnd the two were running together, but the other disciple outran Peter and arrived at the tomb first.PÑwôSo Peter and the other disciple left, and they were going to the tomb.oÑvƒWôSo she ran and went to Simon Peter and to the<f>[1]</f> other disciple (John), whom Jesus loved (esteemed), and said to them, "They have taken away the Lord out of the tomb, and<f>[2]</f> we do not know where they have laid Him!"SÑu	ƒ!ô<pb/>Now on the first day of the week Mary Magdalene came to the tomb early, while it was still dark, and saw the stone <n>[already]</n> removed from the <n>[groove across the entrance of the]</n> tomb.tÑtaô*Therefore, because of the Jewish day of Preparation, and since the tomb was nearby, they laid Jesus there.$Ñs‚Aô)Now there was a garden at the place where He was crucified, and in the garden a new tomb <n>[cut out of solid rock]</n> in which no one had yet been laid.Ñr{ô(So they took Jesus' body and bound it in linen wrappings with the fragrant spices, as is the burial custom of the Jews.-Ñq‚Sô'Nicodemus, who had first come to Him at night, also came bringing a mixture of myrrh and aloes, <n>[weighing]</n> about a hundred <n>[Roman]</n><f>[17]</f> pounds.eÑpƒCô&<pb/>And after this, Joseph of Arimatheaâ€”a disciple of Jesus, but secretly for fear of the Jewsâ€”asked Pilate to let him take away the body of Jesus; and Pilate gave him permission. So he came and took away His body.cÑo?ô%And again another Scripture says, "<e>They shall look at Him whom they have pierced</e>."kÑnOô$For these things took place to fulfill the Scripture, "<e>Not a bone of His shall be broken</e>."AÑm‚{ô#And he (John, the eyewitness) who has seen it has testified, and his testimony is true; and he knows that he is telling the truth, so that you also <n>[who read this]</n> may believe.{Ñloô"But one of the soldiers pierced His side with a spear, and immediately blood and water came <n>[flowing]</n> out.dÑkAô!But when they came to Jesus and saw that He was already dead, they did not break His legs.uÑjcô So the soldiers came and broke the legs of the first man, and of the other who had been crucified with Him.‚%Ñi„CôSince it was the day of Preparation <n>[for the Sabbath]</n>, in order to prevent the bodies from hanging on the cross on the Sabbath (for that Sabbath was a high holy day) the Jews asked Pilate to have their legs<f>[16]</f> broken <n>[to hasten death]</n> and the bodies taken away. Ñh‚9ôWhen Jesus had received the sour wine, He said, <J>"It is finished!"</J> And He bowed His head and <n>[voluntarily]</n><f>[15]</f> gave up His spirit.$Ñg‚AôA jar full of<f>[14]</f> sour wine was placed there; so they put a sponge soaked in the sour wine on <n>[a branch of]</n> hyssop and held it to His mouth.Ñf{ô<pb/>After this, Jesus, knowing that all was now finished, said in fulfillment of the Scripture, <J>"I am thirsty."</J>?Ñe‚wôThen He said to the disciple (John), <J>"Look! <n>[here is]</n> your mother <n>[protect and provide for her]</n>!"</J> From that hour the disciple took her into his own <i>home</i>.=Ñd‚sôSo Jesus, seeing His mother, and the<f>[13]</f> disciple whom He loved (esteemed) standing near, said to His mother, "<n>[Dear]</n> <J>woman, look, <n>[here is]</n> your son!"</J>[Ñcƒ/ô<t>So the soldiers did these things. </t><br/>But standing by the cross of Jesus were His mother, His mother's sister <n>[<f>[11]</f> Salome]</n>,<f>[12]</f> Mary the <i>wife</i> of Clopas, and Mary Magdalene.wÑbƒgôSo they said to one another, "Let us not tear it, but cast lots for it, <i>to decide</i> whose it will be." <i>This was</i> to fulfill the Scripture, "<e>They divided My outer clothing among them, and for My clothing they cast lots</e>."uÑaƒcô<pb/>Then the soldiers, when they had crucified Jesus, took His outer clothes and made four parts, a part for each soldier, and also the tunic. But the<f>[10]</f> tunic was seamless, woven <n>[in one piece]</n> from the top throughout._Ñ`7ôPilate replied, "What I have written I have written <n>[and it remains written]</n>."
