ritual blessing) in the sight of God and asked that he might <n>[be allowed to]</n> find a dwelling place for the<f>[10]</f> God of Jacob.cÔƒ?þ-Our fathers also brought it in <n>[with them into the land]</n> with Joshua when they dispossessed the<f>[9]</f> nations whom God drove out before our fathers, <n>[and so it remained here]</n> until the time of David, Ô‚9þ,<pb/>"Our fathers had the tabernacle of testimony in the wilderness, just as God directed Moses to make it according to the pattern which he had seen.iÔƒKþ+<e>You also took along the tabernacle</e> (portable temple) <e>of Moloch and the star of the god Rompha, the images which you made to worship; and I will remove you beyond Babylon</e> <n>[carrying you away into exile]</n>.'‚SÔ…þ*But God turned away <n>[from them]</n> and handed them over to serve the<f>[8]</f> host of heaven. As it is written <i>and</i> forever remains written in the book of the prophets, '<e>It was not</e> <n>[really]</n> <e>to Me that you offered victims and sacrifices for forty years in the wilderness, was it, O house of Israel</e>?Ô‚þ)In those days they made a calf and brought a sacrifice to the idol, and rejoiced <i>and</i> celebrated over the works of their hands.+Ô‚Oþ(<e>They said to Aaron, 'Make for us gods who will go before us; for this Moses who led us out of the land of Egypt, we do not know what has happened to him</e>.'Ô‚3þ'Our fathers were unwilling to be subject to him <n>[and refused to listen to him]</n>. They rejected him, and in their hearts turned back to Egypt.‚Ô„þ&This is the one who was in the congregation in the wilderness together with the Angel who spoke to him on Mount Sinai, and <i>who was</i> with our fathers; and he received living oracles <n>[divine words that still live]</n> to be handed down to you.Ô‚-þ%This is the Moses who said to the children of Israel, '<e>God will raise up for you a Prophet</e><f>[7]</f><e>like me