<pb/>Now in the church at Antioch there were prophets <n>[who spoke a new message of God to the people]</n> and teachers: Barnabas, Simeon who was called<f>[1]</f> Niger, Lucius of Cyrene, Manaen who had been brought up with<f>[2]</f> Herod <n>[Antipas]</n> the tetrarch, and Saul.Õc‚3þ<pb/>Barnabas and Saul came back<f>[9]</f> from Jerusalem when they had completed their mission, bringing with them John, who was also called Mark. Õb‚9þ<pb/>But the word of the Lord <n>[the good news about salvation through Christ]</n> continued to grow and spread <n>[increasing in effectiveness]</n>._Õaƒ7þAnd at once an angel of the Lord struck him down because he did not give God the glory <n>[and instead permitted himself to be worshiped]</n>, and<f>[8]</f> he was eaten by worms and died <n>[five days later]</n>.ZÕ`-þThe assembled people kept shouting, "It is the voice of a god and not of a man!"+Õ_‚OþOn an appointed day Herod dressed himself in his<f>[7]</f> royal robes, sat on his throne (tribunal, rostrum) and <i>began</i> delivering a speech to the people.‚tÕ^…aþNow Herod <n>[Agrippa I]</n> was<f>[5]</f> extremely angry with the people of Tyre and Sidon; and their delegates came to him in a united group, and after persuading Blastus,<f>[6]</f> the king's chamberlain <n>[to support their cause]</n>, they asked for peace, because their country was fed by <n>[imports of grain and other goods from]</n> the king's country.kÕ]ƒOþWhen Herod had searched for him and could not find him, he interrogated the guards and commanded that they be led away <i>to execution</i>. Then he went down from Judea to Caesarea <n>[Maritima]</n> and spent some time there.rÕ\]þ<pb/>Now when day came, there was no small disturbance among the soldiers over what had become of Peter.‚Õ[ƒ{þBut motioning to them with his hand to be quiet <i>and</i> listen, he described how the Lord had led him out of the prison. And he said, "Report these things to<f>[4]</f> James and the brothers and sisters." Then he left and went to another place.	ÕZ‚þBut <n>[meanwhile]</n> Peter continued knocking; and when they opened <i>the door</i> and saw him, they were completely amazed.ÕYþThey said to her, "You are out of your mind!" But she kept insisting that it was so. They kept saying, "It is his angel!"ÕX‚%þRecognizing Peter's voice, in her joy she failed to open the gate, but ran in and announced that Peter was standing in front of the gateway.`ÕW9þ
When he knocked at the door of the gateway, a servant-girl named Rhoda came to answer.‚ÕV„þWhen he realized what had happened, he went to the house of<f>[2]</f> Mary the mother of John, who was also called<f>[3]</f> Mark, where many <n>[believers]</n> were gathered together and were praying <i>continually</i> <n>[and had been praying all night]</n>.^ÕUƒ5þWhen Peter came to his senses, he said, "Now I know for certain that the Lord has sent His angel and has rescued me from the hand of Herod and from all that the Jewish people were expecting <n>[to do to me]</n>."jÕTƒMþ
When they had passed the first guard and the second, they came to the iron gate that leads into the city. Of its own accord it swung open for them; and they went out and went along one street, and at once the angel left him.ÕS‚7þ	And Peter went out following <i>the angel</i>. He did not realize that what was being done by the angel was real, but thought he was seeing a vision.FÕRƒþThe angel said to him, "Prepare yourself and strap on your sandals <n>[to get ready for whatever may happen]</n>." And he did so. Then the angel told him, "Put on your robe and follow me."QÕQƒþSuddenly, an angel of the Lord appeared <n>[beside him]</n> and a light shone in the cell. The angel struck Peter's side and awakened him, saying, "Get up quickly!" And the chains fell off his hands.@ÕP‚yþ<pb/>The very night before Herod was to bring him forward, Peter was sleeping between two soldiers, bound with two chains, and sentries were in front of the door guarding the prison.|ÕOqþSo Peter was kept in prison, but fervent <i>and</i> persistent prayer for him was being made to God by the church.‚ÕNƒ{þWhen he had seized Peter, he put him in prison, turning him over to four squads of soldiers of four each to guard him <n>[in rotation throughout the night]</n>, planning after the Passover to bring him out before the people <n>[for execution]</n>.)ÕM‚Kþand when he saw that it pleased the Jews, he proceeded to have Peter arrested as well. This was during the days of Unleavened Bread <n>[the Passover week]</n>.IÕLþAnd he had James the brother of John put to death with a sword;!ÕK	‚=þ<pb/>Now at that time<f>[1]</f> Herod <n>[Agrippa I]</n> the king <n>[of the Jews]</n> arrested some who belonged to the church, intending to harm them.YÕJ+þAnd this they did, sending the contribution to the elders by Barnabas and Saul.ÕI‚þSo the disciples decided to send <i>a contribution</i>, each according to his individual ability, to the believers who lived in Judea.VÕHƒ%þOne of them named Agabus stood up and prophesied through the <n>[Holy]</n> Spirit that a severe famine would come on the<f>[1]</f> entire world. And this did happen during the reign of<f>[2]</f> Claudius.RÕGþ<pb/>Now at this time some prophets came down from Jerusalem to Antioch.dÕFƒAþand when he found him, he brought him back to Antioch. For an entire year they met <n>[with others]</n> in the church and instructed large numbers; and it was in Antioch that the disciples were first called Christians.9ÕEmþAnd Barnabas left for Tarsus to search for Saul;‚=ÕD„sþFor Barnabas was a good man <n>[privately and publiclyâ€”his godly character benefited both himself and others]</n> and <i>he was</i> full of the Holy Spirit and full of faith <n>[in Jesus the Messiah, through whom believers have everlasting life]</n>. And a great number of people were brought to the Lord.OÕCƒþWhen he arrived and saw the grace of God <n>[that was bestowed on them]</n>, he rejoiced and <i>began</i> to encourage them all with an unwavering heart to stay true <i>and</i> devoted to the Lord.jÕBMþThe news of this reached the ears of the church in Jerusalem, and they sent Barnabas to Antioch.PÕAƒþAnd the hand (the power and presence) of the Lord was with them, and a great number who believed turned to the Lord <n>[for salvation, accepting and drawing near to Jesus as Messiah and Savior]</n>.FÕ@ƒþBut there were some of them, men of Cyprus and Cyrene, who came to Antioch and <i>began</i> speaking to the Greeks as well, proclaiming <n>[to them]</n> the good news about the Lord Jesus.‚JÕ?…
þSo then <n>[since they were unaware of these developments]</n> those who were scattered because of the persecution that occurred in connection with <n>[the stoning of]</n> Stephen traveled as far as Phoenicia and Cyprus and Antioch, without telling the message <n>[of salvation through Christ]</n> to anyone except Jews.pÕ>ƒYþWhen they heard this, they quieted down and glorified <i>and</i> praised God, saying, "Then God has also granted to the Gentiles repentance <i>that leads</i> to <i>eternal</i> life <n>[that is, real life after earthly death]</n>."kÕ=ƒOþSo, if God gave Gentiles the same gift <n>[equally]</n> as He gave us after we accepted <i>and</i> believed <i>and</i> trusted in the Lord Jesus Christ <n>[as Savior]</n>, who was I to interfere <i>or</i> stand in God's way?"Õ<‚'þThen I remembered the word of the Lord, how He used to say, <J>'John baptized with water, but you will be baptized with the Holy Spirit.'</J>Õ;{þWhen I began to speak, the Holy Spirit fell on them just as <i>He did</i> on us at the beginning <n>[at Pentecost]</n>.Õ:þhe will bring a message to you by which you will be saved <n>[and granted eternal life]</n>, you and all your household.'+Õ9‚Oþ
And Cornelius told us how he had seen the angel standing in his house, saying, 'Send <i>word</i> to Joppa and have Simon, who is also called Peter, brought here;Õ8‚%þThe Spirit told me to go with them without the slightest hesitation. So these six brothers also went with me and we went to the man's house.Õ7wþAnd right then the three men who had been sent to me from Caesarea arrived at the house where we were <i>staying</i>.SÕ6þ
