Just as you once were disobedient <i>and</i> failed to listen to God, but have now obtained mercy because of their disobedience,TÜOƒ!For the gifts and the calling of God are irrevocable <n>[for He does not withdraw what He has given, nor does He change His mind about those to whom He gives His grace or to whom He sends His call]</n>.‚!ÜN„;<pb/>From the standpoint of the gospel, the Jews <n>[at present]</n> are enemies <n>[of God]</n> for your sake <n>[which is for your benefit]</n>, but from the standpoint of God's choice <n>[of the Jews as His people]</n>, they are still loved by Him for the sake of the fathers.cÜM?<t>"<e>This is My covenant with them</e>, </t><t><e>When I take away their sins</e>."</t>‚@ÜL„y<t>and so <n>[at that time]</n> all Israel <n>[that is, all Jews who have a personal faith in Jesus as Messiah]</n> will be saved; just as it is written <n>[in Scripture]</n>, </t><br/><t>"<e>The Deliverer</e> (Messiah) <e>will come from Zion</e>, </t><t><e>He will remove ungodliness from Jacob</e>."</t><br/>‚.ÜK„U<pb/>I do not want you, believers, to be unaware of this mystery <n>[God's previously hidden plan]</n>â€”so that you will not be wise in your own opinionâ€”that a partial hardening has <n>[temporarily]</n> happened to Israel <n>[to last]</n> until the full number of the Gentiles has come in;‚ÜJ„3For if you were cut off from what is by nature a wild olive tree, and against nature were grafted into a cultivated olive tree, how much easier will it be to graft these who are the natural <i>branches</i> back into <n>[the original parent stock of]</n> their own olive tree?#ÜI‚?And even they <n>[the unbelieving Jews]</n>, if they do not continue in their unbelief, will be grafted in; for God has the power to graft them in again.‚ÜH„-Then appreciate the gracious kindness and the severity of God: to those who fell <n>[into spiritual ruin]</n>, severity, but to you, God's <i>gracious</i> kindnessâ€”if you continue in His kindness <n>[by faith and obedience to Him]</n>; otherwise you too will be cut off.sÜG_for if God did not spare the natural branches <n>[because of unbelief]</n>, He will not spare you either.~ÜFƒuThat is true. They were broken off because of their unbelief, but you stand by your faith <n>[as believers understanding the truth of Christ's deity]</n>. Do not be conceited, but <n>[rather stand in great awe of God and]</n> fear <n>[Him]</n>;VÜE%You will say then, "Branches were broken off so that I might be grafted in."oÜDƒWdo not boast over the <n>[broken]</n> branches <i>and</i> exalt yourself at their expense. If you do boast <i>and</i> feel superior, <i>remember that</i> it is not you who supports the root, but the root that <i>supports</i> you.DÜCƒ<pb/>But if some of the branches were broken off, and you <n>[Gentiles]</n>, being like a wild olive shoot, were grafted in among them to share with them the rich root of the olive tree,LÜBƒIf the first portion <n>[of dough offered as the first fruits]</n> is holy, so is the <i>whole</i> batch; and if the root (Abraham, the patriarchs) is holy, so are the branches (the Israelites).fÜAƒEFor if their <n>[present]</n> rejection <n>[of salvation]</n> is for the reconciliation of the world <n>[to God]</n>, what will their acceptance <n>[of salvation]</n> be but <n>[nothing less than]</n> life from the dead?(Ü@‚Iin the hope of somehow making my fellow countrymen jealous <n>[by stirring them up so that they will seek the truth]</n> and <i>perhaps</i> save some of them.Ü?‚	
But <i>now</i> I am speaking to you who are Gentiles. Inasmuch then as I am an apostle to the Gentiles, I magnify my ministry,GÜ>ƒNow if Israel's transgression means riches for the world <n>[at large]</n> and their failure means riches for the Gentiles, how much more will their fulfillment <i>and</i> reinstatement be!‚Ü=„5<pb/>So I say, have they stumbled so as to fall <n>[to spiritual ruin]</n>? Certainly not! But by their transgression <n>[their rejection of the Messiah]</n> salvation <i>has come</i> to the Gentiles, to make Israel jealous <n>[when they realize what they have forfeited]</n>.!Ü<‚;
<t>"<e>Let their eyes be darkened so that they do not see</e>, </t><t><e>And make their backs bend</e> <n>[under their burden]</n> <e>forever</e>."</t>7Ü;‚g	<pb/><t>And David says, </t><br/><t>"<e>Let their table</e> (abundance) <e>become a snare and a trap</e>, </t><t><e>A stumbling block and a retribution to them</e>.</t><br/>‚Ü:ƒ{<t>just as it is written <n>[in Scripture]</n>, </t><br/><t>"<e>God gave them a spirit of stupor</e>, </t><t><e>Eyes that do not see and ears that do not hear</e>, </t><t><n>[a spiritual apathy that has continued]</n> <e>to this very day</e>."</t>zÜ9ƒm<pb/>What then? Israel failed to obtain what it was seeking <n>[that is, God's favor by obedience to the Law]</n>, but the elect <n>[those chosen few]</n> obtained it, while the rest of them became hardened <i>and</i> callously indifferent;AÜ8‚{But if it is by grace <n>[God's unmerited favor]</n>, it is no longer on the basis of works, otherwise grace is no longer grace <n>[it would not be a gift but a reward for works]</n>.Ü7‚)So too then, at the present time there has come to be a remnant <n>[a small believing minority]</n> according to <i>God's</i> gracious choice.Ü6‚But what is God's response to him? "<e>I have kept</e> for Myself <e>seven thousand men who have not bowed the knee to Baal</e>.",Ü5‚Q"Lord, <e>they have killed Your prophets, they have torn down Your altars, and I alone am left</e> <n>[of the prophets]</n>, <e>and they are seeking my life</e>."(Ü4‚IGod has not rejected His <n>[chosen]</n> people whom He foreknew. Or do you not know what the Scripture says of Elijah, how he pleads with God against Israel?'Ü3	‚I<pb/>I say then, has God rejected <i>and</i> disowned His people? Certainly not! For I too am an Israelite, a descendant of Abraham, of the tribe of Benjamin.Ü2‚5
<pb/>But of Israel he says, "<e>All day long I have stretched out My hands</e> <n>[in compassion]</n> <e>to a disobedient and obstinate people</e>."\Ü1ƒ1
