For the Scripture says, "<e>Whoever believes in Him</e> <n>[whoever adheres to, trusts in, and relies on Him]</n> <e>will not be disappointed</e> <n>[in his expectations]</n>."‚]Ü'…3

For with the heart a person believes <n>[in Christ as Savior]</n> resulting in his justification <n>[that is, being made righteousâ€”being freed of the guilt of sin and made acceptable to God]</n>; and with the mouth he acknowledges <i>and</i> confesses <n>[his faith openly]</n>, resulting in <i>and</i> confirming <n>[his]</n> salvation.iÜ&ƒK
