Therefore let the one who thinks he stands firm <n>[immune to temptation, being overconfident and self-righteous]</n>, take care that he does not fall <n>[into sin and condemnation]</n>.Oß#ƒ
Now these things happened to them as an example <i>and</i> warning <n>[to us]</n>; they were written for our instruction <n>[to admonish and equip us]</n>, upon whom the ends of the ages have come.ß"‚

And do not murmur <n>[in unwarranted discontent]</n>, as some of them didâ€”and were destroyed by the<f>[5]</f> destroyer./ß!‚W
	We must not tempt the Lord <n>[that is, test His patience, question His purpose or exploit His goodness]</n>, as some of them didâ€”and they were killed by serpents..ß ‚U
We must not indulge in <n>[nor tolerate]</n> sexual immorality, as some of them did, and twenty-three thousand <n>[suddenly]</n> fell <n>[dead]</n> in a single day!‚)ß„K
Do not be worshipers of handmade gods, as some of them were; just as it is written <n>[in Scripture]</n>, "<e>The people sat down to eat and drink</e> <n>[after sacrificing to the<f>[4]</f> golden calf at Horeb]</n>, <e>and stood up to play</e> <n>[indulging in immoral activities]</n>."ß‚)
<pb/>Now these things <n>[the warnings and admonitions]</n> took place as examples for us, so that we would not crave evil things as they did.\ßƒ1
Nevertheless, God was not well-pleased with<f>[3]</f> most of them, for they were scattered along the ground in the wilderness <n>[because their lack of self-control led to disobedience which led to death]</n>.'ß‚G
and all <n>[of them]</n> drank the same<f>[2]</f> spiritual drink, for they were drinking from a spiritual rock which followed them; and the rock was Christ.Iß
