}	¥Ç×D•·Ñf‡¥                                                                                                                                                                                                              é%‚lalways learning <i>and</i> listening to anybody who will teach them, but never able to come to the knowledge of the truth.]é$ƒ3lFor among them are those who worm their way into homes and captivate <i>morally</i> weak <i>and</i> spiritually-dwarfed women weighed down by <n>[the burden of their]</n> sins, easily swayed by various impulses,Zé#ƒ-lholding to a form of <n>[outward]</n> godliness (religion), although they have denied its power <n>[for their conduct nullifies their claim of faith]</n>. Avoid such people <i>and</i> keep far away from them.gé"Gltraitors, reckless, conceited, lovers of <n>[sensual]</n> pleasure rather than lovers of God,aé!ƒ;l<n>[and they will be]</n> unloving <n>[devoid of natural human affection, calloused and inhumane]</n>, irreconcilable, malicious gossips, devoid of self-control <n>[intemperate, immoral]</n>, brutal, haters of good,Yé ƒ+lFor people will be lovers of self <n>[narcissistic, self-focused]</n>, lovers of money <n>[impelled by greed]</n>, boastful, arrogant, revilers, disobedient to parents, ungrateful, unholy <i>and</i> profane,*é	‚Ol<pb/>But understand this, that in the last days dangerous times <n>[of great stress and trouble]</n> will come <n>[difficult days that will be hard to bear]</n>.é‚land that they may come to their senses and <i>escape</i> from the trap of the devil, having been held captive by him to do his will.kéƒOlHe must correct those who are in opposition with courtesy <i>and</i> gentleness in the hope that God may grant that they will repent and be led to the knowledge of the truth <n>[accurately understanding and welcoming it]</n>,Yéƒ+lThe servant of the Lord must not participate in quarrels, but must be kind to everyone <n>[even-tempered, preserving peace, and he must be]</n>, skilled in teaching, patient <i>and</i> tolerant when wronged.SéƒlBut have nothing to do with foolish and ignorant speculations <n>[useless disputes over unedifying, stupid controversies]</n>, since you know that they produce strife <i>and</i> give birth to quarrels.é‚3lRun away from youthful lustsâ€”pursue righteousness, faith, love, and peace with those <n>[believers]</n> who call on the Lord out of a pure heart.‚é„lTherefore, if anyone cleanses himself from these <i>things</i> <n>[which are dishonorableâ€”disobedient, sinful]</n>, he will be a vessel for honor, sanctified <n>[set apart for a special purpose and]</n>, useful to the Master, prepared for every good work.‚	é„l<pb/>Now in a large house there are not only<f>[2]</f> vessels <i>and</i> objects of gold and silver, but also vessels <i>and</i> objects of wood and of earthenware, and some are for honorable (noble, good) use and some for dishonorable (ignoble, common).‚+é„OlNevertheless, the firm foundation of God <n>[which He has laid]</n> stands <n>[sure and unshaken despite attacks]</n>, bearing this seal: "The Lord knows those who are His," and, "Let everyone who names the name of the Lord stand apart from wickedness <i>and</i> withdraw from wrongdoing."é‚lwho have deviated from the truth. They claim that the resurrection has already taken place, and they undermine the faith of some.]é3land their teaching will spread like gangrene. So it is with Hymenaeus and Philetus,é‚lBut avoid all irreverent babble and godless chatter <n>[with its profane, empty words]</n>, for it will lead to further ungodliness,Véƒ%lStudy <i>and</i> do your best to present yourself to God approved, a workman <n>[tested by trial]</n> who has no reason to be ashamed, accurately handling <i>and</i> skillfully teaching the word of truth.yéƒklRemind <i>the people</i> of these facts, and solemnly charge <i>them</i> in the presence of God to avoid petty controversy over words, which does no good, and <n>[upsets and undermines and]</n> ruins <n>[the faith of]</n> those who listen.é‚l
<t>If we are faithless, He remains faithful <n>[true to His word and His righteous character]</n>, for He cannot deny Himself.</t><br/>méSl<t>If we endure, we will also reign with Him; </t><t>If we deny Him, He will also deny us;</t><br/>é‚l<t>This is a faithful <i>and</i> trustworthy saying: </t><br/><t>If we died with Him, we will also live with Him;</t><br/>uéƒcl
For this reason I <n>[am ready to]</n> patiently endure all things for the sake of those who are the elect (God's chosen ones), so that they too may obtain the salvation which is in Christ Jesus and with it the reward of eternal glory.(é
‚Il	for that <n>[gospel]</n> I am suffering even to <n>[the point of]</n> wearing chains like a criminal; but the word of God is not chained <i>or</i> imprisoned!jéƒMl<pb/>Remember Jesus Christ <n>[the ever-living Lord who has]</n> risen from the dead, <n>[as the prophesied King]</n> descended from David <n>[king of Israel]</n>, according to my gospel <n>[the good news that I preach]</n>,é‚+lThink over the things I am saying <n>[grasp their application]</n>, for the Lord will grant you insight <i>and</i> understanding in everything.é
wlThe hard-working farmer <n>[who labors to produce crops]</n> ought to be the first to receive his share of the crops..é	‚UlAnd if anyone competes as an athlete <n>[in competitive games]</n>, he is not crowned <n>[with the wreath of victory]</n> unless he competes according to the rules.Bé‚}lNo soldier in active service gets entangled in the <n>[ordinary business]</n> affairs of civilian life; <n>[he avoids them]</n> so that he may please the one who enlisted him to serve.é‚1lTake with me your share of hardship <n>[passing through the difficulties which you are called to endure]</n>, like a good soldier of Christ Jesus.‚.é„UlThe things <n>[the doctrine, the precepts, the admonitions, the sum of my ministry]</n> which you have heard me teach<f>[1]</f> in the presence of many witnesses, entrust <n>[as a treasure]</n> to reliable <i>and</i> faithful men who will also be capable <i>and</i> qualified to teach others.é	‚5l<pb/>So you, my son, be strong <n>[constantly strengthened]</n> <i>and</i> empowered in the grace that is <n>[to be found only]</n> in Christ Jesus.qé	ƒ]lthe Lord grant to him that he may find mercy from the Lord on<f>[3]</f> that <n>[great]</n> day. You know very well how many things he did for me <i>and</i> what a help he was at Ephesus <n>[you know better than I can tell you]</n>.^é	7lbut <n>[instead]</n> when he reached Rome, he eagerly searched for me and found meâ€”jé	ƒOlThe Lord grant mercy to the family of Onesiphorus, because he often refreshed me <i>and</i> showed me kindness <n>[comforting and reviving me like fresh air]</n> and he was not ashamed of my chains <n>[for Christ's sake]</n>;!é	‚=l<pb/>You are aware of the fact that all who are in <n>[the province of]</n> Asia turned away <i>and</i> deserted me, Phygelus and Hermogenes among them.‚&é 	„GlGuard <n>[with greatest care]</n> <i>and</i> keep unchanged, the treasure <n>[that precious truth]</n> which has been entrusted to you <n>[that is, the good news about salvation through personal faith in Christ Jesus]</n>, through <n>[the help of]</n> the Holy Spirit who dwells in us.è	‚)l
Keep <i>and</i> follow the pattern of sound teaching (doctrine) which you have heard from me, in the faith and love which are in Christ Jesus.ƒ
è~	†lThis is why I suffer as I do. Still, I am not ashamed; for I know Him <n>[and I am personally acquainted with Him]</n> whom I have believed <n>[with absolute trust and confidence in Him and in the truth of His deity]</n>, and I am persuaded <n>[beyond any doubt]</n> that He is able to guard that which I have entrusted to Him until<f>[2]</f> that day <n>[when I stand before Him]</n>.zè}	olfor which I was appointed a preacher and an apostle and a teacher <n>[of this good news regarding salvation]</n>.‚Kè|	…l
but now <n>[that extraordinary purpose and grace]</n> has been fully disclosed <i>and</i> realized by us through the appearing of our Savior Christ Jesus who <n>[through His incarnation and earthly ministry]</n> abolished death <n>[making it null and void]</n> and brought life and immortality to light through the gospel,ƒ?è{	†yl	for He delivered us <i>and</i> saved us and called us with a holy calling <n>[a calling that leads to a consecrated lifeâ€”a life set apartâ€”a life of purpose]</n>, not because of our works <n>[or because of any personal meritâ€”we could do nothing to earn this]</n>, but because of His own purpose and grace <n>[His amazing, undeserved favor]</n> which was granted to us in Christ Jesus before the world began <n>[eternal ages ago]</n>,‚èz	„%l<pb/>So do not be ashamed to testify about our Lord or about me His prisoner, but with me take your share of suffering for the gospel <n>[continue to preach regardless of the circumstances]</n>, in accordance with the power of God <n>[for His power is invincible]</n>,‚èy	„+lFor God did not give us a spirit of timidity <i>or</i> cowardice <i>or</i> fear, but <n>[He has given us a spirit]</n> of power and of love and of sound judgment <i>and</i> personal discipline <n>[abilities that result in a calm, well-balanced mind and self-control]</n>.pèx	ƒ[lThat is why I remind you to<f>[1]</f> fan into flame the gracious gift of God, <n>[that inner fireâ€”the special endowment]</n> which is in you through the laying on of my hands <n>[with those of the elders at your ordination]</n>.‚Cèw	…lI remember your sincere <i>and</i> unqualified faith <n>[the surrendering of your entire self to God in Christ with confident trust in His power, wisdom and goodness, a faith]</n> which first lived in <n>[the heart of]</n> your grandmother Lois and your mother Eunice, and I am confident that it is in you as well.Xèv	+land as I recall your tears, I long to see you so that I may be filled with joy.(èu	‚Kl<pb/>I thank God, whom I worship <i>and</i> serve with a clear conscience the way my forefathers did, as I constantly remember you in my prayers night and day,èt	‚5l<pb/>to Timothy, my beloved son: Grace, mercy, and peace <n>[inner calm and spiritual well-being]</n> from God the Father and Christ Jesus our Lord.Mès		ƒl<pb/>Paul, an apostle (special messenger, personally chosen representative) of Christ Jesus (the Messiah, the Anointed) by the will of God, according to the promise of life that is in Christ Jesus,èr‚bwhich some have professed and by doing so have erred (missed the mark) <i>and</i> strayed from the faith. </t><br/><t>Grace be with you.}èqƒsb<pb/>O Timothy, guard <i>and</i> keep safe the deposit <n>[of godly truth]</n> entrusted to you, turn away from worldly and godless chatter <n>[with its profane, empty words]</n>, and the contradictions of what is falsely called "knowledge"â€”'èp‚GbIn this way storing up for themselves the <i>enduring</i> riches of a good foundation for the future, so that they may take hold of that which is truly life.{èoob<i>Instruct them</i> to do good, to be rich in good works, to be generous, willing to share <n>[with others]</n>.}ènƒsb<pb/>As for the rich in this present world, instruct them not to be conceited <i>and</i> arrogant, nor to set their hope on the uncertainty of riches, but on God, who richly <i>and</i> ceaselessly provides us with everything for our enjoyment.Uèmƒ#bHe alone possesses immortality <n>[absolute exemption from death]</n> and lives in unapproachable light, whom no man has ever seen or can see. To Him be honor and eternal power <i>and</i> dominion! Amen.Eèlƒbwhich He will bring about in His own timeâ€”He who is the blessed and only Sovereign <n>[the absolute Ruler]</n>, the King of those who reign as kings and Lord of those who rule as lords,jèkMbto keep all His precepts without stain or reproach until the appearing of our Lord Jesus Christ,Xèjƒ)b
I <i>solemnly</i> charge you in the presence of God, who gives life to all things, and <n>[in the presence]</n> of Christ Jesus, who made the good confession <n>[in His testimony]</n> before Pontius Pilate,pèiƒYbFight the good fight of the faith <n>[in the conflict with evil]</n>; take hold of the eternal life to which you were called, and <n>[for which]</n> you made the good confession <n>[of faith]</n> in the presence of many witnesses.‚èh„b<pb/>But as for you,<f>[1]</f> O man of God, flee from these things; aim at <i>and</i> pursue righteousness <n>[true goodness, moral conformity to the character of God]</n>, godliness <n>[the fear of God]</n>, faith, love, steadfastness, and gentleness.‚èg„+b
For the love of money <n>[that is, the greedy desire for it and the willingness to gain it unethically]</n> is a root of all sorts of evil, and some by longing for it have wandered away from the faith and pierced themselves <n>[through and through]</n> with many sorrows.‚$èf„Ab	But those who <n>[are not financially ethical and]</n> crave to get rich <n>[with a compulsive, greedy longing for wealth]</n> fall into temptation and a trap and into many foolish and harmful desires that plunge people into ruin and destruction <n>[leading to personal misery]</n>.Jèe
bBut if we have food and clothing, with these we will be content.}èdsbFor we have brought nothing into the world, so <n>[it is clear that]</n> we cannot take anything out of it, either.IècƒbBut godliness <i>actually</i> is a source of great gain when accompanied by contentment <n>[that contentment which comes from a sense of inner confidence based on the sufficiency of God]</n>.Rèbƒband perpetual friction between men who are corrupted in mind and deprived of the truth, who think that godliness is a source of profit <n>[a lucrative, money-making businessâ€”withdraw from them]</n>.[èaƒ/bhe is conceited and woefully ignorant <n>[understanding nothing]</n>. He has a morbid interest in controversial questions and disputes about words, which produces envy, quarrels, verbal abuse, evil suspicions,nè`ƒUb<pb/>If anyone teaches a different doctrine and does not agree with the sound words of our Lord Jesus Christ, and with the doctrine <i>and</i> teaching which is in agreement with godliness (personal integrity, upright behavior),‚,è_„QbThose who have believing masters are not to be disrespectful toward them because they are brothers <n>[in Christ]</n>, but they should serve them even better, because those who benefit from their kindly service are believers and beloved. Teach and urge these <n>[duties and principles]</n>.`è^	ƒ;b<pb/>All who are under the yoke as bond-servants (slaves) are to regard their own masters as worthy of honor <i>and</i> respect so that the name of God and the teaching <n>[about Him]</n> will not be spoken against.wè]gbLikewise, good deeds are quite evident, and those which are otherwise cannot be hidden <n>[indefinitely]</n>.‚ è\ƒyb<pb/><f>[5]</f> The sins of some people are conspicuous, leading the way for them into judgment <n>[so that they are clearly not qualified for ministry]</n>; but the sins of others appear later <n>[for they are hidden and follow behind them]</n>.è[‚+b<pb/>No longer<f>[4]</f> continue drinking <n>[only]</n> water, but use a little wine for the sake of your stomach and your frequent illnesses.kèZƒObDo not hurry to lay hands on anyone <n>[ordaining and approving someone for ministry or an office in the church, or in reinstating expelled offenders]</n>, and thereby share in the sins of others; keep yourself free from sin.=èY‚sbI solemnly charge you in the presence of God and of Christ Jesus and of His chosen angels that you guard <i>and</i> keep these rules without bias, doing nothing out of favoritism.èX‚3bAs for those <n>[elders]</n> who continue in sin, reprimand them in the presence of all <n>[the congregation]</n>, so that the rest will be warned.èW‚bDo not accept an accusation against an elder unless it is based on <n>[the testimony of at least]</n> two or three witnesses.[èVƒ/bFor the Scripture says, "<e>You shall not muzzle the ox while it is treading out the grain</e> <n>[to keep it from eating]</n>," and, "The worker is worthy of his wages <n>[he deserves fair compensation]</n>."}èUƒsbThe elders who perform their leadership duties well are to be considered worthy of double honor (financial support), especially those who work hard at preaching and teaching <n>[the word of God concerning eternal salvation through Christ]</n>.‚8èT„ibIf any believing woman has <n>[dependent]</n> widows <n>[in her household]</n>,<f>[3]</f> she must assist them <n>[according to her ability]</n>; and the church must not be burdened <n>[with them]</n>, so that it may assist those who are truly widows <n>[those who are all alone and are dependent]</n>.`èS9bSome <n>[widows]</n> have already turned away <n>[from the faith]</n> to follow Satan.èR‚7bSo I want younger <i>widows</i> to get married, have children, manage their households, and not give opponents of the faith any occasion for slander.‚èQƒ}b
Now at the same time, they also learn to be idle as they go from house to house; and not only idle, but also gossips and<f>[2]</f> busybodies <n>[meddlers in things that do not concern them]</n>, talking about things they should not <i>mention</i>.^èP5band so they incur condemnation for having set aside their<f>[1]</f> previous pledge.èO‚3bBut refuse <n>[to enroll the]</n> younger widows, for when they feel their natural desires in disregard of Christ, they wish to marry <i>again</i>,‚#èN„?b
and has a reputation for good deeds; <n>[she is eligible]</n> if she has brought up children, if she has shown hospitality to strangers, if she has washed the feet of the saints (God's people), if she has assisted the distressed, and has devoted herself to doing good in every way.(èM‚Ib	<pb/>A widow is to be put on the list <n>[to receive regular assistance]</n> only if she is over sixty years of age, <n>[having been]</n> the wife of one man,rèLƒ]bIf anyone fails to provide for his own, and especially for those of his own family, he has denied the faith <n>[by disregarding its precepts]</n> and is worse than an unbeliever <n>[who fulfills his obligation in these matters]</n>.èK‚bKeep instructing <n>[the people to do]</n> these things as well, so that they may be blameless <i>and</i> beyond reproach.èJ‚bWhereas she who lives for pleasure <i>and</i> self-indulgence is <i>spiritually</i> dead even while she <i>still</i> lives.>èI‚ubNow a woman who is really a widow and has been left <n>[entirely]</n> alone <n>[without adequate income]</n> trusts in God and continues in supplications and prayers night and day.‚ièH…KbBut if a widow has children or grandchildren <n>[who are adults]</n>, see to it that these first learn to show great respect to their own family <n>[as their religious duty and natural obligation]</n>, and to compensate their parents <i>or</i> grandparents <n>[for their upbringing]</n>; for this is acceptable <i>and</i> pleasing in the sight of God.lèGQb<pb/>Honor <i>and</i> help those widows who are truly widowed <n>[alone, and without support]</n>.
èF‚bto older women as mothers, to younger women as sisters, in all purity <n>[being careful to maintain appropriate relationships]</n>.èE	‚b<pb/>Do not sharply reprimand an older man, but appeal to him as <n>[you would to]</n> a father, to younger men as brothers,}èDƒsbPay close attention to yourself <n>[concentrate on your personal development]</n> and to your teaching; persevere in these things <n>[hold to them]</n>, for as you do this you will ensure salvation both for yourself and for those who hear you.)èC‚KbPractice <i>and</i> work hard on these things; be absorbed in them <n>[completely occupied in your ministry]</n>, so that your progress will be evident to all.‚èB„bDo not neglect the spiritual gift within you, <n>[that special endowment]</n> which was intentionally bestowed on you <n>[by the Holy Spirit]</n> through prophetic utterance when the<f>[3]</f> elders laid their hands on you <n>[at your ordination]</n>.èA‚)b
Until I come, devote yourself to public reading <n>[of Scripture]</n>, to preaching and to teaching <n>[the sound doctrine of God's word]</n>.Jè@ƒ
bLet no one look down on <n>[you because of]</n> your youth, but be an example <i>and</i> set a pattern for the believers in speech, in conduct, in love, in faith, and in <n>[moral]</n> purity.8è?kb<pb/>Keep commanding and teaching these things.‚8è>„ib
It is for this that we labor and strive <n>[often called to account]</n>, because we have fixed our <n>[confident]</n> hope on the living God, who is the<f>[2]</f> Savior of all people, especially of those who believe <n>[in Him, recognize Him as the Son of God, and accept Him as Savior and Lord]</n>.iè=Kb	This is a faithful <i>and</i> trustworthy saying worthy of full acceptance <i>and</i> approval.Mè<ƒbFor physical training is of some value, but godliness (spiritual training) is of value in everything <i>and</i> in every way, since it holds promise for the present life and for the life to come.@è;‚ybBut have nothing to do with irreverent folklore <i>and</i> silly myths. On the other hand, discipline yourself for the purpose of godliness <n>[keeping yourself spiritually fit]</n>.‚è:„-bIf you point out these instructions to the<f>[1]</f> brothers and sisters, you will be a good servant of Christ Jesus, <i>constantly</i> nourished <n>[through study]</n> on the words of the faith and of the good <n>[Christian]</n> doctrine which you have closely followed.kè9Obfor it is sanctified <n>[set apart, dedicated to God]</n> by means of the word of God and prayer.qè8[bFor everything God has created is good, and nothing is to be rejected if it is received with gratitude;Vè7ƒ%bwho forbid marriage and <i>advocate</i> abstaining from <n>[certain kinds of]</n> foods which God has created to be gratefully shared by those who believe and have <n>[a clear]</n> knowledge of the truth. è6‚9b<n>[misled]</n> by the hypocrisy of liars whose consciences are seared as with a branding iron <n>[leaving them incapable of ethical functioning]</n>,jè5	ƒOb<pb/>But the <n>[Holy]</n> Spirit explicitly <i>and</i> unmistakably declares that in later times some will turn away from the faith, paying attention instead to deceitful <i>and</i> seductive spirits and doctrines of demons,‚Eè4…bAnd great, we confess, is the mystery <n>[the hidden truth]</n> of godliness: </t><br/><t>He (Jesus Christ) who was revealed in human flesh, </t><t>Was justified <i>and</i> vindicated in the Spirit, </t><t>Seen by angels, </t><t>Preached among the nations, </t><t>Believed on in the world, </t><t>Taken up in glory.Dè3ƒbin case I am delayed, so that you will know how people ought to conduct themselves in the household of God, which is the church of the living God, the pillar and foundation of the truth.\è21b<pb/>I hope to come to you before long, but I am writing these instructions to you_è1ƒ7b
For those who have served well as deacons gain a high standing <n>[having a good reputation among the congregation]</n>, and great confidence in the faith which is <n>[founded on and centered]</n> in Christ Jesus. è0ybDeacons must be husbands of <i>only</i> one wife, and good managers of <i>their</i> children and their own households.è/‚+b<f>[4]</f> Women must likewise be worthy of respect, not malicious gossips, but self-controlled, <n>[thoroughly]</n> trustworthy in all things.)è.‚Kb
These men must first be tested; then if they are found to be blameless <i>and</i> beyond reproach <n>[in their Christian lives]</n>, let them serve as deacons.cè-ƒ?b	but upholding <i>and</i> fully understanding the mystery <n>[that is, the true doctrine]</n> of the <n>[Christian]</n> faith with a clear conscience <n>[resulting from behavior consistent with spiritual maturity]</n>.uè,ƒcb<pb/><f>[3]</f> Deacons likewise <i>must be</i> men worthy of respect <n>[honorable, financially ethical, of good character]</n>, not double-tongued <n>[speakers of half-truths]</n>, not addicted to wine, not greedy for dishonest gain,1è+‚[bAnd he must have a good reputation <i>and</i> be well thought of by those outside <i>the church</i>, so that he will not be discredited and fall into the devil's trap.‚	è*„band <i>He must</i> not be a new convert, so that he will not <n>[behave stupidly and]</n> become conceited <n>[by appointment to this high office]</n> and fall into the <n>[same]</n> condemnation incurred by the devil <n>[for his arrogance and pride]</n>.tè)ab(for if a man does not know how to manage his own household, how will he take care of the church of God?).è(‚3b<i>He must</i> manage his own household well, keeping his children under control with all dignity <n>[keeping them respectful and well-behaved]</n>rè'ƒ]bnot addicted to wine, not<f>[2]</f> a bully <i>nor</i> quick-tempered <i>and</i> hot-headed, but gentle <i>and</i> considerate, free from the love of money <n>[not greedy for wealth and its inherent powerâ€”financially ethical]</n>.#è&‚?bNow an overseer must be blameless <i>and</i> beyond reproach, the husband of one wife, self-controlled, sensible, respectable, hospitable, able to teach,:è%	‚ob<pb/>This is a faithful <i>and</i> trustworthy saying: if any man <n>[eagerly]</n> seeks the office of<f>[1]</f> overseer (bishop, superintendent), he desires an excellent task.bè$ƒ=bBut <i>women</i> will be<f>[5]</f> preserved (saved) through <n>[the pain and dangers of]</n> the bearing of children<f>[6]</f> if they continue in faith and love and holiness with self-control <i>and</i> discretion.mè#Sband it was not Adam who was deceived, but the woman who was led astray and<f>[4]</f> fell into sin.Mè"b
For Adam was formed first <n>[by God from the earth]</n>, then Eve;è!‚bI do not allow a woman to<f>[3]</f> teach or exercise authority over a man, but to remain quiet <n>[in the congregation]</n>.Kè bA woman must quietly receive instruction with all submissiveness.~èub
but instead <i>adorned</i> by good deeds <n>[helping others]</n>, as is proper for women who profess to worship God.Tèƒ!b	Likewise, <i>I want</i> women to adorn themselves modestly <i>and</i> appropriately and discreetly in proper clothing, not with <n>[elaborately]</n> braided hair and gold or pearls or expensive clothes,/è‚Wb<pb/>Therefore I want the men in every place to pray, lifting up holy hands, without anger and disputing <i>or</i> quarreling <i>or</i> doubt <n>[in their mind]</n>.9è‚kbAnd for this matter I was appointed a preacher and an apostleâ€”I am telling the truth, I am not lying <n>[when I say this]</n>â€”a teacher of the Gentiles in faith and truth.è‚%bwho gave Himself as a ransom <n>[a substitutionary sacrifice to atone]</n> for all, the testimony given at the right <i>and</i> proper time.{èobFor there is <n>[only]</n> one God, and <n>[only]</n> one Mediator between God and mankind, the Man Christ Jesus,è‚bwho<f>[2]</f> wishes all people to be saved and to come to the knowledge <i>and</i> recognition of the <n>[divine]</n> truth.rè]bThis <n>[kind of praying]</n> is good and acceptable <i>and</i> pleasing in the sight of God our Savior,"è‚=bfor<f>[1]</f> kings and all who are in <n>[positions of]</n> high authority, so that we may live a peaceful and quiet life in all godliness and dignity..è	‚Wb<pb/>First of all, then, I urge that petitions (specific requests), prayers, intercessions (prayers for others) and thanksgivings be offered on behalf of all people,"è	‚?bAmong these are Hymenaeus and Alexander, whom I have<f>[4]</f> handed over to Satan, so that they will be disciplined <i>and</i> taught not to blaspheme.}è	ƒubkeeping your faith <n>[leaning completely on God with absolute trust and confidence in His guidance]</n> and having a good conscience; for some <n>[people]</n> have rejected <n>[their moral compass]</n> and have made a shipwreck of their faith.tè	ƒcb<pb/>This command I entrust to you, Timothy, my son, in accordance with the prophecies previously made concerning you, so that <n>[inspired and aided]</n> by them you may fight the good fight <n>[in contending with false teachers]</n>,è	‚bNow to the King of the ages <n>[eternal]</n>, immortal, invisible, the only God, be honor and glory forever and ever. Amen.qè	ƒ]bYet for this reason I found mercy, so that in me as the foremost <n>[of sinners]</n>, Jesus Christ might demonstrate His perfect patience as an example <i>or</i> pattern for those who<f>[3]</f> would believe in Him for eternal life.Hè	ƒb<f>[2]</f> This is a faithful <i>and</i> trustworthy statement, deserving full acceptance <i>and</i> approval, that Christ Jesus came into the world to save sinners, among whom I am foremost.Mè	ƒbThe grace of our Lord <n>[His amazing, unmerited favor and blessing]</n> flowed out in superabundance <n>[for me, together]</n> with the faith and love which are <n>[realized]</n> in Christ Jesus.‚è	„b
even though I was formerly a blasphemer <n>[of our Lord]</n> and a persecutor <n>[of His church]</n> and a shameful <i>and</i> outrageous <i>and</i> violent aggressor <n>[toward believers]</n>. Yet I was shown mercy because I acted out of ignorance in unbelief.lè
