7	”	`»Õ§›ý·Â                                                                                                                          pêEƒYŠTherefore, since the promise remains for some to enter His rest, and those who formerly had the good news preached to them failed to <n>[grasp it and did not]</n> enter because of <n>[their unbelief evidenced by]</n> disobedience,BêDŠand again in this, "<e>They shall not enter My rest</e>."êC‚+Š<pb/>For somewhere <n>[in Scripture]</n> He has said this about the seventh day: "<e>And God rested on the seventh day from all His works</e>";„êBˆŠ<t>For we who believe <n>[that is, we who personally trust and confidently rely on God]</n> enter that rest <n>[so we have His inner peace now because we are confident in our salvation, and assured of His power]</n>, just as He has said, </t><br/><t>"<e>As I swore</e> <n>[an oath]</n> <e>in My wrath</e>, </t><t><e>They shall not enter My rest</e>," </t><t><n>[this He said]</n> although His works were<f>[1]</f> completed from the foundation of the world <n>[waiting for all who would believe]</n>.</t><br/>‚)êA„KŠFor indeed we have had the good news <n>[of salvation]</n> preached to us, just as the Israelites also <n>[when the good news of the promised land came to them]</n>; but the message they heard did not benefit them, because it was not united with faith <n>[in God]</n> by those who heard.aê@	ƒ=Š<pb/>Therefore, while the promise of entering His rest still remains <i>and</i> is freely offered today, let us fear, in case any one of you may seem to come short of reaching it <i>or</i> think he has come too late. ê?‚9ŠSo we see that they were not able to enter <n>[into His restâ€”the promised land]</n> because of unbelief <i>and</i> an unwillingness to trust in God.#ê>‚?ŠAnd to whom did He swear <n>[an oath]</n> that they would not enter His rest, but to those who disobeyed <n>[those who would not listen to His word]</n>?ê=‚ŠAnd with whom was He angry for forty years? Was it not with those who sinned, whose dead bodies were scattered in the desert?ê<‚5Š<pb/>For who were they who heard and yet provoked <i>Him</i> <n>[with rebellious acts]</n>? Was it not all those who came out of Egypt led by Moses?zê;ƒmŠ<t>while it is said, </t><br/><t>"<e>Today</e> <n>[while there is still opportunity]</n> <e>if you hear His voice</e>, </t><t><e>Do not harden your heart, as when they provoked Me</e> <n>[in the rebellion in the desert at Meribah]</n>."</t>[ê:ƒ/ŠFor we <n>[believers]</n> have become partakers of Christ <n>[sharing in all that the Messiah has for us]</n>, if only we hold firm our newborn confidence <n>[which originally led us to Him]</n> until the end,‚ ê9„9Š
But continually encourage one another every day, as long as it is called "Today" <n>[and there is an opportunity]</n>, so that none of you will be hardened <n>[into settled rebellion]</n> by the deceitfulness of sin <n>[its cleverness, delusive glamour, and sophistication]</n>.Wê8ƒ'ŠTake care, brothers and sisters, that there not be in any one of you a wicked, unbelieving<f>[4]</f> heart <n>[which refuses to trust and rely on the Lord, a heart]</n> that turns away from the living God.ê7‚%Š<t><e>So I swore</e> <n>[an oath]</n> <e>in My wrath</e>, </t><t>'<e>They shall not enter My rest</e> <n>[the promised land]</n>.'"</t><br/>‚ê6„Š
<t>"<e>Therefore I was angered with this generation</e>, </t><t><e>And I said, 'They always go astray in their heart</e>, </t><t><e>And they did not know My ways</e> <n>[nor become progressively better and more intimately acquainted with them]</n>';</t><br/>Gê5ƒŠ	<t><e>Where your fathers tried Me by testing</e> <n>[My forbearance and tolerance]</n>, </t><t><e>And saw My works for forty years</e> </t><t><n>[And found I stood their test]</n>.</t><br/>Kê4ƒŠ<t><e>Do not harden your hearts as</e> <n>[your fathers did]</n> <e>in the rebellion</e> <n>[of Israel at<f>[3]</f> Meribah]</n>, </t><t><e>On the day of testing in the wilderness</e>,</t><br/>tê3aŠ<pb/><t>Therefore, just as the Holy Spirit says, </t><br/><t>"<e>Today if you hear His voice</e>,</t><br/>4ê2‚aŠbut Christ is faithful as a Son over His <n>[Father's]</n> house. And we are His house if we hold fast our confidence and sense of triumph in our hope <n>[in Christ]</n>.‚ê1„ŠNow Moses was faithful in <n>[the administration of]</n> all God's house, <n>[but only]</n> as a <i>ministering</i> servant, <n>[his ministry serving]</n> as a testimony of the things which were to be spoken afterward <n>[the revelation to come in Christ]</n>;Tê0!ŠFor every house is built by someone, but the builder of all things is God.ê/‚7ŠYet Jesus has been considered worthy of much greater glory <i>and</i> honor than Moses, just as the builder of a house has more honor than the house.
