After a first and second warning reject a divisive man <n>[who promotes heresy and causes dissensionâ€”ban him from your fellowship and have nothing more to do with him]</n>,6ém‚ev	But avoid foolish <i>and</i> ill-informed <i>and</i> stupid controversies and genealogies and dissensions and quarrels about the Law, for they are unprofitable and useless.ƒél†5vThis is a faithful <i>and</i> trustworthy saying; and concerning these things I want you to speak with great confidence, so that those who have believed God <n>[that is, those who have trusted in, relied on, and accepted Christ Jesus as Savior,]</n> will be careful to participate in doing good <i>and</i> honorable things. These things are excellent <n>[in themselves]</n> and profitable for the people.‚'ék„Gvso that we would be justified <n>[made free of the guilt of sin]</n> by His <n>[compassionate, undeserved]</n> grace, and that we would be <n>[acknowledged as acceptable to Him and]</n> made heirs of eternal life <n>[actually experiencing it]</n> according to our hope (His guarantee).Léjvwhom He poured out richly upon us through Jesus Christ our Savior,séiƒ_vHe saved us, not because of any works of righteousness that we have done, but because of His own compassion <i>and</i> mercy, by the cleansing of the new birth (spiritual transformation, regeneration) and renewing by the Holy Spirit,éh‚7vBut when the goodness <i>and</i> kindness of God our Savior and <i>His</i> love for mankind appeared <n>[in human form as the Man, Jesus Christ]</n>,MégƒvFor we too once were foolish, disobedient, deceived, enslaved to various <i>sinful</i> desires and pleasures, spending <i>and</i> wasting our life in malice and envy, hateful, hating one another."éf‚=vto slander <i>or</i> abuse no one, to be kind <i>and</i> conciliatory and gentle, showing unqualified consideration <i>and</i> courtesy toward everyone.ée	yv<pb/>Remind people to be subject to rulers and authorities, to be obedient, to be ready <i>and</i> willing to do good,Hédƒ	v<pb/>Tell <i>them</i> these things. Encourage and rebuke with full authority. Let no one disregard <i>or</i> despise you <n>[conduct yourself and your teaching so as to command respect]</n>.‚&éc„Evwho <n>[willingly]</n> gave Himself <n>[to be crucified]</n> on our behalf to redeem us <i>and</i> purchase our freedom from all wickedness, and to purify for Himself a chosen <i>and</i> very special people to be His own possession, <i>who are</i> enthusiastic for doing what is good.&éb‚Ev
