, for the faith of God's chosen ones and <n>[to lead and encourage them to recognize and pursue]</n> the knowledge of the truth which leads to godliness,>éEwl<pb/>The Lord be with your spirit. Grace be with you.4éD‚alTry your best to come <n>[to me]</n> before winter. Eubulus wishes to be remembered to you, as do Pudens and Linus and Claudia and all the<f>[5]</f> brothers and sisters.MéClErastus stayed on at Corinth, but I left Trophimus sick at Miletus.[éB/l<pb/>Give my greetings to Prisca and Aquila, and to the household of Onesiphorus.éA‚3lThe Lord will rescue me from every evil assault, and He will bring me safely into His heavenly kingdom; to Him be the glory forever and ever. Amen.wé@ƒglBut the Lord stood by me and strengthened <i>and</i> empowered me, so that through me the <n>[gospel]</n> message might be fully proclaimed, and that all the Gentiles might hear it; and I was rescued from the<f>[4]</f> mouth of the lion.3é?‚_l<pb/>At my first trial no one supported me <n>[as an advocate]</n> <i>or</i> stood with me, but they all deserted me. May it not be counted against them <n>[by God]</n>.Vé>%lBe on guard against him yourself, because he vigorously opposed our message.é=‚#lAlexander the coppersmith did me great harm; <n>[but that is no concern of mine, for]</n> the Lord will repay him according to his actions.ré<]l
