%û‚ûQj;                                 ‚*ð„MÚ<J>But I have this <n>[charge]</n> against you, that you tolerate the woman Jezebel, who calls herself a prophetess <n>[claiming to be inspired]</n>, and she teaches and misleads My bond-servants so that they commit <n>[acts of sexual]</n> immorality and eat food sacrificed to idols.</J>.ð‚UÚ<pb/><J>'I know your deeds, your love and faith and service and patient endurance, and that your last deeds are more numerous <i>and</i> greater than the first.</J>‚/ð„WÚ<t><J>"And to the angel (divine messenger) of the church in<f>[15]</f> Thyatira write:</J> </t><br/><J>"These are the words of the Son of God, who has eyes <n>[that flash]</n> like a flame of fire <n>[in righteous judgment]</n>, and whose feet are like burnished <n>[white-hot]</n> bronze:</J>ƒ%ð†CÚ<J>He who has an ear, let him hear <i>and</i> heed what the Spirit says to the churches. To him who overcomes <n>[the world through believing that Jesus is the Son of God]</n>, to him I will give <n>[the privilege of eating]</n> <i>some</i> of the<f>[13]</f> hidden manna, and I will give him a<f>[14]</f> white stone with a new name engraved on the stone which no one knows except the one who receives it.'</J>‚ð„Ú<J>Therefore repent <n>[change your inner selfâ€”your old way of thinking, your sinful behaviorâ€”seek God's will]</n>; or else I am coming to you quickly, and I will make war <i>and</i> fight against them with the sword of My mouth <n>[in judgment]</n>.</J>rð]Ú<J>You also have some who in the same way are holding to the teaching of the<f>[12]</f> Nicolaitans.</J>‚tð
…aÚ<J>But I have a few things against you, because you have there some <n>[among you]</n> who are holding to the <n>[corrupt]</n> teaching of Balaam, who taught<f>[10]</f> Balak to put a stumbling block before the sons of Israel, <n>[enticing them]</n> to eat things that had been sacrificed to idols and to commit <n>[acts of sexual]</n><f>[11]</f> immorality.</J>‚%ð„CÚ
<pb/><J>'I know where you dwell, <n>[a place]</n> where Satan sits enthroned. Yet you are holding fast to My name, and you did not deny<f>[8]</f> My faith even in the days of<f>[9]</f> Antipas, My witness, My faithful one, who was killed (martyred) among you, where Satan dwells.</J>Yðƒ+Ú<t><J>"And to the angel (divine messenger) of the church in<f>[7]</f> Pergamum write:</J> </t><br/><J>"These are the words of Him who has <i>and</i> wields the sharp two-edged sword <n>[in judgment]</n>:</J>~ð
ƒuÚ<J>He who has an ear, let him hear <i>and</i> heed what the Spirit says to the churches. He who overcomes <n>[the world through believing that Jesus is the Son of God]</n> will not be hurt by the second death (<f>[6]</f> the lake of fire).'</J>‚_ð	…7Ú
<J>Fear nothing that you are about to suffer. Be aware that the devil is about to throw some of you into prison, that you may be tested <n>[in your faith]</n>, and for ten days you will have tribulation. Be faithful to the point of death <n>[if you must die for your faith]</n>, and I will give you the crown <n>[consisting]</n> of life.</J>‚7ð„gÚ	<pb/><J>'I know your suffering and your poverty (but you are rich), and how you are blasphemed <i>and</i> slandered by those who say they are Jews and are not, but are a synagogue of Satan <n>[they are Jews only by blood, and do not believe and truly honor the God whom they claim to worship]</n>.</J>rðƒ]Ú<t><J>"And to the angel (divine messenger) of the church in<f>[5]</f> Smyrna write:</J> </t><br/><J>"These are the words of the First and the Last <n>[absolute Deity, the Son of God]</n> who died and came to life <n>[again]</n>:</J>‚?ð„wÚ<J>He who has an ear, let him hear <i>and</i> heed what the Spirit says to the churches. To him who<f>[4]</f> overcomes <n>[the world through believing that Jesus is the Son of God]</n>, I will grant <n>[the privilege]</n> to eat <n>[the fruit]</n> from the tree of life, which is in the Paradise of God.'</J>MðƒÚ<J>Yet you have this <n>[to your credit]</n>, that you hate the works <i>and</i> corrupt teachings of the<f>[3]</f> Nicolaitans <n>[that mislead and delude the people]</n>, which I also hate.</J>‚oð…WÚ<J>So remember <i>the heights</i> from which you have fallen, and repent <n>[change your inner selfâ€”your old way of thinking, your sinful behaviorâ€”seek God's will]</n> and do the works you did at first <n>[when you first knew Me]</n>; otherwise, I will visit you and remove your lampstand (the church, its impact) from its placeâ€”unless you repent.</J>+ð‚OÚ<J>But I have <i>this</i> <n>[charge]</n> against you, that you have left your first love <n>[you have lost the depth of love that you first had for Me]</n>.</J>KðƒÚ<J>and <n>[I know that]</n> you <n>[who believe]</n> are enduring patiently and are bearing up for My name's sake, and that you have not grown weary <n>[of being faithful to the truth]</n>.</J>‚yð…kÚ<pb/><J>'I know<f>[2]</f> your deeds and your toil, and your patient endurance, and that you cannot tolerate those who are evil, and have tested <i>and</i> critically appraised those who call themselves apostles (special messengers, personally chosen representatives, of Christ), and <n>[in fact]</n> are not, and have found them to be liars <i>and</i> impostors;</J>‚[ð 	…1Ú<pb/><t><J>"To the angel (divine messenger) of the church in<f>[1]</f> Ephesus write:</J> </t><br/><J>"These are the words of the One who holds <n>[firmly]</n> the seven stars <n>[which are the angels or messengers of the seven churches]</n> in His right hand, the One who walks among the seven golden lampstands (the seven churches):</J>}ï	ƒuÚ<J>As for the mystery of the seven stars which you saw in My right hand, and the seven golden lampstands: the seven stars are the angels (<f>[22]</f> divine messengers) of the seven churches, and the seven lampstands are the seven churches.</J>Zï~	ƒ/Ú<J>So write the things<f>[19]</f> which you have seen <n>[in the vision]</n>, and the things<f>[20]</f> which are <n>[now happening]</n>, and the things<f>[21]</f> which will take place after these things.</J>pï}	ƒ[Ú<J>and the Ever-living One <n>[living in and beyond all time and space]</n>. I died, but see, I am alive forevermore, and I have the keys of <n>[absolute control and victory over]</n> death and of Hades (the realm of the dead).</J>Lï|	ƒÚ<pb/>When I saw Him, I fell at His feet as though dead. And He placed His right hand on me and said, <J>"Do not be afraid; I am the First and the Last <n>[absolute Deity, the Son of God]</n>,</J>‚ï{	„ÚIn His right hand He held seven stars, and from His mouth came a sharp two-edged sword <n>[of judgment]</n>; and His face <n>[reflecting His majesty and the<f>[18]</f> Shekinah glory]</n> was like the sun shining in <n>[all]</n> its power <n>[at midday]</n>.ïz	‚-ÚHis feet were like burnished <n>[white-hot]</n> bronze, refined in a furnace, and His voice was <n>[powerful]</n> like the sound of many waters.Mïy	ƒÚHis head and His hair were white like white wool, <n>[glistening white]</n> like snow; and His <n>[all-seeing]</n> eyes were <n>[flashing]</n> like a flame of fire <n>[piercing into my being]</n>.9ïx	‚mÚ
and in the midst of the lampstands <i>I saw</i> someone<f>[17]</f> like the Son of Man, dressed in a robe reaching to His feet, and with a golden sash wrapped around His chest.xïw	kÚ<pb/>Then I turned to see the voice that was speaking with me. And after turning I saw seven golden lampstands;pïv	ƒ[Úsaying, <J>"Write on a scroll what you see <n>[in this revelation]</n>, and send it to the<f>[16]</f> seven churchesâ€”to Ephesus and to Smyrna and to Pergamum and to Thyatira and to Sardis and to Philadelphia and to Laodicea."</J>‚ïu	„Ú
