ïn	„Ú<f>[2]</f> Blessed (happy, prosperous, to be admired) is he who reads and those who hear the words of the prophecy, and who keep the things which are written in it <n>[heeding them and taking them to heart]</n>; for the time <n>[of fulfillment]</n> is near.2ïm	‚_Úwho testified <i>and</i> gave supporting evidence to the word of God and to the testimony of Jesus Christ, <i>even</i> to everything that he saw <n>[in his visions]</n>.‚cïl		…CÚ<pb/><i>This is</i> the<f>[1]</f> revelation of Jesus Christ <n>[His unveiling of the divine mysteries]</n>, which God <n>[the Father]</n> gave to Him to show to His bond-servants (believers) the things which must soon take place <n>[in their entirety]</n>; and He sent and communicated it by His angel (divine messenger) to His bond-servant John,ïk	‚'Ðto the only God our Savior, through Jesus Christ our Lord, be glory, majesty, dominion, and power, before all time and now and forever. Amen.lïj	ƒSÐ<pb/>Now to Him who is able to keep you from stumbling <i>or</i> falling into sin, and to present you unblemished <n>[blameless and faultless]</n> in the presence of His glory with triumphant joy <i>and</i> unspeakable delight,6ïi	‚gÐsave others, snatching them out of the fire; and on some have mercy but with fear, loathing even the clothing spotted <i>and</i> polluted by their shameless immoral freedom.1ïh	_ÐAnd have mercy on some, who are doubting;2ïg	‚_Ðand keep yourselves in the love of God, waiting anxiously <i>and</i> looking forward to the mercy of our Lord Jesus Christ <n>[which will bring you]</n> to eternal life.Aïf	‚}ÐBut you, beloved, build yourselves up on <n>[the foundation of]</n> your most holy faith <n>[continually progress, rise like an edifice higher and higher]</n>, pray in the Holy Spirit,0ïe	‚[ÐThese are the ones who are <n>[agitators]</n> causing divisionsâ€”worldly-minded <n>[secular, unspiritual, carnal, merely sensualâ€”unsaved]</n>, devoid of the Spirit.xïd	kÐThey used to say to you, "In the last days there will be scoffers, following after their own ungodly passions."xïc	kÐBut as for you, beloved, remember the <n>[prophetic]</n> words spoken by the apostles of our Lord Jesus Christ.‚ïb	„ÐThese <i>people</i> are <n>[habitual]</n> murmurers, griping <i>and</i> complaining, following after their own desires <n>[controlled by passion]</n>; they speak arrogantly, <n>[pretending admiration and]</n> flattering people to <i>gain an</i> advantage.bïa	ƒ?Ðto execute judgment upon all, and to convict all the<f>[10]</f> ungodly of all the ungodly deeds they have done in an ungodly way, and of all the harsh <i>and</i> cruel things ungodly sinners have spoken against Him."@ï`	‚{Ð<pb/>It was about these people that<f>[8]</f> Enoch, in the seventh <i>generation</i> from Adam, prophesied, when he said, "Look, the Lord came with<f>[9]</f> myriads of His holy onesï_	‚'Ð
wild waves of the sea, flinging up their own shame like foam; wandering stars, for whom the gloom of deep darkness has been reserved forever.‚Sï^	…!ÐThese men are hidden reefs <n>[elements of great danger to others]</n> in your<f>[7]</f> love feasts when they feast together with you without fear, looking after <n>[only]</n> themselves; <n>[they are like]</n> clouds without water, swept along by the winds; autumn trees without fruit, doubly dead, uprooted <i>and</i> lifeless;Dï]	ƒÐWoe to them! For they have gone the <n>[defiant]</n> way of Cain, and for profit they have run headlong into the error of Balaam, and perished in the rebellion of <n>[mutinous]</n> Korah.Oï\	ƒÐ
But these men sneer at anything which they do not understand; and whatever they do know by <n>[mere]</n> instinct, like unreasoning <i>and</i> irrational beastsâ€”by these things they are destroyed.nï[	ƒWÐ	But even the archangel Michael, when he was disputing with the devil (Satan), and<f>[6]</f> arguing about the body of Moses, did not dare bring an abusive condemnation against him, but <n>[simply]</n> said, "The Lord rebuke you!"`ïZ	ƒ;Ð<pb/>Nevertheless in the same way, these dreamers <n>[who are dreaming that God will not punish them]</n> also defile the body, and reject <n>[legitimate]</n> authority, and revile <i>and</i> mock angelic majesties.‚-ïY	„UÐjust as Sodom and Gomorrah and the adjacent cities, since they in the same way as these <i>angels</i> indulged in gross immoral freedom <i>and</i> unnatural vice and sensual perversity. They are exhibited <n>[in plain sight]</n> as an example in undergoing the punishment of everlasting fire.uïX	ƒeÐAnd angels who did not keep their own designated place of power, but abandoned their proper dwelling place, <n>[these]</n> He has kept in eternal chains under <n>[the thick gloom of utter]</n> darkness for the judgment of the great day,‚ïW	„	Ð<pb/>Now I want to remind you, although you are fully informed once for all, that<f>[5]</f> the Lord, after saving a people out of the land of Egypt, subsequently destroyed those who did not believe <n>[who refused to trust and obey and rely on Him]</n>.ƒïV	†ÐFor certain people have crept in unnoticed <n>[just as if they were sneaking in by a side door]</n>. They are ungodly persons whose condemnation was predicted long ago, for they distort the grace of our God into decadence <i>and</i> immoral freedom <n>[viewing it as an opportunity to do whatever they want]</n>, and deny <i>and</i> disown our only Master and Lord, Jesus Christ.‚~ïU	…wÐ<pb/>Beloved, while I was making every effort to write you about our common salvation, I was compelled to write to you <n>[urgently]</n> appealing that you<f>[3]</f> fight strenuously for <n>[the defense of]</n> the faith which was once for all<f>[4]</f> handed down to the saints <n>[the faith that is the sum of Christian belief that was given verbally to believers]</n>.1ïT	‚]ÐMay mercy and peace and love be multiplied to you <n>[filling your heart with the spiritual well-being and serenity experienced by those who walk closely with God]</n>.‚ïS		„1Ð<pb/><t>Jude, a bond-servant of Jesus Christ, and<f>[1]</f> brother of<f>[2]</f> James, <n>[writes this letter]</n>, </t><br/>To those who are the called (God's chosen ones, the elect), dearly loved by God the Father, and kept <n>[secure and set apart]</n> for Jesus Christ:rïR	_Æ<pb/>Peace be to you. The friends <n>[here]</n> greet you. Greet the friends <n>[personally]</n> by name.NïQ	Æbut I hope to see you soon, and we will speak<f>[2]</f> face to face.ïP	‚+Æ
<pb/>I had many things <n>[to say when I began]</n> to write to you, but I prefer not to put it down with pen (reed) and<f>[1]</f> black (ink);~ïO	ƒwÆDemetrius has received a <i>good</i> testimony <i>and</i> commendation from everyoneâ€”and from the truth <n>[the standard of God's word]</n> itself; and we add our testimony <i>and</i> speak well of him, and you know that our testimony is true.‚aïN	…=Æ<pb/>Beloved, do not imitate what is evil, but <n>[imitate]</n> what is good. The one who practices good <n>[exhibiting godly character, moral courage and personal integrity]</n> is of God; the one who practices <n>[or permits or tolerates]</n> evil has not seen God <n>[he has no personal experience with Him and does not know Him at all]</n>.‚TïM	…#Æ
For this reason, if I come, I will call attention to what he is doing, unjustly accusing us with wicked words <i>and</i> unjustified charges. And not satisfied with this, he refuses to receive the <n>[missionary]</n> brothers himself, and also forbids those who want to <n>[welcome them]</n> and puts <i>them</i> out of the church.(ïL	‚KÆ	<pb/>I wrote something to the church; but Diotrephes, who loves to put himself first, does not accept what we say <i>and</i> refuses to recognize my authority.KïK	ƒÆSo we ought to support such people <n>[welcoming them as guests and providing for them]</n>, so that we may be fellow workers for the truth <n>[that is, for the gospel message of salvation]</n>./ïJ	‚YÆFor these <n>[traveling missionaries]</n> went out for the sake of the Name <n>[of Christ]</n>, accepting nothing <n>[in the way of assistance]</n> from the Gentiles.5ïI	‚eÆand they have testified before the church of your love <i>and</i> friendship. You will do well to <n>[assist them and]</n> send them on their way in a manner worthy of God.ïH	‚Æ<pb/>Beloved, you are acting faithfully in what you are providing for the brothers, and especially <i>when they are</i> strangers;ïG	‚ÆI have no greater joy than this, to hear that my <n>[spiritual]</n> children are living <n>[their lives]</n> in the truth.lïF	ƒSÆFor I was greatly pleased when <n>[some of the]</n> brothers came <n>[from time to time]</n> and testified to your <n>[faithfulness to the]</n> truth <n>[of the gospel message]</n>, <i>that is</i>, how you are walking in truth.>ïE	‚wÆ<pb/>Beloved, I pray that in every way you may succeed <i>and</i> prosper and be in good health <n>[physically]</n>, just as <n>[I know]</n> your soul prospers <n>[spiritually]</n>.ïD		‚Æ<pb/>The elder <n>[of the church addresses this letter]</n> to the beloved <i>and</i> esteemed Gaius, whom I love in truth.CïC	¼
<pb/>The children of your elect (chosen) sister greet you.]ïB	ƒ5¼I have many things to write to you, but I prefer not to do so with paper (papyrus) and black (ink); but I hope to come to you and speak with you<f>[4]</f> face to face, so that<f>[5]</f> your joy may be complete.ïA	‚¼for the one who gives him a greeting <n>[who encourages him or wishes him success, unwittingly]</n> participates in his evil deeds.mï@	ƒU¼
If anyone comes to you and does not bring this teaching <n>[but diminishes or adds to the doctrine of Christ]</n>, do not receive <i>or</i> welcome him into your house, and do not give him a greeting <i>or</i> any encouragement;‚!ï?	„=¼	Anyone who runs on ahead and does not remain in the doctrine of Christ <n>[that is, one who is not content with what He taught]</n>, does not have God; but the one who <i>continues</i> to remain in the teaching <n>[of Christ does have God]</n>, he has both the Father and the Son.Gï>	ƒ	¼Watch yourselves, so that you do not lose what we have accomplished together, but that you may receive a full <i>and</i> perfect reward <n>[when He grants rewards to faithful believers]</n>.‚Sï=	…!¼<pb/>For many deceivers <n>[heretics, posing as Christians]</n> have gone out into the world, those who do not acknowledge <i>and</i> confess the coming of Jesus Christ in the flesh (bodily form). This <n>[person, the kind who does this]</n> is the deceiver and the<f>[3]</f> antichrist <n>[that is, the antagonist of Christ]</n>.pï<	ƒ[¼And this is love: that we walk in accordance with His commandments <i>and</i> are guided continually by His precepts. This is the commandment, just as you have heard from the beginning, that you should <n>[always]</n> walk in love.wï;	ƒi¼Now I ask you, lady, not as if <i>I were</i> writing to you a new commandment, but <n>[simply reminding you of]</n> the one which we have had from the beginning, that we<f>[2]</f> love <i>and</i> unselfishly seek the best for one another.
ï:	‚¼<pb/>I was greatly delighted to find <i>some</i> of your children walking in truth, just as we have been commanded by the Father./ï9	‚Y¼Grace, mercy, and peace (inner calm, a sense of spiritual well-being) will be with us, from God the Father and from Jesus Christ, the Father's Son, in truth and love.Tï8	#¼because of the truth which lives in our hearts and will be with us forever:Zï7		ƒ1¼<pb/>The elder <n>[of the church addresses this letter]</n> to the elect (chosen)<f>[1]</f> lady and her children, whom I love in truthâ€”and not only I, but also all who know <i>and</i> understand the truthâ€”9ï6‚k²<pb/>Little children (believers, dear ones), guard yourselves from idolsâ€”<n>[false teachings, moral compromises, and anything that would take God's place in your heart]</n>.‚pï5…Y²And we <n>[have seen and]</n> know <n>[by personal experience]</n> that the Son of God has <n>[actually]</n> come <n>[to this world]</n>, and has given us understanding <i>and</i> insight so that we may <n>[progressively and personally]</n> know Him who is true; and we are in Him who is trueâ€”in His Son Jesus Christ. This is the true God and eternal life.*ï4‚M²We know <n>[for a fact]</n> that we are of God, and the whole world <n>[around us]</n> lies in the power of the evil one <n>[opposing God and His precepts]</n>.aï3ƒ;²<pb/>We know <n>[with confidence]</n> that anyone born of God does not <i>habitually</i> sin; but He (Jesus) who was born of God <n>[carefully]</n> keeps <i>and</i> protects him, and the evil one does not touch him.ï2²All wrongdoing is sin, and there is sin that does not <i>lead</i> to death <n>[one can repent of it and be forgiven]</n>.‚aï1…;²<pb/>If anyone sees his brother committing a sin that does not <i>lead</i> to death, he will pray <i>and</i> ask <n>[on the believer's behalf]</n> and <i>God</i> will for him give life to those whose sin is not <i>leading</i> to death. There is a sin <i>that leads</i> to death; I do not say that one should pray for this <n>[kind of sin]</n>.‚
