and the stars of the sky fell to the earth, like a fig tree shedding its late <n>[summer]</n> figs when shaken by a strong wind.OðWƒÚI looked when He (the Lamb) broke open the sixth seal, and there was a great earthquake; and the sun became black as<f>[8]</f> sackcloth <n>[made]</n> of hair, and the whole moon became like blood;‚ðV„ÚThen they were each given a white robe; and they were told to rest <i>and</i> wait quietly for a little while longer, until <i>the number of</i> their fellow servants and their brothers and sisters who were to be killed even as they had been, would be completed.DðUƒÚ
They cried in a loud voice, saying, "O Lord, holy and true, how long now before You will sit in judgment and avenge our blood on those <n>[unregenerate ones]</n> who dwell on the earth?"tðTƒaÚ	When He (the Lamb) broke open the fifth seal, I saw underneath the altar the souls of those who had been slaughtered because of the word of God, and because of the testimony which they had maintained <n>[out of loyalty to Christ]</n>.ƒ#ðS†?ÚSo I looked, and behold, an ashen (pale greenish gray) horse <n>[like a corpse, representing death and pestilence]</n>; and its rider's name was Death; and Hades (the realm of the dead) was following with him. They were given authority <i>and</i> power over a fourth part of the earth, to kill with the sword and with famine and with<f>[7]</f> plague (pestilence, disease) and by the wild beasts of the earth.zðRmÚWhen He (the Lamb) broke open the fourth seal, I heard the voice of the fourth living creature call out, "Come."uðQƒcÚAnd I heard <i>something</i> like a voice in the midst of the four living creatures saying, "A quart of wheat for a denarius (a day's wages), and three quarts of barley for a denarius; and do not<f>[6]</f> damage the oil and the wine."_ðPƒ7ÚWhen He (the Lamb) broke open the third seal, I heard the third living creature call out, "Come." I looked, and behold, a black horse <n>[of famine]</n>; and the rider had in his hand a pair of scales (a balance).|ðOƒqÚAnd another, a<f>[5]</f> fiery red horse <n>[of bloodshed]</n>, came out; and its rider was empowered to take peace from the earth, so that men would slaughter one another; and a great sword <n>[of war and violent death]</n> was given to him.hðNIÚWhen He (the Lamb) broke the second seal, I heard the second living creature call out, "Come."OðMƒÚI looked, and behold, a<f>[3]</f> white horse <n>[of victory]</n> whose rider carried a<f>[4]</f> bow; and a crown <n>[of victory]</n> was given to him, and he rode forth conquering and to conquer.jðL	ƒOÚ<pb/>Then I saw as the Lamb (Christ) broke one of the seven<f>[1]</f> seals <n>[of the scroll initiating the judgments]</n>, and I heard one of the four living creatures call out as with a voice of thunder, "<f>[2]</f> Come."ðK‚Ú<pb/>And the four living creatures kept saying, "Amen." And the elders fell down and worshiped <n>[Him who lives forever and ever]</n>.‚^ðJ…5Ú
<pb/><t>And I heard every created thing that is in heaven or on earth or under the earth <n>[in Hades, the realm of the dead]</n> or on the sea, and everything that is in them, saying <n>[together]</n>, </t><br/><t>"To Him who sits on the throne, and to the Lamb (Christ), be blessing and honor and glory and dominion forever and ever."</t>EðIƒÚ<t>saying in a loud voice, </t><br/><t>"Worthy <i>and</i> deserving is the Lamb that was sacrificed to receive power and riches and wisdom and might and honor and glory and blessing."</t>^ðHƒ5ÚThen I looked, and I heard the voice of many angels around the throne and <n>[the voice]</n> of the living creatures and the elders; and they numbered myriads of myriads, and thousands of thousands (innumerable),ðG‚Ú
<t>"You have made them to be a kingdom <n>[of royal subjects]</n> and priests to our God; and they will reign on the earth."</t><br/>‚AðF„{Ú	<t>And they sang a new song <n>[of glorious redemption]</n>, saying, </t><br/><t>"Worthy <i>and</i> deserving are You to take the scroll and to break its seals; for You were slain (sacrificed), and with Your blood You purchased <i>people</i> for God from every tribe and language and people and nation.</t><br/>{ðEƒoÚAnd when He had taken the scroll, the four living creatures and the twenty-four elders fell down before the Lamb (Christ), each one holding a harp and golden bowls full of fragrant incense, which are the prayers of the saints (God's people).eðDCÚAnd He came and<f>[4]</f> took the scroll from the right hand of Him who sat on the throne.‚{ðC…oÚ<pb/>And there<f>[2]</f> between the throne (with the four living creatures) and among the elders I saw a Lamb (Christ) standing, <n>[bearing scars and wounds]</n> as though it had been slain, with seven horns (complete power) and with seven eyes (complete knowledge), which are<f>[3]</f> the seven Spirits of God who have been sent <n>[on duty]</n> into all the earth.pðBƒYÚThen one of the <n>[twenty-four]</n> elders said to me, "Stop weeping! Look closely, the Lion of the tribe of Judah, the Root of David, has overcome <i>and</i> conquered! He can open the scroll and <n>[break]</n> its seven seals."pðAYÚAnd I <i>began</i> to weep greatly because no one was found worthy to open the scroll or look into it.ð@‚ÚAnd no one in heaven or on earth or under the earth <n>[in Hades, the realm of the dead]</n> was able to open the scroll or look into it..ð?‚UÚAnd I saw a strong angel announcing with a loud voice, "Who is worthy <n>[having the authority and virtue]</n> to open the scroll and to<f>[1]</f> break its seals?"$ð>	‚CÚ<pb/>I saw in the right hand of Him who was seated on the throne a scroll written on the inside and on the back, closed <i>and</i> sealed with seven seals.\ð=ƒ1Ú<pb/><t>"Worthy are You, our Lord and God, to receive the glory and the honor and the power; for You created all things, and because of Your will they exist, and were created <i>and</i> brought into being."</t>:ð<‚mÚ
the twenty-four elders fall down before Him who sits on the throne, and they worship Him who lives forever and ever; and they throw down their crowns before the throne, saying,ð;‚!Ú	<pb/>Whenever the living creatures give glory and honor and thanksgiving to Him who sits on the throne, to Him who lives forever and ever,ƒð:†!Ú<t>And the four living creatures, each one of them having six wings, are full of eyes all over and within <n>[underneath their wings]</n>; and day and night they never stop saying, </t><br/><t>"<e>Holy, holy, holy</e> <n>[is the]</n> <e>Lord God, the Almighty</e> <n>[the Omnipotent, the Ruler of all]</n>, <e>who was and who is and who is to come</e> <n>[the unchanging, eternal God]</n>."</t>@ð9‚yÚ<f>[6]</f> The first living creature was like a lion, the second creature like a calf (ox), the third creature had the face of a man, and the fourth creature was like a flying eagle.‚Jð8…
Úand in front of the throne <i>there was something</i> like a sea <i>or</i> large expanse of glass, like <n>[the clearest]</n> crystal. In the center and around the throne were four living<f>[5]</f> creatures who were full of eyes in front and behind <n>[seeing everything and knowing everything that is around them]</n>.Mð7ƒÚFrom the throne came flashes of lightning and <n>[rumbling]</n> sounds and peals of thunder. Seven lamps of fire were burning in front of the throne, which are<f>[4]</f> the seven Spirits of God;@ð6‚yÚTwenty-four <n>[other]</n> thrones surrounded the throne; and seated on these thrones were<f>[3]</f> twenty-four elders dressed in white clothing, with crowns of gold on their heads.‚ð5„ÚAnd He who sat there appeared like <n>[the crystalline sparkle of]</n><f>[2]</f> a jasper stone and <n>[the fiery redness of]</n> a sardius stone, and encircling the throne <i>there was</i> a rainbow that looked like <n>[the color of an]</n> emerald.ð4‚ÚAt once I was in <n>[special communication with]</n> the Spirit; and behold, a throne stood in heaven, with One seated on the throne.‚ð3	„1Ú<pb/>After this I looked, and behold,<f>[1]</f> a door standing open in heaven! And the first voice which I had heard, like <i>the sound</i> of a <n>[war]</n> trumpet speaking with me, said, <J>"Come up here, and I will show you what must take place after these things."</J>hð2IÚ<J>He who has an ear, let him hear <i>and</i> heed what the Spirit says to the churches.'"</J>nð1ƒUÚ<J>He who overcomes <n>[the world through believing that Jesus is the Son of God]</n>, I will grant to him <n>[the privilege]</n> to sit beside Me on My throne, as I also overcame and sat down beside My Father on His throne.</J>Mð0ƒÚ<J>Behold, I stand at the door <n>[of the church]</n> and <i>continually</i> knock. If anyone hears My voice and opens the door, I will come in and eat with him (restore him), and he with Me.</J>‚ð/„Ú<J>Those whom I <n>[dearly and tenderly]</n> love, I rebuke and discipline <n>[showing them their faults and instructing them]</n>; so be enthusiastic and repent <n>[change your inner selfâ€”your old way of thinking, your sinful behaviorâ€”seek God's will]</n>.</J>‚Uð.…#Ú<J>I counsel you to buy from Me gold that has been heated red hot <i>and</i> refined by fire so that you may become <i>truly</i> rich; and white clothes <n>[representing righteousness]</n> to clothe yourself so that the shame of your nakedness will not be seen; and <i>healing</i> salve to put on your eyes so that you may see.</J>sð-ƒ_Ú<J>Because you say, "I am rich, and have prospered <i>and</i> grown wealthy, and have need of nothing," and you do not know that you are wretched and miserable and poor and blind and naked <n>[without hope and in great need]</n>,</J>#ð,‚?Ú<J>So because you are lukewarm (spiritually useless), and neither hot nor cold, I will vomit you out of My mouth <n>[rejecting you with disgust]</n>.</J>4ð+‚aÚ<pb/><J>'I know your deeds, that you are<f>[7]</f> neither cold (invigorating, refreshing) nor hot (healing, therapeutic); I wish that you were<f>[8]</f> cold or hot.</J>‚ ð*ƒyÚ<t><J>"To the angel (divine messenger) of the church in<f>[5]</f> Laodicea write:</J> </t><br/><J>"These are the words of the Amen, the trusted <i>and</i> faithful and true Witness, the<f>[6]</f> Beginning <i>and</i> Origin of God's creation:</J>gð)GÚ
<J>He who has an ear, let him hear <i>and</i> heed what the Spirit says to the churches.'</J>‚zð(…mÚ<J>He who overcomes <n>[the world through believing that Jesus is the Son of God]</n>, I will make him a<f>[4]</f> pillar in the temple of My God; he will most certainly never be put out of it, and I will write on him the name of My God, and the name of the city of My God, the new Jerusalem, which descends out of heaven from My God, and My <n>[own]</n> new name.</J>ð'‚Ú<J>I am coming quickly. Hold tight what you have, so that no one will take your crown <n>[by leading you to renounce the faith]</n>.</J>‚ð&„Ú
<J>Because you have kept the word of My endurance <n>[My command to persevere]</n>, I will keep you <n>[safe]</n> from the hour of trial, that <i>hour</i> which is about to come on the whole <n>[inhabited]</n> world, to test those who live on the earth.</J>}ð%ƒsÚ	<J>Take note, I will make <i>those</i> of the synagogue of Satan, who say that they are Jews and are not, but lieâ€”I will make them come and bow down at your feet and <i>make them</i> know <n>[without any doubt]</n> that I have loved you.</J>Tð$ƒ!Ú<pb/><J>'I know your deeds. See, I have set before you an open door which no one is able to shut, for you have a little power, and have kept My word, and have not renounced <i>or</i> denied My name.</J>‚8ð#„iÚ<t><J>"And to the angel (divine messenger) of the church in<f>[3]</f> Philadelphia write:</J> </t><br/><J>"These are the words of the Holy One, the True One, He who has the key <n>[to the house]</n> of David, He who opens and no one will <n>[be able to]</n> shut, and He who shuts and no one opens:</J>gð"GÚ<J>He who has an ear, let him hear <i>and</i> heed what the Spirit says to the churches.'</J>‚Uð!…#Ú<J>He who overcomes <n>[the world through believing that Jesus is the Son of God]</n> will accordingly be dressed in white clothing; and I will never blot out his name from the Book of Life, and I will confess <i>and</i> openly acknowledge his name before My Father and before His angels <n>[saying that he is one of Mine]</n>.</J>‚ð „Ú<J>But you <n>[still]</n> have a few people in Sardis who have not soiled their clothes <n>[that is, contaminated their character and personal integrity with sin]</n>; and they will walk with Me <n>[dressed]</n> in white, because they are worthy (righteous).</J>ƒð†Ú<J>So remember <i>and</i> take to heart the lessons you have received and heard. Keep <i>and</i> obey them, and repent <n>[change your sinful way of thinking, and demonstrate your repentance with new behavior that proves a conscious decision to turn away from sin]</n>. So then, if you do not wake up, I will come like a thief, and you will not know at what hour I will come to you.</J>‚ðƒ{Ú<J>Wake up, and strengthen <i>and</i> reaffirm what remains <n>[of your faithful commitment to Me]</n>, which is about to die; for I have not found <n>[any of]</n> your deeds completed in the sight of My God <i>or</i> meeting His requirements.</J>‚8ð	„kÚ<pb/><t><J>"To the angel (divine messenger) of the church in<f>[1]</f> Sardis write:</J> </t><br/><J>"These are the words of Him who has<f>[2]</f> the seven Spirits of God and the seven stars: 'I know your deeds; you have a name (reputation) that you are alive, but <n>[in reality]</n> you are dead.</J>gðGÚ<J>He who has an ear, let him hear <i>and</i> heed what the Spirit says to the churches.'</J>@ð{Ú<J>and I will give him the<f>[20]</f> Morning Star.</J>`ðƒ9Ú<J><e>and he shall shepherd</e> <i>and</i> <e>rule them with a rod of iron, as the earthen pots are broken in pieces</e>, as I also have received <i>authority</i> <n>[and power to rule them]</n> from My Father;</J>‚ð„Ú<J>And he who overcomes <n>[the world through believing that Jesus is the Son of God]</n> and he who keeps My deeds <n>[doing things that please Me]</n> until the <n>[very]</n> end, <e>to him I will give authority</e> <i>and</i> <e>power over the nations</e>;</J>FðÚ<J>except to hold tightly to what you have until I come.</J>NðƒÚ<J>But to the rest of you in Thyatira, who do not hold this teaching, who have not explored <i>and</i> known the<f>[19]</f> depths of Satan, as they call themâ€”I place no other burden on you,</J>‚vð…eÚ<J>And I will kill her children (followers) with<f>[17]</f> pestilence <n>[thoroughly annihilating them]</n>, and all the churches will know <n>[without any doubt]</n> that I am He who searches the<f>[18]</f> minds and hearts <n>[the innermost thoughts, purposes]</n>; and I will give to each one of you <n>[a reward or punishment]</n> according to your deeds.</J>NðƒÚ<J><f>[16]</f> Listen carefully, I will throw her on a bed <i>of sickness</i>, and those who commit adultery with her <n>[I will bring]</n> into great anguish, unless they repent of her deeds.</J>;ð‚oÚ<J>I gave her time to repent <n>[to change her inner self and her sinful way of thinking]</n>, but she has no desire to repent of her immorality <i>and</i> refuses to do so.</J>
